E["item:anaya-s-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Anaya's Pendant",z="darkshore",s="Anaya's Pendant is a keepsake carried by the restless ghost of Anaya Dawnrunner among the ruins of Ameth'Aran. It serves as a tragic token of remembrance for her lover, Cerellean Whiteclaw, who survived the Sundering only to find her spirit still tormented millennia later.",h="Anaya's Pendant is a keepsake carried by the restless ghost of Anaya Dawnrunner among the ruins of Ameth'Aran.",sec={{t="A Keepsake Across Millennia",b="Ten thousand years ago, during the cataclysmic destruction of the Well of Eternity, the ancient kaldorei city of Ameth'Aran fell in ruin. Believing his beloved Anaya had perished, Cerellean Whiteclaw carried his profound grief into the long slumber alongside Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage. When he at last awakened, he wandered Darkshore only to discover that Anaya's tormented apparition still drifted through Ameth'Aran, bearing this very pendant. Unable to bear raising a hand against her himself, Cerellean asks passing travelers to release her spirit and recover the heirloom.",sp=0},{t="Parting and Peace",b="Returning the pendant to Cerellean in Auberdine allows the lingering spirit of Anaya Dawnrunner to briefly manifest before him one last time. Freed from the anguish binding her to the haunted ruins of Ameth'Aran, her ghost fades peacefully into the night, leaving Cerellean alone with the pendant and his enduring memory of their ancient love.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Anaya's Pendant come from?",a="The pendant is recovered from the ghost of Anaya Dawnrunner, who wanders the ancient kaldorei ruins of Ameth'Aran in southern Darkshore.",al={"where to get anayas pendant","how do i get anaya pendant","who drops anaya pendant"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Anaya's Pendant?",a="It belongs to Cerellean Whiteclaw, a grieving night elf residing in the coastal town of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"who do i give anayas pendant to","cerellean whiteclaw quest","turn in anayas pendant"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why couldn't Cerellean retrieve the pendant himself?",a="Cerellean discovered his lost love's spirit roaming the ruins of Ameth'Aran, but even after ten thousand years of sorrow, he could not bear the heartbreak of raising his own hand against her.",al={"why didnt cerellean kill anaya","why does cerellean need help"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you return the pendant to Cerellean?",a="When the pendant is brought back to Cerellean in Auberdine, Anaya's spirit briefly appears before him in farewell before fading away into peace, allowing Cerellean to grieve her memory at last.",al={"what happens to anaya","cerellean reaction"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Anaya's Pendant?",a="Anaya's Pendant is an ancient keepsake belonging to Anaya Dawnrunner, a kaldorei who perished thousands of years ago during the destruction of Ameth'Aran. Carried by her restless spirit among the ruins, the pendant serves as a poignant physical token of her enduring love and the life she shared with Cerellean Whiteclaw before the Sundering tore their world apart.",al={"what is anayas pendant","anaya pendant lore","who does the pendant belong to"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The pendant is a poignant reminder of the enduring scars left by the War of the Ancients, where countless lives and loves were torn apart during the Great Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="Like many druids who followed Shan'do Stormrage into the Emerald Dream, Cerellean slept for millennia hoping to escape his grief, only to wake to lingering ghosts in the waking world."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","pendant","well of eternity"},rel={"quest:963","npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:shan-do"},src={"Anaya's Pendant","For Love Eternal"}}
E["item:ancient-moonstone-seal"] = {t="item",n="Ancient Moonstone Seal",z="darkshore",s="The Ancient Moonstone Seal is a powerful relic of Highborne sorcery forged long before the Sundering. Imbued with potent arcane binding magic, it served as the anchor holding the spirit of Asterion captive within the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",h="The Ancient Moonstone Seal is a powerful relic of Highborne sorcery forged long before the Sundering.",sec={{t="A Prison of Highborne Sorcery",b="Forged by Asterion's former master, the powerful Highborne sorcerer Athrikus Narassin, the Ancient Moonstone Seal was crafted to serve as an unbreakable metaphysical anchor. While the Well of Eternity still stood and Queen Azshara reigned, Athrikus used the artifact to bind Asterion's soul to the pillars of Bashal'Aran. Over ten millennia later, Asterion remained an incorporeal prisoner to its magic, unable to break the ward with any strength or spell he possessed.",sp=0},{t="Destruction in Ameth'Aran",b="Following the devastation of the Great Sundering, the seal eventually passed into the claws of the Deth'ryll satyrs who infest the surrounding wilderness of Darkshore. Because ordinary force cannot mar Highborne enchanted stone, destroying the artifact requires exposing it to the ancient blue flame enduring in the twin ruins of Ameth'Aran to the south. Consuming the seal in this arcane fire permanently shatters Athrikus's binding ward, finally releasing Asterion's spirit into the mortal realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="It is an ancient magical relic crafted by the Highborne sorcerer Athrikus Narassin. It serves as an arcane key that binds the ghost of Asterion to his shrine within the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",al={"what is moonstone seal","seal of asterion","bashal'aran seal"},it="identity"},{q="Who possesses the seal before it is recovered?",a="The seal fell into the hands of the Deth'ryll satyr inhabiting the ruins surrounding Bashal'Aran in Darkshore, who used its presence to command lesser grell minions.",al={"who has the seal","where to find moonstone seal","who drops moonstone seal"}},{q="How can the seal be destroyed?",a="Ordinary weapons or contemporary magic cannot harm the relic. It must be cast into the ancient, everlasting flame that still burns within the twin ruins of Ameth'Aran to the south.",al={"how to break the seal","destroy moonstone seal","where do i destroy the seal"}},{q="What happens when the seal is destroyed?",a="Incinerating the seal in Ameth'Aran's flame breaks the ancient binding enchantments holding Asterion, granting his spirit freedom to roam the world after thousands of years of captivity.",al={"what does breaking the seal do","asterion freed"},sp=1},{q="Where does the Ancient Moonstone Seal come from, and who made it?",a="The Ancient Moonstone Seal was crafted millennia ago during the height of the kaldorei empire, prior to the Great Sundering. It was forged through the sorcery of one of the most powerful Highborne lords—Athrikus Narassin—to serve as a mystical binding mechanism.",al={"who made ancient moonstone seal","ancient moonstone seal origin","creator of ancient moonstone seal"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Asterion want the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="Asterion seeks the seal because it is the very anchor that keeps his spirit bound within the ruined shrine of Bashal'Aran. As long as it remains intact, he is trapped behind invisible bars, unable to leave his ancient prison or rest. By recovering the seal, he hopes to destroy it in the ancient flames of Ameth'Aran and finally gain his freedom.",al={"why does asterion want the seal","why find ancient moonstone seal","who wants ancient moonstone seal"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The seal is a haunting relic of the Highborne's unchecked arcane prowess and cruel enslavement practices prior to the Great Sundering.",["class:Mage"]="The moonstone demonstrates the enduring power of ancient elven abjuration magic, maintaining its binding field uninterrupted for over ten thousand years."},kw={"ameth'aran","ancient moonstone seal","asterion","athrikus","bashal'aran","darkshore","deth'ryll","highborne","moonstone"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:954","subzone:ameth-aran","zone:darkshore","topic:highborne","topic:satyr"},src={"Ancient Moonstone Seal","Bashal'Aran (3)","Bashal'Aran (4)"}}
E["item:athrikus-narassin-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Athrikus Narassin's Head",z="darkshore",s="This severed head is proof of the death of Athrikus Narassin, an ancient warlock who directed dark rituals in northern Darkshore. Taken from the heights of the ruined spire, it serves to confirm the disruption of demonic activity centered around the Tower of Althalaxx.",h="This severed head is proof of the death of Athrikus Narassin, an ancient warlock who directed dark rituals in...",sec={{t="Blight Upon Althalaxx",b="Perched at the pinnacle of the Tower of Althalaxx, Athrikus Narassin commanded a coven of dark sorcerers practicing fel magic along the Darkshore coast. Ancient and entrenched, Narassin coordinated demonic summonings that threatened the surrounding wilderness. Claiming his head shatters the coven's leadership, driving back their immediate foothold in the region, even if the lingering corruption promises future vigilance will be needed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Athrikus Narassin?",a="Athrikus Narassin was an ancient and powerful warlock presiding over the cultists entrenched in the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He directed the coven's demonic rituals from the very top of the spire.",al={"who is athrikus","athrikus lore","who is the warlock"},it="identity"},{q="Why is his head needed?",a="Alliance scouts monitoring the Tower of Althalaxx require irrefutable proof that the master warlock has been slain. Presenting his severed head confirms his demise and marks the strike against the demonic forces as a success.",al={"why take the head","athrikus head purpose","what is head for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Athrikus Narassin located?",a="He resides at the very summit of the Tower of Althalaxx, situated in northern Darkshore, heavily guarded by his devoted cultists and summoned demons.",al={"where to find athrikus","athrikus location","tower of althalaxx top"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does killing him eliminate the demonic threat completely?",a="While Athrikus's death deals a severe blow to the dark ritualists and scatters their current operations, scouts believe the demonic forces will eventually regroup, requiring ongoing defense of Darkshore.",al={"are demons gone","is the tower cleansed","did we beat the cult"},it="threat"},{q="What is Athrikus Narassin's Head?",a="It is the severed head of Athrikus Narassin, an ancient night elf warlock commanding the dark forces entrenched within the Tower of Althalaxx. You take it as irrefutable proof that the leader of the local cult has been slain.",al={"what is athrikus head","athrikus narassin head"},it="item",add=true},{q="Where does Athrikus Narassin's Head come from?",a="It is claimed directly from the apex of the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Athrikus Narassin resides at the pinnacle of the ruined structure, surrounded by his most dangerous warlocks and fel summoned minions until struck down.",al={"where did athrikus head come from","where to get athrikus head","who made athrikus head"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Purging Athrikus Narassin removes a festering demonic blight from ancient Kaldorei ruins along the northern shores of Kalimdor.",["class:Warlock"]="Athrikus's mastery of fel powers made him a formidable practitioner, though his reckless visibility in Althalaxx proved his undoing."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus narassin","cultists","darkshore","fel","severed head","warlock"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","zone:darkshore","topic:warlock","quest:494"},src={"Athrikus Narassin's Head","The Tower of Althalaxx (8)"}}
E["item:bottom-of-gelkak-s-key"] = {t="item",n="Bottom of Gelkak's Key",z="darkshore",s="The Bottom of Gelkak's Key is one of three fragments of a shattered mechanical winding key belonging to the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast. After his vessel foundered off Darkshore, the piece was scavenged by the shoreline's native reef crawlers.",h="The Bottom of Gelkak's Key is one of three fragments of a shattered mechanical winding key belonging to the...",sec={{t="Claimed by Crawlers",b="When Gelkak Gyromast's ship was sunk by threshadons off the coast of Darkshore, the gnome was thrown ashore along with his belongings. Among his most prized possessions was the winding key used to activate his mechanical first mate. The key shattered on the coastal rocks into three distinct pieces, and local scavengers immediately descended upon the debris. The bottom piece of the key was snatched up by the aggressive crustaceans wandering the surf—specifically the reef and tide crawlers that pick through the detritus along the tideline.",sp=0},{t="Reassembly",b="Gelkak cannot activate his mechanical crewman without reuniting the bottom fragment with the middle and top sections, which were dragged off by coastal murlocs and inland foreststriders. Only by prying this heavy segment from the shells of the shoreline crabs can the gnome pirate hope to restore his construct and seek vengeance for his ruined expedition.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Bottom of Gelkak's Key used for?",a="It is one of three pieces needed to repair the winding key belonging to the stranded pirate Gelkak Gyromast, which is required to reactivate his mechanical first mate.",al={"what does gelkaks key do","purpose of bottom of gelkaks key","why do i need gelkak key bottom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this key piece come from?",a="It is found on the coast of Darkshore, scavenged by local crabs such as Encrusted Tide Crawlers and Raging Reef Crawlers along the water's edge.",al={"where to find bottom of gelkak key","who drops bottom of gelkaks key","gelkak key bottom location"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the key broken into three pieces?",a="When Gelkak's ship was wrecked by threshadons, he washed ashore and the key struck the shoreline rocks, snapping into fragments that were scattered among the local wildlife.",al={"why did gelkaks key break","how did the key break"}},{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is a stranded gnome pirate camped on the shores of Darkshore after a threshadon attack destroyed his vessel and scattered his gear.",al={"who is gelkak","gelkak gyromast lore"}},{q="What is the Bottom of Gelkak's Key?",a="It is the lowest fragment of a mechanical key belonging to the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast. When his vessel foundered off the coast of Darkshore, the key shattered on the jagged rocks upon impact, and this piece was scavenged from the debris by the local shoreline crawlers.",al={"what is bottom of gelkaks key","bottom of gelkak key","what is this key piece"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will recognize the piece as part of a specialized winding implement designed to power complex clockwork automatons.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes will appreciate that even shipwrecked and stranded on a hostile coastline, Gyromast relied on clockwork ingenuity rather than flesh-and-blood crew."},kw={"crawler","darkshore","first mate","gelkak","gyromast","key","retrieval","shipwreck"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2098","item:middle-of-gelkak-s-key","item:top-of-gelkak-s-key","quest:2078","zone:darkshore","topic:pirate"},src={"Bottom of Gelkak's Key","Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["item:cliffspring-river-sample"] = {t="item",n="Cliffspring River Sample",z="darkshore",s="A glass vial containing murky, foul-smelling water drawn from the base of the Cliffspring River waterfall in Darkshore. Gathered on behalf of Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, the sample provides tangible proof of an encroaching corruption threatening the coastal settlement.",h="A glass vial containing murky, foul-smelling water drawn from the base of the Cliffspring River waterfall in...",sec={{t="A Tainted Current",b="The Cliffspring River flows down from the rugged eastern heights of Darkshore, tumbling past ancient stone bridges before washing out into the sea along Mist's Edge. Lately, the river's crystalline waters have turned foul and visibly corrupted. Fearing that the toxic wash will soon contaminate Auberdine's shoreline and water supply, the night elf Thundris Windweaver commissioned travelers to draw this water sample directly from the pool beneath the river's lower waterfall. The sample confirms the worst: unnatural rot is drifting steadily downstream toward the coast.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of Felwood",b="While local Blackwood furbolgs inhabit the upstream banks and suffer from its darkening influence, the water sample suggests a far deeper malady than simple tribal mischief. Thundris recognizes the foul nature of the corruption as originating high above the cliffs to the east, in the blighted expanse of Felwood. The tainted sample serves as definitive proof that the demonic sickness plaguing the mountaintops is leaching downward into Darkshore's watersheds, forcing Auberdine's defenders to prepare an active response.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Cliffspring River Sample collected?",a="It is drawn from the pool beneath the first waterfall along the Cliffspring River, located north of Auberdine. Travelers must follow the river inland until reaching the waterfall beneath an overhead bridge.",al={"where do i get the sample","cliffspring river location","waterfall pool sample"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver need this water?",a="Thundris fears the river's foulness will contaminate the coastal waters near Auberdine. Gathering and examining a physical sample allows him to analyze the nature of the taint and formulate a plan to counter it.",al={"why gather the water","thundris river quest","purpose of river sample"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is causing the Cliffspring River to turn foul?",a="While the corrupted Blackwood furbolgs dwell along the river, Thundris suspects the true origin lies further east in Felwood, whose lingering demonic blight is seeping into the mountain headwaters.",al={"what poisoned the river","why is the water corrupted","source of river corruption"},it="danger"},{q="Are the Blackwood furbolgs responsible for the poison?",a="They exacerbate the problem along the riverbanks, but they are not the root cause. The furbolgs themselves have fallen prey to the broader corruption washing down from the blighted lands to the east.",al={"did furbolgs do it","blackwood furbolg taint","are furbolgs poisoning water"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Cliffspring River Sample?",a="It is a vial of foul, corrupted river water gathered in an empty sampling tube from the base of the waterfall along the Cliffspring River. It serves as tangible proof that a foul taint is washing downstream through Darkshore.",al={"cliffspring river sample","what is cliffspring river sample","cliffspring water sample"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Cliffspring River Sample come from?",a="The sample is collected from the pool beneath the first waterfall of the Cliffspring River, north of Auberdine. While you gather the natural water yourself using an empty sampling tube, its unnatural foulness originates from corrupting forces upstream flowing down from Felwood.",al={"where does cliffspring river sample come from","cliffspring river sample origin","who made cliffspring sample"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, any corruption of northern Kalimdor's waters is a grave omen of the ongoing blight spreading outward from Felwood.",["class:Druid"]="Druids are keenly attuned to the balance of natural waterways, making the unnatural toxicity of the Cliffspring sample an urgent priority to study and cleanse."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","felwood","sample","thundris","tube","waterfall","windweaver"},rel={"quest:4762","quest:4761","item:empty-sampling-tube","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood","subzone:mist-s-edge","topic:furbolg"},src={"Cliffspring River Sample","The Cliffspring River"}}
E["item:corrupted-kor-gem"] = {t="item",n="Corrupted Kor Gem",z="darkshore",s="A Corrupted Kor Gem is a potent magical conduit warped by the dark rites of the naga residing around Blackfathom Deeps. Spellcasters covet such stones for their capacity to store sheer arcane force, though the gem's tainted state demands purification before it can serve righteous crafts.",h="A Corrupted Kor Gem is a potent magical conduit warped by the dark rites of the naga residing around...",sec={{t="Vessels of Tainted Power",b="Kor gems naturally possess the rare ability to capture and contain substantial magical energies, making them invaluable focuses for sorcerers and enchanted smithing. Along the coastline near the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, however, the resident naga oracles and tide priestesses claim these gems for their own shadowy rituals. Through foul enchantments, the serpent-kin warp the stone, suffusing it with malevolent, sea-borne corruption. While this infusion taints the gem's nature, the core latent power remains potent, drawing those in need of exceptional magical foci to harvest them from the naga.",sp=0},{t="Purification and Smithing",b="A Corrupted Kor Gem cannot safely be worked into sacred implements without cleansing. Night elf sages, such as Thundris Windweaver of Auberdine, understand the ancient methods needed to scour away the naga's taint. Purifying the gem diminishes its volatile raw power to an extent, but stabilizes it so holy champions—most notably paladins forging blessed armaments under the guidance of artisans like Jordan Stilwell—can utilize the stone without succumbing to insidious darkness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Kor Gem used for?",a="Kor gems act as powerful conduits and reservoirs for arcane energy. Spellcasters utilize them to hold immense reserves of power for their incantations, while skilled blacksmiths embed them into enchanted weapons to channel magical forces.",al={"what are kor gems","purpose of kor gem","kor gem lore"},it="power"},{q="Where are Corrupted Kor Gems found?",a="Corrupted Kor Gems are carried by naga spellcasters—specifically Blackfathom Tide Priestesses and Blackfathom Oracles—who dwell outside and within the ancient ruins leading to Blackfathom Deeps on the Ashenvale and Darkshore border.",al={"where to find corrupted kor gem","kor gem location","who drops kor gem"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why must the gem be purified?",a="The naga saturate the gems with foul magic during their rituals. Attempting to use a corrupted gem in sacred crafting could contaminate the forge or the wielder, requiring a master of nature or light, such as Thundris Windweaver, to purge the evil before it is worked into an arm.",al={"cleanse kor gem","why purify kor gem","is the gem evil"},it="motive"},{q="Does cleansing the gem weaken its power?",a="Yes. Removing the naga's taint purges the wild, malicious energy that bloated the gem, making the stone slightly weaker overall. However, the residual energy remains pure, stable, and strong enough for consecrated metalworking.",al={"does purification ruin the gem","weaker after purification"}},{q="What is a Corrupted Kor Gem?",a="A Corrupted Kor Gem is a magical vessel originally meant to store raw arcane or spellcasting energy, but twisted by dark sorcery. Naga spellcasters have infused the stone with their own vile power, turning an otherwise neutral conduit into a tainted relic brimming with malevolent energy.",al={"what is corrupted kor gem","corrupted kor gem info","tell me about corrupted kor gem"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Corrupted Kor Gem come from, and who made it?",a="While Kor gems were originally crafted as conduits for spellcasters to store magical energy, these corrupted versions are held and altered by the naga dwelling around Blackfathom Deeps in northwestern Ashenvale. Naga priestesses and oracles have saturated the gems with their own foul magic, transforming them into tools of dark ritual.",al={"who made corrupted kor gem","corrupted kor gem origin","where did kor gem come from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want a Corrupted Kor Gem?",a="Holy paladins seek out the gem at the behest of the blacksmith Landen Stilwell to aid in forging a weapon of righteousness, though it must first be cleansed of its evil magic by Thundris Windweaver. Its ability to hold vast reserves of energy makes it invaluable for potent ritual craft once properly purified.",al={"why get corrupted kor gem","who wants corrupted kor gem","why do i need kor gem"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Paladins seeking to forge sacred armaments must recover and purify a Kor Gem as a testament to their ability to confront evil and cleanse darkness into righteous strength.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elf scholars like Thundris Windweaver recognize the danger of naga relics encroaching on Darkshore and safeguard the knowledge needed to cleanse the ancient stones."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","corrupted kor gem","kor gem","naga","purification","thundris windweaver","tide priestess"},rel={"quest:1442","quest:1653","zone:blackfathom","topic:naga","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Corrupted Kor Gem","Seeking the Kor Gem","The Path of the Adept"}}
E["item:crawler-leg"] = {t="item",n="Crawler Leg",z="darkshore",s="A Crawler Leg is a harvested limb taken from the various crabs prowling the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore. Though worthless to most travelers, these hardy chitinous appendages are surprisingly suited to mechanical improvisation.",h="A Crawler Leg is a harvested limb taken from the various crabs prowling the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore.",sec={{t="Gnomish Ingenuity on the Coast",b="The crabs of Darkshore—ranging from pygmy tide crawlers to larger reef crawlers—are known for their sturdy, resilient shells. While night elf sentinels pay little mind to the discarded limbs of coastal vermin, the eccentric gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle found an unexpected use for them. Operating out of Auberdine, Wizbang designed his prototype long-distance communication devices, known as buzzboxes, to run on improvised local components. The segmented joints and durable chitin of crawler legs provide the precise mechanical friction and leverage required to repair Buzzbox 827, situated along the shoreline just south of town.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are crawler legs used for?",a="Crawler legs are collected to repair Buzzbox 827, an experimental communication station placed along the Darkshore coastline just south of Auberdine by the gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle.",al={"crawler leg purpose","why keep crawler legs","buzzbox crawler leg"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where do crawler legs come from?",a="They can be scavenged from various species of crabs along the beaches of Darkshore, including Pygmy Tide Crawlers, Young Reef Crawlers, Encrusted Tide Crawlers, and Reef Crawlers.",al={"crawler leg source","which crabs drop crawler legs","where to find crawler leg"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does a mechanical buzzbox need crab legs?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle intentionally engineered his machines to utilize parts from nearby wildlife for ongoing field maintenance. The rigid joints and chitinous segments of the crawler legs slot directly into the buzzbox's grinding gears to restore its internal mechanisms.",al={"why crabs for machine","buzzbox crab legs lore","how does crawler leg fix buzzbox"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Crawler Leg?",a="A Crawler Leg is a severed limb harvested from the various species of crawlers skittering along the mist-shrouded shores of Darkshore. With their rigid, chitinous shells and durable joints, these legs are surprisingly tough and suited for rugged, improvised mechanical repairs.",al={"what is crawler leg","crawler leg item","about crawler legs"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle's decision to use crab appendages as makeshift mechanical levers reflects classic gnomish field improvisation, bypassing standard metal linkages in favor of immediately available local resources.",["race:Gnome"]="Only a gnome would see a beach crawling with aggressive crustaceans and conclude that their severed legs are the ideal replacement parts for a delicate long-distance telecommunications network."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 827","crawler leg","darkshore","reef crawler","tide crawler","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:983","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},src={"Crawler Leg","Buzzbox 827 (quest)"}}
E["item:curative-animal-salve"] = {t="item",n="Curative Animal Salve",z="darkshore",s="Curative Animal Salve is an herbal remedy brewed by druidic herbalists to soothe and heal wildlife afflicted by spreading ecological sickness. Formulated in both Darkshore and the Barrens, it serves as a frontline treatment for sickly creatures suffering from the land's unseen taints.",h="Curative Animal Salve is an herbal remedy brewed by druidic herbalists to soothe and heal wildlife afflicted...",sec={{t="Mending the Wilds",b="Crafted from locally gathered herbal reagents, Curative Animal Salve is prepared in ten-dose batches to treat wildlife caught in the throes of spreading corruption. In the misty forests of Darkshore, Alanndarian Nightsong directs young druids to apply the ointment to sickly deer wandering between the Cliffspring River and the borders of Ashenvale. Far to the south in the arid expanse of the Barrens, Tonga Runetotem brews an identical remedy to treat sickly gazelles grazing north of the Crossroads. While both herbalists work with local authorities to produce larger supplies, field practitioners administer the salve directly to beasts suffering from environmental malaise.",sp=0},{t="Symptoms of a Deeper Malaise",b="Applying the salve directly eases an animal's suffering, yet the Cenarion Circle views these afflictions as mere symptoms of a much greater disturbance. In Moonglade, Dendrite Starblaze observes that neither the afflicted deer of the coast nor the suffering gazelles of the savannah are random casualties. Instead, they are unwitting victims of a spreading blight that touches Kalimdor from multiple directions. Administering the salve serves as a fundamental rite for initiates, testing their dedication to safeguarding the natural world and mastering the arts of cleansing poison.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Curative Animal Salve used for?",a="The salve is applied directly to afflicted wildlife to cure their ailments. Druids use it to treat sickly deer wandering through Darkshore or sickly gazelles grazing north of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"curative animal salve purpose","how to use curative animal salve","what does the salve do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who prepares the salve?",a="In Darkshore, Alanndarian Nightsong prepares the salve in Auberdine using gathered reagents. In the Barrens, Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads brews the concoction for Horde druids.",al={"who makes the salve","where does the salve come from"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the deer and gazelles sick in the first place?",a="According to Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle, the wildlife are victims of a growing taint and corruption spreading throughout Kalimdor, serving as early casualties of an unbalancing ecological blight.",al={"why are animals sickly","what is poisoning darkshore deer","barrens gazelle sickness"},it="motive"},{q="How many doses does a batch contain?",a="A standard field batch provides enough ointment for ten individual applications before the herbal mixture is entirely exhausted.",al={"how many charges","how many uses on salve"},gp=true},{q="What is Curative Animal Salve?",a="Curative Animal Salve is an herbal remedy concocted to treat afflicted wildlife suffering from spreading unnatural sickness. Prepared by druidic allies using local reagents, it cleanses the malaise poisoning innocent creatures such as the deer of Darkshore and the gazelles of the Barrens.",al={"curative salve","what is animal salve","curative animal salve lore"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Administering this remedy is a foundational trial in learning to soothe poisons and disease, proving your devotion to the Cenarion Circle's mission across Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="Utilizing the salve in the Barrens demonstrates how tauren druids embody the teachings of Cenarius, working in harmony with ancestral circle rites to heal the earth."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","curative animal salve","curing the sick","power over poison","sickly deer","sickly gazelle","tonga runetotem"},rel={"quest:6124","quest:6125","topic:cenarion-circle","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:tonga-runetotem","zone:darkshore","zone:barrens"},src={"Curative Animal Salve","Curing the Sick (Alliance)","Curing the Sick (Horde)"}}
E["item:darkshore-grouper"] = {t="item",n="Darkshore Grouper",z="darkshore",s="Darkshore Grouper is a sturdy saltwater fish native to the misty coastal waters along Darkshore. Prized both as a tasty staple catch and a sporting quarry, it has become harder to harvest from the docks due to murloc activity driving local fishermen from their boats.",h="Darkshore Grouper is a sturdy saltwater fish native to the misty coastal waters along Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Staple of the Shrouded Coast",b="Found in the cold sea waters of Darkshore, the Darkshore Grouper is a prized catch for coastal anglers. The fish is valued for its culinary versatility, making its way into an array of simple coastal dishes favored by travelers and residents around Auberdine. While it can be hauled out of the surf with basic angling gear, fishermen consider hooking them as enjoyable as eating them.",sp=0},{t="The Murloc Menace",b="Historically, fishermen such as Gubber Blump took small vessels out into deeper waters to haul in grouper by the dozen. However, increasing aggression from coastal murlocs has grounded most boats around Auberdine. With anglers confined to the shorelines and docks, locals suspect the encroaching murlocs are devouring the local grouper stock, making a good haul harder to come by without patience.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Darkshore Grouper be found?",a="Darkshore Grouper are caught by casting a fishing line into the saltwater along the Darkshore coastline, including the waters surrounding Auberdine.",al={"where to fish grouper","darkshore grouper location","how to catch darkshore grouper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Darkshore Grouper in Auberdine?",a="Gubber Blump, a dwarven fisherman staying in Auberdine, asks travelers to catch Darkshore Grouper for him in exchange for a prized Blump Family Fishing Pole.",al={"who needs grouper","gubber blump fish","grouper quest giver"},it="wants"},{q="Why aren't fishermen using boats to catch grouper?",a="Aggressive murlocs have moved along the coastline of Darkshore, making boat trips out onto the water far too dangerous for local fishermen.",al={"why are boats stopped","auberdine fishing boats","murlocs grouper"},it="conflict"},{q="Do you need to be on a quest to catch a Darkshore Grouper?",a="No. Although it is the target of tasks requested by locals like Gubber Blump, Darkshore Grouper is a regular saltwater fish that can be hooked by any angler casting their line into Darkshore waters.",al={"is grouper a quest item","can i fish grouper anytime"},gp=true},{q="What is Darkshore Grouper?",a="Darkshore Grouper is a local saltwater fish swimming off the misty coastline of Darkshore. Highly prized by local anglers like Gubber Blump, it is celebrated both as great sport to reel in from the surf and as versatile fare for home cooking.",al={"what is darkshore grouper","darkshore grouper fish","about darkshore grouper"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Darkshore Grouper come from?",a="Darkshore Grouper is a wild saltwater fish native to the coastal ocean waters along Darkshore. It is not crafted or created by anyone, though catching it requires casting a line into the surf off the shore and docks.",al={"darkshore grouper origin","where does darkshore grouper come from","where is darkshore grouper from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Gubber Blump want Darkshore Grouper?",a="Gubber Blump simply loves catching and eating them, boasting that there are plenty of fine dishes you can cook up with a fresh catch. Because hostile murlocs have driven the local fishing boats out of the water, he relies on helpful travelers to pull them from the coast.",al={"why want darkshore grouper","why does gubber want grouper","what is darkshore grouper used for"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Darkshore Grouper serves as a versatile ingredient for simple coastal recipes, making it a handy catch for traveling chefs looking to hone their trade along the shore.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven angler Gubber Blump represents his family's proud fishing heritage on the shores of Kalimdor, rewarding anyone who can match his kin's catching skills."},kw={"auberdine","blump family fishing pole","darkshore","darkshore grouper","fishing","grouper","gubber blump","murloc"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","item:gaffer-jack"},src={"Darkshore Grouper","The Family and the Fishing Pole"}}
E["item:death-cap"] = {t="item",n="Death Cap",z="darkshore",s="The Death Cap is a rare, potent fungus found hidden in the shadowed cavern behind Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. Sought by night elf alchemists for its unique properties, harvesting it requires venturing into a subterranean den warned against by the Grove of the Ancients.",h="The Death Cap is a rare, potent fungus found hidden in the shadowed cavern behind Cliffspring Falls in...",sec={{t="A Toxic Bloom in the Dark",b="The Death Cap grows exclusively in the subterranean dampness of the cave tucked behind Cliffspring Falls, situated along the northeastern mountain ridges of Darkshore. Unlike the more plentiful scaber stalks that carpet the surrounding cavern floor, the Death Cap is scarce and distinct. Night elf herbalists like Barithras Moonshade value the fungus for experimental brewing, though retrieving even a single specimen requires braving a cavern whispered to harbor a nascent corruption.",sp=0},{t="Omen of Cliffspring",b="Harvesting a Death Cap is as much a reconnaissance mission as an alchemical errand. Guardians from the Grove of the Ancients warned local Kaldorei against approaching the falls, sensing a foul presence taking root in the darkness. Those who step into the cavern to pluck the mushroom must face whatever lurking forces have claimed the damp hollow as their lair.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find a Death Cap?",a="Death Caps grow inside the hidden cave behind Cliffspring Falls, located in northeastern Darkshore against the mountain wall.",al={"death cap location","where is death cap","cliffspring cave mushroom"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this mushroom?",a="Barithras Moonshade, an alchemist residing in the coastal settlement of Auberdine, seeks the Death Cap to brew a specialized potion.",al={"who needs death cap","barithras mushroom quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why didn't Barithras Moonshade collect it himself?",a="Tree guardians from the Grove of the Ancients warned Barithras to avoid the cavern behind Cliffspring Falls, sensing that an encroaching evil had made the cave its hiding place.",al={"why not get it himself","barithras warning"},it="motive"},{q="How does the Death Cap differ from a Scaber Stalk?",a="While scaber stalks are relatively plentiful throughout the Cliffspring cavern floor, the Death Cap is a rarer, more potent fungus requiring careful scouting to find.",al={"death cap vs scaber stalk","difference between mushrooms"},it="item"},{q="What is a Death Cap?",a="The Death Cap is an exceedingly rare and potent mushroom found deep within the shadowy recesses of Darkshore. Unlike ordinary woodland fungi, it thrives only in specific, hidden caverns, such as the cavern tucked behind Cliffspring Falls. Its ominous name reflects both its rarity and its potential danger, making it a prized specimen for alchemists and herbalists studying the unique flora of the region.",al={"what is death cap","death cap mushroom","what kind of mushroom is death cap"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Though gathering the Death Cap for Barithras requires no professional sickle, any herbalist will appreciate the hazard of harvesting rare fungi in damp, corrupted subterranean pockets.",["race:NightElf"]="Retrieving the Death Cap serves two masters: aiding Barithras's potion-making in Auberdine while verifying the dire premonitions voiced by the Grove of the Ancients."},kw={"auberdine","barithras moonshade","cave mushrooms","cliffspring falls","darkshore","death cap","grove of the ancients","scaber stalk"},rel={"quest:947","npc:barithras-moonshade","subzone:cliffspring-falls","item:scaber-stalk","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:952"},src={"Death Cap","Cave Mushrooms"}}
E["item:electropeller"] = {t="item",n="Electropeller",z="darkshore",s="An electropeller is a specialized mechanical component engineered by the gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle. Intended to power an explosive waterfowl decoy, a full bag of these gadgets was lost across Darkshore's freshwater rivers during an ill-fated nighttime outing.",h="An electropeller is a specialized mechanical component engineered by the gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle.",sec={{t="Mishaps along the Riverbank",b="Gnomish engineering requires precision, but the inventors behind it are not always so methodical. Wizbang Cranktoggle, an eccentric gnome operating out of Auberdine, devised the electropeller as a propulsion component for an experimental, self-propelled, exploding duck decoy. While scouting the waterways of Darkshore after having one too many drinks, Cranktoggle blacked out and returned to consciousness hours later with singed hair and an empty pack. His collection of electropellers had tumbled into the freshwater currents, leaving the components scattered throughout Darkshore's rivers and lakes until recovered by patient anglers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an electropeller used for?",a="Electropellers are motorized propulsion mechanisms designed by Wizbang Cranktoggle. He invented them specifically to power an experimental, self-propelled, exploding duck decoy he was developing in Darkshore.",al={"electropeller purpose","what does an electropeller do","why duck decoy"},it="purpose"},{q="How did these parts end up in the rivers of Darkshore?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle was roaming Darkshore at night searching for a testing waterway while a bit intoxicated. He passed out and woke up back in Auberdine with scorched hair, having accidentally dropped his entire sack of parts into the freshwater streams.",al={"why in the water","how did electropellers get lost","cranktoggle mistake"},it="origin"},{q="Where can electropellers be recovered?",a="They drift in Darkshore's inland freshwater bodies, including the Cliffspring River and the Wildbend River, where lucky anglers can dredge them up from the water.",al={"where to fish electropellers","electropeller locations","cliffspring river fishing"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants these components returned?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome residing in Auberdine, needs twelve of them back so he can carry on with his decoy research.",al={"who needs electropellers","who is cranktoggle","auberdine gnome quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is an electropeller?",a="An electropeller is a specialized mechanical propulsion component crafted by gnome engineering. These motorized parts are designed to drive aquatic devices, specifically the eccentric inventions conceived by Wizbang Cranktoggle, such as his motorized duck decoys.",al={"what is electropeller","electropeller item","what are electropellers"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The electropeller is classic gnomish contraption work: ambitious, motorized, and hazardous, designed for an explosive duck decoy that ended up in the river before it ever saw a proper test run.",["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle carries on the proud gnomish tradition of pairing wild technical ambition with baffling misadventures, cheerfully asking passing anglers to salvage the results of his late-night experiments."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring river","darkshore","duck decoy","electropeller","electropellers","wildbend river","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1580","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","item:gaffer-jack","quest:1579","subzone:wildbend-river","quest:4762"},src={"Electropeller","Electropellers"}}
E["item:empty-cleansing-bowl"] = {t="item",n="Empty Cleansing Bowl",z="darkshore",s="The Empty Cleansing Bowl is a ritual vessel given by Thundris Windweaver to aid in investigating the corruption of the Blackwood furbolgs. When filled at the Auberdine moonwell and combined with food samples, it creates a mixture capable of temporarily breaking a satyr's demonic sway.",h="The Empty Cleansing Bowl is a ritual vessel given by Thundris Windweaver to aid in investigating the...",sec={{t="A Vessel of Purification",b="Entrusted to adventurers by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, the Empty Cleansing Bowl is crafted to carry sacred waters from the local moonwell. The night elves discovered that the northern Blackwood furbolgs fell under demonic madness orchestrated by satyrs, who exert their will through enchanted talismans. By drawing pure lunar water into the bowl and blending it with the furbolgs' harvested nuts, grains, and fruits, the vessel produces a blessed meal that temporarily restores sanity to the afflicted creatures, exposing the satyr overseer responsible.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do I do with the Empty Cleansing Bowl?",a="Take the bowl to the Auberdine moonwell and dip it into the blessed waters to create a Filled Cleansing Bowl. Afterwards, you will need to gather grain, nut, and fruit samples from the northern Blackwood furbolg camp to combine with it.",al={"empty cleansing bowl use","how to use empty cleansing bowl","where to fill cleansing bowl"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why do the night elves need this bowl to fight the furbolg corruption?",a="The Blackwood furbolgs are bound by the dark magic of satyr talismans. Thundris Windweaver uses the bowl to hold a sanctified mixture that temporarily cures the furbolgs of their frenzy, drawing out their hidden satyr controller, Xabraxxis.",al={"why cleansing bowl","cleansing bowl purpose"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Who provides the Empty Cleansing Bowl?",a="Thundris Windweaver, a night elf scholar in Auberdine, gives you the bowl when assigning the task to uncover the source of the Blackwood corruption along the Cliffspring River.",al={"who gives cleansing bowl","cleansing bowl questgiver"},it="origin"},{q="What happens once the mixture is prepared?",a="Placing the finished mixture near the northern camp's bonfire cleanses the surrounding furbolgs long enough to draw the fury of the satyr Xabraxxis, allowing you to slay him and claim his Talisman of Corruption.",al={"cleansing bowl bonfire","place cleansing bowl"},sp=1},{q="What is the Empty Cleansing Bowl?",a="The Empty Cleansing Bowl is a ritual vessel entrusted to you by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. Crafted to hold the sanctified waters of a moonwell along with wild foodstuffs, it serves as the essential component for preparing a purifying offering capable of lifting the demonic taint afflicting the local wildlife and furbolgs.",al={"what is empty cleansing bowl","cleansing bowl lore","empty cleansing bowl purpose"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The cleansing ritual demonstrates the power of Elune's moonwells to undo vile demonic taint, offering hope that the night elves' old allies among the furbolgs might eventually be saved.",["class:Druid"]="Using moonwell waters to break unnatural afflictions reflects the core druidic calling to mend the wounded balance of nature across Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cleansing bowl","darkshore","empty cleansing bowl","moonwell","thundris windweaver","xabraxxis"},rel={"quest:4763","quest:4761","subzone:auberdine","item:talisman-of-corruption","topic:furbolg","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore","quest:4762"},src={"Empty Cleansing Bowl","The Blackwood Corrupted"}}
E["item:empty-cliffspring-falls-sampler"] = {t="item",n="Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler",z="darkshore",s="The Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler is a specialized flask entrusted to novice night elf druids by the Cenarion Circle. It is used to collect a water specimen from the mouth of Cliffspring River cave in Darkshore to help diagnose a foul poison corrupting the local wildlife.",h="The Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler is a specialized flask entrusted to novice night elf druids by the...",sec={{t="Investigating the Tainted Waters",b="Cliffspring Falls provides the principal freshwater source for northern Darkshore, making any disturbance to its headwaters a mortal danger to the local ecosystem. When the native deer population began succumbing to a virulent wasting poison, Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle provided these empty samplers to young druids sent out from Moonglade. Druids must venture deep into the cliffs near the falls, right to the entrance of a cave now overrun by hostile naga, to scoop up a viable water sample.",sp=0},{t="A Recipe for a Cure",b="Once filled, the container holds a murk that reveals a deeper ecological blight. Transported to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, the polluted sample confirms that foul agents are corrupting the water table. By studying the contaminants trapped within the glass, Alanndarian and the Cenarion druids gain the insight required to formulate an antidote and bestow the initiate with fundamental druidic healing rites.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this sampler?",a="It is an empty container given to druids to collect tainted water from the mouth of the cavern at Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. The sample allows Cenarion herbalists to diagnose and cure the poisoning affecting local wildlife.",al={"sampler use","what is cliffspring sampler for","empty sampler purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the water sample taken?",a="The sample must be scooped directly from the mouth of the cave near Cliffspring Falls, high in the northeastern hills of Darkshore. Hostile naga inhabit the cavern entrance, making the sampling hazardous.",al={"where to fill sampler","cliffspring sampler location","fill sampler spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who receives the filled container?",a="The filled sampler is delivered to Alanndarian Nightsong, a night elf healer and Cenarion representative stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",al={"who gets the filled sampler","where to turn in sampler","alanndarian sampler"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls being sampled instead of other rivers?",a="Cliffspring Falls serves as the primary freshwater source for northern Darkshore. Dendrite Starblaze traced the illness sickening the region's deer back to these headwaters, making a direct water sample essential to developing a remedy.",al={"why cliffspring falls","what is poisoning darkshore","cliffspring poison"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler?",a="It is a specialized vessel provided to Cenarion Circle druids to collect an uncontaminated sample of water from Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. Because the falls are thought to be tainted, having a sterile, dedicated container is essential for studying the toxic liquid without contaminating the sample or harming the bearer.",al={"what is cliffspring falls sampler","cliffspring sampler item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler come from, and who made it?",a="The sampler is supplied by the Cenarion Circle druids in Moonglade, specifically through Dendrite Starblaze. Sensing that something unnatural had begun poisoning Darkshore's wildlife, the Circle prepared these containers so trusted initiates could secure pure samples directly from suspected contamination sites.",al={"who gave me cliffspring sampler","who made sampler","sampler origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Filling this sampler at the naga-infested cave is a rite of passage for young druids, directly leading to learning Cure Poison.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Darkshore's pristine forest water by lurking naga threatens both the wild beasts and the settlement of Auberdine."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","cenarion circle","cliffspring falls","cure poison","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","sampler"},rel={"item:filled-cliffspring-falls-sampler","quest:6122","quest:6125","subzone:cliffspring-falls","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:dendrite-starblaze","zone:darkshore","topic:cenarion-circle"},src={"Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler","The Principal Source (Alliance)"}}
E["item:empty-sampling-tube"] = {t="item",n="Empty Sampling Tube",z="darkshore",s="The Empty Sampling Tube is a glass phial provided by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. It is intended to collect corrupted water from the Cliffspring River so night elf scholars can study the encroaching taint threatening Darkshore.",h="The Empty Sampling Tube is a glass phial provided by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",sec={{t="Testing the Waters",b="As the wilderness of Darkshore succumbs to creeping blight, the natural waterways have begun to turn foul. Thundris Windweaver, an investigator stationed in Auberdine, provides this empty glass tube to gather concrete evidence from the Cliffspring River. Drawn from the pool beneath the first waterfall north of town, the resulting sample allows night elf naturalists to examine the nature of the corruption washing toward Mist's Edge.",sp=0},{t="Tracing the Source",b="While hostile Blackwood furbolgs inhabit camps along the riverbanks, Windweaver suspects they are merely victims and vectors rather than the ultimate origin of the rot. Filling the tube confirms that the contamination flows down from the tainted heights of Felwood to the east. The collected specimen serves as the foundation for crafting a potential cure and preparing a direct response against the blight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Empty Sampling Tube?",a="It is a sealed glass vessel used to collect a water specimen from the corrupted Cliffspring River north of Auberdine. The sample is brought to Thundris Windweaver so he can analyze the foul substances spreading through Darkshore.",al={"why do i have this tube","what does the sampling tube do","tube purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the water sample supposed to be taken?",a="The tube must be filled at the first waterfall along the Cliffspring River, located north of Auberdine beneath an overhead bridge, right where the water pools before spilling into Mist's Edge.",al={"where to fill tube","cliffspring river location","sampling tube spot"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who provided this tube?",a="Thundris Windweaver, a night elf naturalist studying the environmental threats around Auberdine, entrusts the tube to adventurers willing to brave the tainted wilderness.",al={"who gives the tube","tube quest giver","thundris windweaver"},it="origin"},{q="What is polluting the Cliffspring River?",a="Although the local Blackwood furbolgs inhabit the riverbanks and exacerbate the filth, the true source of the foul taint is the corrupted woodland of Felwood situated high in the mountains to the east.",al={"why is the river green","what corrupted the water","cliffspring taint"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What is the Empty Sampling Tube?",a="It is a clean, specially prepared glass vial given to you to collect water from the Cliffspring River. Thundris Windweaver needs an uncontaminated vessel to secure a pure specimen of the foul wash currently flowing down into the sea north of Auberdine.",al={"what is empty sampling tube","empty tube lore","about empty sampling tube"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Thundris want a sample collected in this tube?",a="Darkshore's waters are rapidly sickening, and Thundris suspects the foul taint washing down the Cliffspring River reaches Auberdine's coast. By inspecting a fresh sample drawn in this vessel, he hopes to determine whether local Blackwood furbolgs or darker corruptions from the eastern highlands of Felwood are responsible, giving the night elves a basis for their counter-measures.",al={"why is empty sampling tube wanted","why collect cliffspring water","thundris sample why"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The sampling tube represents an early effort to diagnose the demonic taint of Felwood that bleeds into Darkshore's pristine rivers and sickens the local wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, testing the Cliffspring River is critical to preventing the corrupting runoff from poisoning their coastal haven at Mist's Edge."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring river","darkshore","empty sampling tube","mist's edge","thundris windweaver","water sample"},rel={"quest:4762","item:cliffspring-river-sample","quest:4761","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood","subzone:auberdine","subzone:mist-s-edge","topic:furbolg"},src={"Empty Sampling Tube","The Cliffspring River"}}
E["item:empty-water-tube"] = {t="item",n="Empty Water Tube",z="darkshore",s="The Empty Water Tube is a simple glass vessel provided in Auberdine to collect sacred moonwell water. It is meant to carry the blessed liquid up to the strange red crystal perched on the eastern cliffs of Darkshore.",h="The Empty Water Tube is a simple glass vessel provided in Auberdine to collect sacred moonwell water.",sec={{t="A Vessel for Blessed Waters",b="Sentinels and scholars studying the mysterious red crystal along Darkshore's eastern ridge require pure lunar essence to test its nature. Because mundane glass or flasks can easily contaminate consecrated water, this sealed vial is specifically entrusted to investigators visiting the moonwell in Auberdine. Once filled, its contents are carried up the mountain slopes to see how the alien mineral responds to Elune's magic.",sp=0},{t="Probing Felwood's Shadow",b="The mountains immediately east of Darkshore border Felwood, a realm thoroughly poisoned by demonic corruption. Auberdine's defenders suspect that the ominous crimson monolith resting near the cliffs shares a sinister link with that ruined forest. By cascading moonwell water across its lattice, researchers hope the sacred waters will unveil the crystal's inner structure without triggering a catastrophic release of whatever power lies trapped inside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Empty Water Tube?",a="It is an empty container given to you in Auberdine to draw water directly from the settlement's moonwell, which is needed to analyze a bizarre red crystal found along the eastern heights of Darkshore.",al={"empty water tube purpose","why do i have empty water tube","what do i do with water tube"},it="purpose"},{q="Where should the tube be filled?",a="It must be dipped into the moonwell situated within Auberdine. Filling it transforms the item into a Moonwell Water Tube.",al={"where to fill water tube","where do i fill empty water tube","fill water tube location"},gp=true},{q="Why is moonwell water needed for the crystal?",a="Moonwell water carries the potent, purifying magic of Elune. Scholars believe pouring it over the mysterious red crystal will react with its surface and reveal clues about its origin and composition.",al={"why moonwell water","what does moonwell water do to crystal","red crystal moonwell water"}},{q="Why are Auberdine's residents worried about the crystal?",a="The crystal sits near the high ridge overlooking Felwood, a forest badly corrupted by the Burning Legion. Local watchers fear that if the crystal is linked to that tainted wilderness, it could pose a severe threat to Darkshore.",al={"is the crystal dangerous","crystal danger darkshore","why investigate red crystal"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Empty Water Tube?",a="It is a simple, empty glass vial provided to you in Auberdine so you can gather water from the village's moonwell. Once filled, you will use its blessed contents to test the mysterious, alien red crystal resting against the mountains of Darkshore.",al={"what is empty water tube","empty water tube","vial for moonwell water"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Handling consecrated moonwell water is a sacred duty for the Kaldorei, who revere the moonwells as holy reservoirs blessed by the goddess Elune.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold moonwells in deep reverence, relying on their untainted waters to study anomalies and cleanse strange disruptions encroaching from corrupted lands like Felwood."},kw={"as water cascades","auberdine","darkshore","empty water tube","felwood","moonwell","moonwell water tube","red crystal"},rel={"quest:4812","item:moonwell-water-tube","quest:4811","quest:4813","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood"},src={"Empty Water Tube","As Water Cascades"}}
E["item:filled-cliffspring-falls-sampler"] = {t="item",n="Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler",z="darkshore",s="The Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler contains murky water drawn from the headwaters near Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. Gathered on behalf of the Cenarion Circle, it serves as crucial evidence in uncovering what is poisoning the local deer population.",h="The Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler contains murky water drawn from the headwaters near Cliffspring Falls in...",sec={{t="A Tainted Source",b="Cliffspring Falls provides the principal drinking water for much of Darkshore, cascading down from the eastern highlands toward the sea. Recently, however, the wildlife relying on these waters—specifically the local deer—have fallen prey to a debilitating, unnatural malady. At the behest of Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade, druidic initiates retrieve this sample directly from the mouth of a cave infested by hostile naga. The vial holds visibly putrid liquid, confirming that the region's primary fresh water supply is actively corrupted.",sp=0},{t="Path to a Remedy",b="Brought to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, the foul sample provides the physical proof the Cenarion Circle needs to study the poison. Rather than simply disposing of it, Alanndarian uses the polluted water to analyze the contaminant's makeup. Deciphering the exact properties of the sludge allows the druids to synthesize a curative salve, an essential step in developing the rite that grants practitioners power over poison.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler?",a="It contains contaminated water scooped from the mouth of the cavern near Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. The water is visibly discolored and carries the poison that has been sickening local deer.",al={"sampler contents","what water is in the vial","what is in the sample"},it="identity"},{q="Who asks for this water sample?",a="Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle instructs young druids to collect the sample, while Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine receives it to analyze the poison and formulate a cure.",al={"who wants the water sample","who do i give the sampler to","who needs the filled sampler"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important?",a="Cliffspring Falls is the principal source of drinking water for the Darkshore region. Any corruption introduced into the falls spreads through the local waterways and affects the entire wilderness.",al={"why cliffspring falls","importance of cliffspring falls"},it="purpose"},{q="What is causing the water to turn foul?",a="The water originates near a cave recently overrun by hostile naga. Their presence coincides with the fouling of the headwaters, spreading unnatural sickness throughout the local fauna.",al={"who poisoned the water","why is the falls poisoned","naga cliffspring falls"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler come from, and who made it?",a="The empty glass sampling tube is provided to young druids by Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade on behalf of the Cenarion Circle. It becomes the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler once you take it to the mouth of the naga-infested cave beside Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore and draw water directly from the tainted stream.",al={"origin filled cliffspring falls sampler","who made cliffspring sampler","where do you get cliffspring sampler"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Retrieving and analyzing this tainted water is a vital proving trial for Alliance druids, forming the investigative groundwork for mastering Cure Poison.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Darkshore, securing the Cliffspring headwaters is essential to preserving Auberdine's ecology against foul foreign corruption."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring falls","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","poisoned water","sampler"},rel={"quest:6122","item:empty-cliffspring-falls-sampler","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:dendrite-starblaze","subzone:cliffspring-falls","quest:6125","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},src={"Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler","The Principal Source (Alliance)"}}
E["item:fine-crab-chunks"] = {t="item",n="Fine Crab Chunks",z="darkshore",s="Fine Crab Chunks are prime cuts of meat gathered from the coastal crustaceans roaming the beaches of Darkshore. Highly prized for their culinary versatility, they are sought after by local shore-dwellers and hungry fishermen looking to prepare an endless variety of seafood dishes.",h="Fine Crab Chunks are prime cuts of meat gathered from the coastal crustaceans roaming the beaches of...",sec={{t="Fruit of the Sea",b="The misty, jagged shores of Darkshore are thick with skittering crustaceans, specifically Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers. While many travelers view these armored shore-prowlers as pests or aggressive hazards along the waterline, enterprising gourmands consider their meat among the finest bounty of the coast. Prized cuts harvested from these creatures yield rich, tender morsels that lend themselves to practically any cooking method imaginable, from boiling and broiling to deep frying and savory stews.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield Fine Crab Chunks?",a="They are harvested from the Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers that roam along the rocky beaches and tidal shallows of Darkshore.",al={"where do fine crab chunks drop","which crabs drop chunks","crab meat source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants Fine Crab Chunks in Darkshore?",a="Gubber Blump, an enthusiastic fisherman stationed on the docks of Auberdine, seeks out these choice cuts. An avid lover of seafood, he prizes them for an elaborate repertoire of home-cooked crab dishes.",al={"who needs fine crab chunks","who turns in crab chunks","gubber blump crab"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Can you prepare these into actual meals?",a="While these specific raw chunks serve primarily as a supply collected for Gubber Blump rather than a direct crafting recipe ingredient, local culinary tradition treats crab meat as remarkably versatile—suitable for baking, barbecuing, boiling, broiling, frying, and mixing into salads or stews.",al={"can you cook fine crab chunks","what can you make with fine crab chunks","crab recipes"},gp=true},{q="What are Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Fine Crab Chunks are prime cuts of meat carved from the sturdy crabs along Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast. Prized for their tenderness and versatility, they are considered by local enthusiasts to be the true fruit of the sea, suitable for nearly any preparation imaginable.",al={"what are fine crab chunks","fine crab chunks lore","what is fine crab meat"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do Fine Crab Chunks come from?",a="These choice morsels are harvested directly from the wild crustaceans prowling Darkshore's coastline, particularly the Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers. They are not crafted by mortal hands, but butchered fresh from the creatures that thrive in the cold surf.",al={"where do fine crab chunks come from","source of fine crab chunks","fine crab chunks origin"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Gubber Blump want Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Gubber Blump, an eccentric fisherman stationed at the Auberdine docks, is utterly obsessed with crab meat. Stranded with his fishing rod, he relies on travelers to gather fresh chunks so he can whip up an endless assortment of crab-based recipes, from baked and broiled dishes to crab salads and stews.",al={"why does gubber want crab chunks","who wants fine crab chunks","why collect fine crab chunks"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Any aspiring shoreline chef will appreciate Gubber Blump's encyclopedic passion for crab, spanning soups, salads, pepper rubs, and regional delicacies like Ironforge surprise crab.",["faction:Alliance"]="Supplying the dockside residents of Auberdine helps sustain the fragile Alliance outpost amidst the gloomy perils of Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","crab","darkshore","encrusted tide crawler","fine crab chunks","fruit of the sea","gubber blump","reef crawler"},rel={"quest:1138","npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},src={"Fine Crab Chunks","Fruit of the Sea"}}
E["item:fine-moonstalker-pelt"] = {t="item",n="Fine Moonstalker Pelt",z="darkshore",s="A Fine Moonstalker Pelt is the thick, pristine hide taken from the most mature predatory moonstalkers roaming southern Darkshore. Terenthis of Auberdine uses these prized furs to weave an enchanted cloak that allows searchers to slip past the woods' hostile beasts unnoticed.",h="A Fine Moonstalker Pelt is the thick, pristine hide taken from the most mature predatory moonstalkers roaming...",sec={{t="Hides of the Pack Leaders",b="While common moonstalkers prowl throughout the mist-laden forests of Darkshore, only the older moonstalker sires and matriarchs possess coats dense and healthy enough to yield a fine pelt. These powerful wildcats establish territories along the Wildbend River and further south toward the borders of Ashenvale, where they hunt with lethal patience.",sp=0},{t="A Cloak of Deception",b="Gathering these hides is no mere trophy hunt. Terenthis requests five intact pelts to fashion an enchanted garment for travelers searching for the missing night elf Volcor. When woven and bound with nature magic, the pelts form a cloak of concealment that cloaks its wearer in an illusion, dampening their presence to Darkshore's wildlife as long as they refrain from aggressive actions.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What creatures yield a Fine Moonstalker Pelt?",a="Only the mature leaders of the moonstalker packs yield these pelts—specifically moonstalker sires and moonstalker matriarchs. Younger or common moonstalkers lack the necessary hide quality.",al={"what drops fine moonstalker pelt","where to get moonstalker pelt","which cats have pelts"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Where can the mature moonstalkers be found?",a="These formidable wildcats make their home in southern Darkshore, particularly near the banks of the Wildbend River and further south along the forest road toward Ashenvale.",al={"where are the sires and matriarchs","moonstalker sire location","moonstalker matriarch location"},gp=true},{q="Why does Terenthis need these pelts?",a="Terenthis uses five of the pelts to craft an enchanted cloak. This cloak is imbued with magic designed to conceal a rescuer from predatory beasts while searching for the missing ranger Volcor.",al={"what are pelts used for","why collect moonstalker pelts","terenthis pelt quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does the finished cloak make you completely invisible?",a="The cloak projects a delicate natural illusion that deters beasts, but it is fragile. Terenthis warns that doing much beyond speaking to others will disrupt the enchantment and dispel the disguise.",al={"how does the cloak work","cloak illusion limits","cloak break stealth"},gp=true},{q="What is a Fine Moonstalker Pelt?",a="A Fine Moonstalker Pelt is the prime hide harvested from the mature moonstalker sires and matriarchs roaming the wilds of Darkshore. These formidable night saber cats possess thick, supple fur capable of holding delicate natural enchantments, making their pelts far more prized and durable than the scruff of younger specimens.",al={"fine moonstalker pelt","what is moonstalker pelt","fine pelt"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Fine Moonstalker Pelt come from?",a="These pelts come naturally from the largest adult moonstalkers stalking the coasts and forests of Darkshore, particularly near the Wildbend River and farther south toward the Ashenvale border. Only fully grown moonstalker sires and matriarchs yield hides thick and healthy enough to be considered fine pelts.",al={"where to get fine moonstalker pelt","moonstalker pelt source","who drops fine moonstalker pelt"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Stalking the sires and matriarchs near the Wildbend River tests a hunter's tracking skills against some of the fiercest predators in coastal Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves respect the sacred ferocity of the moonstalkers, taking their hides only out of dire necessity to aid fallen kin like Volcor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fine moonstalker pelt","matriarch","moonstalker","sire","terenthis","volcor","wildbend river"},rel={"quest:986","npc:terenthis","npc:volcor","subzone:wildbend-river","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Fine Moonstalker Pelt","A Lost Master"}}
E["item:flagongut-s-fossil"] = {t="item",n="Flagongut's Fossil",z="darkshore",s="Flagongut's Fossil is an ancient specimen recovered from the dig sites of the Wetlands. Entrusted to the dwarven Explorers' League, it holds latent secrets that Archaeologist Flagongut seeks to decipher using a mysterious relic known as the Stone of Relu.",h="Flagongut's Fossil is an ancient specimen recovered from the dig sites of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Excavation and Study",b="Unearthed as part of the dwarven expeditions across Khaz Modan, this ancient fossil represents more than just petrified stone. Archaeologist Flagongut believes it holds forgotten powers tied to the deep antiquity of the world, comparable to artifacts found across the sea in Darkshore. For safekeeping during regional studies, the fossil was held by Prospector Whelgar at his excavation site in the southern hills of the Wetlands.",sp=0},{t="Unlocking the Relic",b="When Flagongut discovered the Stone of Relu, he realized it was the deciphering key required to unravel the fossil's mysteries. However, an ambush by mottled raptors on the road caused the stone to be lost. To finally unlock the specimen, Flagongut requires adventurers to retrieve the fossil from Whelgar's dig and recover the swallowed stone from the Wetlands wildlife.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Flagongut's Fossil?",a="It is an ancient archaeological specimen recovered from the Wetlands, kept for analysis by the dwarven Explorers' League to uncover secrets of the world's ancient past.",al={"what is the fossil","flagongut fossil lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the fossil located?",a="It is located in the cave at the top of Whelgar's Excavation Site, nestled in the southern mountains of the Wetlands, guarded by raptors and oozes that overrun the dig.",al={"fossil location","where is flagongut fossil","whelgar fossil cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Flagongut need it returned?",a="Flagongut believes that paired with the Stone of Relu, he can decipher the fossil's latent magical secrets and compare its nature to similar findings uncovered in Kalimdor.",al={"why does flagongut want it","what will flagongut do with it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How is it connected to Darkshore?",a="Flagongut sees a parallel between this Wetlands specimen and the fossil found by Prospector Remtravel across the sea in Darkshore, believing the Stone of Relu might unlock the power in both relics.",al={"darkshore connection","remtravel fossil"},it="ties"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven explorers, fossils like Flagongut's are not mere curiosities; they are physical links to the ancient past that the Explorers' League is dedicated to unearthing.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing artifacts from Whelgar's ruined dig site prevents valuable history from being destroyed by wild beasts or scavenged by hostile forces in the marsh."},kw={"excavation","explorers' league","flagongut","fossil","relu","stone of relu","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:prospector-whelgar","subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","item:stone-of-relu","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore","quest:729"},src={"Flagongut's Fossil","The Absent Minded Prospector (5)"}}
E["item:gaffer-jack"] = {t="item",n="Gaffer Jack",z="darkshore",s="A Gaffer Jack is a specialized engineering component used for intricate mechanical adjustments, such as tuning stintle pegs. A crate of them was carelessly lost beneath the waves off the coast of Auberdine by the eccentric gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle during his voyage across the sea.",h="A Gaffer Jack is a specialized engineering component used for intricate mechanical adjustments, such as...",sec={{t="Lost at Sea",b="Seeking peace and quiet away from the clattering forge-works and noisy taverns of Ironforge, gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle booked passage aboard a ship bound for Auberdine. Having indulged in a bit too much drink during the ocean voyage, Wizbang managed to fumble and drop an entire container of gaffer jacks over the railing. These small mechanical fasteners sank into the misty coastal waters of Darkshore, leaving him stranded without the vital parts required to tune his stintle pegs.",sp=0},{t="Sunken Salvage",b="Because gaffer jacks were spilled into the surf along the shoreline, they occasionally snag on the hooks of patient fishermen casting into the coastal waters of Darkshore. Recovering these lost components allows Wizbang to assemble his bizarre contraptions, though dredging tiny metal hardware out of the open sea remains a testament to both extraordinary patience and pure luck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Gaffer Jack used for?",a="According to the gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle, gaffer jacks are essential engineering components required to tune stintle pegs for his experimental inventions.",al={"gaffer jack purpose","what does a gaffer jack do","gaffer jack use"},it="purpose"},{q="How did these end up in the ocean around Auberdine?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle took a ship from the Eastern Kingdoms seeking peace and quiet away from Ironforge. During the voyage, he drank too heavily and accidentally dropped his crate of gaffer jacks overboard into the waters of Darkshore.",al={"why are gaffer jacks in the water","who dropped gaffer jacks","gaffer jack lost"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Gaffer Jacks recovered?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle, an eccentric gnome inventor staying in the port town of Auberdine, needs eight of them returned to continue building his strange inventions.",al={"who needs gaffer jacks","gaffer jack turn in","who takes gaffer jacks"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Gaffer Jacks be found?",a="They are submerged along the coastline of Darkshore, resting on the seabed where anglers occasionally snag them while fishing the coastal surf.",al={"where to get gaffer jacks","how to find gaffer jacks","gaffer jack location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a Gaffer Jack?",a="A Gaffer Jack is a specialized engineering component used by tinkerers like Wizbang Cranktoggle. Specifically, Wizbang relies on them to properly tune his stintle pegs, making them an indispensable part of his invention toolkit.",al={"what is gaffer jack","gaffer jacks lore","what are gaffer jacks"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Fellow tinkerers will recognize the sheer frustration of losing proprietary hardware like gaffer jacks, without which delicate mechanisms like stintle pegs cannot be calibrated.",["race:Gnome"]="Leaving the bustle of Ironforge for a quiet life in Auberdine might be unorthodox for a gnome, but misplacing an entire crate of essential parts over the rail of a ship after drinking too much is entirely in character."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fishing","gaffer jack","ironforge","stintle pegs","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:1579","quest:1580","item:electropeller","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:1141","npc:gubber-blump"},src={"Gaffer Jack","Gaffer Jacks"}}
E["item:glowing-soul-gem"] = {t="item",n="Glowing Soul Gem",z="darkshore",s="A Glowing Soul Gem is a dark ritual artifact carried by operatives of the Cult of the Dark Strand in northern Ashenvale. Imbued with shadowy sorcery, the stone traps the spirit of an unwitting victim to fuel the cult's sinister operations.",h="A Glowing Soul Gem is a dark ritual artifact carried by operatives of the Cult of the Dark Strand in northern...",sec={{t="A Vessel of Dark Sorcery",b="Northeast of Maestra's Post, in the shadowed ruins of Ordil'Aran, members of the Cult of the Dark Strand wield dark sorcery under the watchful eyes of their shadowy masters. Among their ranks, operatives carry Glowing Soul Gems—vessels enchanted to trap and torment the souls of the dead. Rather than mere decorative trinkets, these stones act as conduits of magical energy, anchoring bound spirits to serve the cult's shadowy ends.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Ordil'Aran",b="Seeking to dismantle the Dark Strand's influence across northern Kalimdor, Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post investigates these artifacts. Deciphering the enchantments woven into a Glowing Soul Gem reveals not just dark arcane formulas, but an imprisoned soul crying out from within the gem, exposing the sinister experiments linking the cultists in Ashenvale to their kin at the Tower of Althalaxx.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Glowing Soul Gem?",a="It is an enchanted soulstone used by the Cult of the Dark Strand. Imbued with shadow magic, it traps spirits inside to harness their essence and fuel the cult's foul sorcery.",al={"what is soul gem","soul gem darkshore","glowing soul gem lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this soul gem come from?",a="It is carried by members of the Cult of the Dark Strand—including their cultists, assassins, enforcers, and adepts—operating out of the ruins of Ordil'Aran in northern Ashenvale.",al={"who drops soul gem","glowing soul gem location","ordil'aran gem"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants this soul gem and why?",a="Delgren the Purifier, stationed at Maestra's Post, seeks the gem. He believes deciphering its enchantments will uncover the secret source of the cult's power and reveal what they are plotting.",al={"delgren soul gem","why delgren wants soul gem","maestra's post soul gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when the soul gem is deciphered?",a="Unraveling the enchantments on the gem releases the ghost trapped within it, freeing the tormented soul and exposing the twisted depths of the Dark Strand's practices.",al={"what is inside soul gem","ghost in soul gem"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks understand the art of trapping spirits within soulstones better than anyone, recognizing the Dark Strand's gem as a cruder, necromantic derivative of soul manipulation.",["class:Priest"]="Priests viewing the soul gem can sense the agony of the spirit imprisoned within, recognizing the urgent need to cleanse the artifact and release the soul to peace."},kw={"althalaxx","cult of the dark strand","dark strand","delgren the purifier","glowing soul gem","maestra's post","ordil'aran","soul gem"},rel={"quest:965","zone:ashenvale","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:darkshore"},src={"Glowing Soul Gem","The Tower of Althalaxx (4)"}}
E["item:grell-earring"] = {t="item",n="Grell Earring",z="darkshore",s="Grell Earrings are crude baubles scavenged and worn by the feral creatures infesting the ruins of Bashal'Aran. Though unremarkable at a glance, their proximity to ancient relics allows sensitive spirits to trace the lingering magical seals holding them in torment.",h="Grell Earrings are crude baubles scavenged and worn by the feral creatures infesting the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",sec={{t="Traces in the Brass",b="The Wild Grells and Vile Sprites lurking around the collapsed marble of Bashal'Aran hoard assorted trinkets, frequently fashioning earrings from scraps they scavenge among the ruins. To most mortals, these items are worthless refuse. However, to Asterion, an ancient night elf bound as a tormented phantom within the ruins, they serve as dowsing implements. By scrutinizing the resonant magical traces absorbed by these earrings, Asterion attempts to locate the ancient seal that imprisons his spectral form.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Grell Earrings come from?",a="They are collected from the corpses of Wild Grells and Vile Sprites inhabiting the ruined night elven settlement of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore.",al={"grell earring drop","where to get grell earrings","who drops grell earrings"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Asterion want these earrings?",a="Asterion is an ancient spirit held captive in Bashal'Aran by potent magic. He uses the earrings as magical conduits to detect traces of the nearby seal that has bound his soul for centuries.",al={"asterion earrings","why collect grell earrings","grell earring use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Do the grells know they carry magical traces?",a="No. The grells and sprites simply hoard and wear the shiny trinkets out of primal instinct. They have unknowingly brushed against the magical seal hidden within the ruins, leaving residual traces on the metal.",al={"are the earrings magic","do grells know magic"}},{q="Does Asterion find what he needs from the earrings?",a="The earrings themselves do not hold the seal, but examining them reveals that the creatures have been in recent contact with it, guiding the search deeper into the surrounding ruins.",al={"did the earrings work","asterion seal location"}},{q="What is a Grell Earring?",a="A Grell Earring is a simple piece of adornment worn by the wild grells and vile sprites infesting the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. While mundane trinkets on their own, these scavenged earpieces have absorbed subtle magical emanations from the ruins and whatever relics the creatures have handled.",al={"what are grell earrings","grell earring lore","what is grell earring"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The earrings demonstrate how inanimate metals can passively absorb and retain the ambient magical signature of ancient warding seals over long periods.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing sacred elven ruins overrun by thieving sprites wearing scavenged brass is a bitter reminder of how low the once-grand estates of ancient Kalimdor have fallen."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","darkshore","grell earring","seal","vile sprite","wild grell"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:954","zone:darkshore"},src={"Grell Earring","Bashal'Aran (2)"}}
E["item:grizzled-scalp"] = {t="item",n="Grizzled Scalp",z="darkshore",s="A Grizzled Scalp is the thick, furred hide taken from grizzled thistle bears roaming the southern forests of Darkshore. While seemingly an odd trophy, these pelts are sought by the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle to supply his hidden wilderness machinery.",h="A Grizzled Scalp is the thick, furred hide taken from grizzled thistle bears roaming the southern forests of...",sec={{t="A Peculiar Fermentation",b="Travelers hunting along the road south of Auberdine encounter the weathered grizzled thistle bears, known for their rough, thick pelts. While skinning dangerous predators is second nature to wilderness stalkers, bringing four of their scalps to Buzzbox 525 reveals a far less dignified purpose. The apparatus does not need bear fur for engineering repairs or scientific analysis. Instead, the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle utilizes the hidden buzzboxes scattered across Darkshore as covert distilleries. Since the local night elves frown upon illicit brewing operations within their settlements, Wizbang relies on gullible adventurers gathering bear scalps and other bizarre ingredients to produce his beloved 'thistle bear beer.'",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Grizzled Scalps?",a="Grizzled Scalps are obtained from grizzled thistle bears and their matriarch, the Den Mother, in the forests south of Auberdine along the main trail in Darkshore.",al={"grizzled scalp location","who drops grizzled scalps","thistle bear scalp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are Grizzled Scalps used for?",a="They are deposited into Buzzbox 525, an automated mechanical terminal hidden in the bushes alongside the road far south of Auberdine.",al={"grizzled scalp use","what do i do with grizzled scalps"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Buzzbox 525 need bear scalps?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle secretly uses his buzzbox network to distill bootleg liquor away from watchful night elf eyes. The grizzled scalps serve as an ingredient in his homebrewed thistle bear beer.",al={"why does wizbang want scalps","buzzbox 525 purpose"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Wizbang hiding his brewing in Darkshore's wilderness?",a="The night elves residing in Auberdine do not appreciate an unauthorized, noisy alcohol trade in their sacred groves. Wizbang hid his contraptions in the brush along the wilderness roads to keep his moonshine operation running undetected.",al={"why hide buzzbox","wizbang liquor darkshore"},sp=1},{q="What is a Grizzled Scalp?",a="A Grizzled Scalp is the thick, furred crown harvested from the rugged bears wandering the wilds of Darkshore. These seasoned beasts endure the harsh northern climate, developing resilient, bristled hides that trappers and curious inventors prize for their unique density.",al={"what is grizzled scalp","grizzled scalp info","tell me about grizzled scalps"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Grizzled Scalp come from?",a="These scalps come from the mature thistle bears native to Darkshore, primarily the Grizzled Thistle Bears and the ferocious Den Mother. Rather than crafted goods, they are raw trophies taken directly from the wild beasts roaming south of Auberdine.",al={"where do grizzled scalps come from","grizzled scalp source","who drops grizzled scalps"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The buzzbox network demonstrates the gnomish talent for disguising automated brewing stills as field-repair communication arrays.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves protect Darkshore's wildlife and take a dim view of both wanton poaching and surreptitious gnomish stills cluttering their wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 525","darkshore","grizzled scalp","grizzled thistle bear","thistle bear beer","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1003","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},src={"Grizzled Scalp","Buzzbox 525 (quest)"}}
E["item:highborne-relic-classic"] = {t="item",n="Highborne Relic (Classic)",z="darkshore",s="Highborne Relics are ancient magical implements recovered from the restless spirits haunting the ruins of Ameth'Aran in Darkshore. Imbued with the arcane dabblings that shattered ancient Kalimdor, they are sought by night elf scholars who wish to see them destroyed before their dormant powers can cause further harm.",h="Highborne Relics are ancient magical implements recovered from the restless spirits haunting the ruins of...",sec={{t="Remnants of the Sundering",b="Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne caste practiced reckless arcane magic, ultimately bringing ruin upon ancient Kalimdor. Today, their former estates lie in shattered ruin across Darkshore. Within the crumbling columns of Ameth'Aran, wailing and writhing apparitions wander the forest floor, endlessly clinging to the physical implements of their bygone sorcery. These relics remain persistent tether-points of arcane taint, clutched by ghosts who refuse to release the instruments of their own undoing.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Arcane Taint",b="For modern night elf society, which largely renounced arcane magic after the Great Sundering, such artifacts represent a grave hazard. Scholars like Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, acting upon scouting reports from the Sentinels, actively commission travelers to wrest these relics from the spectral hands of the cursed spirits. Once gathered, the relics are systematically destroyed to ensure that the ancient evils and catastrophic mistakes of the Highborne cannot be repeated.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Highborne Relics come from?",a="They are recovered from the ghostly specters haunting the ruins of Ameth'Aran, located east of the main road in southern Darkshore. Cursed, writhing, and wailing Highborne spirits carry them amidst the ancient stones.",al={"where do i find highborne relics","who drops highborne relics","relic location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want these relics?",a="Thundris Windweaver fears the lingering arcane corruption still clinging to these ancient items. He collects them so they can be completely dismantled and destroyed, preventing anyone from reviving the dangerous Highborne sorcery.",al={"why collect relics","what happens to the relics","windweaver goal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the Highborne spirits still in Ameth'Aran?",a="The spirits are ancient Highborne nobility who perished when the world shattered ten thousand years ago. Cursed by their hubris and lingering attachment to arcane magic, their restless souls remain bound to the ruins of their former city.",al={"why are ametharan ghosts there","who are the cursed highborne","why ghosts in darkshore"},it="history"},{q="Are Highborne Relics safe to use?",a="No. The night elves consider them tainted by the foul, unchecked arcane practices that triggered the Great Sundering. Their dormant magic is considered hazardous, which is why scholars demand their destruction rather than their study.",al={"can i use highborne relics","are relics dangerous"},it="power"},{q="What is a Highborne Relic?",a="A Highborne Relic is an ancient magical implement crafted by the Highborne sorcerers of ancient Kalimdor. These enchanted tools survive in the hands of the restless spirits haunting the shattered ruins of Ameth'Aran, bearing the lingering taint of the arcane sorcery that precipitated the Great Sundering.",al={"what is highborne relic","highborne relics lore","what are these relics"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, these relics serve as a grim reminder of the disastrous arcane arrogance that tore their ancient civilization apart.",["class:Mage"]="Mages might find the relics' arcane craftsmanship fascinating, but the local night elf authorities tolerate no hesitation in destroying them."},kw={"ameth'aran","arcane","darkshore","highborne","highborne relic","sentinels","thundris windweaver"},rel={"quest:968","subzone:ameth-aran","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:highborne","topic:sentinels","quest:4761"},src={"Highborne Relic (Classic)","Tools of the Highborne"}}
E["item:highperch-venom-sac"] = {t="item",n="Highperch Venom Sac",z="darkshore",s="Highperch Venom Sacs are harvested from the wild wyverns nesting upon the towering spires of Highperch in Thousand Needles. While orcs prize wyverns as aerial mounts, select apothecaries and traders value their potent stingers even more than the living beasts.",h="Highperch Venom Sacs are harvested from the wild wyverns nesting upon the towering spires of Highperch in...",sec={{t="A Potent Harvest",b="The high spires of Thousand Needles house thriving prides of wild wyverns, particularly around the elevated crags of Highperch. These winged predators rely on powerful venom delivered through their barbed tails to paralyze and kill prey. While the Horde often domesticates these creatures as loyal wind riders, their venom sacs command a remarkably high price among alchemists, hunters, and opportunistic merchants across Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Faraway Buyer",b="Though native to the deep canyons of central Kalimdor, this venom draws interest far across the continent. In the quiet port town of Auberdine, the night elf Fiora Longears pays handsomely for fresh sacs collected from Highperch's broods. She seeks samples swollen with venom—typically found only on young wyverns or fertile females—fueling trade in dangerous reagents far from the beasts' natural desert habitat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures carry these venom sacs?",a="They are collected directly from the wild wyverns inhabiting Highperch in Thousand Needles, including Highperch Wyverns, Patriarchs, Consorts, and the matriarch Heartrazor.",al={"where do venom sacs drop","who drops highperch venom","wyvern venom drop"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Fiora Longears want this venom in Darkshore?",a="Fiora Longears recognizes that wyvern venom is intensely valuable in specific trading circles—sometimes even more lucrative than the mounts themselves. She commissions travelers venturing to Highperch in Thousand Needles to retrieve intact sacs for trade.",al={"why fiora want venom","auberdine venom buyer","who buys wyvern venom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are all wyvern venom sacs identical?",a="The potency and volume vary. The most prize-worthy sacs are swollen and bursting with poison, which is typically found among young wyverns or fertile breeding females.",al={"wyvern venom quality","bursting venom sacs"}},{q="How does the Horde utilize these wyverns compared to the Alliance?",a="The Horde primarily captures and breeds wyverns as aerial mounts and scouts known as wind riders. Independent traders and Alliance contacts, lacking domestic taming networks, instead harvest the beasts directly for their lethal chemical reagents.",al={"horde wyvern use","do orcs use the venom"}},{q="What is a Highperch Venom Sac?",a="A Highperch Venom Sac is an organ harvested from the wild wyverns that nest upon the towering mesa of Highperch in Thousand Needles. While wyverns are best known across Kalimdor as winged mounts utilized by the Horde, their venom is prized for its sheer potency. The sacs taken from the beasts atop Highperch are particularly rich and swollen with this deadly toxin, making them a lucrative prize for alchemists and traders who deal in exotic animal reagents.",al={"what is highperch venom sac","highperch venom sac","wyvern venom sac"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The highly concentrated paralyzing venom harvested from untamed Thousand Needles wyverns represents one of the most potent natural toxins found in Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Striking at the Highperch nests serves a double purpose for the Alliance: collecting valuable biological reagents for trade while culling wild stock that could otherwise be captured and broken as Horde mounts."},kw={"auberdine","fiora longears","heartrazor","highperch","poison","thousand needles","venom sac","wyvern"},rel={"quest:1135","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1132","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},src={"Highperch Venom Sac","Highperch Venom"}}
E["item:horn-of-awakening"] = {t="item",n="Horn of Awakening",z="darkshore",s="The Horn of Awakening is a sounding instrument kept in a chest by Kerlonian Evershade in southern Darkshore. It is used to rouse the drowsy druid whenever he collapses into a slumber on the road to Ashenvale.",h="The Horn of Awakening is a sounding instrument kept in a chest by Kerlonian Evershade in southern Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Remedy for Drowsy Druids",b="Kerlonian Evershade, a Druid of the Claw recently awoken from centuries inside the Emerald Dream, finds himself persistently lethargic in the waking realm. Journeying south toward Maestra's Post, he entrusts this horn to travelers willing to escort him. Whenever exhaustion overtakes him along the perilous wilderness trail, a clear blast from the instrument jolts his senses, prodding him back to his feet before wild beasts or cultists can seize upon his slumber.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Horn of Awakening found?",a="The horn rests inside Kerlonian's Chest, beside Kerlonian Evershade's campsite in southern Darkshore near the border of Ashenvale.",al={"horn location","where is horn of awakening","kerlonians chest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Kerlonian need the horn to stay awake?",a="Having spent long ages slumbering within the Emerald Dream, Kerlonian struggles to adjust to mortal wakefulness and constantly lapses into sudden, deep naps while traveling.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","why does he fall asleep","emerald dream slumber"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Kerlonian trying to go?",a="He is attempting to reach Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale to rendezvous with Liladris Moonriver.",al={"kerlonian destination","where is he walking","maestras post escort"}},{q="What is the Horn of Awakening?",a="The Horn of Awakening is a personal instrument belonging to the night elf druid Kerlonian Evershade. Having recently emerged from the Emerald Dream, Kerlonian suffers from bouts of deep, untimely slumber on his travels. He keeps this horn secured in his chest specifically so an escort can sound it to rouse him whenever he collapses along the road.",al={"horn of awakening","what is this horn","kerlonian horn"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Claw spent generations slumbering in the Barrow Dens communing with the Emerald Dream, and returning to waking reality often leaves them dazed and disoriented.",["race:NightElf"]="Waking horns and traditional sounding instruments have long been vital tools among the night elves for rousing dormant guardians during times of sudden invasion."},kw={"ashenvale","darkshore","druid of the claw","emerald dream","horn of awakening","kerlonian evershade","maestra's post"},rel={"npc:kerlonian-evershade","quest:5321","subzone:maestra-s-post","topic:emerald-dream","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:druid"},src={"Horn of Awakening","The Sleeper Has Awakened (Classic)"}}
E["item:ilkrud-magthrull-s-tome"] = {t="item",n="Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome",z="darkshore",s="Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome is a grimoire recovered from a dangerous orc warlock residing within the corrupted depths of Ashenvale. Brought to Delgren the Purifier, its foul contents reveal the broader dark dealings surrounding the cultists operating out of the Tower of Althalaxx.",h="Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome is a grimoire recovered from a dangerous orc warlock residing within the corrupted...",sec={{t="A Grimoire of Corruption",b="Ilkrud Magthrull is a formidable orc warlock entrenched at the Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale, a site poisoned by lingering demonic influence. Surrounded by summoned minions, Magthrull recorded his foul rituals and shadowy communications within this personal tome. While the Argent Dawn paladin Delgren the Purifier had long known of the warlock's presence, the uncovered links between Magthrull and the dark cultists gathering at the Tower of Althalaxx made recovering the book an urgent priority.",sp=0},{t="Unraveling the Cult",b="Upon claiming the tome from Magthrull's slain grasp, it is delivered to Delgren at Maestra's Post. Delgren seeks to decipher the warlock's writings to understand the network coordinating demonic activities across the borders of Darkshore and Ashenvale. The text provides vital intelligence on the shadowy conspirators pulling the strings behind the corruption taking root in northern Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who owns this tome?",a="The book belongs to Ilkrud Magthrull, a powerful orc warlock who established himself among the demonic ruins of Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale.",al={"who is ilkrud magthrull","who wrote the tome","ilkrud magthrull"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the tome found?",a="It is recovered directly from Ilkrud Magthrull himself at the Fire Scar Shrine, located south of the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale.",al={"tome location","how to get the tome","where to find ilkrud"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want the book?",a="Delgren seeks to study Magthrull's writings to uncover the dark ties connecting local demon-worshipers to the cultists inhabiting the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"why delgren wants the tome","what is in the tome","delgren book purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after the tome is recovered?",a="Delgren examines the text at Maestra's Post to decipher Magthrull's demonic communications and determine the next step in dismantling the cult's network.",al={"turn in tome","what does delgren do with the book"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome come from, and who made it?",a="The book contains the personal writings and dark research of Ilkrud Magthrull, a powerful orc warlock dwelling amidst the demonic corruption of Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale. Penned by the warlock himself, the volume compiles his dark spells and notes, kept close at hand until his downfall.",al={"who wrote ilkrud magthrull tome","ilkrud tome origin","where did the tome come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Recovering the tome aids Brother Delgren, a fellow warrior of the Holy Light standing vigilant against shadow and corruption in the untamed wilderness of Ashenvale.",["class:Warlock"]="Magthrull's grimoire is a prized record of dark bindings, detailing the subjugation of voidwalkers and succubi at the tainted Fire Scar Shrine."},kw={"ashenvale","delgren the purifier","fire scar shrine","ilkrud magthrull","maestra's post","tome","tower of althalaxx","warlock"},rel={"quest:965","npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:fire-scar-shrine","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:ashenvale","topic:warlock"},src={"Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome","The Tower of Althalaxx (5)"}}
E["item:insane-scribbles"] = {t="item",n="Insane Scribbles",z="darkshore",s="Torn from the baffling Twilight Tome, these Insane Scribbles are a fragment of dark literature carried by cultists in Darkshore. Merely looking at the dancing text and distorted scrollwork induces severe dizziness and mental strain. Ancient protectors of the forest study such fragments to decipher the sinister motives of the Twilight's Hammer.",h="Torn from the baffling Twilight Tome, these Insane Scribbles are a fragment of dark literature carried by...",sec={{t="A Maddening Manuscript",b="Gazing upon the pages of the Twilight Tome proves profoundly hazardous to mortal sanity. The script writhes across the parchment, while graceful scrollwork warps into grotesque, unsettling imagery before the reader's eyes. Tearing loose even a single sheet—these Insane Scribbles—is an ordeal that leaves the bearer lightheaded and disoriented. Despite the chaotic incoherence of the script, the parchment hums with a primal, deeply ancient magic tied directly to dark powers long buried beneath Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Clues for the Ancients",b="Brought to Onu, the venerable ancient presiding over the Grove of the Ancients, the scribbles offer a glimpse into the encroachments blighting Darkshore. Onu recognizes the chaotic energy clinging to the parchment as the unmistakable handiwork of the Old Gods. For the defenders of Kalimdor, piecing together the scribbles is a crucial step toward uncovering precisely why the Twilight's Hammer has gathered along the mist-shrouded shores.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens if you try to read these scribbles?",a="The text defies easy translation. Merely looking at the parchment causes the letters to swim and the surrounding designs to morph into horrifying shapes, inducing sudden dizziness and mental exhaustion in anyone attempting to decipher them.",al={"reading insane scribbles","what does the text say","can you read the scribbles"},it="danger"},{q="Where were these scribbles torn from?",a="They were ripped from the Twilight Tome, a foul grimoire kept by the Twilight's Hammer cultists operating in Darkshore.",al={"where do scribbles come from","twilight tome origin"},it="origin"},{q="Who can understand or study the scribbles?",a="The Ancient of Lore, Onu, examines the recovered parchment. Drawing upon centuries of knowledge, Onu senses the ancient, primal magic binding the ink and seeks to determine the cult's purpose in the region.",al={"who wants the scribbles","onu scribbles"},it="purpose"},{q="What kind of power radiates from the parchment?",a="The parchment pulses with chaotic, primal magic tied to the Old Gods, reflecting the dark deities worshipped by the Twilight's Hammer.",al={"what magic is in the scribbles","magic type"},it="power"},{q="What are the Insane Scribbles?",a="They are a single, maddening page torn from the dark text known as the Twilight Tome. The writing upon it swims, dances, and twists into grotesque shapes before your eyes, radiating a chaotic and primal magical aura that threatens to overwhelm your senses if you stare too long.",al={"what are insane scribbles","insane scribbles lore","what is this parchment"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Onu want the Insane Scribbles?",a="The ancient Onu senses the chaotic touch of the Old Gods woven into the parchment. He seeks to study these recovered writings in hopes of deciphering what the secretive Twilight's Hammer cult is plotting within the forests and shores of Darkshore.",al={"why does onu want insane scribbles","who wants the scribbles","why bring scribbles to onu"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="Priests sensitive to mental assaults and void-touched energies will recognize the twisting script as a perilous manifestation of madness directly opposing the clarity of the Light.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, relics of the Twilight's Hammer represent a corrupting threat to the ancient peace and sacred lands of Darkshore."},kw={"darkshore","insane scribbles","madness","old gods","onu","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:950","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:light"},src={"Insane Scribbles","Return to Onu"}}
E["item:laird-s-response"] = {t="item",n="Laird's Response",z="darkshore",s="Laird's Response is a sealed dispatch penned by the fish curer Laird in the coastal port of Auberdine. Written for Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village, the letter details curious ecological differences between mainland marine life and the unusually large fish thriving along Teldrassil's shores.",h="Laird's Response is a sealed dispatch penned by the fish curer Laird in the coastal port of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Matter of Scales and Roots",b="After reviewing catch reports from across the Veiled Sea, Laird of Auberdine noted a striking discrepancy: the fish hauled from Teldrassil's coast are remarkably larger and more plentiful than those taken along the mainland beaches of Darkshore. In this written response addressed to Nessa Shadowsong, Laird shares his working theory—that the unnatural presence and raw vitality of the newly planted World Tree may be warping and stimulating the surrounding marine life. Delivered by travelers returning across the waters, the letter prompts wonder and quiet curiosity among the fisherfolk of Rut'theran Village.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Laird's Response?",a="It is a written dispatch penned by Laird, a fish merchant and curer stationed in Auberdine, intended as an answer to an inquiry from Nessa Shadowsong in Teldrassil.",al={"what is this item","lairds response letter","what is lairds response"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Laird writing to?",a="The response is sent to Nessa Shadowsong, a night elf residing in Rut'theran Village at the southern base of Teldrassil.",al={"who receives lairds response","who gets this letter","nessa laird letter"}},{q="What does the letter say about the fish?",a="Laird notes that fish caught along Teldrassil's shores are markedly larger and more bountiful than those found in mainland Darkshore, suggesting that the World Tree itself might be influencing local marine life.",al={"why are the fish big","fish difference darkshore teldrassil","what did laird find"}},{q="How does the message travel back to Rut'theran Village?",a="Carriers can either board the regular ferry departing from the Auberdine docks or arrange a hippogryph flight with the flight master Caylais Moonfeather.",al={"how to get back to nessa","ruttheran boat darkshore","auberdine ferry to nessa"},gp=true},{q="Where does Laird's Response come from, and who wrote it?",a="This written reply is penned by Laird, a resident of Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore. He writes it to address questions sent across the sea from Rut'theran Village regarding the local marine life.",al={"who wrote laird's response","where does lairds response come from","laird response origin"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Nessa want Laird's Response?",a="Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village eagerly awaits Laird's observations on how mainland catches compare to Teldrassil's waters. The strange, oversized fish around the great boughs of the World Tree have puzzled fishermen, and Laird's notes confirm that mainland Darkshore sees nothing like them, suggesting Teldrassil itself is transforming the local wildlife.",al={"why does nessa want lairds response","why is laird's response wanted","who wants laird's response"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves tending the shores of Teldrassil, Laird's notes offer an intriguing, if slightly unnerving, clue about how the young World Tree already exerts an unnatural influence over surrounding nature."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fishing","laird","laird's response","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:6343","npc:laird","quest:6344","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},src={"Laird's Response","Return to Nessa"}}
E["item:letter-to-delgren"] = {t="item",n="Letter to Delgren",z="darkshore",s="The Letter to Delgren is an urgent missive penned by Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Addressed to his mentor, the paladin Delgren the Purifier, it details the sinister operations of the demonic Dark Strand cult. Delivering it carries vital intelligence southward to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.",h="The Letter to Delgren is an urgent missive penned by Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx in...",sec={{t="A Warning Sent South",b="As cultists of the Dark Strand gather around the ruins of the Tower of Althalaxx, the night elf Balthule Shadowstrike keeps watch over their escalating malice. Lacking the martial might to eradicate the cult alone, Balthule drafts this dispatch to request aid from his tutor in the Holy Light, Delgren the Purifier. Because the cult's foul rites threaten more than just Darkshore's coastline, the message must be carried the entire length of the region into western Ashenvale, where Delgren works in concert with night elf Sentinels to hunt down demonic and undead threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Letter to Delgren?",a="It is a sealed message written by Balthule Shadowstrike, reporting the rising activities of the demonic Dark Strand cult at the Tower of Althalaxx. It is addressed to the paladin Delgren the Purifier.",al={"what is this letter","letter to delgren","balthule's letter"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale. Dedicated to the Holy Light, he has offered his martial skills to aid the night elf Sentinels in purging demons and undead from the ancient forests, while mentoring Balthule in holy warfare.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","where is delgren"}},{q="Why is Balthule sending the letter so far away?",a="Balthule is Delgren's pupil and looks specifically to his mentor's expertise against demonic corruption. Delgren has both the combat prowess and the backing of local Sentinel forces at Maestra's Post to mount an organized response against the Dark Strand's dark rituals.",al={"why send to ashenvale","why not tell auberdine"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this letter need to be delivered?",a="The letter must be carried south through all of Darkshore and across the border into Ashenvale, reaching Maestra's Post along the western road.",al={"where do i take the letter","letter delivery location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where does the Letter to Delgren come from, and who wrote it?",a="The letter was penned by Balthule Shadowstrike, a night elf stationed in northern Darkshore near the Tower of Althalaxx. Seeking to purge the demonic corruption taking root in the ancient ruins, Balthule wrote this urgent missive to summon the aid and counsel of his mentor, the paladin Delgren the Purifier.",al={"who wrote letter to delgren","where did letter to delgren come from","who sent letter to delgren"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why is the Letter to Delgren so important?",a="The missive contains critical intelligence exposing the Dark Strand cult's sinister operations at the Tower of Althalaxx. Delgren the Purifier has dedicated himself to helping the night elves cleanse demons and undead from the forests, and Balthule needs his mentor alerted immediately so they can confront the growing threat.",al={"why does delgren need the letter","why want letter to delgren","importance of letter to delgren"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="This missive highlights an unusual fellowship: a human paladin training a night elf student in the Holy Light, bridging ancient Kaldorei lands with the martial faith of the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="The message reflects growing cooperation within the Alliance, as human champions and night elf Sentinels join forces to combat demonic cults infiltrating northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","dark strand","darkshore","delgren the purifier","letter to delgren","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:paladin","topic:sentinels"},src={"Letter to Delgren","The Tower of Althalaxx (3)"}}
E["item:lunar-fungus"] = {t="item",n="Lunar Fungus",z="darkshore",s="Lunar Fungus is a potent medicinal growth harvested from fungal blooms deep within Darkshore's cavern systems. Druid initiates collect these mushrooms alongside common herbs to brew a restorative salve capable of treating diseased wildlife.",h="Lunar Fungus is a potent medicinal growth harvested from fungal blooms deep within Darkshore's cavern systems.",sec={{t="Properties and Ecology",b="Harvested from Lunar Fungal Blooms, this distinctive fungus thrives in dark, subterranean caverns across Darkshore. The Cenarion Circle values it for its amplifying effects; when blended with a soothing water base and common Earthroot, the fungus provides the necessary potency to create an effective counteragent against debilitating afflictions. Because it grows primarily in damp underground spaces frequented by territorial moonkin, obtaining it requires careful navigation of the untamed wilderness.",sp=0},{t="A Lesson in Healing",b="In Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong directs young druids to harvest Lunar Fungus as part of their studies into nature's restorative arts. By witnessing how physical reagents like this fungus counteract virulent poisons in the local deer, initiates learn the underlying principles of herbal remedies before advancing to channel natural antidotes directly through shapeshifting and raw spiritual power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lunar Fungus used for?",a="Lunar Fungus provides curative potency when preparing a restorative salve. Alanndarian Nightsong combines it with Earthroot and clean water to treat sickened deer throughout the wilds of Darkshore.",al={"lunar fungus purpose","what does lunar fungus do","why collect lunar fungus"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Lunar Fungus grow?",a="It sprouts from Lunar Fungal Blooms nestled within the caves east of Auberdine in Darkshore. These dark caverns are shared with irritable moonkin that defend their territory from intruders.",al={"lunar fungus location","where to find lunar fungus","lunar fungus blooms"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who requires this fungus in Auberdine?",a="The druid Alanndarian Nightsong requests Lunar Fungus from students of the wild as part of their training, utilizing its natural medicinal properties to formulate remedies for ailing forest animals.",al={"who needs lunar fungus","auberdine herbal quest"},it="target"},{q="Why do druid initiates have to gather physical herbs to cure poison?",a="Understanding physical antidotes is a fundamental step in druidic education. By gathering wild reagents like Lunar Fungus and observing how specific ingredients counteract specific toxins, students grasp the principles of healing before learning to purge poisons directly through spiritual magic.",al={"why druids gather herbs","druid poison cure training"}},{q="What is Lunar Fungus?",a="Lunar Fungus is a potent medicinal mushroom native to Darkshore. It flourishes inside dark caverns east of Auberdine, harvested from larger clusters known as lunar fungal blooms. Druids prize the fungus for its natural potency, utilizing its properties as an essential ingredient when brewing alchemical salves to treat poisoned wildlife.",al={"what is lunar fungus","lunar fungus info","about lunar fungus"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Young druids seek out Lunar Fungus in Darkshore's caves as part of their foundational rites to master curative magic and heal poisoned wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="Tending the corrupted woodland creatures around Auberdine with native remedies like Lunar Fungus is an ongoing duty for the guardians of Darkshore."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cure poison","darkshore","earthroot","lunar fungal bloom","lunar fungus"},rel={"quest:6123","quest:6125","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Lunar Fungus","Gathering the Cure (Alliance)"}}
E["item:mathystra-relic"] = {t="item",n="Mathystra Relic",z="darkshore",s="Mathystra Relics are ancient night elven artifacts scattered among the overgrown ruins of Mathystra in northern Darkshore. Though remnants of a fallen elven bastion, they retain dormant shards of magic that have drawn the interest of the Twilight's Hammer cult.",h="Mathystra Relics are ancient night elven artifacts scattered among the overgrown ruins of Mathystra in...",sec={{t="Remnants of a Fallen Bastion",b="Before the Great Sundering, Mathystra stood as a proud city and bastion of elven civilization along the Kalimdor coast. Today, its toppled columns and cracked stones sit half-swallowed by brush and sea mist, haunted by restless spirits and lurking beasts. Scattered across the ruins are ancient relics dating back to that golden age. Though worn by ten thousand years of neglect, these artifacts still hold faint traces of elven arcane craft, making them dangerous prizes if left unattended.",sp=0},{t="A Looming Peril",b="The ancient tree of lore, Onu, seeks these relics after discovering that the sinister Twilight's Hammer cult is attempting to weaponize forgotten elven writings unearthed at the Master's Glaive. The cultists seek to harness ancient Kaldorei magic to hasten the return of their dark masters. By studying these scattered remnants, Onu and the guardians of Darkshore hope to unravel the cult's intentions and protect the fading power of Mathystra from being turned toward dark ends.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Mathystra Relics?",a="They are fragments and artifacts left behind from the ancient night elven city of Mathystra. Despite being thousands of years old, they still retain remnants of the magical craftsmanship of the pre-Sundering elven civilization.",al={"what is mathystra relic","elven relics mathystra","what are these relics"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these relics found?",a="They lie scattered amid the broken stones, tumbled pillars, and tall grasses within the Ruins of Mathystra, located in the northern reaches of Darkshore.",al={"mathystra relic location","where to find relics","relic locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Mathystra Relics?",a="The Ancient of Lore named Onu, who resides at the Grove of the Ancients in southern Darkshore, asks travelers to gather them for study.",al={"who needs relics","who do i bring relics to","onu relics"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer interested in them?",a="The cult has been deciphering ancient elven texts uncovered nearby at the Master's Glaive. They seek to twist and exploit the magical secrets of the ancient elves to assist in summoning their shadowy masters into the world.",al={"why twilight hammer wants relics","twilight's hammer mathystra"},it="motive"},{q="Where do the Mathystra Relics come from, and who made them?",a="These artifacts hail from the ancient night elven city of Mathystra, crafted long ago during an era when the great bastion shone across northern Darkshore. Left behind after the ancient settlement crumbled into ruin, they still hold lingering shards of elven magic.",al={"origin of mathystra relics","who made the mathystra relics","where are mathystra relics from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, recovering these relics is both a matter of safeguarding dangerous ancient arcana from the Twilight's Hammer and honoring the heritage of a city lost to the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="Working closely with ancients like Onu, druids help protect the delicate balance of Darkshore by ensuring forgotten magical remnants do not fuel dark summonings."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","mathystra","mathystra relic","onu","ruins of mathystra","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:951","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","zone:darkshore","quest:952","topic:twilight-s-hammer","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:944"},src={"Mathystra Relic","Mathystra Relics"}}
E["item:middle-of-gelkak-s-key"] = {t="item",n="Middle of Gelkak's Key",z="darkshore",s="The Middle of Gelkak's Key is a broken metal fragment belonging to the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast. After his vessel went down off the coast of Darkshore, this central section was snatched away by scavengers among the local Greymist murlocs.",h="The Middle of Gelkak's Key is a broken metal fragment belonging to the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak...",sec={{t="A Fragment in the Silt",b="When Gelkak Gyromast's ship was dragged beneath the waves by wild threshadons, the gnome pirate tumbled ashore with his most precious belongings shattered on the rocky shoals. Among the wreckage was a specialized winding key meant for his mechanical first mate. The key snapped into three distinct fragments during the catastrophe, scattering across the strand. While the tops and bottoms ended up carried off by coastal beasts, the middle section caught the eye of the Greymist murlocs prowling the Darkshore surf, who quickly hoarded the shiny metallic piece in their camps and wreckage holdings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Middle of Gelkak's Key used for?",a="It is one of three fragments needed by the shipwrecked pirate Gelkak Gyromast on the Darkshore coast. Once reassembled with the top and bottom pieces, the full key is used to reactivate his mechanical first mate.",al={"what does gelkaks key do","middle of gelkaks key use","why do i need this key"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did this key piece end up?",a="The middle fragment was scavenged by the Greymist murloc tribe. It can be pried from Greymist raiders, oracles, netters, tidehunters, and other tribe members wandering the beaches and shipwrecks of Darkshore.",al={"who has the middle key","where to find middle of gelkak key","middle key dropped by"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the key broken in the first place?",a="Gelkak's ship was sunk just offshore by aggressive threshadons. When the gnome was washed ashore amidst the splintered debris, the key smashed against the coastal rocks and fractured into three pieces before local scavengers carried them off.",al={"how did the key break","why is it in pieces"},it="history"},{q="What is the Middle of Gelkak's Key?",a="It is the central section of a three-piece key belonging to the shipwrecked goblin pirate Gelkak Gyromast. When his vessel sank off Darkshore's coast and he washed ashore, the key shattered on the jagged rocks, leaving this fragment among the wreckage.",al={"middle of gelkaks key","gelkaks key middle piece","what is this key piece"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Middle of Gelkak's Key come from, and who made it?",a="The key belongs to Gelkak Gyromast, brought aboard his vessel before it was destroyed by threshadons off the coast of Darkshore. While Gelkak owned the key to operate his mechanical first mate, its precise maker is unknown.",al={"who made gelkaks key","origin of middle key piece","where did the key come from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Gelkak Gyromast want the middle key piece?",a="Gelkak Gyromast needs this central piece alongside the other two fragments to reassemble the entire key. Without the complete key, he cannot wind up and reactivate his mechanical first mate to exact revenge on the local shoreline beasts.",al={"why does gelkak want this key","who wants gelkaks key","why is the key needed"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The key is a custom mechanical component designed to wind and operate a clockwork first mate, showing off classic gnomish ingenuity even in pirate hands."},kw={"clockwork","darkshore","gelkak gyromast","greymist","middle of gelkak's key","murloc","shipwreck"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2098","quest:2078","item:top-of-gelkak-s-key","item:bottom-of-gelkak-s-key","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","topic:pirate"},src={"Middle of Gelkak's Key","Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["item:mist-veil-s-lockbox"] = {t="item",n="Mist Veil's Lockbox",z="darkshore",s="Mist Veil's Lockbox is a sturdy strongbox resting in the submerged wreckage of the night elven vessel Mist Veil off the coast of Darkshore. It holds the captain's log and personal effects, which were lost when the ship was ambushed and sunk by coastal murlocs.",h="Mist Veil's Lockbox is a sturdy strongbox resting in the submerged wreckage of the night elven vessel Mist...",sec={{t="Lost to the Depths",b="The night elven vessel Mist Veil met its end while sailing the treacherous coastal waters toward Auberdine. Ambushed by hostile murlocs alongside its sister ship, the Silver Dawning, the vessel was overwhelmed and sent to the ocean floor. Its captain perished during the attack, leaving behind their logbook and prized personal belongings sealed inside this lockbox. Resting in the flooded hold, the chest remains a grim trophy surrounded by the very creatures responsible for the catastrophe.",sp=0},{t="Rest for the Crew",b="For the surviving sailors who managed to reach Auberdine, the loss of their vessel and commander remains an open wound. Gorbold Steelhand seeks the recovery of the Mist Veil's Lockbox so the captain's final effects can be properly honored and laid to rest. Braving the flooded ruins to salvage the chest offers some measure of solace to the grief-stricken survivors stranded on the mainland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Mist Veil's Lockbox?",a="The lockbox contains the captain's log and personal effects. The captain perished when the ship sank, and the surviving crew in Auberdine wish to have these mementos returned to honor their fallen leader.",al={"contents of mist veil lockbox","what does the lockbox hold","what is in the box"},it="item"},{q="How did the Mist Veil sink?",a="The Mist Veil was ambushed by coastal murlocs while navigating the waters toward Auberdine. Overwhelmed by the creatures, the ship foundered and sank to the seabed alongside its companion vessel, the Silver Dawning.",al={"why did the ship wreck","who sank mist veil","what happened to the mist veil"},it="history"},{q="Where is the lockbox found?",a="It is located underwater off the coast of Darkshore, north of Auberdine. The strongbox rests inside the flooded hull of the sunken Mist Veil wreckage, which is heavily infested with murlocs.",al={"where is mist veil's lockbox","mist veil location","lockbox location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the lockbox recovered?",a="Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine seeks the lockbox on behalf of the surviving crew members, hoping to bring closure and peace to the fallen captain's memory.",al={"who takes the lockbox","who gives the quest","gorbold lockbox quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Mist Veil's Lockbox?",a="It is the captain's chest recovered from the sunken vessel Mist Veil, resting beneath the waves off the coast of Darkshore north of Auberdine. Kept secure aboard the vessel until murlocs brought the ship down, it preserves the late night elf captain's logs, journals, and private effects from the ruined voyage.",al={"what is mist veil lockbox","mist veils lockbox","what is the lockbox"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The fallen captain was an esteemed night elf mariner, and securing their logbook helps put a respected spirit to rest in the waters off Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering this box honors the fallen crew and aids the struggling maritime community stationed at Auberdine."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","gorbold steelhand","lockbox","mist veil","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"quest:982","item:silver-dawning-s-lockbox","npc:gorbold-steelhand","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc"},src={"Mist Veil's Lockbox","Deep Ocean, Vast Sea"}}
E["item:moonstalker-fang"] = {t="item",n="Moonstalker Fang",z="darkshore",s="Moonstalker Fangs are sharp canine teeth taken from the predatory moonstalkers roaming the misty woods of Darkshore. They are gathered by travelers assisting Wizbang Cranktoggle with the maintenance of his automated sampling devices.",h="Moonstalker Fangs are sharp canine teeth taken from the predatory moonstalkers roaming the misty woods of...",sec={{t="A Grinding Mechanism",b="Moonstalkers are stealthy saber cats that haunt the forest fringes of Darkshore, stalking prey between the shadowed pines. Their elongated fangs serve as formidable hunting weapons, capable of shearing flesh and bone. For the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle, however, the teeth serve a very different mechanical purpose. Stationed north of Auberdine near the bridge, his automated contraption known as Buzzbox 323 is calibrated specifically to crush these durable fangs to dust as part of his erratic ecological surveys.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Moonstalker Fangs come from?",a="They are harvested from the various moonstalkers native to Darkshore, including moonstalker runts, adults, sires, matriarchs, and the elusive prowler known as Shadowclaw.",al={"where to get moonstalker fangs","who drops moonstalker fangs","fang source"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Moonstalker Fangs?",a="The gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle requires six of these fangs to feed into Buzzbox 323, an automated monitoring device located north of Auberdine near the river bridge.",al={"who needs fangs","what quest uses fangs","buzzbox 323 turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens to the fangs inside the machine?",a="Upon being placed into Buzzbox 323, internal gears activate and immediately grind the hard fangs into fine dust, advancing Wizbang's peculiar field experiments.",al={"what does buzzbox 323 do","why grind fangs"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Moonstalker Fang?",a="A Moonstalker Fang is a sharp, predatory canine tooth taken from the predatory moonstalkers roaming the misty forests of Darkshore. These nocturnal saber cats use their formidable fangs to hunt woodland prey, making them prized trophies and surprisingly durable material for peculiar local contraptions.",al={"moonstalker fang","what are moonstalker fangs","moonstalker teeth"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle's eccentric remote communication devices demonstrate classic gnome engineering, even if his slurred speech and bizarre sampling choices raise eyebrows.",["class:Hunter"]="Taking down moonstalkers requires keeping keen senses sharp against ambush predators that naturally blend into the darkened canopy of the shoreline."},kw={"buzzbox 323","darkshore","moonstalker","moonstalker fang","shadowclaw","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1002","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},src={"Moonstalker Fang","Buzzbox 323 (quest)"}}
E["item:moonwell-water-tube"] = {t="item",n="Moonwell Water Tube",z="darkshore",s="A vial filled with consecrated water drawn from the moonwell in Auberdine. Its potent, purifying nature magic is used to test and react with a mysterious red crystal embedded along Darkshore's eastern ridges.",h="A vial filled with consecrated water drawn from the moonwell in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Vessel of Purifying Waters",b="Drawn directly from the shimmering moonwell resting in Auberdine, the Moonwell Water Tube contains liquid steeped in the blessed energies of Elune. Moonwells serve night elf settlements as sacred reservoirs of restorative magic and purity, rendering even a small phial remarkably potent against corruption or unknown mystical phenomena.",sp=0},{t="Investigating the Red Crystal",b="The tube was prepared specifically to test a massive, alien red crystal that appeared against the eastern cliffside of Darkshore. Because the corrupted heights of Felwood loom directly above the mountain wall, researchers feared the crimson formation shared a dark origin. When the blessed water cascades across the crystal's facets, the magic forces the opaque stone to turn briefly transparent, revealing the humming mysteries locked inside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the water drawn from?",a="The water is scooped directly from the sacred moonwell located in the night elf haven of Auberdine, right in the heart of Darkshore.",al={"where do i fill the tube","water tube source","auberdine moonwell water"},it="origin"},{q="Why use moonwell water on the red crystal?",a="Moonwell water holds concentrated nature and lunar magic. Pouring it onto the bizarre red crystal tests its mystical composition, triggering an ethereal reaction that makes the opaque mineral surface momentarily clear.",al={"why moonwell water","purpose of the water tube","what does the water do"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the researchers concerned about the crystal?",a="The crystal rests directly beneath the eastern mountains bordering Felwood. Given Felwood's deep demonic taint, scholars fear the alien formation may be an extension of that corruption seeping down into Darkshore.",al={"why test the crystal","red crystal danger","felwood connection"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Moonwell Water Tube?",a="The Moonwell Water Tube is a simple glass vial filled with blessed water drawn directly from the moonwell in Auberdine. Moonwells hold potent, sacred magic nurtured by night elf druids and priestesses, making the liquid inside far more than ordinary spring water. Carrying it allows researchers to bring a small, concentrated measure of Elune's purifying power into the field to test unknown phenomena.",al={"what is moonwell water tube","moonwell water tube item","what is this tube of water"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why is the Moonwell Water Tube needed?",a="Investigators in Auberdine need the Moonwell Water Tube to analyze an ominous red crystal embedded along Darkshore's eastern mountains. Because the crystal is suspected of sharing a dark connection to corrupted Felwood high above, the researchers believe pouring the moonwell's pure, potent magic over its surface will safely react with the stone and reveal its inner composition.",al={"why do i need moonwell water tube","why want moonwell water","purpose of moonwell water tube"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Using blessed waters from a moonwell to probe foreign corruption reflects the kaldorei reliance on Elune's grace to reveal hidden truths.",["class:Druid"]="Druids recognize moonwell water as a vital conduit of the balance of nature, uniquely suited to counteracting unnatural corruption."},kw={"as water cascades","auberdine","darkshore","empty water tube","felwood","moonwell water tube","red crystal"},rel={"quest:4812","item:empty-water-tube","quest:4811","quest:4813","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood"},src={"Moonwell Water Tube","As Water Cascades"}}
E["item:mysterious-fossil"] = {t="item",n="Mysterious Fossil",z="darkshore",s="The Mysterious Fossil is an ancient specimen unearthed along the coast of Darkshore by Prospector Remtravel. Its curious characteristics have drawn the intense curiosity of the dwarven Explorers' League, prompting scholars to shuttle it across the sea to uncover its hidden secrets.",h="The Mysterious Fossil is an ancient specimen unearthed along the coast of Darkshore by Prospector Remtravel.",sec={{t="A Curious Discovery",b="While conducting fieldwork among the wild shores of Darkshore, Prospector Remtravel uncovered a fossil unlike the common petrified stone scattered across Kalimdor. Deeming it of monumental historical importance, Remtravel arranged for the specimen to be delivered to dwarven scholars rather than let it languish in the wilderness. When brought before Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus, the relic immediately stood out as an extraordinary find.",sp=0},{t="Ties Across the Ocean",b="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker noted that the specimen bore an uncanny resemblance to another rare fossil once displayed at an Explorers' League gathering in Ironforge. That earlier piece had been studied by Archaeologist Flagongut, who suspected the stone possessed latent power waiting to be awakened. To confirm its origins and unlock its potential secrets, Greywhisker directed couriers to carry the fossil across the ocean to Flagongut, who awaits transport in the Deepwater Tavern of Menethil Harbor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where was the Mysterious Fossil found?",a="The fossil was discovered in Darkshore by Prospector Remtravel during his fieldwork along the ancient northern coastline of Kalimdor.",al={"fossil location","where is it found","origin of fossil"},it="place"},{q="Why does the Explorers' League want this fossil?",a="The Explorers' League is dedicated to studying ancient artifacts and the origins of the world. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker believes this specimen is tied to research presented by Archaeologist Flagongut, who theorized that such fossils might hold unlockable power.",al={"why do dwarves want it","explorers league interest","what does the fossil do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is a researcher for the Explorers' League. Known for studying similar petrified relics, he is currently staying at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor while awaiting escort to the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands.",al={"who is flagongut","flagongut location","where is flagongut"},it="people"},{q="Who is Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker is the senior representative of the Explorers' League stationed in Darnassus, overseeing dwarven research and archaeological efforts across northern Kalimdor.",al={"greywhisker","who is greywhisker","darnassus dwarf archaeologist"},it="people"},{q="What is the Mysterious Fossil?",a="The Mysterious Fossil is an ancient relic unearthed in the wilderness of Darkshore by the dwarven Prospector Remtravel. Unlike mundane petrified remains, this specimen bears a striking resemblance to an extraordinary artifact previously showcased to the Explorers' League in Ironforge. Its peculiar nature suggests it holds dormant secrets or power waiting to be unlocked by an experienced archaeologist.",al={"mysterious fossil lore","what is this fossil","mysterious fossil info"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, this fossil represents another missing piece in the Explorers' League's ongoing quest to piece together ancient titan heritage and unearth forgotten mysteries.",["faction:Alliance"]="The transfer of the relic highlights the vital logistical chain binding Alliance outposts, connecting field scouts in Darkshore to scholars in Darnassus and Menethil Harbor."},kw={"darkshore","explorers league","flagongut","greywhisker","menethil harbor","mysterious fossil","remtravel"},rel={"quest:729","npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","npc:archaeologist-flagongut","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern"},src={"Mysterious Fossil","The Absent Minded Prospector (3)","The Absent Minded Prospector (4)"}}
E["item:nessa-s-collection"] = {t="item",n="Nessa's Collection",z="darkshore",s="Nessa's Collection is a package of fish bones and scales gathered from the waters surrounding Rut'theran Village. Prepared for study by fish vendor Laird in Auberdine, it illustrates the unusually massive size of aquatic life thriving around the roots of Teldrassil.",h="Nessa's Collection is a package of fish bones and scales gathered from the waters surrounding Rut'theran...",sec={{t="Bounty of the World Tree",b="Nessa Shadowsong, a fisherwoman residing in Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil, gathered this collection of fish bones and scales to compare the island's marine life with that of the Kalimdor mainland. The waters feeding into the Great Tree yield catches of staggering proportions, prompting Nessa to send physical proof across the sea to Laird, a fish merchant operating along the docks of Auberdine. Transferred by way of the village's hippogryph master, Vesprystus, the parcel serves as practical evidence of Teldrassil's burgeoning vitality.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Comparison",b="Upon inspecting the contents in Darkshore, Laird discovers that the specimens far outstrip their mainland counterparts. The collection contains jawbones nearly twice the size of fish native to the Darkshore coastline, along with individual scales as large as a clenched fist. For coastal night elves, the package provides a clear look at how drastically the waters around Teldrassil differ from the somber shores of northern Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Nessa's Collection?",a="The collection consists of fish bones, oversized jawbones, and fist-sized scales harvested from fish caught in the waters off Rut'theran Village.",al={"nessas collection contents","what is in the package","fish bones parcel"},it="item"},{q="Who is the collection being sent to?",a="It is sent to Laird, a night elf fish vendor stationed in the harbor village of Auberdine on the Darkshore coast.",al={"who gets nessas collection","who is laird","delivery destination"},it="target"},{q="Why did Nessa gather these fish specimens?",a="Nessa wanted to compare the remarkably large fish thriving around Teldrassil with the marine life found along mainland Kalimdor.",al={"why send fish bones","nessa fish comparison","bounty of teldrassil reason"},it="motive"},{q="How does the collection reach Auberdine?",a="A traveler carries the package to Rut'theran's hippogryph master, Vesprystus, who arranges passage across the water to Auberdine so the parcel can be delivered to Laird.",al={"how is it delivered","vesprystus delivery","hippogryph parcel"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Nessa's Collection?",a="Nessa's Collection is a package of fish bones and scales gathered from the waters around Rut'theran Village. It represents the unusual marine bounty thriving at the base of the World Tree Teldrassil, packed securely for transport across the sea to the Kalimdor mainland.",al={"what is nessa's collection","nessas collection","nessa collection item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Nessa's Collection come from, and who made it?",a="The collection was assembled by Nessa Shadowsong, a night elf residing in Rut'theran Village at the southern base of Teldrassil. Drawing from the remarkably large catches brought in by the local island fishermen, she gathered choice specimens to send overseas.",al={"who made nessa's collection","where does nessa collection come from","nessa collection origin"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Nessa's Collection?",a="A fish vendor named Laird in Auberdine awaits the specimens so he can study them. Nessa hopes to compare the astonishing size and vigor of Rut'theran's catches with mainland fish, and Laird is eager to examine jawbones twice their normal size and scales as large as a fist.",al={"why does laird want nessas collection","why deliver nessas collection","nessas collection purpose"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The collection offers night elves their first look at the unusually vigorous nature of Teldrassil's surrounding waters as they transition from their island home to the mainland."},kw={"auberdine","fish bones","laird","nessa shadowsong","nessa's collection","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"quest:6341","quest:6342","npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},src={"Nessa's Collection","The Bounty of Teldrassil","Flight to Auberdine"}}
E["item:phial-of-scrying"] = {t="item",n="Phial of Scrying",z="darkshore",s="The Phial of Scrying is an enchanted vessel provided by the ancient protector Onu in Darkshore. When used, it manifests a scrying bowl that allows distant communion across the corrupted woodlands.",h="The Phial of Scrying is an enchanted vessel provided by the ancient protector Onu in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Lens Across Darkshore",b="Entrusted to scouts investigating deep within Darkshore, the Phial of Scrying contains mystical waters that conjures a temporary scrying bowl upon the earth. This tool enables long-distance divination, allowing travelers venturing into perilous reaches like the Master's Glaive to commune directly with Onu without immediately journeying back to his grove.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Cult",b="Onu provides the phial specifically to monitor the unsettling presence of the Twilight's Hammer cultists. By establishing a scrying link at the site of the ancient fallen master impaled by an enormous glaive, the scout confirms that dark cultists are actively gathering around the ancient remains, seeking slivers of forgotten power that linger even in death.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does the Phial of Scrying do?",a="When uncorked, the phial manifests a magical scrying bowl on the ground, allowing an adventurer in the field to contact and speak with the ancient protector Onu across vast distances.",al={"use phial of scrying","scrying bowl function","what is this phial for"},it="power"},{q="Who provides the Phial of Scrying?",a="The ancient treant Onu entrusts the phial to scouts in Darkshore when tasking them with reconnoitering the Master's Glaive to the south.",al={"who gives phial of scrying","where do i get the phial"},it="origin"},{q="What happens if the phial is lost or exhausted?",a="If the phial is lost or used before completing your mission, Onu can provide another while he is meditating in Darkshore.",al={"lost phial of scrying","get another phial","replace phial"},gp=true},{q="Why is Onu scrying into the Master's Glaive?",a="Onu suspects the Twilight's Hammer cult is gathering at the Master's Glaive to tap into remnants of dark power left behind by the ancient entity impaled there.",al={"why scry master's glaive","onu glaive mission"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Phial of Scrying?",a="The Phial of Scrying is an enchanted vessel containing mystical waters provided by the ancient of lore, Onu. When poured out in the field, it creates a temporary Scrying Bowl that serves as a magical conduit, allowing you to establish a direct spiritual link with the ancient across vast distances.",al={"what is phial of scrying","phial of scrying lore","scrying phial explained"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Onu want you to use the Phial of Scrying?",a="Deep within Darkshore, the ancient treant Onu cannot physically travel to the Master's Glaive to investigate the presence of the Twilight's Hammer cult. He needs the phial so you can scout the site of the fallen ancient master and instantly report your discoveries back to him without having to make the long journey north first.",al={"why use phial of scrying","why does onu want phial","why need phial of scrying"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Darkshore, ancient tools of divination like scrying waters are vital for maintaining vigilance over holy woodlands encroached upon by alien cults.",["class:Druid"]="Druids recognize scrying bowls as a harmonious blend of natural water and communion magic, allowing the forest's wardens to exchange whispers across corrupted ground."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","quest:960","subzone:master-s-glaive","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Phial of Scrying","The Master's Glaive (quest)"}}
E["item:scaber-stalk"] = {t="item",n="Scaber Stalk",z="darkshore",s="Scaber Stalks are rare mushrooms that flourish in the damp, secluded cavern hidden behind Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. Prized by herbalists and alchemists for their unusual properties, they are sought by Barithras Moonshade for his concoctions.",h="Scaber Stalks are rare mushrooms that flourish in the damp, secluded cavern hidden behind Cliffspring Falls...",sec={{t="A Rare Fungal Specimen",b="Scaber Stalks are obscure mushrooms found deep within the cavern nestled behind Cliffspring Falls, situated along the northeastern mountains of Darkshore. Unlike ordinary forest flora, these pale stalks thrive strictly in the secluded dampness of the subterranean cave network. Their remote and hazardous habitat makes gathering them exceedingly rare, leading alchemists like Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine to commission daring scouts willing to brave the dark.",sp=0},{t="A Shadow in the Falls",b="Harvesting Scaber Stalks carries far more danger than ordinary foraging. The venerable tree-spirits at the Grove of the Ancients issued warnings to local night elves, having sensed a dark and growing evil establishing itself within the Cliffspring Falls cave. While alchemists value the stalks alongside rare Death Caps for experimental draughts, collecting them inevitably brings gatherers face to face with whatever malice has taken root beneath the mountains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do Scaber Stalks grow?",a="Scaber Stalks grow exclusively inside the damp cave tucked behind Cliffspring Falls, located in northeastern Darkshore along the mountainous ridge.",al={"scaber stalk location","where are scaber stalks","scaber stalk cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Scaber Stalks?",a="Barithras Moonshade, a night elf scholar residing in Auberdine, seeks Scaber Stalks along with a Death Cap to brew a specialized potion.",al={"who uses scaber stalk","barithras moonshade mushrooms","who needs scaber stalks"},it="target"},{q="Why didn't Barithras Moonshade collect the stalks himself?",a="Barithras was warned away from the cave by the Grove of the Ancients, whose spirits sensed that a dangerous new evil had taken refuge behind the waterfall.",al={"why not get them himself","barithras warning","cliffspring cave warning"},it="motive"},{q="What else grows alongside Scaber Stalks?",a="The cavern also shelters the lethal Death Cap mushroom, another rare specimen required by Barithras for his alchemical research.",al={"other mushrooms in the cave","death cap and scaber stalk","cliffspring mushrooms"},gp=true},{q="What is a Scaber Stalk?",a="A Scaber Stalk is a rare species of cave mushroom native to the shadowy cavern tucked behind Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. While subterranean fungi are common throughout northern Kalimdor, this particular variety flourishes in damp, dark grottos that harbor sinister energies.",al={"what is scaber stalk","scaber stalk info","scaber stalk mushroom"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Scaber Stalks?",a="Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine seeks Scaber Stalks as a vital ingredient for brewing specialized potions. Because these potent fungi only grow in the secluded cave near Cliffspring Falls, herbalists and alchemists must rely on adventurous travelers to harvest them.",al={"why gather scaber stalk","scaber stalk use","what are scaber stalks for"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="While not a standard traded herb, these subterranean stalks offer valuable insight into how unique cavern climates and encroaching shadows alter local fungal biology.",["race:NightElf"]="Heeding the warnings of the Grove of the Ancients, night elves approach the harvesting of these cave mushrooms with great caution due to the corrupting presence festering near Cliffspring Falls."},kw={"auberdine","barithras moonshade","cave mushrooms","cliffspring falls","darkshore","death cap","scaber stalk"},rel={"quest:947","item:death-cap","subzone:cliffspring-falls","npc:barithras-moonshade","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:952"},src={"Scaber Stalk","Cave Mushrooms"}}
E["item:sea-creature-bones"] = {t="item",n="Sea Creature Bones",z="darkshore",s="Sea Creature Bones are skeletal samples gathered from the massive marine carcasses washing ashore along the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore. Sent directly to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, these remains are central to an ongoing investigation into what is driving these great beasts to strand themselves upon the beaches.",h="Sea Creature Bones are skeletal samples gathered from the massive marine carcasses washing ashore along the...",sec={{t="A Portent on the Shore",b="The fog-blanketed beaches of Darkshore have recently witnessed an alarming surge of massive sea creatures—including giant threshers far larger than those native to the local shallows—flinging themselves onto the shallows until they perish. The sight is viewed as an ominous portent by the night elves. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, an investigator dispatched by the Temple of the Moon to Auberdine, collects bone specimens from these beached leviathans to ship by hippogryph to Darnassus for close examination.",sp=0},{t="Carrion and Scavengers",b="Recovering these bones is fraught with danger, as the immense carcasses inevitably attract local scavengers. The coastal Greymist murlocs frequently swarm the dead and dying leviathans, feeding on the remains and defending the feeding grounds aggressively. Although the murlocs are far too weak to hunt such colossal creatures on their own, their opportunistic presence along Mist's Edge forces investigators and adventurers to fight through the scavenging packs to secure viable bone fragments for study.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are these creatures washing ashore?",a="The exact cause remains unknown. While occasional strandings are a natural hazard, their sudden and dramatic increase is considered unnatural and alarming by the priestesses of Elune, prompting their formal investigation.",al={"why are threshers beaching","darkshore dead whales","why do creatures strand darkshore"},it="threat"},{q="Who wants these bones?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, an investigator stationed in Auberdine, collects the bones on behalf of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, where scholars and priestesses hope to determine what is disturbing the sea.",al={"who takes the bones","who turns in sea creature bones","gwennyth darkshore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Did the murlocs kill these giant beasts?",a="No. The local Greymist murlocs are far too weak to bring down marine beasts of that size. They are merely scavengers that gather in large numbers to feed upon the carcasses once they are beached.",al={"did murlocs kill the thresher","greymist murlocs killed sea monster"}},{q="Where are the bones recovered from?",a="They are retrieved directly from the massive carcasses stranded along the shoreline of Darkshore, particularly on the sands south of Auberdine and along Mist's Edge.",al={"where to find sea creature bones","beached sea creature locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are these Sea Creature Bones?",a="They are skeletal remnants scavenged from the massive carcass of a beached sea beast—specifically an unusually large thresher—stranded along the misty coastline of Darkshore. Scavenged by local Greymist murlocs, these massive remains serve as vital physical evidence for researchers trying to understand why the ocean's behemoths are perishing on shore.",al={"what are sea creature bones","sea creature bones lore","giant bones darkshore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do the Sea Creature Bones come from?",a="These bones come from colossal marine threshers native to the surrounding waters that have inexplicably hurled themselves onto the beaches of Mist's Edge south of Auberdine. Rather than being crafted or slain by local predators, the bones belong naturally to deep-sea beasts that mysteriously drove themselves ashore to die.",al={"where do sea creature bones come from","origin of sea creature bones","beached sea creature origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The sudden mass strandings along Darkshore deeply disturb the night elves, who revere the harmony of the natural world and see these beachings as a dark omen requiring the attention of the Temple of the Moon.",["class:Druid"]="The inexplicable deaths of ancient marine predators signal a profound disturbance in the waters off Kalimdor, troubling any guardian devoted to maintaining ecological balance."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","greymist murlocs","gwennyth bly'leggonde","mist's edge","sea creature bones","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","quest:4723","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:mist-s-edge","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:murloc"},src={"Sea Creature Bones","Washed Ashore","Beached Sea Creature (1)"}}
E["item:sea-turtle-remains"] = {t="item",n="Sea Turtle Remains",z="darkshore",s="Sea Turtle Remains are skeletal samples salvaged from the carcasses of giant sea turtles along the coast of Darkshore. They serve as vital specimens for night elf researchers in Auberdine investigating an alarming surge of marine strandings.",h="Sea Turtle Remains are skeletal samples salvaged from the carcasses of giant sea turtles along the coast of...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Strand",b="Giant sea creatures have begun beaching themselves all along Darkshore's mist-shrouded shores, while others lie submerged just off the coast near sunken wrecks. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, stationed in Auberdine, oversees the collection of skeletal fragments and tissue from these corpses. The Temple of the Moon in Darnassus urgently requests these samples, concerned by theories that the beasts may be fleeing an unnatural disturbance in the waters surrounding the newly grown world tree, Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="Recovering these remains is perilous work. Coastal tribes of murlocs routinely congregate around the massive carcasses, picking the bones clean and nesting beside them. Scholars require fresh bone fragments and tissue before the scavengers destroy any surviving evidence that might explain the creatures' fatal migration.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are these remains used for?",a="The remains are collected by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine. She prepares them for scholars and priestesses at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, who are attempting to discern why so many ocean creatures are dying along Darkshore.",al={"why collect turtle remains","turtle bones use","sea turtle quest darkshore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are sea turtles beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="The exact cause remains under investigation, but researchers fear marine life is fleeing something unsettling in the waters around Teldrassil. The strandings are not isolated incidents, pointing to widespread ecological distress.",al={"why are turtles dying","turtle strandings darkshore","beached sea creatures"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these carcasses found?",a="Giant skeletal sea turtles are scattered along Darkshore's coastline, with some resting in shallow waters near sunken ships west of Auberdine and others strewn on beaches surrounded by murloc encampments.",al={"turtle remains locations","where to find skeletal sea turtle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is studying these remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a researcher in Auberdine, collects the findings and submits detailed reports directly to the Sisterhood of Elune at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"who wants the remains","gwennyth blyleggonde"},it="people"},{q="What are these Sea Turtle Remains?",a="These remains are skeletal samples recovered from giant sea turtles that have washed ashore along Darkshore's coastline or died in its shallow waters. Though scavenged by local predators and murlocs, salvageable bones and tissue linger, offering physical clues about the creatures' final moments.",al={"what are sea turtle remains","sea turtle remains lore","what is sea turtle remains"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do the Sea Turtle Remains come from?",a="They are gathered directly from massive skeletal carcasses lying along the shores and coastal waters of Darkshore, including specimens near Auberdine. They are natural remains of marine beasts rather than crafted objects, left behind when dying turtles swim aground and perish.",al={"where do sea turtle remains come from","origin of sea turtle remains","source of sea turtle remains"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The mass stranding of sea life directly off your ancestral coast is an ominous sign, particularly with suspicions pointing back toward the waters encircling Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="The unnatural death of wild marine leviathans signals a deeper corruption upsetting the balance of nature along the Kalimdor coast."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea turtle","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea turtle remains","teldrassil","temple of the moon","washed ashore"},rel={"quest:3524","npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","quest:940","topic:murloc"},src={"Sea Turtle Remains","Washed Ashore (2)","Beached Sea Turtle (1)"}}
E["item:silver-dawning-s-lockbox"] = {t="item",n="Silver Dawning's Lockbox",z="darkshore",s="The Silver Dawning's Lockbox is a sturdy chest resting within the sunken wreckage of the vessel Silver Dawning off the coast of Darkshore. It holds the personal effects and ship log of the vessel's fallen captain, lost during an ambush by coastal murlocs.",h="The Silver Dawning's Lockbox is a sturdy chest resting within the sunken wreckage of the vessel Silver...",sec={{t="Sunken Remnants",b="The ship Silver Dawning was en route across the sea toward the port of Auberdine when disaster struck. Coastal murlocs swarmed the vessel, driving it down into the dark surf north of the harbor. The captain perished in the assault alongside the crew, leaving the wreckage submerged beneath the waves as a grim monument claimed by the creatures. Inside the flooded hull remains the captain's personal lockbox, holding the ship's log and private belongings. Recovering these effects offers a final measure of peace to the surviving crew members ashore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Silver Dawning's Lockbox located?",a="The lockbox sits inside the submerged wreckage of the Silver Dawning, an overturned vessel resting on the ocean floor north of Auberdine off the Darkshore coast.",al={"lockbox location","where is silver dawning box","silver dawning wreck"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Silver Dawning?",a="As the Silver Dawning sailed toward Auberdine across the ocean, it was ambushed by local murlocs. The vessel was overcome, wrecked, and sank beneath the waves, claiming the life of its captain.",al={"why did silver dawning sink","silver dawning backstory","how did ship wreck"},it="history"},{q="What is inside the lockbox?",a="The chest contains the personal effects and sea log kept by the captain of the Silver Dawning, preserved against the ocean depths.",al={"silver dawning contents","what is in the box"},it="item"},{q="Who is seeking the lockbox?",a="Gorbold Steelhand, a dwarf stationed in Auberdine, asks brave swimmers to dive into the wrecks and retrieve the lockbox so the fallen captain's surviving crew can properly honor their memory.",al={"who wants the lockbox","who gives the quest","turn in lockbox"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Silver Dawning's Lockbox?",a="It is the personal chest belonging to the late captain of the Silver Dawning. When the vessel was overrun and sunk by murlocs off the northern coast of Darkshore, the lockbox went down with the wreck. It holds the captain's log and surviving personal effects, resting deep underwater amidst the prowling creatures.",al={"what is silver dawnings lockbox","silver dawning chest lore","captain lockbox silver dawning"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The lockbox preserves the final writings and relics of a kaldorei captain who died defending their vessel right off the shores of northern Kalimdor.",["race:Dwarf"]="Gorbold Steelhand takes it upon himself to see the fallen captains honored and their belongings returned to their surviving mates."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","gorbold steelhand","lockbox","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"quest:982","npc:gorbold-steelhand","item:mist-veil-s-lockbox","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc"},src={"Silver Dawning's Lockbox","Deep Ocean, Vast Sea"}}
E["item:stone-of-relu"] = {t="item",n="Stone of Relu",z="darkshore",s="The Stone of Relu is an ancient archaeological relic recovered from the Wetlands. Believed by Archaeologist Flagongut to be the key to unlocking latent powers within primordial fossils, it was briefly lost when local raptors ambushed the scholar on the road.",h="The Stone of Relu is an ancient archaeological relic recovered from the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Key to Ancient Relics",b="Discovered during Explorers' League operations, the Stone of Relu is believed to hold the deciphering power needed to unlock prehistoric fossils gathered from Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Archaeologist Flagongut identified the artifact as the catalyst required to unleash secrets within both his own Wetlands specimens and the fossil unearthed by Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Lost in the Marshes",b="While Flagongut was traveling along the Wetland roads to rendezvous with Prospector Whelgar, a pack of mottled raptors ambushed him. During the scramble, the relic was lost and swallowed by one of the ravenous beasts, forcing the League to enlist adventurers to hunt the marsh raptors and cut the ancient stone from their gullets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Stone of Relu?",a="The Stone of Relu is an ancient artifact sought by Archaeologist Flagongut. He believes it acts as a cipher or catalyst capable of unlocking the hidden mysteries and power dormant inside prehistoric fossils.",al={"stone of relu","what is this stone","relu artifact"},it="identity"},{q="How did the stone end up inside a raptor?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut was carrying the relic along the Wetlands road to meet Prospector Whelgar when mottled raptors attacked his party. In the chaos, the stone was lost and ingested by one of the scavenging beasts.",al={"why do raptors have it","who dropped the stone","how was it lost"}},{q="What is Flagongut planning to do with the stone?",a="Flagongut intends to pair the stone with his recovered fossil and the fossil found by Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore, using the relic to decipher and release their latent magical secrets.",al={"what does flagongut want","stone of relu purpose"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the Explorers' League, the Stone of Relu is a vital tool in piecing together the origins of ancient life and the forgotten legacy of the world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance expeditions in Menethil Harbor rely on recovered artifacts like the Stone of Relu to justify the arduous excavations across the perilous marshlands."},kw={"archaeologist flagongut","explorers league","fossil","mottled raptor","prospector whelgar","stone of relu","wetlands"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","quest:729","item:flagongut-s-fossil","npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore"},src={"Stone of Relu","The Absent Minded Prospector (5)"}}
E["item:strangely-marked-box"] = {t="item",n="Strangely Marked Box",z="darkshore",s="A Strangely Marked Box is a piece of cargo discovered inside the harnesses strapped to dead sea turtles along the Darkshore coastline. Its mysterious exterior bears the runic script of the serpentine naga, offering night elf scholars proof that these sea creatures did not strand themselves by accident.",h="A Strangely Marked Box is a piece of cargo discovered inside the harnesses strapped to dead sea turtles along...",sec={{t="Trophies of the Deep",b="While several giant sea turtles and sea creatures simply wash ashore along Darkshore's mist-veiled beaches, others tell a far more ominous tale. Scattered carcasses bear the splintered remnants of riding harnesses and abandoned carriages bound straight to their shells. Within the ruins of these buckled contraptions lie sealed containers covered in foreign, sinuous runes. Scavenging Greymist murlocs frequently take up residence in the hollow ribcages and broken wagons, picking at the carrion and guarding whatever remnants were left behind.",sp=0},{t="Evidence of Naga Expansion",b="When brought to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a researcher representing the Temple of the Moon in Auberdine, the markings on the box reveal their true origin. The script and the strapped carriages belong to the naga, who use massive turtles as beasts of burden to ferry logistical supplies and war equipment onto dry land. The discovery of these supply boxes confirms that the naga are deliberately operating along the northern shores and may be driving mounts south toward Ashenvale, prompting the priesthood in Auberdine to ship the relics directly to Darnassus for further study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Strangely Marked Box found?",a="The box is recovered from abandoned carriages strapped to the shells of beached sea turtle carcasses along the coast of Darkshore. These carcasses are often surrounded and defended by Greymist murlocs feeding on the carrion.",al={"where to find strangely marked box","box location","turtle carriage box"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who made the Strangely Marked Box?",a="The box and its inscriptions were created by the naga. They affix cargo carriages to living sea turtles to haul provisions, arms, and equipment out of the ocean depths and onto the shores of Kalimdor.",al={"who made the box","markings on box","box runes","what are the markings"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants this box in Auberdine?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a researcher working in Auberdine on behalf of the Temple of the Moon, collects the box to analyze the strange beachings and understand the growing naga threat.",al={"who do i turn this in to","box turn in","who wants the box"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Why were the sea turtles carrying these boxes?",a="The naga domesticate or enslave giant sea turtles as beasts of burden, strapping harnesses and carriages to their backs for battle and to carry their supplies onto land. Gwennyth suspects one such turtle was killed while heading further south, perhaps toward Ashenvale.",al={"why do turtles have boxes","turtle carriages","why are turtles strapped"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens to the box after giving it to Gwennyth?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde forwards the box and the rest of the coastal survey findings up to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus so the night elf leadership can study the extent of the naga incursion.",al={"where does the box go","box sent to darnassus"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Strangely Marked Box?",a="It is a piece of cargo discovered inside a buckled carriage strapped to the shell of a beached sea turtle along Darkshore's coastline. Marked with peculiar runes, the crate serves as physical evidence of organized maritime transport along the coast, abandoned after the carrying creature perished and was subsequently overrun by scavengers.",al={"what is the marked box","what is strangely marked box","strangely marked box item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want the Strangely Marked Box?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde seeks the box on behalf of the Temple of the Moon to investigate why massive sea creatures are beaching themselves upon Darkshore. Deciphering the markings confirms that the turtles were harnessed and used as beasts of burden by hostile naga transporting supplies inland, clues she forwards directly to scholars in Darnassus.",al={"why does gwennyth want the box","why deliver strangely marked box","marked box purpose"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Finding naga supply boxes lashed to native sea turtles along Darkshore warns the kaldorei that their ancient, mutated kin are systematically pushing ashore from the Great Sea.",["class:Priest"]="Securing relics from the shore aids the Temple of the Moon's scholars in Auberdine as they work to safeguard the coast from marine corruption."},kw={"auberdine","carriage","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","naga","sea turtle","strangely marked box"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:4722","topic:naga","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:murloc","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Strangely Marked Box","Beached Sea Turtle (2)","Beached Sea Turtle (4)"}}
E["item:talisman-of-corruption"] = {t="item",n="Talisman of Corruption",z="darkshore",s="The Talisman of Corruption is a vile demonic trinket used by the satyr Xabraxxis to poison the minds of Darkshore's Blackwood furbolgs. Carried within the satyr's personal pouch, it serves as a magical conduit that binds the tribe to fel madness.",h="The Talisman of Corruption is a vile demonic trinket used by the satyr Xabraxxis to poison the minds of...",sec={{t="A Conduit of Madness",b="The night elves of Auberdine have long struggled to understand why the Blackwood furbolgs turned so aggressively upon their former allies. Thundris Windweaver discovered that the tribe's downfall was not a natural descent, but deliberate sabotage orchestrated by the satyrs. Using talismans like this one, demonic agents project corrupting sorcery across the wilderness, tainting food supplies and twisting peaceful forest spirits into frenzied beasts. By channeling fell magics directly through these devices, the satyrs hold an unbroken grip over the minds and wills of the local tribes.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Grip",b="To draw out the satyr responsible, adventurers must purify samples of the furbolgs' food using blessed moonwell water, cleansing the camp long enough to enrage its overseer. Slaying Xabraxxis breaks his immediate hold and yields his demon bag, inside which the talisman rests. Delivering the talisman to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine allows the Kaldorei to neutralize its foul emanations and study how to permanently undo the demonic affliction plaguing the forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Talisman of Corruption?",a="It is a demonic device used by the satyr Xabraxxis to channel foul magic and corrupt the minds and food sources of the Blackwood furbolgs in Darkshore.",al={"what is talisman of corruption","talisman purpose","what does the talisman do"},it="identity"},{q="Who carries the talisman?",a="It is kept within the demon bag carried by Xabraxxis, a satyr who oversees the northern Blackwood furbolg camp near the Cliffspring River.",al={"who drops talisman of corruption","where to find talisman of corruption","how to get talisman"},it="origin"},{q="How do you draw out the owner of the talisman?",a="You must collect samples of the furbolgs' fruit, grain, and nuts, combine them with moonwell water in a cleansing bowl, and place the offering by the bonfire near the river. Cleansing the furbolgs enrages Xabraxxis, prompting him to attack.",al={"how to summon xabraxxis","how to find xabraxxis","summon satyr darkshore"},gp=true},{q="What happens to the talisman after it is recovered?",a="It is turned over to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. He secures the artifact for disposal and studies it to learn how to permanently liberate the furbolgs from demonic corruption.",al={"who do i give the talisman to","turn in talisman of corruption","thundris windweaver talisman"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei of Auberdine, recovering the talisman is a vital step toward freeing their ancestral furbolg allies from demonic degradation and healing the land.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view devices like the talisman as direct perversions of the natural order, twisting sacred beasts into feral pawns of the Burning Legion's leftover minions."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","furbolg","satyr","talisman of corruption","thundris windweaver","xabraxxis"},rel={"quest:4763","topic:satyr","topic:furbolg","item:empty-cleansing-bowl","quest:4761","quest:4762","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},src={"Talisman of Corruption","The Blackwood Corrupted"}}
E["item:tharnariun-s-hope"] = {t="item",n="Tharnariun's Hope",z="darkshore",s="Tharnariun's Hope is a specialized trap crafted by the night elf Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore. Designed to pacify diseased wildlife rather than harm it, the device projects a calming light intended to tame rabid thistle bears so they can be examined for a cure.",h="Tharnariun's Hope is a specialized trap crafted by the night elf Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Gentle Snare",b="As a mysterious affliction spreads through Darkshore, the local thistle bears have grown increasingly frenzied and violent. Rather than sanctioning a cull of the afflicted wildlife, the druid Tharnariun Treetender crafted this unique trap in the hope of studying and curing the illness. When laid upon the ground, Tharnariun's Hope emits a soothing radiance. Any rabid thistle bear that steps across the trap's light has its frenzy temporarily broken, rendering the beast docile enough to follow an adventurer back to Tharnariun's camp for treatment.",sp=0},{t="The Elusive Remedy",b="While the trap succeeds in subduing the maddened beasts without drawing blood, the underlying corruption proves far more vicious than anticipated. When Tharnariun channels his healing magic into the captured bear, the restorative power violently clashes with the virulent infection, causing the afflicted creature to collapse and perish. Despite the heartbreaking failure of his initial trial, Tharnariun insists his determination will not waver until the true nature of the forest's sickness is uncovered.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Tharnariun's Hope do?",a="It is an enchanted ground trap designed to pacify a rabid thistle bear. Placing it on the forest floor creates a field of light that temporarily calms a bear crossing its threshold, allowing the beast to be led peacefully back to Tharnariun Treetender.",al={"tharnariuns hope use","how does the trap work","what is this trap"},it="power"},{q="Why does Tharnariun want a live bear captured?",a="Tharnariun believes that the sickness afflicting Darkshore's wildlife can be cured rather than ended through slaughter. He needs a living subject to test his cleansing remedies directly.",al={"why capture thistle bear","why catch a rabid bear","what does tharnariun want"},it="motive"},{q="Can you get another trap if you lose it?",a="Yes. Tharnariun assures travelers that his hope is eternal. If a trap is triggered in vain or lost in the wild, returning to him will provide another device to finish the task.",al={"lost tharnariuns hope","failed trap","trap disappeared"},gp=true},{q="What happens to the bear once it is brought back?",a="Upon the bear's arrival, Tharnariun casts a healing enchantment to purge the corruption. Tragically, the foul sickness is too entrenched; the magic overwhelms the beast, and it dies within moments.",al={"does the bear survive","can tharnariun cure the bear","bear dies at tharnariun"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Tharnariun's Hope?",a="Tharnariun's Hope is an enchanted snare devised by Tharnariun Treetender. When laid upon the ground, it radiates a calming light capable of temporarily pacifying the afflicted, rabid thistle bears wandering Darkshore. The soothing enchantment makes a frenzied beast gentle and willing to follow you back to Auberdine.",al={"what is tharnariuns hope","tharnariun hope item","tharnariun trap"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Tharnariun's Hope come from, and who made it?",a="The trap was crafted and enchanted by Tharnariun Treetender, a night elf naturalist stationed in Darkshore. Horrified by the mysterious sickness driving the forest's wildlife into madness, he fashioned this device using gentle magic to subdue infected beasts without causing them further harm.",al={"who made tharnariuns hope","origin of tharnariun's hope","tharnariun trap creator"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Tharnariun's Hope?",a="Tharnariun needs the trap used to capture a living, rabid thistle bear so he can study the corruption ravaging Darkshore. Ordinary hunting would only slay the beast, but this snare pacifies the animal long enough for you to lead it safely into his care in hopes of discovering a cure.",al={"why use tharnariun's hope","why need tharnariun trap","purpose of tharnariuns hope"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The trap embodies the Cenarion ideal of preservation over extermination, demonstrating a refusal to strike down corrupted beasts when a chance for redemption remains.",["race:NightElf"]="The degradation of Darkshore's beloved thistle bears strikes at the heart of the kaldorei bond with nature, making the device a poignant symbol of desperate compassion."},kw={"darkshore","plagued lands","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun","tharnariun's hope","thistle bear","trap"},rel={"quest:2118","npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2139","zone:darkshore"},src={"Tharnariun's Hope","Plagued Lands"}}
E["item:thresher-eye"] = {t="item",n="Thresher Eye",z="darkshore",s="Thresher Eyes are organic harvesting samples taken from the threshers prowling the coastal waters of Darkshore. They are sought by the eccentric gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle to service his automated field devices known as Buzzboxes.",h="Thresher Eyes are organic harvesting samples taken from the threshers prowling the coastal waters of...",sec={{t="Ecological Samples for Gnomish Gadgets",b="Off the misty shores of Darkshore, aquatic predators known as Darkshore Threshers hunt along the surf and outer shallows. While dangerous to local fishermen and travelers, these beasts possess large ocular organs that have drawn the peculiar interest of Wizbang Cranktoggle. Stationed nearby and deeply fond of crawler wine, the gnomish engineer demands these eyes as essential components to repair Buzzbox 411, an automated surveying machine positioned along the northern beaches.",sp=0},{t="The Purpose of the Eyes",b="Wizbang never fully elaborates on how slimy sea-creature eyes repair delicate mechanical apparatuses, whether functioning as crude optical lenses, chemical agents, or esoteric biological gears. Regardless of the questionable engineering logic, feeding three of these harvested eyes into Buzzbox 411's maintenance hatch successfully restores the machine's comms link, allowing Wizbang to dispense rewards through static-choked transmissions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Thresher Eyes come from?",a="Thresher Eyes are harvested from Darkshore Threshers and Elder Darkshore Threshers swimming in the ocean waters off the coast of Darkshore, particularly near Auberdine.",al={"where do thresher eyes drop","how to get thresher eye","thresher eye source"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want Thresher Eyes?",a="Wizbang claims the eyes are needed to repair Buzzbox 411, a gnomish contraption located north of Auberdine on the shoreline. Inserting them into the machine's hatch reactivates its systems.",al={"why need thresher eyes","buzzbox 411 eyes","what are thresher eyes for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does an eye fix a machine?",a="Gnomish engineering often defies conventional logic, especially when guided by Wizbang Cranktoggle's inebriated schemes. Whether he uses the retinas for optical focusing or simply incorporates organic parts into his eccentric designs, the device accepts them and powers back on.",al={"why eyes for a machine","gnome machine biological parts"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Buzzbox 411?",a="Buzzbox 411 is one of several communication and monitoring devices deployed across Darkshore by Wizbang Cranktoggle. Once loaded with requested materials, it allows Wizbang to communicate remotely and dispense supplies.",al={"buzzbox 411 purpose","who built buzzbox 411"},it="target"},{q="What is a Thresher Eye?",a="A Thresher Eye is the ocular organ harvested from the predatory threshers swimming in the coastal waters off Darkshore. While mundane biological matter to most, eccentric tinkerers like Wizbang Cranktoggle find bizarre mechanical or chemical utility for them in repairing sensitive sampling devices.",al={"what is thresher eye","thresher eyes"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizbang's reliance on raw animal parts to mend complex mechanical relays offers a baffling, albeit humorous, study in unorthodox gnomish contraptions.",["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle represents the wilder fringes of gnomish ingenuity, tinkering with field machinery along Kalimdor's wilderness between cups of crawler wine."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 411","darkshore","darkshore thresher","thresher eye","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1001","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:983","topic:gnome"},src={"Thresher Eye","Buzzbox 411 (quest)"}}
E["item:top-of-gelkak-s-key"] = {t="item",n="Top of Gelkak's Key",z="darkshore",s="The Top of Gelkak's Key is one of three shattered fragments of a mechanical key belonging to the shipwrecked gnome Gelkak Gyromast. After his vessel was lost off the coast of Darkshore, this jagged brass section was snatched up by a giant foreststrider roaming the nearby woods.",h="The Top of Gelkak's Key is one of three shattered fragments of a mechanical key belonging to the shipwrecked...",sec={{t="A Shattered Mechanism",b="When Gelkak Gyromast's ship was attacked and sunk by ravenous threshadons off the coast of Darkshore, the gnome washed ashore clutching the winding key meant for his mechanical first mate. The impact against the coastal rocks broke the instrument into three pieces. Before the dizzy pirate could gather his wits, the indigenous beasts scavenged the wreckage, with a giant foreststrider making off with this ornate upper portion into the misty forest.",sp=0},{t="Restoring the First Mate",b="The key is essential for winding up and activating Gelkak's mechanical first mate, an automaton the marooned gnome intends to use to exact vengeance on the local wildlife. Recovering this fragment, along with the middle and bottom sections pilfered by shore murlocs and reef crawlers, allows Gyromast to piece the device together and bring his construct to life.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Top of Gelkak's Key used for?",a="It is one of three broken segments required by the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast to repair his mechanical winding key. Once assembled, the key is used to reactivate his mechanical first mate.",al={"what does gelkaks key do","use of top of gelkaks key","gelkak key purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did a foreststrider get this piece of the key?",a="When Gelkak was shipwrecked and cast upon the Darkshore beaches, his key smashed on the rocks. Curious beasts immediately rummaged through the debris, and a giant foreststrider swallowed or carried off the upper brass piece into the woods northeast of the shore.",al={"why do tallstriders have the key","who took gelkak key top","how did foreststrider get key"}},{q="Where are the other pieces of the key?",a="The middle section was snatched by Greymist murlocs haunting the nearby shipwreck, while the bottom section was carried off by the crabs scouring the tideline.",al={"where are other key parts","middle and bottom of gelkak key","gelkak key fragments"},gp=true},{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is an eccentric gnome pirate who found himself marooned along the shores of Darkshore after threshadons wrecked his vessel. Stranded and furious, he plots revenge against the creatures of the coast.",al={"who is gelkak","gelkak gyromast lore"},it="people"},{q="What is the Top of Gelkak's Key?",a="It is one of three broken fragments of a specialized key belonging to the shipwrecked gnome Gelkak Gyromast. When his vessel was brought down off the coast of Darkshore, the key shattered upon the rocky shoreline. This particular upper segment was scavenged by the local giant foreststriders wandering the nearby woods.",al={"top of gelkaks key","what is gelkaks key top","gelkaks key fragment"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The key is designed to wind and activate a clockwork automaton, showcasing the ingenious and sturdy mechanical craftsmanship typical of gnome tinkers.",["race:Gnome"]="Seeing a fellow gnome surviving a catastrophic shipwreck through raw eccentricity and clockwork contraptions is a familiar and endearing sight."},kw={"darkshore","first mate","foreststrider","gelkak","gyromast","key","pirate","retrieval"},rel={"quest:2098","npc:gelkak-gyromast","item:middle-of-gelkak-s-key","item:bottom-of-gelkak-s-key","quest:2078","zone:darkshore","topic:pirate","topic:murloc"},src={"Top of Gelkak's Key","Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["item:worn-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Worn Parchment",z="darkshore",s="Worn Parchments are fragmented ritual writings carried by cultists encamped around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Gathered by scouts, these tattered scraps provide the first concrete clues identifying the sinister sect gathering in the ruins.",h="Worn Parchments are fragmented ritual writings carried by cultists encamped around the Tower of Althalaxx in...",sec={{t="Fragments of a Sinister Plot",b="North along the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore, dark spellcasters and their zealous followers have seized the ruined Tower of Althalaxx. The foot soldiers patrolling the grounds outside, known as Dark Strand Fanatics, carry scraps of worn parchment among their personal effects. While a single piece appears as nothing more than fragmented scribbles and esoteric symbols, piecing together multiple fragments reveals the presence of a previously unknown organization: the Cult of the Dark Strand.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking the Cult",b="Balthule Shadowstrike, a scout monitoring the tower from a nearby overlook, uses these gathered parchments to assess the threat for Delgren the Purifier and the sentinels in Auberdine. piecing the texts together confirms that the warlocks in the tower are not independent outcasts, but an organized coven working toward a calculated, malevolent objective.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who carries these worn parchments?",a="The parchments are carried by Dark Strand Fanatics, the cultist foot soldiers encamped outside around the perimeter of the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore.",al={"who drops worn parchment","where to get worn parchment","worn parchment source"},it="people"},{q="What is written on the parchments?",a="Individually, they are cryptic fragments of ritual notes and orders. Once gathered together and deciphered by Balthule Shadowstrike, they reveal the name and existence of the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"what does worn parchment say","worn parchment text","parchment meaning"},it="item"},{q="Why is Balthule Shadowstrike collecting them?",a="Balthule was tasked by Delgren the Purifier to watch the Tower of Althalaxx. He needs the writings to decipher why warlocks have gathered at the ruins and assess the danger to Darkshore before reporting back.",al={"who wants worn parchment","balthule quest","why collect parchments"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Cult of the Dark Strand?",a="They are a secretive gathering of cultists and warlocks operating out of the ruins of Althalaxx. Even seasoned scouts like Balthule Shadowstrike have never encountered their order before finding these writings.",al={"dark strand cult","who are dark strand","cult of dark strand"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Worn Parchment?",a="These worn parchments are written scraps and scrolls carried by the Dark Strand cultists camped around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. When pieced together, their contents reveal the shadowy dealings and presence of a warlock sect known as the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"what is worn parchment","worn parchment lore","worn parchment info"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Worn Parchment come from, and who made it?",a="The parchments originate from the Dark Strand Fanatics and warlocks who have congregated around the ruins of the Tower of Althalaxx. The cultists carry these written scraps as part of their communications and mysterious rites, though the exact author of each scroll remains unknown.",al={"where does worn parchment come from","who made worn parchment","who wrote worn parchment"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The writings carried by the Dark Strand reveal an organized coven operating in secret on night elf lands, wielding fel and shadow away from the gaze of both the Alliance and Horde.",["race:NightElf"]="The presence of dark spellcasters and demonic corruption near ancient ruins like Althalaxx is a severe desecration of Darkshore's sacred wilderness."},kw={"althalaxx","balthule shadowstrike","dark strand","darkshore","fanatics","worn parchment"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","quest:965","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:warlock"},src={"Worn Parchment","The Tower of Althalaxx (2)"}}
E["npc:alanndarian-nightsong"] = {t="npc",n="Alanndarian Nightsong",z="darkshore",s="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore dedicated to tending to the region's beleaguered fauna. She works alongside travelers to remedy the blights plaguing the local wildlife, particularly the native striders and forest creatures corrupted by dark forces.",h="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore dedicated to tending to the region's...",sec={{t="A Caretaker in Auberdine",b="Situated in the coastal settlement of Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong watches over the fragile ecological balance of Darkshore. As mysterious taints seep into the soil and waters, the creatures of the ancient woods have begun to succumb to sickness and unnatural aggression. Alanndarian acts as a guardian and naturalist, seeking practical remedies to ease their suffering and restore their natural vigor.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Stront and Sick",b="Much of Alanndarian's attention is focused on identifying the root causes of the afflictions spreading through the local fauna. Through careful gathering of botanical reagents and researching the principal water sources of the region, she crafts salves and curative draughts. She enlists wandering adventurers to apply these cures directly to ailing forest creatures, attempting to stave off the spreading corruption before it permanently overtakes Darkshore's wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf naturalist located in the port town of Auberdine in Darkshore. She focuses on caring for afflicted local wildlife and finding herbal cures for the unnatural sicknesses plaguing the coast.",al={"alanndarian","who is alanndarian nightsong","alanndarian nightsong lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Alanndarian Nightsong be found?",a="She makes her home in Auberdine, the primary night elf hub along the foggy coastline of Darkshore.",al={"alanndarian location","where is alanndarian","find alanndarian nightsong"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does she ask adventurers to perform?",a="Alanndarian asks adventurers to track down the sources of sickness tainting Darkshore's creatures, collect vital curative components from the wilderness, and administer remedies directly to ailing animals such as deer and striders.",al={"alanndarian quests","auberdine sick animal quests","what does alanndarian want"},it="purpose"},{q="Is she related to other Nightsongs?",a="Her surname connects her to other prominent night elves of the Nightsong lineage, such as Master Nightsong in Darnassus and Falara Nightsong, though her immediate daily focus remains the stewardship of Darkshore's wilderness.",al={"nightsong family","master nightsong relation","falara nightsong"},it="ties"},{q="Why are the creatures in Darkshore sick?",a="The woodlands and waterways of Darkshore suffer from an creeping corruption seeping through ancient ruins and corrupted elementals, driving native wildlife to madness and wasting sickness.",al={"why are darkshore animals sick","corrupted striders darkshore","darkshore blight"},it="threat"},{q="Can she train tallstrider pets?",a="Though rumor holds she has great knowledge of striders, she does not actively train tamed pets for hunters in the field, keeping her focus instead on wild populations.",al={"tallstrider trainer","strider training auberdine","train my strider"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Alanndarian Nightsong on?",a="She stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the wider Alliance. Stationed in Auberdine, she works directly to protect the wildlife of Darkshore and assists travelers loyal to the Kaldorei cause.",al={"alanndarian nightsong faction","alanndarian nightsong alliance or horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Alanndarian Nightsong want?",a="Alanndarian is dedicated to understanding and reversing the strange afflictions plaguing the local fauna. She seeks aid in uncovering the source of these sicknesses and gathering the necessary ingredients to craft remedies that will heal Darkshore's corrupted creatures.",al={"alanndarian nightsong goal","what is alanndarian trying to do"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Alanndarian Nightsong in Darkshore?",a="She makes her home in the port town of Auberdine to watch over the wilderness of Darkshore. From here, she keeps a close eye on the creeping corruption unsettling the region's wildlife and coordinates efforts to restore balance to the land.",al={"why is alanndarian in auberdine","alanndarian darkshore reason"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alanndarian serves as a vital contact for Alliance travelers landing in Auberdine, helping newcomers understand the delicate state of northern Kalimdor's wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="Her reverence for the forest and dedication to purifying corrupted wildlife reflect the core preservationist ideals of the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find a kindred spirit in Alanndarian's pursuit to identify waterborne taints and physically cure poisoned creatures across Darkshore.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters attuned to beast behaviors assist Alanndarian closely, using their tracking skills to locate wild striders and distressed game."},kw={"alanndarian","auberdine","cure","darkshore","kaldorei","nightsong","strider","wildlife"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6124","quest:6123","quest:6122","quest:2178","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Alanndarian Nightsong"}}
E["npc:archaeologist-flagongut"] = {t="npc",n="Archaeologist Flagongut",z="darkshore",s="Archaeologist Flagongut is a dwarven scholar representing the Explorers' League, stationed within the Deepwater Tavern at Menethil Harbor. Though originally en route to the local dig at the Whelgar Excavation Site, he becomes an important contact for field reports traveling across the sea from Darkshore.",h="Archaeologist Flagongut is a dwarven scholar representing the Explorers' League, stationed within the...",sec={{t="A Scholar in Port",b="Archaeologist Flagongut can be found resting with a mug in hand at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Like many members of Ironforge's Explorers' League, he traveled west across Khaz Modan aiming to assist with discoveries near the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. Despite being far from the high halls of the library, he maintains vital ties with field researchers, helping process lost relics and reports ferried across the Great Sea from remote expeditions.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Field",b="Dwarven curiosity is rarely confined to one continent, and Flagongut finds himself sorting through the chaotic field research of absent-minded colleagues operating on the shores of Kalimdor. When relics or notes recovered from the excavation sites of Darkshore arrive at the harbor, Flagongut ensures the findings are cataloged and delivered onward to the senior league leadership back in Ironforge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Flagongut is a dwarven researcher from the Explorers' League. He is stationed in Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern, where he reviews excavation field work and communicates with dig sites.",al={"who is flagongut","flagongut npc","archaeologist flagongut lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Flagongut at the Deepwater Tavern?",a="He originally arrived at Menethil Harbor to reach the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. While in port, he uses the tavern as a base to handle mail, incoming artifacts, and correspondence from abroad.",al={"why is flagongut in menethil","flagongut location","what is flagongut doing here"},it="why_here"},{q="How is Flagongut connected to Darkshore?",a="Flagongut serves as the Wetlands contact for the long-running research chain started by Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore. Adventurers crossing from Auberdine to Menethil bring Remtravel's findings directly to Flagongut to be passed along to Ironforge.",al={"flagongut darkshore connection","why darkshore quest in wetlands"},it="ties"},{q="What organization does he belong to?",a="He belongs to the Explorers' League, King Magni Bronzebeard's royal society dedicated to uncovering the ancient origins, relics, and history of the dwarven race across Azeroth.",al={"flagongut faction","flagongut explorers league"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Archaeologist Flagongut on?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is aligned with Ironforge and the Alliance. As an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League, his loyalties lie with his kin and their scholarly mission to excavate and catalog ancient relics across the known world.",al={"flagongut faction","who does flagongut work for","flagongut allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Archaeologist Flagongut want?",a="Flagongut originally journeyed through Menethil Harbor to reach the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. He seeks information and assistance regarding his fellow League member, Prospector Remtravel, whose ongoing archaeological troubles in distant Darkshore require urgent reports and delivery back home.",al={"flagongut goal","what does flagongut need","why talk to flagongut"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Flagongut represents the far-reaching ambitions of the Explorers' League, proving that even a tavern by the sea can serve as an outpost for piecing together Titan secrets.",["faction:Alliance"]="Flagongut acts as a logistical bridge between the night elf lands of Darkshore and the eastern Alliance strongholds of Khaz Modan."},kw={"archaeologist","deepwater tavern","explorers' league","flagongut","menethil harbor","remtravel","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern","topic:explorers-league","quest:729","zone:wetlands","zone:darkshore","topic:dwarf"},src={"Archaeologist Flagongut"}}
E["npc:archaeologist-hollee"] = {t="npc",n="Archaeologist Hollee",z="darkshore",s="Archaeologist Hollee is a dwarven researcher stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine. Working on behalf of dwarven excavation interests, she keeps tabs on archaeological findings and surveys throughout the ancient, fog-shrouded wilderness of Darkshore. She frequently coordinates with prospectors scouring the region for relics and geological anomalies.",h="Archaeologist Hollee is a dwarven researcher stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Scholar in Kaldorei Lands",b="While Darkshore is predominantly guarded and settled by the night elves, the presence of dwarven scholars like Archaeologist Hollee reflects Ironforge's growing curiosity about Kalimdor. The Explorers' League sends representatives far across the seas to uncover traces of ancient history, and Darkshore's ruins offer tempting ground for study. Hollee makes her temporary base out of Auberdine, acting as a regional contact for wandering surveyors and expedition teams.",sp=0},{t="Keeping Tabs on Remtravel",b="A major part of Hollee's day-to-day work involves tracking her fellow field researchers, particularly the scatterbrained Prospector Remtravel. Entrusted with significant surveying tasks across the wild coast, Remtravel often wanders far afield without reporting back on schedule. Hollee frequently enlists travelers passing through Auberdine to track him down, recover missing survey data, and ensure that field research does not fall prey to the local wildlife or encroaching threats.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Archaeologist Hollee?",a="Archaeologist Hollee is a dwarf stationed in Auberdine in Darkshore. She conducts and oversees regional field research on behalf of dwarven archaeological efforts on the western continent.",al={"who is hollee","hollee darkshore","dwarf in auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Hollee be found?",a="She is located in the coastal port town of Auberdine, situated on the western coast of Darkshore.",al={"hollee location","where is archaeologist hollee"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are dwarves conducting research in Darkshore?",a="Following the third war and the deepening alliance between Ironforge and the night elves, dwarven researchers have traveled to Kalimdor to study ancient relics, geological formations, and long-buried history that might shed light on their own ancestry.",al={"why are dwarves in darkshore","ironforge in kalimdor"},it="why_here"},{q="What trouble does she need help with?",a="Hollee is primarily concerned with Prospector Remtravel, an absent-minded surveyor who wandered off into the southern reaches of Darkshore and failed to report back with his findings.",al={"hollee quests","absent minded prospector quest"},it="wants"},{q="What is the relationship between Hollee and Prospector Remtravel?",a="They are colleagues working on the same excavation and survey efforts in Darkshore. While Remtravel does the practical fieldwork out among the ruins, Hollee coordinates reports and liaises with travelers from Auberdine.",al={"who is remtravel","remtravel and hollee"},it="ties"},{q="Does Hollee belong to the Explorers' League?",a="She represents dwarven archaeological and prospecting expeditions allied with Ironforge, which are typically organized under the aegis of the Explorers' League operating out of the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"explorers league hollee","hollee faction"},it="side"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a compatriot so far across the sea in the misty woods of Darkshore is a reminder of Ironforge's boundless thirst for uncovering ancient history.",["faction:Alliance"]="Hollee represents the cooperation between the Eastern Kingdoms and the night elves, utilizing Auberdine as a base to study Kalimdor's distant past."},kw={"archaeologist hollee","auberdine","darkshore","explorers league","ironforge","prospector remtravel","the absent minded prospector","trouble in darkshore"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:729","quest:730","topic:dwarf"},src={"Archaeologist Hollee"}}
E["npc:asterion"] = {t="npc",n="Asterion",z="darkshore",s="Asterion is an ancient Highborne spirit bound to the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Once the trusted second to governor Athrikus Narassin ten millennia ago, he was mysteriously imprisoned in a magical moonstone seal that held him through mortal life and into the afterlife. Today, his specter remains shackled to the ruined shrine, surrounded by demonic beasts and dreaming of liberation.",h="Asterion is an ancient Highborne spirit bound to the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Servant of Ancient Splendor",b="Before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister cities blessed by Queen Azshara herself. Azshara appointed Athrikus Narassin to govern the twin settlements, and Asterion served as his right hand. Respected for both his physical combat prowess and his command of arcane sorcery, Asterion lived among the people of Bashal'Aran while frequently traveling between the sister cities to manage the needs of their citizens.",sp=0},{t="The Moonstone Prison",b="For reasons lost to time, Asterion fell out of favor with his master. Athrikus fashioned a powerful moonstone seal, forging an inescapable magical cage to confine Asterion within Bashal'Aran. The imprisonment stretched through centuries of agonizing confinement; worse still, when Asterion finally perished, he discovered death offered no release. His spirit remained bound to the ruined shrine, left behind when the world cracked open and demons overran the ancient settlement.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance from the Grave",b="Though vile satyrs and grells roam the ruins of Bashal'Aran feeding on residual arcane power, they shun the shrine where Asterion's ghost lingers. If an Alliance adventurer retrieves the moonstone seal from the satyrs and shatters it in Ameth'Aran, Asterion's spectral chains finally break. Yet freedom does not bring him peace; sensing that Athrikus Narassin still endures, the ancient mage turns his thoughts from ten thousand years of despair toward vengeance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient Highborne ghost found at the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Before the Sundering, he was an accomplished mage and the second-in-command to governor Athrikus Narassin.",al={"asterion lore","who is the ghost in bashal'aran","ghost elf darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Asterion imprisoned?",a="Athrikus Narassin bound Asterion using a magical moonstone seal. The exact reasons for their falling out remain unknown, but the sorcery was so potent that even Asterion's death failed to break the enchantment, trapping his ghost for millennia.",al={"why is asterion trapped","asterion prison","why did athrikus trap asterion"},it="why_here"},{q="Why don't the satyrs in Bashal'Aran attack him?",a="While the satyrs and grells in the ruins feast on the lingering arcane energies of Bashal'Aran, they keep their distance from the shrine where Asterion is bound. They held possession of the moonstone seal that anchors his captivity rather than meddling directly with his spirit.",al={"do satyrs attack asterion","why demons leave asterion alone"}},{q="Where did Asterion live in life?",a="Asterion made his home among the people of Bashal'Aran, traveling frequently south to its twin city of Ameth'Aran to tend to civic affairs under the authority of Queen Azshara's governor.",al={"asterion home","where was asterion from"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after you free him?",a="Once his seal is shattered in Ameth'Aran, Asterion is finally released from his agonizing spectral prison. However, instead of passing peacefully into the afterlife, he realizes that his old tormentor Athrikus still lives and turns his focus toward revenge.",al={"what happens to asterion","does asterion move on","asterion vengeance"},sp=1},{q="Is Asterion hostile to modern night elves?",a="No. Despite being an ancient Highborne from Queen Azshara's court, Asterion is peaceful toward Alliance travelers and seeks their assistance in breaking his ancient magical bondage.",al={"is asterion friendly","asterion alliance"},it="side"},{q="What does Asterion want?",a="Asterion seeks release from the ancient magical prison that has trapped his spirit for ten thousand years. Athrikus Narassin bound him to Bashal'Aran using a moonstone seal, leaving Asterion to suffer even beyond physical death. He desperately needs you to recover this seal from the satyrs and shatter it in Ameth'Aran, ending his long torment and allowing his thoughts to turn toward retribution against his former master.",al={"asterion goal","what does asterion need","asterion motives"},sp=1,it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Asterion tied to?",a="In ancient times, Asterion served directly under Athrikus Narassin, the Highborne lord appointed by Queen Azshara to govern Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. As second-in-command, Asterion tended to the needs of both settlements. Despite his loyal service, Athrikus used his dark craft to bind Asterion in an arcane moonstone prison for reasons lost to history, turning their ancient bond into a legacy of betrayal.",al={"asterion master","who imprisoned asterion","athrikus narassin asterion"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Asterion is a tragic relic from before the Sundering, showing the cruel internal politics that consumed the Highborne even before Azshara invited the Burning Legion into their lands.",["class:Mage"]="In life, Asterion was celebrated for his mastery of the arcane alongside his prowess in physical combat, making him an intriguing study in early Kaldorei spellcraft.",["faction:Alliance"]="Asterion is one of the rare Highborne spirits willing to trust and aid Alliance adventurers, seeking their help to break his ten-thousand-year-old prison."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus","bashal'aran","darkshore","highborne","moonstone","narassin","satyr"},rel={"quest:954","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","zone:azshara"},src={"Asterion"}}
E["npc:balthule-shadowstrike"] = {t="npc",n="Balthule Shadowstrike",z="darkshore",s="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore near the Tower of Althalaxx. Serving as a forward agent for Delgren the Purifier, he keeps watch over the sinister cultists and dark practitioners occupying the ancient elven ruins. Adventurers traveling along the northern coast are often directed to him to assist in unravelling and disrupting the dark rituals underway at the tower.",h="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore near the Tower of Althalaxx.",sec={{t="A Scout in the Shadows",b="Perched in the wilderness just west of the Tower of Althalaxx, Balthule Shadowstrike maintains a lonely and perilous vigil. Darkshore's northern reaches are thick with restless spirits and shadowed ruins, but the activity around the tower poses a particularly acute threat. Balthule operates under the direction of Delgren the Purifier, observing the movements of dark casters who have crept into the ancient Highborne remnants.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Cult",b="The sorcerers and cultists who have claimed the Tower of Althalaxx are engaged in dark, forbidden magic, harvesting artifacts and souls from the surrounding ruins. Balthule relies on traveling Alliance champions to venture into the tower grounds, strike down the cultist leadership, and recover parchment and talismans that reveal the true scope of their summoning efforts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore. He acts as an advance scout and agent working in concert with Delgren the Purifier to monitor evil cultist activities in the area.",al={"who is balthule","balthule role","balthule shadowstrike npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Balthule Shadowstrike located?",a="He is stationed in northern Darkshore, positioned just west of the ominous Tower of Althalaxx near the coastline.",al={"where is balthule","balthule location","find balthule shadowstrike"},gp=true},{q="What is his mission at the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="He was sent to spy upon the dark spellcasters and cultists who have taken up residence in the Tower of Althalaxx, helping to gather intelligence and coordinate strikes to disrupt their corrupt rituals.",al={"why is balthule here","what does balthule want","althalaxx quest guy"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Argent Dawn paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale who coordinates the campaign against the dark forces plaguing northern Darkshore. Balthule serves as his forward eyes and ears.",al={"who is delgren","balthule superior","delgren connection"},it="ties"},{q="What kind of enemies occupy the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The tower and its surrounding grounds are overrun by dark cultists, sorcerers, and summoned demonic or shadowy minions bent on using ancient Highborne power for sinister purposes.",al={"who is in the tower","althalaxx enemies","tower of althalaxx cultists"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the Alliance interested in these ruins?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven structure. The presence of foul sorcery and demonic activity so close to elven lands represents a direct threat to the safety of Darkshore and the night elves of Darnassus.",al={"why care about the tower","alliance darkshore presence"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Balthule Shadowstrike on?",a="Balthule serves the Alliance and his fellow night elves. He works directly as a scout and operative for Delgren the Purifier, keeping watch over threats rising in northern Darkshore.",al={"balthule faction","who does balthule serve","is balthule alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Balthule Shadowstrike want?",a="Balthule wants to uncover the dark rituals taking place within the Tower of Althalaxx. By spying on the cultists holding the ruin, he seeks to gather enough intelligence for Delgren the Purifier to cleanse the corruption taking root along the coast.",al={"what does balthule want","balthule goal","what is balthule trying to do"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Balthule Shadowstrike here?",a="Delgren the Purifier dispatched Balthule to keep vigil outside the Tower of Althalaxx. Perched in hiding nearby, his duty is to observe the hostile occupants and enlist capable travelers to disrupt their dark schemes.",al={"why is balthule in darkshore","why is balthule here","what brought balthule here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the desecration of ancient Kalimdor ruins by foul cultists is an outrage that Balthule seeks to avenge before the corruption spreads further into their lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Balthule serves as an important forward contact for Alliance members sent north from Auberdine to excise the dark cultists operating around the Tower of Althalaxx.",["class:Rogue"]="Operating deep in hostile territory right under the noses of dangerous spellcasters, Balthule exemplifies the patience and vigilance of a true elven scout."},kw={"althalaxx","balthule","cultists","darkshore","delgren","mathystra","purifier","scout","shadowstrike"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","npc:delgren-the-purifier","quest:965","zone:darkshore","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","topic:night-elf","topic:highborne"},src={"Balthule Shadowstrike"}}
E["npc:barithras-moonshade"] = {t="npc",n="Barithras Moonshade",z="darkshore",s="Barithras Moonshade is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore. Positioned within the coastal settlement, he seeks the help of adventurers willing to explore the shadowy wilderness and gather rare subterranean flora.",h="Barithras Moonshade is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="Resident of Auberdine",b="Standing watch within the village of Auberdine, Barithras Moonshade contributes to the night elves' efforts to study and manage the unsettled land of Darkshore. He directs travelers to venture into nearby subterranean caverns to harvest specific fungi, such as death cap mushrooms, for study and use.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Ancients",b="Beyond local flora, Barithras assists in guiding capable adventurers southward to make contact with Onu, one of the venerable ancients striving to heal Darkshore's tainted soil and soothe its restless natural spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Barithras Moonshade?",a="Barithras Moonshade is a night elf resident found in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore. He tasks adventurers with investigating local flora and contacting guardians in the region.",al={"who is barithras","barithras moonshade","who is this night elf"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Barithras Moonshade?",a="He can be found standing in the port settlement of Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore.",al={"barithras location","where is barithras","barithras moonshade location"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does Barithras give?",a="Barithras tasks travelers with entering nearby caverns to harvest mushrooms, such as the dangerous death cap, and later points adventurers southward to meet with the ancient Onu.",al={"barithras quests","what quests does barithras give","cave mushrooms quest"},gp=true},{q="Is Barithras related to the other Moonshades?",a="Several other night elves carry the Moonshade surname across Kalimdor, including Sentinels and Keepers, suggesting a shared lineage among their people.",al={"moonshade family","other moonshades","is barithras related to sentinel moonshade"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Barithras Moonshade on?",a="Barithras Moonshade stands firmly with the night elves of Auberdine and the wider Alliance. Stationed in Darkshore, he looks out for the settlement's well-being and aids travelers who work to protect the surrounding wilderness.",al={"barithras moonshade faction","who does barithras serve","barithras alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Barithras Moonshade want?",a="Barithras seeks assistance with local matters around Darkshore, dispatching capable adventurers to gather resources such as cave mushrooms and directing them onward to consult with ancient allies like Onu in the groves to the south.",al={"barithras moonshade goal","what does barithras need","barithras moonshade quests"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Barithras helps his kin in Auberdine safeguard Darkshore by monitoring its flora and maintaining ties with ancient forest guardians like Onu.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Those attuned to plant life will appreciate Barithras's interest in Darkshore's peculiar cavern-dwelling fungi."},kw={"auberdine","barithras","cave mushrooms","darkshore","death cap","moonshade","onu"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:947","topic:night-elf"},src={"Barithras Moonshade"}}
E["npc:cerellean-whiteclaw"] = {t="npc",n="Cerellean Whiteclaw",z="darkshore",s="Cerellean Whiteclaw is a night elf resting near the docks and inn of Auberdine in Darkshore. Haunted by the memory of his lost love from the ancient Sundering, he struggles to lay her restless spirit to peace.",h="Cerellean Whiteclaw is a night elf resting near the docks and inn of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Love Torn asunder",b="Ten thousand years ago, prior to the War of the Ancients, Cerellean Whiteclaw shared his life with Anaya Dawnrunner. When the demonic invasion tore ancient Kalimdor apart, Anaya perished in the destruction of her city, Ameth'Aran. Stricken with grief, Cerellean followed Malfurion Stormrage into the long druidic slumber, yet the Emerald Dream offered him little respite from her memory. Upon awakening millennia later, he wandered Darkshore in a grief-stricken haze, only to discover that Anaya's ghost remained bound to the very stones where she fell.",sp=0},{t="A Plea for Release",b="Though he yearns to grant Anaya peace, Cerellean cannot bear the sorrow of striking down her tormented shade himself. He appeals to passing travelers to venture south into the haunted ruins of Ameth'Aran, put her spirit to rest, and recover her pendant. Once freed, Anaya's shade briefly visits Cerellean on the docks of Auberdine, reassuring him of her enduring love and promising that they will one day be reunited in the afterlife.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cerellean Whiteclaw?",a="Cerellean Whiteclaw is an ancient night elf residing near the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore. He mourns his lost love, Anaya Dawnrunner, who perished during the War of the Ancients ten millennia ago.",al={"who is cerellean","cerellean whiteclaw","auberdine docks elf"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner was Cerellean's beloved who lived in the ancient city of Ameth'Aran. She was killed during the War of the Ancients when the city fell to ruin, and her tortured spirit lingered among the wreckage for thousands of years.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","cerellean's love","cerellean lover"},it="ties"},{q="Why doesn't Cerellean lay Anaya's spirit to rest himself?",a="Cerellean remains so deeply attached and heartbroken that he lacks the emotional strength to confront and destroy her ghostly form himself. He relies on sympathetic travelers to deliver her final release.",al={"why doesn't cerellean fight anaya","why need adventurer"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the ruins of Ameth'Aran?",a="The ruins of Ameth'Aran lie in southern Darkshore, east of the main road. The area is haunted by ghosts of ancient kaldorei who perished during the Great Sundering.",al={"where is ameth'aran","anaya location","where is anaya"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Cerellean Whiteclaw on?",a="Cerellean is a kaldorei citizen aligned with the night elves and the Alliance. He stands peacefully in Auberdine, consumed by his personal grief rather than political or military ambition, seeking help from any traveler willing to aid him.",al={"cerellean whiteclaw faction","who does cerellean serve","cerellean alliance or horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Cerellean Whiteclaw want?",a="Cerellean wants to grant eternal peace to the spirit of his lost love, Anaya Dawnrunner. Tormented by the sight of her ghost bound to the ruins of Ameth'Aran, he seeks someone with the strength to destroy her spectral form and return her pendant to him, freeing her from her ancient agony.",al={"cerellean goal","what does cerellean need","cerellean whiteclaw quest goal"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Cerellean Whiteclaw in Darkshore?",a="After awakening from millennia in the Emerald Dream alongside Malfurion Stormrage, Cerellean wandered Kalimdor in a grief-stricken daze. His sorrow drew him back toward the ruins of Ameth'Aran, where Anaya perished, leaving him lingering near the docks of Auberdine, unable to move on.",al={"why is cerellean in auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw location reason","why is cerellean here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Cerellean's tragic story reflects the deep, enduring scars left upon the kaldorei by the War of the Ancients and the Great Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="Like many druids, Cerellean entered the long slumber alongside Malfurion Stormrage, though the Emerald Dream proved unable to wash away his earthly heartbreak."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","ghost","sundering"},rel={"quest:963","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:night-elf"},src={"Cerellean Whiteclaw"}}
E["npc:delgren-the-purifier"] = {t="npc",n="Delgren the Purifier",z="darkshore",s="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post on the northern edge of Ashenvale. Operating alongside comrades Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, he aids the night elves in cleansing demonic and shadow magic threatening the frontier, with a particular focus on the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand.",h="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post on the northern edge of Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Crusader on the Kaldorei Frontier",b="Human paladins are a rare sight deep within the ancient forests of Kalimdor, but Delgren the Purifier arrived with a mission. Affiliated with the Argent Dawn, Delgren traveled west with a cadre of holy warriors determined to assist the Alliance's new night elf allies against the lingering evils of demons and undead remnants from the Third War. Stationed near the border of Darkshore and Ashenvale, he maintains a watchful vigil over travelers passing south from Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Dark Strand",b="Delgren's immediate crusade pits him directly against the Cult of the Dark Strand, a malevolent cabal operating around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Teaming with the scout Balthule Shadowstrike, Delgren orchestrates strikes into the cult's territory, investigating their dark rituals and sending adventurers to strike down cultists, shatter their summoning focuses, and root out corrupt warlocks who dare traffic with demonic shadow.",sp=1},{t="An Unorthodox Mind",b="Despite his fierce devotion to the Holy Light and zealous nickname, Delgren possesses an unusual perspective on Kalimdor's tangled politics. Much to the annoyance and disdain of his conservative superiors, he took the time to learn Orcish. This rare linguistic skill hints at an unconventional mind—one that seeks to understand the enemies and neighbors sharing this untamed continent rather than relying solely on blind dogma.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post along the road in northern Ashenvale. As an agent of the Argent Dawn, he assists the night elves in defending their lands from demonic corruption, cultists, and lingering shadows left in the wake of the Legion's invasion.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","who is the paladin at maestras post"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Delgren?",a="Delgren stands at Maestra's Post, a small night elven outpost in northwestern Ashenvale just south of the border trail leading into Darkshore.",al={"where is delgren","delgren location","delgren coordinates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is a human paladin all the way out in Ashenvale?",a="Delgren journeyed west with a company of Argent Dawn paladins to offer aid to the Alliance's night elven allies. Their purpose is to help purge demonic incursions, undead remnants, and dark cults that threaten northern Kalimdor.",al={"why is delgren in ashenvale","why are there humans in ashenvale","delgren mission"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Delgren's connection to the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="Delgren and his companions monitor the corrupt activities radiating from the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He directs adventurers to investigate the ruin, hunt the Cult of the Dark Strand, and dismantle their dark summoning practices.",al={"delgren althalaxx","tower of althalaxx quests","cult of the dark strand"},it="purpose"},{q="Why did Delgren learn Orcish?",a="Delgren learned Orcish to better comprehend the situation and inhabitants of Kalimdor, a decision that earned him notable disapproval from his superiors within the order.",al={"delgren speaks orcish","does delgren speak orcish","delgren orc language"},it="motive"},{q="Who does Delgren work with at Maestra's Post?",a="He operates alongside Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, working as a coordinated unit to monitor border threats, handle logistics, and purge shadow cultists along the Ashenvale frontier.",al={"delgren companions","who is at maestras post"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Delgren the Purifier on?",a="Delgren is a human paladin aligned with the Argent Dawn and loyal to the Alliance. He and his fellow paladins traveled across the sea specifically to aid their night elf allies in purifying Kalimdor of lingering evils.",al={"delgren faction","delgren alliance or horde","who does delgren serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Delgren the Purifier want?",a="Delgren seeks to cleanse the ancient lands of Ashenvale and Darkshore of demonic taint and undead corruption. His primary focus is dismantling the Cult of the Dark Strand and ending their dark rituals around the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"delgren goal","what is delgren doing","delgren mission"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Delgren represents the far reach of the Holy Light on Kalimdor, demonstrating how paladins adapt their crusade against demons and dark magic far beyond the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers heading south from Darkshore, Delgren and his companions provide a reassuring military foothold along the dangerous Ashenvale road.",["race:NightElf"]="Though traditional kaldorei are often skeptical of foreign creeds, Delgren's company has earned trust through their practical crusade against the demonic cults troubling ancient ruins."},kw={"althalaxx","argent dawn","ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","cult of the dark strand","delgren","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","npc:feero-ironhand","quest:965","topic:argent-dawn","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},src={"Delgren the Purifier"}}
E["npc:elder-starweave"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Starweave",z="darkshore",s="Elder Starweave is an ancestral night elf spirit honored during the Lunar Festival. Found resting at the port town of Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore, she shares the wisdom of ancient ages with passing pilgrims.",h="Elder Starweave is an ancestral night elf spirit honored during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Auberdine",b="Appearing as an ethereal shade among the coastal dwellings of Auberdine, Elder Starweave is one of the revered ancestors honored by the Cenarion Circle and the peoples of Kalimdor. While many travelers rush through the port on their way inland or across the sea, those who pause before her receive an ancestral blessing. Starweave speaks of celestial movements, observing that the stars of the modern era trace unfamiliar paths that serve as beacons of hope and fortitude for future generations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Starweave?",a="Elder Starweave is a night elf ancestral spirit who appears in Auberdine during the Lunar Festival to offer greetings, ancient wisdom, and Coins of Ancestry to travelers.",al={"elder starweave lore","who is starweave","starweave the elder"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Elder Starweave be found?",a="She can be found lingering near the settlement of Auberdine along the shoreline of Darkshore.",al={"where is elder starweave","elder starweave location","starweave spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does she appear as a spirit?",a="She is an honored ancestor brought forth during the Lunar Festival, appearing in spiritual form so the living may pay respects to those who shaped the night elves' distant past.",al={"why is starweave a ghost","is starweave dead","why ghost"},it="origin"},{q="Can Horde players speak to her?",a="Yes. Ancestral elders honored during the Lunar Festival welcome travelers of all affiliations, though Horde adventurers must navigate the Alliance-friendly port of Auberdine with caution.",al={"can horde visit starweave","horde elder starweave"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Starweave on?",a="Elder Starweave is aligned with the night elves and the Alliance. As an honored ancestral elder resting in Darkshore, she watches over her people and offers her celestial blessings and wisdom to travelers loyal to the Alliance who seek her out.",al={"is elder starweave alliance","elder starweave faction","who does elder starweave serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Elder Starweave here in Darkshore?",a="Elder Starweave lingers in Darkshore as an ancestral spirit to observe the world and guide younger generations. She watches the shifting constellations, reading the signs of the heavens as beacons of hope and strength for the trials of the coming ages.",al={"why is elder starweave in darkshore","why is starweave here","elder starweave purpose"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Meeting Elder Starweave in Darkshore connects kaldorei adventurers directly to their long lineage of forebears who looked to Elune and the stars through ancient cataclysms.",["class:Druid"]="Druids observing the festival find Starweave's celestial reflections aligned with the Cenarion teachings of renewal, memory, and harmony with the natural world."},kw={"ancestor","auberdine","coin of ancestry","darkshore","elder starweave","lunar festival","starweave"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:night-elf","quest:8721"},src={"Elder Starweave"}}
E["npc:gelkak-gyromast"] = {t="npc",n="Gelkak Gyromast",z="darkshore",s="Gelkak Gyromast is a gnome who talks like a pirate captain, found stranded along the foggy shoreline of Mist's Edge in northern Darkshore. His ship was sunk offshore by threshadons, and he wants his mechanical first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, back in working order.",h="Gelkak Gyromast is a gnome who talks like a pirate captain, found stranded along the foggy shoreline of...",sec={{t="Castaway on Mist's Edge",b="Perched on the desolate northern coast of Darkshore just west of the ancient Ruins of Mathystra, Gelkak Gyromast represents a peculiar sight among the gloomy night elven shores. Talking like an old sea dog, the self-styled captain lost his ship to the threshadons just offshore. When he washed up on the misty sands, the key to his mechanical first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, broke on the rocks, and its pieces were carried off by the crawlers, foreststriders and murlocs rummaging through the wreckage.",sp=0},{t="The Threshwackonator Malfunction",b="Once adventurers recover the key, Gyromast sends them to switch on his first mate and lead it back to him, eager to set it loose on the murlocs and beasts of the coast. The Threshwackonator 4100 follows obediently, only to malfunction and turn hostile the moment it reaches its captain, leaving the adventurers to destroy it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is an eccentric gnome who talks like a pirate captain, stranded on the northern beach of Darkshore known as Mist's Edge, just west of the Ruins of Mathystra.",al={"gelkak","who is gelkak","gyromast"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gelkak stranded in Darkshore?",a="His ship was sunk just offshore by threshadons, and he washed up on the desolate northern coast with the broken key to his mechanical first mate.",al={"why is gelkak here","gelkak darkshore"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Threshwackonator 4100?",a="The Threshwackonator 4100 is Gelkak's mechanical creation and self-proclaimed first mate. He wants it back in working order so it can take revenge on the murlocs and beasts of the coast.",al={"threshwackonator","gelkak machine","robot"}},{q="What help does Gelkak need from travelers?",a="Gelkak asks capable adventurers to recover the three pieces of his broken key from the crawlers, foreststriders and murlocs of the coast, then use it to start the Threshwackonator 4100 and lead it back to him.",al={"gelkak quests","gyromast quests"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Gelkak Gyromast on?",a="Gelkak is a gnome aligned with the Alliance, though out here on the lonely strands of Darkshore he acts strictly on his own behalf. Stranded far from any major settlement, he welcomes any friendly Alliance traveler willing to lend a hand with his mechanical mishaps.",al={"gelkak gyromast faction","is gelkak alliance","who does gelkak serve"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Seeing a fellow gnome stranded on the edge of Kalimdor is a stark reminder of how far from home a gnome's adventures can carry him.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gelkak's predicament is a classic tale of a gnome far from home, pinning his hopes of revenge on a device as impressive as the Threshwackonator 4100."},kw={"darkshore","gelkak gyromast","gnome inventor","mathystra","mist's edge","threshwackonator 4100"},rel={"subzone:mist-s-edge","quest:2098","quest:2078","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","zone:darkshore","topic:gnome"},src={"Gelkak Gyromast"}}
E["npc:gorbold-steelhand"] = {t="npc",n="Gorbold Steelhand",z="darkshore",s="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarven merchant stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore. Operating far from the snowy halls of Khaz Modan, he supplies travelers, crafters, and local night elves with general goods and trade supplies.",h="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarven merchant stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Trader in Kalimdor",b="While most of Kalimdor's northern reaches are populated by the secretive night elves, Alliance outposts like Auberdine rely on merchants from across the Great Sea to keep trade moving. Gorbold Steelhand represents the far-reaching presence of Ironforge commerce in the region. Working alongside the kaldorei, he sells trade goods, reagents, crafting sundries, and tools to adventurers preparing to explore the treacherous shores and forests of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Maritime Ventures",b="Beyond stocking daily goods, Gorbold keeps a keen eye on the perilous coastal waters off Auberdine. Darkshore's reef-strewn waters are notorious for swallowing Alliance vessels, and merchants like Gorbold have a direct interest in the cargo lost beneath the waves. Travelers willing to dive into the deep ocean can often find him interested in the salvage and lost logs scattered across sunken wrecks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gorbold Steelhand?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarven general trade merchant based in the coastal port of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"gorbold","who is gorbold steelhand","dwarf in auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="What does Gorbold Steelhand sell?",a="He carries general trade supplies, crafting ingredients, gathering tools, and reagents such as vials and thread used by tradesfolk passing through Auberdine.",al={"what does gorbold sell","gorbold trade goods","gorbold vendor list"},gp=true},{q="Why is an Ironforge dwarf living in Darkshore?",a="Auberdine serves as a key Alliance transit hub connecting Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms. Dwarves frequently travel here for commerce, exploration, and supporting allied night elf operations.",al={"why is a dwarf here","why is gorbold in darkshore","ironforge in auberdine"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Gorbold offer any quests?",a="Yes, he directs adventurers toward sunken wreckage off the coast of Darkshore in the quest 'Deep Ocean, Vast Sea' to recover lost ship cargo.",al={"gorbold quest","deep ocean vast sea quest giver"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gorbold Steelhand on?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is firmly allied with the Alliance. As an Ironforge dwarf doing business in the night elf haven of Auberdine, he maintains friendly relations with local kaldorei and welcomes travelers loyal to the Alliance who pass through Darkshore.",al={"gorbold steelhand faction","is gorbold steelhand alliance","gorbold allegiance"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a familiar Ironforge face like Gorbold in the misty, nocturnal environment of Darkshore provides dwarven travelers a welcome reminder of home.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gorbold illustrates the practical cooperation between the eastern races of the Alliance and the night elves, keeping trade flowing across the Great Sea."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","deep ocean vast sea","gorbold","ironforge","merchant","steelhand","vendor"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:982","topic:dwarf"},src={"Gorbold Steelhand"}}
E["npc:gubber-blump"] = {t="npc",n="Gubber Blump",z="darkshore",s="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fisherman and trainer stationed along the shores of Auberdine in Darkshore. Positioned on the sands between the docks and the flight master, he is an enthusiastic lover of the angling craft and seafood, particularly fresh crab meat.",h="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fisherman and trainer stationed along the shores of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="The Angler of Auberdine",b="While most dwarves find comfort beneath stone or beside a roaring forge, Gubber Blump prefers the misty coastline of Darkshore. Stationed along the beach at Auberdine, between the flight master and the ferry pier, Gubber teaches the art of fishing and sells basic angling gear to passing travelers. He holds a deep culinary appreciation for crab meat, though he frequently relies on adventurers to help secure his catches along the dangerous coast, as well as reclaim sentimental family fishing tackle.",sp=0},{t="Family Ties and Ocean Favors",b="Gubber is known to share candid stories about his family, notably his cousin Graun Blump, whom he insists possesses both a beard and an unusual odor. Travelers who lend a hand with his coastal errands—whether hauling in crawler legs or retrieving his family pole—often earn a thoughtful handwritten letter of thanks from Gubber, usually accompanied by a shiny fishing lure to encourage their future casts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gubber Blump?",a="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fishing trainer and vendor located on the beach in Auberdine, situated right between the village docks and the hippogryph master.",al={"who is gubber blump","gubber blump npc","where is gubber blump"},it="identity"},{q="What does Gubber Blump teach or sell?",a="He trains novices in the fishing profession and stocks basic gear for prospective anglers, including standard fishing poles and shiny baubles.",al={"what does gubber sell","gubber blump trainer","darkshore fishing trainer"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does Gubber Blump give out?",a="Gubber asks travelers to recover his lost family fishing pole and gather fine crab meat from the coast in quests such as 'The Family and the Fishing Pole' and 'Fruit of the Sea'.",al={"gubber blump quests","fruit of the sea","the family and the fishing pole"},gp=true},{q="Who is Graun Blump?",a="Graun Blump is Gubber's dwarven cousin. Gubber candidly remarks that she sports a notable beard and has a rather unusual smell.",al={"graun blump","gubber blump cousin"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Gubber Blump on?",a="Gubber Blump is an Alliance-aligned dwarf stationed peacefully alongside the night elves of Auberdine. While he mostly minds his own business and focuses on his craft, he openly welcomes Alliance travelers to trade, train, and share in coastal catches.",al={"is gubber blump alliance","gubber blump faction","who does gubber blump serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Gubber Blump want?",a="Gubber is passionate about fishing and culinary delicacies, holding a particular fondness for fresh crab meat harvested from the local waters. Above all, he wants to enjoy the bounties of the sea, recover his family's lost tackle, and teach fellow anglers the finer points of the trade.",al={"what is gubber blumps goal","what does gubber blump need","gubber blump motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Gubber Blump in Darkshore?",a="Gubber has made his home along the shoreline of Auberdine, nestled between the docks and the flight master. The misty coast provides ample fishing grounds and a steady harvest of reef crabs, making it an ideal post for a dwarven angler looking to fish in peace.",al={"why is gubber blump here","why is a dwarf in darkshore","why is gubber in auberdine"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gubber is passionate about coastal fare, particularly fresh reef crawler meat, making him a kindred spirit to cooks seeking ingredients from Darkshore's waters.",["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a dwarf happily settled on a foggy Kalimdor shoreline rather than in Khaz Modan is an uncommon sight, though his forthright banter about kin proves he has not lost his Ironforge roots."},kw={"auberdine","blump","darkshore","fishing","graun blump","gubber","reef crawler","shiny bauble"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:1141","quest:1138","topic:dwarf"},src={"Gubber Blump"}}
E["npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde"] = {t="npc",n="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",z="darkshore",s="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf residing in the coastal port of Auberdine. Stationed along the misty Darkshore coast, she watches the tides and directs travelers to investigate the strange remains washing ashore. Her concerns center on the mysterious sea creatures and massive turtles whose carcasses have begun littering the northern beaches.",h="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf residing in the coastal port of Auberdine.",sec={{t="Watcher of the Shifting Sands",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde makes her home in Auberdine, the bustling seaside haven of Darkshore. While many in town concern themselves with the forest or shipping across the Veiled Sea, Gwennyth keeps her gaze firmly on the coastline. The tides have recently turned grim, depositing the remains of colossal marine life onto the surf. To understand what is happening in the waters offshore, she relies on willing adventurers to scour the sands, retrieve skeletal samples, and bring back answers.",sp=0},{t="The Stranded Giants",b="The beaches north and south of Auberdine have seen an alarming influx of beached sea creatures and ancient sea turtles. Rather than letting their deaths go unnoticed, Gwennyth tasks travelers with inspecting these fallen titans. By studying the bones and discovering what drove these beasts ashore or took their lives, she hopes to piece together the hidden perils lurking off the shores of northern Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="She is a night elf inhabitant of Auberdine in Darkshore who studies the recent ecological disturbances along the shoreline. She enlists travelers to survey the beach and investigate strange wash-ups from the sea.",al={"who is gwennyth","gwennyth auberdine","gwennyth lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="She can be found in the coastal settlement of Auberdine, situated near the beach and docks along the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore.",al={"where is gwennyth","gwennyth location","find gwennyth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is she interested in beached creatures?",a="The sudden deaths and beachings of massive sea turtles and mysterious marine behemoths point to an imbalance or unseen predator in the waters off Darkshore. Gwennyth seeks to understand the cause by examining remains recovered from along the coast.",al={"why beached turtles","why does she want bones","washed ashore quest"},it="wants"},{q="What quests does Gwennyth offer?",a="She sends adventurers out on 'Washed Ashore' and serves as the turn-in point for various discoveries related to the beached sea creatures and beached sea turtles found along Darkshore's coastline.",al={"gwennyth quests","what does she give"},gp=true},{q="Is she part of the Cenarion Circle or the Sentinels?",a="Neither. She is a Priestess of the Moon serving the Sisters of Elune in Auberdine rather than a Cenarion druid or Sentinel commander, yet she shares her kin's deep concern for the health and balance of Darkshore's natural environment.",al={"gwennyth faction","is gwennyth a druid"},it="side"},{q="What does her name mean?",a="While fitting the rhythmic naming style of the kaldorei, her unusual surname 'Bly'Leggonde' is an anagram of 'Leggy Blonde', a playful touch from the world's creators.",al={"bly leggonde meaning","gwennyth name easter egg"},it="name"},{q="Why is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Darkshore?",a="Gwennyth makes her home in the coastal port of Auberdine, keeping watch over Darkshore's mist-shrouded beaches. Disturbed by the unnatural blight washing up on the coast, she monitors the shoreline for stranded marine wildlife and enlists passing travelers to investigate beached sea creatures and turtles suffering from the strange corruption afflicting the waters.",al={"why is gwennyth here","gwennyth bly'leggonde auberdine why","why is gwennyth in darkshore"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the unnatural death of great sea beasts off the shores of Darkshore is a troubling sign of imbalance in their ancestral lands, making Gwennyth's beachside watch especially urgent.",["class:Druid"]="Druids committed to preserving Kalimdor's natural harmony will find Gwennyth's reports of stranded marine life an alarming indicator of disturbance within the coastal ecosystem.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary coastal port in northern Kalimdor; keeping its waterways and beaches safe from hidden threats is vital to all allied races venturing through."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","beached sea turtle","blyleggonde","darkshore","gwennyth","kaldorei","veiled sea","washed ashore"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:3524","quest:4722","quest:4723","topic:night-elf"},src={"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde"}}
E["npc:kerlonian-evershade"] = {t="npc",n="Kerlonian Evershade",z="darkshore",s="Kerlonian Evershade is a night elf Druid of the Claw resting at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore. Having recently awakened from the long slumber within the Emerald Dream, he requires aid navigating the corrupted wilds to reach the safety of Maestra's Post.",h="Kerlonian Evershade is a night elf Druid of the Claw resting at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore.",sec={{t="Awakening in Darkshore",b="Kerlonian Evershade belongs to the Druids of the Claw, followers of the bear totem who spent centuries sleeping in barrows and communion with the Emerald Dream. Called to wake following the Third War, many druids emerged disoriented into a world ravaged by corruption. Found resting beneath the ancient trees of the Grove of the Ancients, Kerlonian is still shaking off the supernatural grogginess of his prolonged rest. His immediate concern is traveling safely through the troubled forests of Darkshore toward Maestra's Post on the border of Ashenvale.",sp=0},{t="A Treacherous Journey",b="The road out of the Grove of the Ancients is far from secure. The spreading blight in Darkshore has riled the local wildlife and brought hostile prowlers and grell close to the sacred clearings. Weakened from sleep and struggling with sudden bouts of exhaustion, Kerlonian relies on sympathetic travelers of the Alliance to protect him as he makes his way south to rejoin his fellow night elves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kerlonian Evershade?",a="Kerlonian Evershade is a night elf Druid of the Claw stationed near the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore. He recently woke from the Emerald Dream and needs assistance traveling safely through the woods.",al={"who is kerlonian","kerlonian evershade lore","druid in grove of the ancients"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Kerlonian fall asleep while walking?",a="Like many Druids of the Claw who slept for centuries in barrow dens, Kerlonian is still suffering from the lingering stupor of the Emerald Dream. His body and mind have not fully adjusted to waking reality, causing sudden spells of drowsiness.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","sleeper has awakened quest druid","kerlonian sleepy"}},{q="Where is he trying to go?",a="He seeks safe passage south to Maestra's Post, a night elf outpost situated on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale, where he can safely recuperate.",al={"kerlonian destination","where does kerlonian go","grove of the ancients escort destination"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Druid of the Claw?",a="Druids of the Claw are night elf druids who venerate the bear ancient, Ursoc. They channel strength, resilience, and feral might, traditionally guarding barrows and night elf lands while spending ages asleep in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is druid of the claw","druids of the claw lore"}},{q="Whose side is Kerlonian Evershade on?",a="Kerlonian is a night elf Druid of the Claw aligned with the Cenarion Circle and the Darnassian night elves of the Alliance. His devotion lies with nature, the Emerald Dream, and his fellow druidic brethren who safeguard the ancient groves across Kalimdor.",al={"kerlonian faction","is kerlonian alliance","kerlonian evershade side"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Kerlonian Evershade want?",a="Having recently stirred from his long slumber in the Emerald Dream, Kerlonian desires nothing more than safe passage back to the fellowship of his fellow night elves at Maestra's Post. His deep trance leaves him groggy, making simple travel through Darkshore treacherous.",al={"kerlonian goal","kerlonian evershade what does he want","kerlonian purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Kerlonian Evershade here?",a="Kerlonian rests in Darkshore at the Grove of the Ancients, where he has long slumbered in communion with the Emerald Dream alongside other Druids of the Claw. Newly awoken from this deep state, he lingers near the ancient stones until he can muster the strength to travel.",al={"why is kerlonian in darkshore","kerlonian grove of ancients","why is kerlonian asleep here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Kerlonian Evershade tied to?",a="Kerlonian belongs to the Druids of the Claw, an order within the Cenarion Circle devoted to the bear spirit and tasked with guarding the wild. He is also bound in kinship and duty to the night elves stationed at Maestra's Post along the Ashenvale border.",al={"kerlonian order","kerlonian ties","who does kerlonian serve"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druid adventurers will recognize Kerlonian's plight intimately, as all disciples of the Cenarion Circle must grapple with the heavy toll of deep communion with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elf travelers, guiding Kerlonian represents safeguarding one of their ancient defenders, freshly returned to a world vastly changed since the Third War."},kw={"darkshore","druid of the claw","emerald dream","evershade","grove of the ancients","kerlonian","the sleeper has awakened"},rel={"quest:5321","quest:952","quest:2561","zone:darkshore","topic:druid"},src={"Kerlonian Evershade"}}
E["npc:laird"] = {t="npc",n="Laird",z="darkshore",s="Laird is a night elf fish vendor found inside the seaside inn of Auberdine. Working along Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast, he provides trade goods and culinary recipes to travelers and fishermen braving the rugged shoreline.",h="Laird is a night elf fish vendor found inside the seaside inn of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Harbor Merchant",b="Situated inside the bustling inn of Auberdine, Laird sells fresh fish and supplies to sailors, locals, and journeying adventurers. Darkshore's waters are notoriously turbulent and rife with danger compared to the sheltered shores of Teldrassil, but Laird knows well that risk brings reward. For daring anglers willing to cast their lines along the misty beaches, the local catch yields a handsome profit.",sp=0},{t="Ties Across the Water",b="Laird remains closely connected to fishing operations across the channel in Teldrassil. He serves as an essential contact for courier runs between the island boughs of Rut'theran Village and the mainland port, receiving shipments from his fellow fisher Nessa Shadowsong and ensuring the lines of coastal commerce stay open.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Laird?",a="Laird is located indoors on the ground floor of the inn in Auberdine, the main Alliance settlement along the coast of Darkshore.",al={"laird location","where is laird","laird auberdine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Laird sell?",a="He sells various caught fish and cooking ingredients, as well as the culinary instruction for preparing a Fillet of Frenzy.",al={"laird vendor","what does laird sell","laird wares"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Laird?",a="Laird is the recipient of a delivery originating from Nessa Shadowsong at Rut'theran Village in the quest Flight to Auberdine, after which he asks adventurers to carry word back across the sea.",al={"laird quests","auberdine fish quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Laird think Darkshore fishing is worthwhile despite the danger?",a="Laird notes that while the misty shoreline of Darkshore harbors far more hazards than the tranquil waters of Teldrassil, the abundant and exotic sea life makes the trade far more profitable for enterprising fishers.",al={"laird gossip","is darkshore good for fishing"}},{q="Who is Laird?",a="Laird is a night elf fisherman and fish vendor who makes his living in Darkshore. Based inside the bustling inn at Auberdine, he trades with travelers and fishers who ply the misty waters along the coastline, offering cooking recipes and fresh fish to those passing through.",al={"who is laird","laird auberdine","laird identity"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Laird on?",a="Laird is allied with the night elves and the Alliance. Residing peacefully within Auberdine, he welcomes Alliance adventurers and local fishermen to rest at the inn and browse his goods.",al={"laird faction","is laird alliance","who does laird serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Laird here?",a="Laird remains at the Auberdine inn to buy and sell coastal catches. Although Darkshore's coastline carries perils absent from Teldrassil, he recognizes that daring fishers can reap substantial profits from the local waters, making the port a prime location for his trade.",al={"why is laird in auberdine","laird purpose darkshore"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Laird want?",a="Laird seeks a thriving coastal fish trade. He encourages local fishing ventures despite the dangers of Darkshore's shores and is glad to supply hungry travelers with seafood and culinary recipes.",al={"what does laird want","laird goals","laird motives"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Culinary travelers visiting Darkshore often seek out Laird for his recipe on how to properly fillet and cook the fierce frenzy fish native to Kalimdor's waters.",["race:NightElf"]="Laird represents the everyday night elf tradesmen who have established themselves along the mainland shores to support Kalimdor's growing coastal network."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fillet of frenzy","fish vendor","laird","nessa shadowsong"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6342","quest:6343","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Laird"}}
E["npc:prospector-remtravel"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Remtravel",z="darkshore",s="Prospector Remtravel is a dwarven archaeologist affiliated with the Explorers' League, stationed deep in the gloomy woodlands of Darkshore. He oversees an excavation site unearthing ancient relics, though his scattered focus and perilous surroundings leave him in constant need of assistance.",h="Prospector Remtravel is a dwarven archaeologist affiliated with the Explorers' League, stationed deep in the...",sec={{t="A Dwarven Dig in Elven Lands",b="Sent far across the sea by the Explorers' League, Prospector Remtravel established his dig site along the southern reaches of Darkshore. While the night elves are often protective of their ancestral territories, the League's insatiable drive to uncover the origins of Azeroth pushes prospectors into every forgotten corner. Remtravel's work unearths fossilized history and ancient stones, but the aggressive native wildlife and hostile local threats make managing a frontier dig almost more than one scatterbrained dwarf can handle.",sp=0},{t="The Absent-Minded Scholar",b="True to his reputation, Remtravel easily becomes lost in his own thoughts and research notes. Venturing too far from camp in search of fossils or lost artifacts frequently leads to disaster, leaving him cornered by predators or hostile creatures. Those who run across him in the wild usually find themselves tasked with safeguarding his fragile discoveries—and rescuing the prospector himself before the perils of Darkshore put an end to his mission.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="He is an archaeologist and surveyor from Ironforge representing the Explorers' League. He has established a small excavation camp in southern Darkshore to uncover ancient relics and fossils.",al={"who is remtravel","remtravel lore","who is the dwarf in darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an Ironforge dwarf digging in Darkshore?",a="The Explorers' League is scouring the known world for titan artifacts, lost history, and ancient fossils. Darkshore is an ancient, ruined land with deep ties to the distant past, making it a prime site for dwarven archaeological investigation.",al={"why is a dwarf in darkshore","what is the explorers league doing in darkshore","why dig here"},it="why_here"},{q="Why is he called absent-minded?",a="Remtravel has a habit of losing track of his surroundings and his own equipment while absorbed in scholarly pursuits. He frequently wanders into dangerous territory without realizing the predators and beasts closing in around him.",al={"why absent minded","is remtravel crazy","what happened to remtravel"}},{q="Is Prospector Remtravel related to anyone in the League?",a="He is believed to be the adventurous uncle mentioned by Karna Remtravel, an explorer who credits her uncle with inspiring her passion for discovery and the wider world.",al={"remtravel family","karna remtravel uncle","who is karna remtravel"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Prospector Remtravel on?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a loyal subject of Ironforge and an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League. Because Ironforge stands alongside Darnassus in the Grand Alliance, he operates openly within night elf lands, counting on friendly travelers to aid his research and keep the local perils at bay.",al={"prospector remtravel faction","who does remtravel serve","remtravel alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Prospector Remtravel want?",a="Like many in the Explorers' League, Remtravel seeks ancient relics and geological curiosities buried in unfamiliar soil. He is determined to uncover the history beneath Darkshore's surface, though his absent-minded focus on his findings often blinds him to the immediate dangers prowling around his dig site.",al={"what is remtravel looking for","remtravel goal","why is remtravel digging"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Remtravel represents the Explorers' League's relentless determination to piece together dwarven origins, even when it requires pitching tents in the cold, damp woods of Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="While night elves tolerate peaceful Alliance guests, the League's noisy digging and disturbing of ancient soils often tests the patience of local sentinels and druids."},kw={"absent minded prospector","darkshore","explorers league","fossils","ironforge","prospector remtravel","remtravel","remtravels excavation"},rel={"subzone:remtravel-s-excavation","quest:729","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","topic:dwarf","topic:night-elf"},src={"Prospector Remtravel"}}
E["npc:ranger-glynda-nal-shea"] = {t="npc",n="Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea",z="darkshore",s="Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea is a seasoned night elf sentry stationed in the coastal town of Auberdine. From her post near the town watch, she directs local defense efforts across Darkshore, dispatching travelers to eliminate lurking threats and investigate strange coastal phenomena.",h="Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea is a seasoned night elf sentry stationed in the coastal town of Auberdine.",sec={{t="Guardian of Auberdine",b="As Darkshore grapples with rising corruption and hostile incursions, Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea coordinates vital scout work from Auberdine. She keeps a watchful eye over the surrounding wilderness, relying on capable adventurers to maintain the perimeter and safeguard night elf holdings along the fog-shrouded coast.",sp=0},{t="Threats Along the Coast",b="Glynda is keenly focused on the mounting perils encroaching on the shorelines, particularly the emboldened murlocs gathering south of town. She oversees bounties on notorious menaces like Murkdeep and tasks scouts with examining curious artifacts, including a mysterious crimson crystal found embedded on the heights overlooking the sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea?",a="She is an elven ranger stationed in Auberdine who organizes scout patrols and defensive tasks across Darkshore on behalf of the night elf sentinels.",al={"glynda nal'shea","who is glynda","ranger glynda"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Glynda Nal'Shea be found?",a="She is located in Auberdine, the main Alliance settlement in Darkshore, typically found near the sentinel watch and town entrances.",al={"glynda location","where is glynda","where to find glynda"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea offer?",a="She offers tasks dealing with regional hazards, including bounties like WANTED: Murkdeep! and investigations involving the mysterious red crystal along the cliffs of Darkshore.",al={"glynda quests","what does glynda give"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is Glynda concerned about Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is a vicious murloc chieftain responsible for attacks on night elf outposts and travelers along the southern coast, posing an ongoing threat to the security of Auberdine.",al={"who is murkdeep","why kill murkdeep"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Red Crystal quest line?",a="It is a line of scout investigations initiated by Glynda, tasking adventurers with climbing the eastern cliffs of Darkshore to examine an odd, pulsing crystal and retrieve fragments for study.",al={"red crystal darkshore","the red crystal quest"}},{q="What faction does Glynda Nal'Shea serve?",a="She serves the night elves of Darnassus and acts as a military outpost commander for the Alliance in Darkshore.",al={"glynda faction","who does glynda work for"},it="side"},{q="Why is Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea here in Darkshore?",a="Stationed in Auberdine, Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea helps guard Darkshore against the countless dangers pressing in on the night elf settlement. Between encroaching murlocs along the coast, mysterious cultist writings, and aggressive troll incursions from the Shatterspear tribe, she keeps watch over local threats and directs capable adventurers to neutralize them before Auberdine is overwhelmed.",al={"why is glynda here","ranger glynda purpose darkshore","why is glynda in auberdine"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea want you to do?",a="Glynda seeks to secure the safety of Darkshore and unravel the unnatural disturbances troubling the region. She enlists your aid in hunting down dangerous threats like the infamous murloc Murkdeep, investigating mysterious relics such as the large red crystal on the mountainside, and repelling the Shatterspear trolls who have encroached upon night elf lands.",al={"what does glynda want","glynda nalshea tasks","ranger glynda goals"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Glynda Nal'Shea represents the ongoing vigilance required to protect the sacred shores of Kalimdor from aggressive beasts and ancient corruptions.",["class:Hunter"]="Fellow rangers and trackers will find kindred spirit in Glynda's sharp instincts and direct approach to eliminating wild beasts and shoreline predators.",["faction:Alliance"]="Glynda provides Alliance travelers arriving by boat from Teldrassil or the Eastern Kingdoms with essential bounties to secure Darkshore's perimeter."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda","murkdeep","nal'shea","night elf","ranger","red crystal","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:4740","quest:4811","quest:4812","quest:4813","quest:954"},src={"Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea"}}
E["npc:red-jack-flint"] = {t="npc",n="Red Jack Flint",z="darkshore",s="Red Jack Flint is a seasoned human mariner stationed within Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor. A member of the crew of the vessel Maiden's Virtue, he serves as a point of contact for travelers seeking passage or contacts across the sea toward Kalimdor.",h="Red Jack Flint is a seasoned human mariner stationed within Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Sailor in Menethil Keep",b="Found inside the stone walls of Menethil Keep, Red Jack Flint is an experienced seafarer tied to the harbor's maritime trade. As part of the crew of the Maiden's Virtue, he navigates the dangerous sea routes linking the marshlands of Khaz Modan with distant shores. Rather than staying confined to naval routine, Flint directs capable adventurers to allies across the Great Sea, including contacts in Kalimdor like Fiora Longears.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Red Jack Flint?",a="Red Jack Flint is a human sailor and crew member of the Maiden's Virtue. He is stationed in Menethil Keep within Menethil Harbor, helping bridge contacts between the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor.",al={"who is flint","red jack flint lore","what does flint do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Red Jack Flint be found?",a="He can be found resting inside Menethil Keep, the primary stone fortress defending Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"red jack flint location","where is flint","find red jack flint"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What ship does Red Jack Flint sail on?",a="He serves aboard the Maiden's Virtue, a merchant vessel operating out of Menethil Harbor.",al={"flints ship","what ship is red jack on","maidens virtue"}},{q="Who does Red Jack Flint send travelers to see?",a="He directs travelers to make contact with Fiora Longears, an associate situated across the Great Sea in Darkshore.",al={"flint quest","fiora longears connection","where does flint send you"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Red Jack Flint on?",a="Red Jack Flint stands with the Alliance. Stationed among the guards and mariners of Menethil Harbor, he offers guidance and contacts to Alliance travelers moving between the Eastern Kingdoms and the shores of Kalimdor.",al={"red jack flint faction","is red jack flint alliance","red jack flint allegiance"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers charting courses across the sea from Khaz Modan, sailors like Red Jack Flint provide vital connections to outposts along Kalimdor's northern coast."},kw={"fiora longears","maidens virtue","menethil harbor","menethil keep","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","quest:1132","zone:darkshore"},src={"Red Jack Flint"}}
E["npc:sentinel-aynasha"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Aynasha",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Aynasha is an operative of the night elven Sentinels serving in the wild borders of Darkshore. Tasked with scouting enemy movements and carrying critical intelligence, she regularly faces peril against hostile forces threatening northern Kalimdor.",h="Sentinel Aynasha is an operative of the night elven Sentinels serving in the wild borders of Darkshore.",sec={{t="On the Front Lines",b="As a scout and archer for the Sentinels, Aynasha is deployed to the dangerous frontiers where night elven lands clash with hostile incursions. Carrying out stealth missions and bearing urgent dispatches across rugged terrain, she relies on her marksmanship and survival instincts to evade enemy patrols and survive deep within contested territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Aynasha?",a="Aynasha is an active scout and archer within the night elven Sentinels, the primary military and defensive force protecting northern Kalimdor and its borders.",al={"who is aynasha","aynasha role","sentinel aynasha lore"},it="identity"},{q="What threats does she monitor in Darkshore?",a="Operating along the fringes of Darkshore, she keeps watch over hostile encampments, rogue furbolg tribes, and foreign incursions that menace the night elf wilderness.",al={"aynasha enemies","darkshore threats","who is she fighting"},it="threat"},{q="Why is she often isolated on the road?",a="Sentinels frequently travel alone or in small scouting pairs to carry urgent intelligence between posts without drawing unnecessary attention from hostile forces.",al={"why is she alone","aynasha solo mission","sentinel scout duties"},it="why_here"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Aynasha represents the vigilant vanguard of the Kaldorei military, defending the ancient woods against encroaching foreign powers and wild corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers in Kalimdor, Sentinel scouts like Aynasha are vital points of contact along the dangerous wilderness roads."},kw={"archer","aynasha","darkshore","kaldorei","night elf","scout","sentinel"},rel={"zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","quest:5713"},src={"Sentinel Aynasha"}}
E["npc:sentinel-elissa-starbreeze"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf guardian stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore. Operating from the upper floor of a lodge across the bridge, she monitors growing regional threats and directs travelers toward pressing concerns in the wilderness.",h="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf guardian stationed in Auberdine along the misty coast of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Vigilant Eye in Auberdine",b="While many Sentinels patrol the foggy coastline and woodlands directly, Elissa Starbreeze coordinates defensive efforts from Auberdine. Stationed on the upper level of the building just northeast across the bridge from the town inn, she stays alert to unusual disturbances in Darkshore. Her tasks frequently point adventurers toward remote points of interest, including the mysterious Tower of Althalaxx looming far to the north, ensuring that shadowy incursions do not take the coastal settlement unawares.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="She is located in Auberdine in Darkshore. Cross the small bridge northeast of the town's inn, and head up to the second floor of the building there to find her on duty.",al={"elissa starbreeze location","where is elissa starbreeze","auberdine starbreeze"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is her duty in Darkshore?",a="As a member of the Night Elf Sentinels, she helps safeguard Auberdine by tracking potential dangers across Darkshore. She directs capable scouts and adventurers to investigate distant outposts and strange threats, such as the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"what does elissa do","elissa starbreeze role"},it="purpose"},{q="Does she have family among the night elves?",a="She shares the Starbreeze surname with several notable night elves across the lands, including priestesses and military officers such as Belysra Starbreeze and Lieutenant Morra Starbreeze.",al={"starbreeze family","who is elissa related to"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf guard serving the Sentinels in the coastal port of Auberdine. Stationed in Darkshore, she watches over the settlement and directs capable travelers toward pressing troubles throughout the surrounding wilds, including investigations near the enigmatic Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"who is elissa starbreeze","elissa starbreeze night elf","sentinel starbreeze identity"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze on?",a="She is completely loyal to the Sentinels, the night elves of Darnassus, and the broader Alliance. Stationed in Auberdine, she works to safeguard night elven settlements and interests across the shores of Kalimdor.",al={"what faction is elissa starbreeze","is elissa starbreeze alliance","elissa starbreeze loyalty"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze here in Auberdine?",a="Elissa is posted in Darkshore as part of the regional Sentinel detachment guarding Auberdine. From her outpost above the village, she coordinates scouts and recruits adventurers to monitor sinister activities unfolding along the coastline and inland ruins.",al={"why is elissa starbreeze in auberdine","elissa starbreeze location darkshore","what brought elissa starbreeze here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Sentinel Starbreeze represents the watchful, disciplined protection the Sentinels provide to Kalimdor's northern outposts like Auberdine.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers arriving from Teldrassil, Starbreeze serves as one of the early contacts directing aid deeper into the haunted wastes of Darkshore."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","darkshore","elissa starbreeze","night elf","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","npc:elanaria","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze"}}
E["npc:sentinel-onaeya"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Onaeya",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Onaeya is a night elf guardian stationed at Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale, near the border with Darkshore. Tasked with holding the line against encroaching perils, she rallies capable Alliance adventurers to safeguard the forest and honor fallen defenders.",h="Sentinel Onaeya is a night elf guardian stationed at Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale, near the...",sec={{t="A Guard on the Frontier",b="Maestra's Post serves as a critical wayside outpost along the road from Darkshore into the dense, contested canopy of Ashenvale. Sentinel Onaeya stands guard outside the settlement's main lodge, keeping a vigilant watch over travelers and coordinating defensive actions. Between hostile wildlife, corrupting forces, and border tensions, sentinels like Onaeya represent the first line of defense for night elf settlements in the region.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Post",b="When hostilities flare and the perimeter falls under pressure, Onaeya remains squarely focused on the battle at hand. She coordinates strikes against nearby threats and works to recover and honor fallen comrades, relying on capable adventurers arriving from Darkshore to reinforce the outpost's beleaguered defenders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Onaeya?",a="Sentinel Onaeya is a night elf sentinel stationed at Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale. She acts as a quest giver and frontline defender, directing travelers to assist the outpost.",al={"onaeya","sentinel onaeya","who is onaeya"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Sentinel Onaeya located?",a="She can be found standing just outside the main building at Maestra's Post, along the northern roadway in Ashenvale right below the border with Darkshore.",al={"onaeya location","where is sentinel onaeya","find onaeya"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What faction does Sentinel Onaeya belong to?",a="She is a member of the Night Elf Sentinels and is loyal to the Alliance. Horde adventurers will find her hostile on sight.",al={"onaeya faction","is onaeya alliance","onaeya friendly to horde"},it="side"},{q="Why is Sentinel Onaeya too busy to talk sometimes?",a="When Maestra's Post comes under attack or is actively threatened, Onaeya focuses entirely on defense, warning passersby that the post is in the middle of a skirmish.",al={"cant talk","onaeya in combat","were in a bit of a fight here"}},{q="What kind of tasks does Sentinel Onaeya give?",a="Onaeya recruits capable scouts and fighters to strike at nearby dangers, honor fallen defenders, and help keep the roads through northwestern Ashenvale clear for travelers.",al={"onaeya quests","what quests does onaeya have"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Maestra's Post important to the Sentinels?",a="Maestra's Post acts as a crucial checkpoint connecting Darkshore's supply routes to the heart of Ashenvale. Holding it prevents hostile incursions from cutting off night elf travelers moving south.",al={"why maestras post","maestras post importance"},it="place"},{q="Why is Sentinel Onaeya stationed at Maestra's Post?",a="Sentinel Onaeya stands watch just outside the main shelter of Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale. As a night elf sentinel stationed along the frontier, she helps safeguard the outpost against surrounding threats and coordinates defenders during skirmishes when the post comes under pressure.",al={"why is onaeya here","sentinel onaeya location reason","why is onaeya at maestras post"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves traveling south from Darkshore, Onaeya represents the front line defending sacred Ashenvale woodland from external threats.",["faction:Alliance"]="Onaeya coordinates essential defensive tasks for Alliance travelers transitioning from the coastal wilds into the contested forests of Ashenvale.",["faction:Horde"]="As a dedicated sentinel holding Maestra's Post, Onaeya is an active enemy combatant guarding the northern approaches into Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","darkshore","maestra's post","night elf","onaeya","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","quest:5713"},src={"Sentinel Onaeya"}}
E["npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf scout stationed along the main road of Darkshore, just west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran. Tasked with patrolling the troubled coastal wilderness, she directs travelers and recruits aid to investigate the restless spirits haunting the shattered elven settlements nearby.",h="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf scout stationed along the main road of Darkshore, just west of the...",sec={{t="Watch upon the Road",b="Standing sentinel along the overgrown highway of Darkshore, Tysha Moonblade keeps a vigilant eye over an increasingly unstable land. Directly to her east lie the haunted remnants of Ameth'Aran, where cursed Highborne ghosts and malevolent banshees linger among ancient stone pillars. Recognizing that Auberdine's limited defenses are stretched thin by threats across the coast, Tysha enlists capable adventurers passing by to uncover the history behind Ameth'Aran's tragic fall and put down the restless dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf guardian patrolling the main road in central Darkshore, stationed just west of the ruins of Ameth'Aran. She watches the route against wandering beasts and restless specters.",al={"who is tysha","tysha moonblade lore","sentinel tysha"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="She is posted along the north-south road in Darkshore, situated directly west across from the ancient ruin site of Ameth'Aran.",al={"tysha moonblade location","where is tysha","where is sentinel tysha"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does she give to adventurers?",a="Tysha directs travelers into the nearby ruins of Ameth'Aran to investigate the ancient tragedy that ruined the ancient night elf settlement, helping quiet the tormented ghosts that haunt its tumbled columns.",al={"tysha moonblade quests","fall of ametharan quest giver","what does tysha want"},gp=true},{q="Is she related to anyone else in Darkshore?",a="Sharing a surname, she is likely related to Mariner Moonblade, who can also be found serving night elf interests along the Darkshore coastline.",al={"mariner moonblade relation","tysha moonblade family"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade on?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade serves the Sentinels of the night elves and stands firmly with the Alliance. As a guardian of Kalimdor's sacred wilderness, she watches the trails of Darkshore to protect her kin and their ancient lands from encroaching perils.",al={"tysha moonblade faction","who does tysha moonblade serve","is tysha moonblade alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade here?",a="Stationed along the road just west of the haunted ruins of Ameth'Aran, Sentinel Moonblade patrols this thoroughfare to monitor the nearby ancient grounds. Darkshore is rife with agitated spirits and lurking enemies, requiring vigilance to keep passing travelers and nearby elven settlements secure.",al={"why is tysha moonblade in darkshore","tysha moonblade post","why is tysha near ameth'aran"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Sentinel Tysha Moonblade want?",a="Moonblade seeks competent Alliance adventurers to uncover the tragic history haunting the ruins of Ameth'Aran. By directing allies to investigate the shattered relics and ancient accounts of the city's fall, she hopes to bring clarity and rest to the restless spirits lingering in the wilderness.",al={"what does tysha moonblade need","tysha moonblade mission","why does tysha need help"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Tysha represents the vigilant Sentinels trying to maintain peace over lands still scarred by the ancient Sundering, asking fellow night elves to lay their cursed ancestors to rest.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers making the journey south from Auberdine toward Ashenvale, Tysha is one of the few friendly outposts along an otherwise perilous, monster-infested road."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","highborne","night elf","sentinel","tysha moonblade"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:953","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Tysha Moonblade"}}
E["npc:terenthis"] = {t="npc",n="Terenthis",z="darkshore",s="Terenthis is a night elf druid stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine. Representing the Cenarion Circle, he is investigating the alarming corruption spreading through Darkshore and Teldrassil. He enlists capable travelers to gauge rising threats along the coast and assist local allies trapped by corrupted wildlife.",h="Terenthis is a night elf druid stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",sec={{t="Investigating the Taint",b="Sent to Auberdine by the Cenarion Circle, Terenthis focuses on tracking the spread of Fel Moss and other corruptive forces seeping into Darkshore from Teldrassil. The night elves view this creeping blight with immense concern, fearing the wild balance of northern Kalimdor may fracture completely if left unchecked. Terenthis works to uncover the root causes of the rot and devise ways to halt its advance before it consumes the forests.",sp=0},{t="A Plea from Grimclaw",b="Terenthis also acts as a liaison for dire emergencies in the field. When the loyal bear Grimclaw arrives in Auberdine wounded and alone, Terenthis recognizes that the creature's master, the druid Volcor, has run into grave trouble. Lacking the ability to leave his post, Terenthis directs passing adventurers into the wilderness to find Volcor, who has been ambushed and pinned down by aggressive furbolg tribes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a night elf druid affiliated with the Cenarion Circle, currently residing in the harbor town of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"terenthis lore","who is terenthis","terenthis auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Terenthis in Auberdine?",a="He was dispatched to investigate how widely Fel Moss and magical corruption have spread from Teldrassil into Darkshore, seeking a way to put an end to the blight.",al={"what is terenthis doing","terenthis purpose","why is terenthis here"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the bear beside Terenthis doing there?",a="The bear, Grimclaw, sought out Terenthis in Auberdine for help after his master, the druid Volcor, was attacked and wounded by hostile furbolgs.",al={"terenthis bear","grimclaw","why is there a bear in auberdine"},it="ties"},{q="What organization does Terenthis belong to?",a="Terenthis is a member of the Cenarion Circle, the druidic order dedicated to preserving balance and safeguarding nature across Kalimdor.",al={"terenthis faction","is terenthis cenarion circle"},it="side"},{q="What threats is Terenthis most concerned with?",a="He is primarily concerned with Fel Moss corruption affecting the regional wildlife, as well as the rising hostility of local furbolg tribes that threaten travelers and druids alike.",al={"darkshore corruption","fel moss threat","terenthis concerns"},it="threat"},{q="Does Terenthis offer any tasks to adventurers?",a="Yes. He directs adventurers to assess corrupting threats along the coast, coordinate with fellow druids like Thundris Windweaver, and mount a rescue for Volcor.",al={"terenthis quests","what does terenthis want"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What does Terenthis want?",a="Terenthis wants to determine the full extent of the Fel Moss corruption creeping into Darkshore and discover why Teldrassil and its surrounding wilderness are falling to taint. Ultimately, he seeks to purge this creeping blight and restore balance to the forest before the corruption permanently takes root.",al={"terenthis goal","what is terenthis trying to do","terenthis motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion Circle brother, Terenthis represents the front line against the unnatural corruption spilling from Teldrassil into the mainland.",["race:NightElf"]="Terenthis exemplifies the kaldorei commitment to purifying their sacred lands from lingering fel taint and protecting innocent forest life."},kw={"auberdine","cenarion circle","darkshore","fel moss","furbolg","grimclaw","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:986","quest:984","quest:4761","quest:994","quest:995","topic:furbolg"},src={"Terenthis"}}
E["npc:tharnariun-treetender"] = {t="npc",n="Tharnariun Treetender",z="darkshore",s="Tharnariun Treetender is a night elf naturalist stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore. Dedicated to safeguarding the delicate balance of the wild, he monitors the creeping corruption afflicting the regional flora and fauna. Travelers passing through the port often find him calling upon allies to heal diseased beasts and protect nature from further decline.",h="Tharnariun Treetender is a night elf naturalist stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Guardian in Auberdine",b="Perched on the rugged coast of Darkshore, the port town of Auberdine faces threats on multiple fronts, from hostile satyrs to foul shoreline washaways. Tharnariun Treetender focuses his efforts squarely on the natural world that surrounds the village. Firmly believing that neglecting nature invites ruin, he spends his time observing the decline of the local woods and seeking ways to push back the sickness spreading across the forest floor.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Afflicted",b="Much of Darkshore's wildlife has fallen prey to strange plagues and corrupted blights, driving creatures mad and twisting peaceful animals into rabid threats. Rather than merely slaughtering them out of fear, Tharnariun seeks a remedy. Through carefully concocted cleansers and targeted efforts to eliminate the worst of the contagion, he endeavors to rescue what remains of the wilderness before the woodland falls entirely into decay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun is a night elf caretaker stationed in Auberdine along the coast of Darkshore. He dedicates his life to watching over the forest and diagnosing the unnatural afflictions troubling the local wildlife.",al={"who is tharnariun","tharnariun lore","tharnariunreetender"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tharnariun Treetender?",a="He is located in the night elf coastal village of Auberdine, situated on the western edge of the Darkshore wilderness.",al={"where is tharnariun","tharnariun treetender location","tharnariun map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What problems is Tharnariun investigating in Darkshore?",a="He investigates the spreading corruption and foul plagues infecting the land and its wildlife, sending adventurers out to cleanse infected beasts and halt the blight.",al={"what does tharnariun want","tharnariun purpose","why help tharnariun"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Tharnariun care so much about diseased animals?",a="As a protector of the wilds, Tharnariun believes that night elves cannot neglect nature without suffering the consequences. He works to cleanse the sick creatures rather than abandoning the forest to corruption.",al={"why save the beasts","tharnariun animal quest"},it="motive"},{q="What quests does Tharnariun Treetender offer?",a="He directs adventurers through tasks involving the blighted lands and wildlife, notably 'Plagued Lands', 'Cleansing of the Infected', and 'Tharnariun's Hope'.",al={"tharnariun quests","tharnariun treetender tasks"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Tharnariun a druid?",a="The sources never name him a druid outright. While he shares the naturalist convictions of the Cenarion Circle regarding the preservation of beasts and flora, he acts primarily as a dedicated caretaker and treetender for the wilderness of Darkshore.",al={"is tharnariun druid","tharnariun class"}},{q="Whose side is Tharnariun Treetender on?",a="Tharnariun Treetender stands firmly with the night elves and the Alliance. Stationed in Auberdine, his loyalties lie with the preservation of Kalimdor's natural heritage and his kaldorei kin, welcoming travelers of the Alliance who are willing to aid in protecting the wilderness from encroaching blight.",al={"tharnariun treetender faction","is tharnariun alliance","who does tharnariun serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Tharnariun Treetender want?",a="Tharnariun seeks to protect and cleanse the fragile ecosystem of Darkshore. Troubled by strange afflictions twisting the local fauna, he devotes his efforts to uncovering the root causes of the corruption and finding remedies to heal or mercifully put down the infected wildlife before nature completely unravels.",al={"tharnariun goal","what is tharnariun trying to do","tharnariun treetender purpose"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Tharnariun's warnings resonate deeply with their ancient duty to watch over the natural balance of northern Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find Tharnariun's concern for blighted wildlife closely aligned with their own sacred mission to restore harmony to corrupted lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary coastal gateway in northern Kalimdor, making Tharnariun's defense of the surrounding woods vital to the outpost's safety."},kw={"auberdine","cleansing","corruption","darkshore","infected","kaldorei","plagued lands","tharnariun","treetender"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:2118","quest:2138","quest:2139","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tharnariun Treetender"}}
E["npc:vesprystus"] = {t="npc",n="Vesprystus",z="darkshore",s="Vesprystus is the night elf flight master stationed at the docks of Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil. He oversees the roost of trained hippogryphs that carry travelers between the great World Tree and mainland Kalimdor.",h="Vesprystus is the night elf flight master stationed at the docks of Rut'theran Village at the base of...",sec={{t="Keeper of the Rut'theran Roost",b="Perched at the southern base of Teldrassil in Rut'theran Village, Vesprystus tends the hippogryphs that bridge the isolated elven boughs to the rest of the world. While a magical portal connects Rut'theran directly to the canopy city of Darnassus above, crossing the sea toward Darkshore and the mainland requires wings. Vesprystus works in coordination with the flight master at Auberdine across the straight, ensuring safe passage for sentinels, emissaries, and adventurers journeying into Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Vesprystus fly travelers?",a="Vesprystus connects Rut'theran Village directly across the water to the port of Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore. From Auberdine, travelers can catch connecting hippogryph routes south toward Ashenvale and other night elf enclaves across Kalimdor.",al={"where can he take me","vesprystus flight paths","rut'theran flight route"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What creatures does Vesprystus tend?",a="He manages a roost of loyal night elf hippogryphs, ancient winged beasts native to northern Kalimdor. Night elves have raised and bonded with hippogryphs for generations to navigate forest canopies and rugged coastlines.",al={"what mounts does he have","vesprystus animals","what does he fly"},gp=true},{q="How do you reach Darnassus from where Vesprystus stands?",a="You do not need a flight to reach Darnassus from Rut'theran Village. A shimmering pink-tinted portal stands just up the path from Vesprystus's roost, instantly transporting travelers up to the city canopy.",al={"how to get to darnassus from vesprystus","vesprystus to darnassus","path to darnassus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Vesprystus?",a="Vesprystus is a night elf hippogryph master stationed at Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil. He is responsible for managing the roosts and providing reliable aerial transport for travelers moving between the great boughs of Darnassus above and the coastal settlements of northern Kalimdor.",al={"who is vesprystus","vesprystus night elf","vesprystus lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Vesprystus on?",a="He is loyal to Darnassus and the Alliance. His roosts serve night elf sentinels, druids, and visiting allies who need safe, swift passage into and out of Teldrassil.",al={"vesprystus alliance","vesprystus faction","who does vesprystus serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Vesprystus here?",a="Rut'theran Village serves as the vital harbor and arrival point for Teldrassil. Because the World Tree rises steeply from the ocean, overland travel is impossible. Vesprystus stays here to keep the roosts supplied and ensure hippogryphs are always ready to ferry messengers, provisions, and travelers across the water to the mainland.",al={"why is vesprystus at rut'theran","vesprystus purpose here","why is vesprystus in ruttheran"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Vesprystus want?",a="He wants to ensure his hippogryphs are well cared for and that flight routes connecting Teldrassil to neighboring outposts remain open and secure. He aids travelers and couriers carrying essential deliveries across the sea.",al={"what does vesprystus need","vesprystus goals","vesprystus motivation"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elf adventurers leaving Teldrassil for the first time, Vesprystus is often the handler who sends them soaring toward their very first glimpse of mainland Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Vesprystus forms a vital transit link for any Alliance traveler arriving at Teldrassil's docks and needing swift transport to coastal Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","flight master","hippogryph master","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"subzone:rut-theran-village","quest:6342","quest:6341","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Vesprystus"}}
E["npc:volcor"] = {t="npc",n="Volcor",z="darkshore",s="Volcor is an injured night elf scout stranded deep within Blackwood Den in northern Darkshore. Trapped by hostile Blackwood furbolgs, he relies on his faithful companion Grimclaw and the aid of Auberdine's defenders to escape.",h="Volcor is an injured night elf scout stranded deep within Blackwood Den in northern Darkshore.",sec={{t="Trapped in the Den",b="While tracking the corrupted Blackwood tribe in their subterranean lair, Volcor was ambushed and severely wounded. Unable to fight his way past the hostile furbolgs on his own, he sent his loyal bear companion, Grimclaw, out into the wilds of Darkshore to seek help from the settlement of Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="A Way to Freedom",b="Once contacted by scouts alerted by Terenthis, Volcor offers two avenues of escape depending on his savior's strengths. Those who favor direct action can carve a bloody path through the cave's defenders, while those adept at subterfuge can use cunning and quiet movement to slip past the sentries unnoticed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Volcor located?",a="Volcor is hidden deep inside Blackwood Den, a furbolg cave located in northern Darkshore, just east of the main road heading north from Auberdine.",al={"volcor location","where is volcor","find volcor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Volcor trapped in Blackwood Den?",a="He was scouting the Blackwood furbolgs when he was attacked and wounded. Cut off from the cave entrance, he could not bypass the hostile sentries without aid.",al={"why is volcor in a cave","what happened to volcor"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is Volcor's loyal bear companion. When Volcor was trapped, he sent Grimclaw out to find help in Auberdine, which ultimately alerted the druid Terenthis.",al={"who is the bear","volcor bear","grimclaw lore"},it="ties"},{q="How can you help Volcor escape?",a="Volcor allows you to choose your method of rescue: you can either fight your way out through the cave's furbolg guards in a frontal assault, or sneak past them using stealth.",al={"escape through force or stealth","volcor escort quest","rescue volcor"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who sent you to find Volcor?",a="Terenthis, a night elf druid stationed in Auberdine, directs adventurers to look for Volcor after Grimclaw is found wandering without his master.",al={"who gave the volcor quest","terenthis connection"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What tribe of furbolgs attacked him?",a="The Blackwood tribe, a corrupted group of furbolgs native to northern Darkshore that has succumbed to madness and hostility.",al={"which furbolgs","blackwood furbolgs"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf explorer and wanderer of Darkshore. Accompanied by his loyal bear companion, Grimclaw, he ventured deep into the forests until he ran afoul of the hostile Blackwood furbolgs, leaving him wounded and stranded within their den.",al={"who is volcor","volcor identity","volcor night elf"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Volcor on?",a="Volcor is allied with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. His trusted contacts reside in the coastal haven of Auberdine, where friends like Terenthis look after his safety and welcome travelers who aid him.",al={"volcor faction","is volcor alliance","volcor allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Volcor want?",a="Trapped and weakened deep inside Blackwood Den, Volcor simply wants to escape alive and make his way back to the safety of Auberdine. Having sent Grimclaw ahead to find help, he now relies on passing allies to guide him past the hostile furbolgs.",al={"what does volcor want","volcor goal","volcor motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Volcor's plight illustrates the growing danger facing the Kaldorei in Darkshore as formerly peaceful furbolg allies fall to corruption.",["class:Druid"]="The bond between Volcor and Grimclaw mirrors the deep connection druids share with nature's beasts, making his rescue a matter of natural balance.",["class:Rogue"]="Volcor appreciates tactical finesse, offering rogues the chance to bypass the Blackwood guards quietly rather than relying on brute force."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood den","darkshore","escape through force","escape through stealth","furbolg","grimclaw","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"quest:986","subzone:blackwood-den","npc:terenthis","subzone:auberdine","quest:994","quest:995","zone:darkshore","topic:furbolg"},src={"Volcor"}}
E["npc:wizbang-cranktoggle"] = {t="npc",n="Wizbang Cranktoggle",z="darkshore",s="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome engineer residing on the upper floor of the Auberdine inn. Despite being far from the cog-filled halls of Gnomeregan or Ironforge, he has turned his mechanical ingenuity toward setting up and maintaining automated communication devices known as buzzboxes across the wild coast of Darkshore.",h="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome engineer residing on the upper floor of the Auberdine inn.",sec={{t="An Engineer in Auberdine",b="While the night elves of Auberdine prefer living in harmony with nature and leaning upon ancient customs, Wizbang Cranktoggle represents the curious, tinkering presence of the Alliance. Perched on the top floor of Auberdine's inn, surrounded by tools and spare components, Wizbang pays little mind to the solemn druidic traditions of Kalimdor, focusing instead on pragmatic mechanical challenges.",sp=0},{t="The Buzzbox Network",b="Wizbang's primary project along Darkshore is deploying and maintaining his peculiar invention: the buzzbox. Designed to establish automated reporting and long-distance communication across the rugged, sprawling coastline, these contraptions often suffer from coastal weathering and the hostility of local wildlife. Wizbang frequently recruits travelers to gather components, salvage tools like gaffer jacks, and recover electropellers to keep his mechanical surveillance functioning.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang is located on the upper floor of the inn in the seaside night elf settlement of Auberdine, in Darkshore.",al={"wizbang location","where is wizbang","auberdine gnome location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Wizbang Cranktoggle doing in Darkshore?",a="He is an Alliance engineer working on establishing and maintaining a network of automated communication machines called buzzboxes throughout the Darkshore wilderness.",al={"why is wizbang in auberdine","wizbang purpose","what does wizbang do"},it="why_here"},{q="What are buzzboxes?",a="Buzzboxes are mechanical communication and monitoring devices invented by Wizbang Cranktoggle to relay information across Darkshore, though they frequently break down due to wildlife attacks and harsh weather.",al={"what is a buzzbox","buzzbox lore","buzzbox purpose"},it="item"},{q="Is Wizbang related to any other gnomes?",a="He shares a surname with Delber Cranktoggle, suggesting they may belong to the same family of tinkerers.",al={"cranktoggle family","who is delber cranktoggle","wizbang relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Why do the night elves tolerate his tinkering in Auberdine?",a="As fellow members of the Grand Alliance, the night elves provide lodging and refuge to allied races in Auberdine, even if gnomish contraptions contrast sharply with traditional elven harmony.",al={"night elves and gnomes","why allow engineering in auberdine"},it="conflict"},{q="What tasks does Wizbang give to adventurers?",a="Wizbang asks adventurers to help repair and configure his buzzbox machines, which involves scouring the shoreline for specialized parts like electropellers and gaffer jacks.",al={"wizbang quests","what quests does wizbang offer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an enterprising gnomish engineer currently staying on the upper floor of the inn in Auberdine. While night elves generally prefer nature over clanking machinery, Wizbang has set up shop along the coast to deploy and maintain his network of mechanical contraptions known as buzzboxes.",al={"who is wizbang","wizbang cranktoggle identity","who is the gnome in auberdine"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Wizbang Cranktoggle on?",a="Wizbang is loyal to Gnomeregan and the Grand Alliance. He operates openly out of Auberdine under the hospitality of the night elves, offering his technical expertise and tasks to Alliance travelers passing through Darkshore.",al={"wizbang cranktoggle faction","is wizbang alliance","wizbang cranktoggle allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Wizbang Cranktoggle want?",a="Wizbang wants to establish and maintain an automated surveillance and communication network across Darkshore using his buzzbox inventions. Because the local wilderness is perilous and machinery frequently breaks down, he seeks adventurers to gather native materials, creature parts, and mechanical components to keep his network operational.",al={"what does wizbang want","wizbang cranktoggle goals","why does wizbang need parts"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Seeing a fellow gnome operating an experimental communication network along Kalimdor's rugged coast is a welcome reminder of Gnomeregan's relentless inventiveness.",["profession:Engineering"]="Wizbang's reliance on custom tools like gaffer jacks and electropellers highlights the classic gnomish mindset: mechanical answers to logistical problems in uncharted lands.",["race:NightElf"]="While elven sentinels and druids rely on whisps, messengers, and natural bonds, Wizbang brings loud, whirring gears and metal boxes into Darkshore's sacred woods."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox","cranktoggle","darkshore","electropellers","engineer","gaffer jacks","gnome","wizbang"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:983","quest:1579","quest:1580","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},src={"Wizbang Cranktoggle"}}
E["quest:1001"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 411",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 411 is an Alliance quest found along the windswept coastline of Darkshore. Operating through an eccentric mechanical relay network, the intoxicated gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle enlists travelers to gather coastal thresher eyes to bring his second research machine back online.",h="Buzzbox 411 is an Alliance quest found along the windswept coastline of Darkshore.",sec={{t="Voice Through the Static",b="After assisting with the repairs of Buzzbox 827 further south, the voice of the gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle crackles over the mechanical transmitter once more. Stationed somewhere safely out of sight, Wizbang directs adventurers further north along Darkshore's mist-laden beach to locate another damaged terminal: Buzzbox 411. Between transmissions punctuated by hiccups and muttered praises of crawler wine, he reveals that local aquatic predators hold the components necessary to keep his coastal apparatus functional.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Beneath the Surf",b="Restoring Buzzbox 411 requires diving into the chilly, turbulent waters off the coast of Auberdine. Darkshore threshers prowl the shallows, aggressive marine beasts whose ocular organs contain precisely the properties Wizbang claims are needed to recalibrate the device. Feeding the requested thresher eyes into the waiting hatch of the machine jolts the apparatus back into operation, rewarding the courier and opening the line for another increasingly slurred assignment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Buzzbox 411?",a="Buzzbox 411 is a mechanical transmitter device situated north of Auberdine along the Darkshore shoreline. It serves as part of an experimental listening and research network maintained by the gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle.",al={"buzzbox 411","what is buzzbox 411","buzzbox 411 purpose"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome tinkerer who communicates remotely through the Buzzbox network. He spends his field research heavily enjoying crawler wine while relying on passing adventurers to do the hazardous fieldwork of collecting animal parts.",al={"wizbang","who is wizbang","who made buzzbox"},it="people"},{q="Why does a machine need Thresher Eyes?",a="Gnomish engineering frequently blends bizarre organic matter with mechanical components to perform unorthodox tasks. Whether Wizbang truly needs the eyes for optical sensors or is merely using them in biological research while drunk, he insists they are vital to repairing Buzzbox 411.",al={"why thresher eyes","thresher eyes for machine","buzzbox eyes"},it="item"},{q="Where is Buzzbox 411 located?",a="Buzzbox 411 is planted right on the beach in Darkshore, located north of the night elf settlement of Auberdine.",al={"where is buzzbox 411","buzzbox 411 location","find buzzbox 411"},gp=true},{q="Where do I find Darkshore Threshers?",a="Darkshore threshers swim in the coastal waters off Auberdine and along the nearby shores, easily found by swimming out past the surf line.",al={"where are threshers","thresher eye source","thresher location"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Buzzbox 411 is fixed?",a="Once Buzzbox 411 hums back to life, Wizbang Cranktoggle thanks you over the static, downs another drink, and immediately asks if you are willing to fix his next machine, Buzzbox 323.",al={"next buzzbox","what comes after buzzbox 411","buzzbox chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want Buzzbox 411 repaired?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is working down the Darkshore coastline to restore his network of automated communication devices. While he maintains the machines remotely, he relies on passing adventurers to supply local organic components—allowing him to keep his contraptions operational across the wilderness without interrupting his drinking back at camp.",al={"wizbang motive","why repair buzzbox 411","why does wizbang need this"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are Darkshore threshers?",a="Darkshore threshers are predatory marine beasts that prowl the chilly coastal waters off Auberdine. Equipped with sharp senses and multiple ocular lenses suited for murky depths, their biological parts happen to provide the unusual optical properties Wizbang needs to calibrate the mechanisms of Buzzbox 411.",al={"darkshore threshers","who are threshers","what are threshers"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Wizbang need you instead of doing this himself?",a="Wizbang is an eccentric tinkerer who clearly prefers the comfort of his workshop and a steady supply of crawler wine over braving the freezing ocean surf. With dangerous threshers prowling the coastal waters, outsourcing the hunting and field repairs to capable adventurers lets him expand his network without leaving his stool.",al={"why me buzzbox 411","why doesnt wizbang do it","why wizbang needs adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle represents the quintessential gnomish approach to fieldwork: bold innovation, peculiar component choices, and delegating the dangerous swimming to whoever is passing by.",["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic thresher eyes to calibrate a mechanical transmitter demonstrates the eccentric, boundary-pushing methods favored by unconventional tinkerers.",["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine's sentinels keep a watchful eye on Darkshore's waters, though they typically leave peculiar gnomish contraptions on the shoreline to their own devices."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 411","crawler wine","darkshore","gnome","thresher eyes","tinkering","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:983","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Buzzbox 827",["end"]="Buzzbox 411",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1001,ri={"Thresher Eye"}},src={"Buzzbox 411 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1002"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 323",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 323 is the third task in a field-research line along the coast of Darkshore, commissioned through a speaker device by the eccentric gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle. Players must gather Moonstalker fangs from local predators and deposit them into the humming contraption situated north of Auberdine.",h="Buzzbox 323 is the third task in a field-research line along the coast of Darkshore, commissioned through a...",sec={{t="A Slurred Transmission",b="After operating Buzzbox 411 further south, the voice of the gnomish inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle crackles to life over the speaker. Interspersed with the sounds of heavy drinking and slurred directions, Wizbang directs adventurers north toward Auberdine, pointing them to Buzzbox 323 near a road bridge. His research requires six Moonstalker Fangs, harvested from the fierce feline hunters roaming the shrouded forests of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Field Machinery",b="Approaching Buzzbox 323 reveals a machine that chatters with static and faint muttering even before repairs begin. Once the requested fangs are placed inside its intake hopper, the machine violently rattles to life, noisily pulverizing the teeth to dust. Wizbang's boozy voice promptly resumes over the transceiver, celebrating the delivery before prodding the traveler toward the next machine in his scattered network.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Buzzbox 323 located?",a="Buzzbox 323 stands alongside the main road north of Auberdine, just near the bridge crossing the local river in Darkshore.",al={"buzzbox 323 location","where is buzzbox 323","find buzzbox 323"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is speaking through the Buzzbox?",a="The voice belongs to Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome inventor stationed elsewhere in Darkshore who communicates through remote transmitters while heavily indulging in ale.",al={"who talks in buzzbox","buzzbox gnome","wizbang cranktoggle"},it="identity"},{q="What does Buzzbox 323 do with the fangs?",a="Upon dropping the Moonstalker fangs inside, internal gears immediately grind them down into fine powder as part of Wizbang's automated biological sampling mechanism.",al={"what happens to the fangs","why moonstalker fangs","buzzbox grinding"},it="item"},{q="Where can I find Moonstalkers in Darkshore?",a="Moonstalkers and their runts prowl the shaded woodlands and hills bordering the road both north and south of Auberdine.",al={"where are moonstalkers","moonstalker fang farm","moonstalker location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quest comes before and after Buzzbox 323?",a="This assignment follows Buzzbox 411, which required thresher eyes, and directly precedes Buzzbox 525, which sends you to collect grizzled scalps from thistle bears far south along the road.",al={"buzzbox quest chain","what follows buzzbox 323","buzzbox order"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizbang sound so incoherent?",a="Wizbang is thoroughly intoxicated while giving instructions, pausing to search for his ale and taking loud gulps between sentences.",al={"why is wizbang drunk","buzzbox voice slurring"}},{q="Why does Wizbang want Moonstalker Fangs placed in Buzzbox 323?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is working his way through maintaining his network of automated Buzzbox sampling machines scattered across Darkshore. Each contraption is designed to process parts from the local wildlife, and Buzzbox 323 specifically requires six moonstalker fangs to calibrate its internal grinding mechanisms and continue its mysterious field work.",al={"why buzzbox 323","wizbang buzzbox motive","why moonstalker fangs"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are the Moonstalkers you are sent to hunt?",a="Moonstalkers are stealthy saber cats native to the shadowed forests of Darkshore. They prowl among the ancient ruins and tangled woodlands, hunting prey under the cover of perpetual dusk and preying upon travelers who wander too far from Auberdine's guarded roads.",al={"what are moonstalkers","darkshore moonstalkers","who are the targets"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's remote acoustic communication network showcases typical gnomish engineering flair—even if his personal discipline leaves much to be desired.",["race:NightElf"]="While native night elves treat the fierce Moonstalkers with reverent caution, gnomish science reduces their lethal fangs to pulverized machine fuel.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Buzzbox series demonstrates automated material processing coupled with long-range voice relay, an impressive technical design despite its rough operation."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox","buzzbox 323","cranktoggle","darkshore","fangs","moonstalker","wizbang"},rel={"quest:1001","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Buzzbox 411",["end"]="Buzzbox 323",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=1002,ri={"Moonstalker Fang"}},src={"Buzzbox 323 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1003"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 525",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 525 is the final stage in a series of communicative machines scattered along the coast of Darkshore. Created by the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle, the contraption demands animal remnants to function—while slowly unraveling the inventor's true, illicit ambitions.",h="Buzzbox 525 is the final stage in a series of communicative machines scattered along the coast of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Slurred Transmission",b="After servicing Buzzbox 323, travelers receive garbled instructions broadcast straight through the machine's rattling speakers. Wizbang Cranktoggle's speech grows increasingly slurred, filled with drunken chuckles and rambling directions leading far south along the main road of Darkshore. He directs his helpers to hunt down the local grizzled thistle bears and deliver four of their thick scalps into the compartment of Buzzbox 525, concealed carefully behind a fence in the roadside brush.",sp=0},{t="The Distiller's Secret",b="Upon arriving at the hidden machine, the curious hum of machinery is drowned out by raucous singing echoing from within the iron plating. As the grizzly bear scalps are deposited into the receptacle, Wizbang finally comes clean about his network. The contraptions are far more than mere communications equipment: they double as automated micro-breweries and distilleries. Disdainful of the night elves' strict and abstemious customs in Auberdine, the gnome built his contraptions to distill forbidden woodland spirits—using animal harvest like bear scalps to brew potent batches of 'thistle bear beer.'",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Buzzbox 525 located?",a="Buzzbox 525 sits far south down the main road from Auberdine. Wizbang tucked it away just off the path near a rustic fence line, partially concealed beneath bushes.",al={"buzzbox 525 location","where is buzzbox 525","buzzbox 525 find"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizbang want grizzled scalps?",a="Wizbang claims the scalps are needed to repair Buzzbox 525, just as the earlier machines needed crawler legs, thresher eyes and moonstalker fangs. The drunken song about thistle bear beer coming from the box hints at another purpose.",al={"why grizzled scalps","buzzbox bear scalps","what are scalps for"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Why does Wizbang hide the Buzzboxes out in the wilderness?",a="The night elves residing in Auberdine do not appreciate reckless moonshining or an illicit alcohol trade within their serene settlements. By scattering the machines along the desolate Darkshore road, Wizbang keeps his brewing network hidden from elven authorities.",al={"why are buzzboxes hidden","why hide buzzbox","wizbang secret"},sp=1,it="why_here"},{q="Who is speaking through the Buzzbox?",a="The voice belongs to Wizbang Cranktoggle, an enterprising gnome tinkerer who installed voice transmitters inside his makeshift brewing apparatuses across Darkshore.",al={"who talks in buzzbox","buzzbox voice","wizbang identity"},it="identity"},{q="Can Wizbang speak through the machine without the scalps?",a="Yes. Upon completing the task, Wizbang admits that the audio transceivers function regardless of whether materials are fed into the hatch. His request for ingredients was entirely to keep his automated distilling operation supplied.",al={"is the buzzbox broken","did wizbang lie"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="What song does the Buzzbox sing?",a="Before you deposit the scalps, the speaker repeatedly chants a drunken limerick: 'Though crawler wine's sweet, and thresher ale fine, and moonstalker moonshine is grand. There's nothing so dear, as a thistle bear beer, and soon I shall have some on hand!'",al={"buzzbox singing","thistle bear beer song"}},{q="What are you sent to hunt for Buzzbox 525?",a="You are sent to hunt grizzled thistle bears, sturdy predators that roam the woods south of Auberdine. Wizbang needs their thick, grizzled pelts fed directly into the mechanical hopper of Buzzbox 525 to complete his peculiar southern concoction.",al={"what do i kill for buzzbox 525","buzzbox 525 target","grizzled thistle bears darkshore"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Wizbang ask you instead of the sentinels to collect bear scalps?",a="Wizbang cannot turn to Auberdine's night elf sentinels because his operation is completely illicit. The night elves strictly forbid his covert brewing operations in Darkshore, forcing him to hide his distilling machines in the wilderness and rely on roaming travelers who do not ask too many questions.",al={"why not ask sentinels","why does wizbang need me buzzbox","why ask adventurer buzzbox"},sp=1,it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The strict stewardship of Darkshore leaves little patience for reckless gnomish tinkering.",["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's multi-purpose transceivers showcase typical gnomish ambition, blending complex engineering with questionable practical priorities."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 525","darkshore","grizzled scalp","thistle bear","thistle bear beer","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1002","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Buzzbox 323",["end"]="Buzzbox 525",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=1003,ri={"Grizzled Scalp"}},src={"Buzzbox 525 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1132"] = {t="quest",n="Fiora Longears",z="darkshore",s="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor. Directed by the enthusiastic recruiter Red Jack Flint in Menethil Harbor, travelers take ship across the Great Sea to report to his high elf contact, Fiora Longears, on the docks of Auberdine.",h="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Call to the West",b="For many humans, dwarves, and gnomes, the Eastern Kingdoms feel fraught with old conflicts and scarred earth. In the bustling port of Menethil Harbor, the sailor Red Jack Flint spends his days urging adventurous travelers to board a vessel bound across the Great Sea. Describing Kalimdor as an uncharted realm of fortune and opportunity, Flint directs bold wanderers to Auberdine to meet his associate, an elf named Fiora Longears.",sp=0},{t="Arrival in Auberdine",b="Crossing the ocean brings travelers to Darkshore, a misty, storm-swept coast governed by the night elves. Waiting on the wooden docks of Auberdine, Fiora Longears receives arrivals recommended by Flint. Trusting Flint's eye for character, Fiora welcomes newly arrived Alliance heroes and prepares to direct them inland toward the ancient forests of Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is a high elf stationed at the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore. She acts as a welcoming partner and contact for Red Jack Flint, greeting Alliance travelers arriving from the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"fiora longears","who is fiora"},it="identity"},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="The quest is offered by Red Jack Flint, an energetic human sailor located in Menethil Harbor along the coast of the Wetlands.",al={"quest giver","where to get fiora longears quest","who gives quest"},gp=true},{q="How do I reach Fiora Longears from Menethil Harbor?",a="Board the passenger vessel docked at Menethil Harbor that sails westward across the Great Sea directly to the harbor town of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"how to get to auberdine","ship to auberdine","boat from menethil"},gp=true},{q="What happens after meeting Fiora Longears?",a="Upon greeting you in Auberdine, Fiora commends Flint's recommendation and offers the next leg of your journey, sending you inland to Astranaar in Ashenvale.",al={"what comes next","follow up quest","journey to astranaar quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the relationship between Red Jack Flint and Fiora Longears?",a="Flint refers to Fiora as his partner across the sea. While Flint scouts eager adventurers in the Eastern Kingdoms, Fiora receives them in Kalimdor to facilitate Alliance operations and travel inland.",al={"are flint and fiora partners","red jack flint fiora connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Alliance recruiting travelers to Kalimdor?",a="Kalimdor represents vast new territory and resources for the Alliance, as well as a front where night elven allies need assistance protecting their ancestral lands from threats like the Horde and demonic remnants.",al={"why go to kalimdor","why darkshore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Red Jack Flint want to send you to Kalimdor?",a="Red Jack Flint sees himself as an agent of opportunity, tasked with inspiring promising adventurers in Menethil Harbor to cross the Great Sea. Bound to the docks himself and longing for ocean voyages, his role is to spot hardy souls and direct them to his night elf partner, Fiora Longears, who helps newcomers find their footing and take up the Alliance's burgeoning efforts across Kalimdor.",al={"red jack flint motive","why send me to fiora","why does jack flint want this done"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This journey represents the bridge between the Eastern Kingdoms and the night elven territories of Kalimdor, uniting the Alliance's eastern and western frontiers.",["race:NightElf"]="Fiora Longears serves as an official welcoming presence for eastern allies arriving at Auberdine, preparing them for the ancient wilds of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","fiora longears","kalimdor","menethil harbor","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"npc:red-jack-flint","subzone:auberdine","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore","quest:1133","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Red Jack Flint",["end"]="Fiora Longears",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1132},src={"Fiora Longears (quest)"}}
E["quest:1135"] = {t="quest",n="Highperch Venom",z="darkshore",s="Fiora Longears in Auberdine tasks Alliance adventurers with journeying far south to the canyons of Thousand Needles. There, atop the elevated bluffs of Highperch, roost dangerous wyverns prized for their exceptionally potent venom.",h="Fiora Longears in Auberdine tasks Alliance adventurers with journeying far south to the canyons of Thousand...",sec={{t="A Lucrative Expedition",b="While resting in the seaside port of Auberdine, travelers may cross paths with Fiora Longears. While orcs commonly capture and domesticate wyverns as aerial mounts, Fiora points out a far more clandestine trade: the creature's lethal venom. Certain buyers across Kalimdor value fresh venom sacs far more than the beasts themselves, prompting Fiora to recruit hunters willing to brave long distances and precarious heights.",sp=0},{t="The Crags of Highperch",b="The quarry nests far south of Darkshore, within the towering sandstone mesas of Thousand Needles. At a roost known as Highperch, the local wyverns possess an unusually concentrated toxin. Reaching their nests requires navigating hostile Horde territory and scaling treacherous terrain, where hunters must slay wyverns to extract intact venom sacs before hauling the prize back to Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the wyverns for this quest?",a="The wyverns inhabit Highperch, a tall mesa nestled in the western stretches of Thousand Needles, far south of Darkshore.",al={"highperch location","where is highperch","wyvern location"},gp=true},{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is an Alliance contact stationed in Auberdine on the Darkshore coast. She recruits daring adventurers to procure rare and valuable natural reagents from across Kalimdor.",al={"fiora longears","who gives highperch venom"},it="identity"},{q="Why is wyvern venom so valuable?",a="Wyvern venom is extremely potent and prized in select underground circles, apothecaries, and trade networks. While the Horde primarily values wyverns as aerial mounts, their venom glands fetch a handsome price among alchemists and poison-makers.",al={"why wyvern venom","wyvern poison use"},it="power"},{q="Why is an Auberdine quest sending me so far south?",a="Fiora is an enterprising dealer seeking exotic specimens that cannot be found along the calm shores of Darkshore. Highperch in Thousand Needles harbors a distinct, concentrated breed of wyvern not found in the northern forests.",al={"why thousand needles","why send to thousand needles"},it="place"},{q="What happens when you return the venom sacs?",a="Fiora inspects the sacs and notes they are bursting with venom, remarking that such quality usually only comes from young wyverns or fertile females, congratulating you on the hunt.",al={"fiora reaction","quest completion highperch venom"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Highperch safe for Alliance travelers?",a="No. Thousand Needles contains heavy Horde presence, centering around nearby settlements like Freewind Post. Scaling Highperch means contending with both wild predators and hostile Horde scouts.",al={"is highperch dangerous","alliance in thousand needles"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Fiora Longears want this done?",a="Fiora has an eye for lucrative commerce and rare reagents. While most know wyverns only as beasts of burden tamed by the Horde, she knows that certain circles pay dearly for potent venom. Harvesting the sacs from Highperch allows her to turn a handsome profit in those specialized markets.",al={"why does fiora want venom","fiora longears motive","why harvest wyvern venom"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Highperch Venom Sac for?",a="The venom sacs contain the deadly, potent toxin of the wild wyverns that nest upon the heights of Thousand Needles. Highly prized by select alchemists, poisoners, and exotic traders, these bursting sacs fetch an enormous price in markets dealing in rare and dangerous beasts.",al={"what are highperch venom sacs for","venom sac use","why collect venom sacs"},it="item",add=true},{q="What are the creatures nesting at Highperch?",a="Highperch is a towering mesa in Thousand Needles that serves as a wild roost for native wyverns. Untamed and fiercely territorial, these winged predators glide the desert canyons, using their venomous stingers to fell prey before dragging meals up to their rocky aeries.",al={"what are highperch wyverns","who are you hunting at highperch","what live at highperch"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Rogues naturally understand the dark allure of exotic toxins. Sourcing pure, unrefined wyvern venom gives an intimate appreciation for Kalimdor's deadliest biological agents.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, sending hunters deep into the arid barrens of Thousand Needles highlights how far trade interests and curious reagents reach outside Ashenvale and Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Venturing into Thousand Needles places Alliance adventurers deep behind enemy lines, right beneath the watchful eyes of the Horde's tauren and orc patrols."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fiora","highperch","longears","thousand needles","venom","wyvern"},rel={"quest:1132","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Fiora Longears",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1135,ri={"Highperch Venom Sac"}},src={"Highperch Venom"}}
E["quest:1138"] = {t="quest",n="Fruit of the Sea",z="darkshore",s="Fruit of the Sea is an Alliance quest offered by the fisherman Gubber Blump on the docks of Auberdine. Passionate about culinary crustacean dishes, Gubber asks travelers to scour the Darkshore coastline for fine crab chunks while he tends to his fishing lines.",h="Fruit of the Sea is an Alliance quest offered by the fisherman Gubber Blump on the docks of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Passion for Crustaceans",b="Gubber Blump, a fisherman casting his line off the long wooden piers of Auberdine, harbors an obsessive culinary devotion to crab meat. Viewing crabs as the true bounty of the ocean, Gubber envisions an endless repertoire of recipes ranging from baked, barbecued, and boiled preparations to elaborate local specialties like whipper root crab and Ironforge surprise crab.",sp=0},{t="Combing the Tidepools",b="Because Gubber cannot tear himself away from his fishing rod, he relies on passing adventurers to gather ingredients along Darkshore's mist-shrouded beaches. The coastline teems with reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers scuttling among the breakers, making them an accessible, if occasionally pinch-happy, source of meat for an aspiring coastal cook.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Fruit of the Sea?",a="The quest is given by Gubber Blump, an Alliance fisherman stationed on the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"fruit of the sea quest giver","who gives fruit of the sea","gubber blump quest"},it="people",gp=true},{q="What creatures drop the Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Fine Crab Chunks are harvested from reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers found walking the shores and shallow surf along the Darkshore coastline.",al={"where do fine crab chunks drop","what drops crab chunks","which crabs drop fine crab chunks"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Gubber gather the crab meat himself?",a="Gubber is fully occupied fishing from the piers of Auberdine and cannot abandon his line to hunt crawling crabs along the beach.",al={"why doesn't gubber get his own crab","why does gubber need help"},it="why_me"},{q="What dishes does Gubber want to make?",a="Gubber boasts about an enormous variety of preparation styles, including crab salad, soup, stew, pepper crab, lemon crab, whipper root crab, and a regional recipe he calls Ironforge surprise crab.",al={"gubber crab recipes","what recipes does gubber mention","crab dishes"},it="motive"},{q="Is Gubber Blump's speech referencing something?",a="Yes. His monologue cataloging every conceivable method to cook crab is a clear homage to Benjamin Buford 'Bubba' Blue from the film Forrest Gump, who famously delivered an identical speech about shrimp.",al={"gubber blump pop culture reference","forrest gump bubba reference"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest begins and turns in at the port village of Auberdine, with the hunting taking place along the shores of Darkshore in northern Kalimdor.",al={"where is fruit of the sea","what zone is fruit of the sea in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the Fine Crab Chunks for?",a="Gubber Blump intends to use them in an endless variety of culinary dishes. To him, crabs are the fruit of the sea, perfect for baking, barbecuing, boiling, broiling, frying, and mixing into soups, stews, and salads.",al={"fine crab chunks use","why fine crab chunks","what does gubber do with crab chunks"},it="item",add=true},{q="What are the crawlers along Darkshore's coast?",a="Reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers are native crustaceans that scavenge Darkshore's long, misty coastlines and shallow tide pools. While dangerous to careless beachcombers, their meat is prized by fishermen and cooks like Gubber Blump for rich coastal feasts.",al={"what are reef crawlers","encrusted tide crawlers darkshore","darkshore crabs"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gubber's enthusiastic breakdown of crab recipes serves as inspiration for any cook looking to make the most of local coastal catches.",["race:Dwarf"]="Hearing an outsider in northern Kalimdor dream about cooking an 'Ironforge surprise crab' is a quaint reminder of home for traveling Khaz Modan mountaineers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as a vital landing hub for Alliance explorers arriving in Kalimdor, offering small favors like helping local fishermen settle in."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","encrusted tide crawlers","fine crab chunks","fruit of the sea","gubber blump","reef crawlers"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Gubber Blump",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=1138,ri={"Fine Crab Chunks"}},src={"Fruit of the Sea"}}
E["quest:1140"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest represents the sixth chapter in the crusade against the cultists of the Tower of Althalaxx, directed by Delgren the Purifier from Maestra's Post. Delgren deciphers orcish writings recovered from the cult's emissaries to reveal that the warlock Athrikus Narassin has hidden two trapped Highborne soulgems inside demonic satyr strongholds deep in Ashenvale. Champions are dispatched to Night Run and Satyrnaar to shatter these vessels, freeing the tormented ancient spirits and shattering Athrikus's dark source of power.",h="This quest represents the sixth chapter in the crusade against the cultists of the Tower of Althalaxx...",sec={{t="Deciphering the Scribblings",b="After cutting down the orcish courier Ilkrud Magthrull, Delgren the Purifier puts his controversial studies of the Orcish tongue to good use. While his peers in the Holy Light often scoffed at learning the language of their adversaries, Delgren's pragmatic insight unravels the cult's clandestine trade. The notes reveal that Athrikus Narassin secured two potent soulgems containing the essences of ancient Highborne, hiding them far to the northeast within the defiled groves of Night Run and Satyrnaar.",sp=0},{t="Unholy Alliances",b="The presence of Highborne soulgems inside satyr encampments exposes a foul convergence between Athrikus's dark cabal and the demonic scions of the Burning Legion. Bound above ritual circles of imprisonment, these ancient spirits suffer endless torment to fuel dark spellcraft. Venturing into the blood-soaked altars of the satyr requires confronting not only wild demonic corruption, but the lurking daggers of hidden satyr stalkers sworn to guard these arcane conduits.",sp=1},{t="Weakening Athrikus",b="By smashing the crimson stones and liberating the Highborne souls from their circles of agony, adventurers strike a devastating blow to Athrikus's reservoir of mystic strength. Delgren notes that with these soulgems destroyed, the leader of the Althalaxx cult is severely weakened. The deed also leaves the holy crusader unsettled by the night elves' quiet unease regarding the satyrs, prompting him to resolve to bring the lingering demonic blight to the attention of Auberdine's leaders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Delgren know how to read Orcish?",a="Delgren took the initiative to study the language of the orcs, despite being ridiculed by others in his holy order. He believes that understanding an enemy's tongue is vital to gaining tactical insight, which directly allows him to translate the recovered notes from Ilkrud Magthrull.",al={"delgren reads orc","how does delgren know orcish","delgren translation"}},{q="What are the soulgems and why are they held by satyrs?",a="The soulgems are crimson focus stones binding the ancient spirits of Highborne elves, suspended over ritual circles of imprisonment. Athrikus Narassin bargained or placed them within satyr sanctuaries like Night Run and Satyrnaar, drawing upon their misery to fuel the cult's arcane power.",al={"althalaxx soulgems","why do satyrs have the gems","trapped highborne souls"}},{q="Where are Night Run and Satyrnaar located?",a="Both locations are demonic satyr strongholds nestled in the forested heights of northeastern Ashenvale, east of Maestra's Post.",al={"where is night run","where is satyrnaar","satyr camp locations"},gp=true},{q="Why are the night elves reluctant to talk about the satyrs?",a="Delgren notices that his elven hosts avoid discussing the satyrs because the creatures were once night elves themselves. The satyrs were warped into goat-legged fiends during the ancient War of the Ancients after surrendering to demonic corruption, making their existence an enduring source of grief and shame for the Kaldorei.",al={"why secretive about satyr","night elf satyr connection","satyr history elven"}},{q="How does freeing these souls help stop the Tower of Althalaxx cult?",a="Athrikus Narassin relies heavily on the stolen spiritual energy held within the Highborne soulgems. Shattering the floating gems and releasing the trapped ghosts starves his rituals of power, leaving him vulnerable to a direct assault at the tower.",al={"why shatter soulgems","athrikus power source","weakening athrikus"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Elissa that Delgren mentions speaking to?",a="Elissa Starbreeze is a prominent night elf Sentinel stationed in Auberdine who coordinates local defenses in Darkshore. Delgren plans to confer with her regarding the entrenched satyr infestation threatening northern Kalimdor.",al={"elissa auberdine","who is elissa","delgren elissa"}},{q="Who are you sent against to free the Highborne souls?",a="You are sent deep into the corrupted ruins of Night Run and Satyrnaar against the satyrs who hold the soulgems. These demonic servants of the Burning Legion have allied with Athrikus Narassin and his dark cult, keeping the ancient Highborne souls imprisoned within floating red gems above their dark circles of imprisonment.",al={"who are you fighting","who guards the soulgems","satyrs in night run and satyrnaar"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier send you instead of going himself?",a="Delgren the Purifier is stationed at Maestra's Post, coordinating the defense and intelligence against cultist and demonic incursions across the border. Infiltrating deep into fortified satyr strongholds like Night Run and Satyrnaar requires a seasoned adventurer who can slip past enemy lines and shatter the gems without pulling an entire garrison away from the outpost.",al={"why does delgren need me","why cant delgren go","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Delgren the Purifier reflects a pragmatic brand of holy crusader, using the language of his foes to unearth demonic corruption and cleanse the tormented dead.",["race:NightElf"]="Liberating Highborne ancestors from satyr desecration is a solemn duty, confronting the tragic remnants of your people's ancient past.",["class:Priest"]="Shattering the circles of imprisonment brings peace to anguished spirits suffering centuries of demonic torment."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","athrikus","delgren","highborne","maestra's post","night run","satyrnaar","soulgems"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:night-run","subzone:satyrnaar","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1140},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (6)"}}
E["quest:1141"] = {t="quest",n="The Family and the Fishing Pole",z="darkshore",s="Gubber Blump, a dwarf dwelling on the docks of Auberdine, seeks assistance catching native Darkshore grouper. Hostile murlocs prowling the coast have disrupted the town's small fishing boats, leaving Gubber stranded on shore and offering an heirloom rod to anyone willing to cast their line.",h="Gubber Blump, a dwarf dwelling on the docks of Auberdine, seeks assistance catching native Darkshore grouper.",sec={{t="A Dwarf Far From Ironforge",b="Gubber Blump takes great pride in his lineage, declaring that the Blump name has long been synonymous with the art of angling. While night elves occupy most of Auberdine, dwarves and gnomes have settled into its docks and bustling port facilities. Rather than digging into stone, Gubber spends his days gazing out over the misty waters of the Veiled Sea, eager to haul in the local bounty.",sp=0},{t="Murloc Infestations and Darkshore Grouper",b="The Darkshore grouper is a prized coastal fish, versatile in cooking and famously spirited on the line. Normally, local fishermen would row small craft out into deeper waters to haul them in. However, the aggressive arrival of coastal murlocs has brought civilian boat traffic to a standstill. Fearing the creatures are devouring all the local fish stocks, Gubber recruits travelers willing to angle from the shoreline.",sp=0},{t="The Blump Legacy",b="To reward those who bring him a hearty catch, Gubber parts with a Blump Family Fishing Pole. By his estimation, anyone capable of hauling in a batch of feisty groupers measures up to the legendary anglers of his bloodline—including his bearded, sharp-scented cousin Graun Blump. To a dwarf of his eccentric tastes, handing over a family rod is the ultimate sign of respect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gubber Blump?",a="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fisherman stationed on the docks of Auberdine in Darkshore. Hailing from a proud family of anglers, he teaches basic fishing techniques and passes down his family's signature rods to promising fishermen.",al={"who is gubber","gubber blump lore","auberdine dwarf fisherman"},it="identity"},{q="Why aren't boats going out from Auberdine to fish?",a="Hostile murlocs have overrun large stretches of the Darkshore coastline. Their aggressive presence has made launching small personal fishing crafts far too dangerous, keeping local anglers pinned to the piers and shallows.",al={"why no boats","darkshore fishing boats","auberdine boat trouble"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Darkshore grouper?",a="It is a native saltwater fish found off the misty coast of Darkshore. Anglers prize the grouper for both the challenge of landing one and its versatility in various hearty coastal recipes.",al={"darkshore grouper","grouper darkshore"}},{q="Who is Graun Blump?",a="Graun is Gubber Blump's cousin. According to Gubber, she possesses a full beard, smells rather pungent, and stands among the finest anglers their family has ever produced.",al={"graun blump","gubber cousin"},it="ties"},{q="Why are there dwarves in a night elf town like Auberdine?",a="Following the Third War and the forging of the Alliance, Ironforge dwarves and gnomes traveled across the sea to Kalimdor to trade, establish maritime links, and assist their new night elf allies with harbor infrastructure.",al={"why dwarves in auberdine","dwarves in darkshore"},it="arrival"},{q="What is the Blump Family Fishing Pole?",a="It is a sturdy fishing rod crafted and used by the Blump clan. Gubber bestows these treasured poles upon travelers who prove they have genuine angling talent along Darkshore's waters.",al={"blump fishing pole","blump family rod","gubber reward pole"},it="power"},{q="Why does Gubber Blump want Darkshore grouper?",a="Gubber comes from a proud lineage of dwarf fishermen and genuinely loves the craft. He normally sails out onto the bay to catch Darkshore grouper, but the recent arrival of aggressive murlocs has halted boat traffic entirely. Worried that the murlocs are gorging themselves on the local stock, Gubber is eager to secure some grouper and see another promising angler carry on good fishing practices.",al={"gubber blump motive","why does gubber want fish","why catch grouper"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Darkshore Grouper used for?",a="Darkshore grouper make for fine eating and can be prepared in a variety of local recipes. While Gubber admits that they make plenty of tasty dishes, he personally cares far more about the thrill of hooking and reeling them in than eating them.",al={"what are darkshore grouper for","darkshore grouper use","grouper purpose"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Finding a fellow dwarf passionately dedicated to fishing rather than subterranean smithing or brewing is an eccentric reminder of your people's varied pursuits.",["profession:Cooking"]="Darkshore grouper makes for a reliable, nutritious catch along the northern Kalimdor coast, serving as a staple ingredient for frontier camp meals.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as a vital Alliance port on Kalimdor, where mainland races and night elves cooperate daily against coastal hazards like murlocs."},kw={"auberdine","blump family fishing pole","darkshore grouper","fishing","graun blump","gubber blump","murloc","veiled sea"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle"},m={start="Gubber Blump",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=1141,ri={"Darkshore Grouper"}},src={"The Family and the Fishing Pole"}}
E["quest:1143"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks the direct assault on Athrikus Narassin, the ancient dark sorcerer holding the pinnacle of the Tower of Althalaxx. Under the direction of Balthule Shadowstrike, an Alliance operative must breach the ruined keep and execute the cabal's master. Eliminating Athrikus strikes a devastating blow to the demonic worship corrupting northern Darkshore.",h="This quest marks the direct assault on Athrikus Narassin, the ancient dark sorcerer holding the pinnacle of...",sec={{t="Breaching the Summit",b="Perched upon the ruined heights of northern Darkshore, the Tower of Althalaxx has become a foul center of demonic summoning. Balthule Shadowstrike, monitoring the ruin from nearby, determines that the time to act is immediate. At the tower's peak dwells Athrikus Narassin, an ancient and formidable night elven warlock who orchestrates the dark rituals taking place beneath its shattered stone roof.",sp=0},{t="A Decisive Strike",b="Athrikus surrounds himself with loyal warlocks and dark magic far deadlier than the cultists patrolling the slopes below. Striking down the master cultist requires cutting through his inner circle and securing his severed head as proof. While Balthule notes that the demonic presence may one day seek to regroup, Athrikus's demise robs the cult of its commanding intellect and buys precious safety for Darkshore.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Athrikus Narassin?",a="Athrikus Narassin is an ancient night elf warlock commanding the cultists stationed at the Tower of Althalaxx. He directs the dark summonings and demonic rites infesting the ruins in northern Darkshore.",al={"athrikus","who is athrikus","boss of althalaxx"},it="target"},{q="Where can Athrikus Narassin be found?",a="Athrikus resides at the very top of the Tower of Althalaxx, guarded by a coterie of seasoned warlocks and summoned minions.",al={"where is athrikus","athrikus location","top of althalaxx"},gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike, an Alliance scout camped near the base of the Tower of Althalaxx, issues the mission to slay Athrikus.",al={"quest giver","balthule","balthule shadowstrike"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Delgren mentioned in the quest?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance ally stationed nearby who sent you to coordinate with Balthule to eliminate the demonic cabal.",al={"delgren","delgren the purifier"},it="allies"},{q="What happens after Athrikus is defeated?",a="Balthule confirms that Athrikus's death deals a critical blow to demonic operations in the area, though he warns that the dark forces will eventually regroup.",al={"after athrikus","tower of althalaxx ending"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Tower of Althalaxx dangerous to Darkshore?",a="The cultists and warlocks residing in the tower practice fel sorcery and summon demons into night elven lands, threatening the wilderness and the nearby settlements.",al={"why clean tower","althalaxx threat"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike want Athrikus Narassin killed?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike knows that Athrikus Narassin leads the cabal of cultists and warlocks occupying the ruined Tower of Althalaxx. By striking directly at Athrikus atop the spire, Balthule hopes to shatter their leadership and drive back the demonic forces creeping across northern Darkshore before their corrupt rites spread further.",al={"why kill athrikus","balthule motive","balthule shadowstrike quest reason"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is Athrikus Narassin's Head for?",a="Athrikus Narassin's head serves as irrefutable proof that the ancient warlock has truly been slain. Bringing it back to Balthule Shadowstrike assures him and his allies that the dark master of the tower can no longer command his followers or summon demonic forces into Darkshore.",al={"athrikus narassin head use","why bring athrikus head","athrikus head quest item"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Balthule send you to face Athrikus instead of going himself?",a="Athrikus resides at the very summit of the tower, surrounded by his deadliest warlocks. While Balthule considers waiting for Delgren the Purifier's reinforcements, Delgren placed his absolute faith in your proven combat prowess by sending you in the first place, leaving you as their best chance to strike swiftly before the cultists reinforce.",al={"why me balthule","why doesnt balthule fight athrikus","why send me alone"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Confronting Athrikus Narassin represents a bitter reminder of the arcane and demonic corruption that once devastated night elven civilization.",["class:Warlock"]="Athrikus commands potent demonic magic from the summit of Althalaxx, serving as a lethal example of how unbound fel worship draws lethal attention.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing northern Darkshore from demonic cultists is vital to protecting Alliance travel corridors between Auberdine and the lands beyond."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus","balthule","darkshore","demonic","narassin","shadowstrike","warlock"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","quest:494","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=1143,ri={"Athrikus Narassin's Head"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (8)"}}
E["quest:1167"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks the tense pause before confronting Athrikus Narassin at the Tower of Althalaxx. Sent northward by Delgren the Purifier, adventurers reconvene with the scout Balthule Shadowstrike to gather intelligence on erratic, dark occurrences rocking the spire.",h="This quest marks the tense pause before confronting Athrikus Narassin at the Tower of Althalaxx.",sec={{t="A Scout's Report",b="After purifying corrupted relics and unraveling the cult's grip along Darkshore's border, Delgren the Purifier dispatches you back north to consult his sentinel partner, Balthule Shadowstrike. Before assaulting the sorcerer Athrikus directly, Delgren recognizes the necessity of fresh battlefield reconnaissance, trusting Balthule's tireless watch from the ruins overlooking the tower.",sp=0},{t="Disturbances in the Spire",b="Upon reaching Balthule's vigil, the scout describes an alarming escalation within the upper sanctum. Sudden flashes of blinding luminescence, agonizing screams cutting through the mist, and erratic strikes of lightning have begun to violently wrack the ancient elven tower, heralding an unstable and dangerous climax to Athrikus's dark work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Delgren send me back to Balthule?",a="Delgren knows that charging blindly into Athrikus's lair is reckless. Balthule has been keeping constant eyes on the Tower of Althalaxx, making him the only one who knows what Athrikus and his cultists have been doing in recent moments.",al={"why see balthule","talk to balthule","delgren orders"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Balthule Shadowstrike located?",a="Balthule maintains an observation campsite on the hills just west of the Tower of Althalaxx, watching the ruins in northern Darkshore.",al={"balthule location","find balthule","where is balthule"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What recent events did Balthule witness at the tower?",a="Balthule witnessed a blinding flash erupting from the tower's uppermost chamber, followed by wretched screams carrying across the coast and erratic bolts of lightning striking the ground.",al={"what happened at the tower","balthule screams","tower flash"}},{q="Who is Athrikus?",a="Athrikus Narassin is the dark sorcerer leading the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx, whose fell rituals Delgren and Balthule are determined to stop.",al={"who is athrikus","athrikus narassin","tower boss"},it="identity"},{q="Is Delgren the Purifier a local night elf?",a="No, Delgren is a human paladin and warrior of the Holy Light stationed on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale, allied with night elf scouts to purge demonic corruption.",al={"who is delgren","delgren race","is delgren an elf"},it="identity"},{q="What kind of ruin is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="It is a highborne or ancient night elf spire along the craggy northern cliffs of Darkshore, long abandoned before fallen arcanists and demonic cultists claimed it for forbidden rites.",al={"althalaxx background","what is the tower","tower lore"},it="place"},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want this done?",a="Delgren the Purifier is dedicated to rooting out dark, corrupting magic and demonic influence. The cultists occupying the Tower of Althalaxx threaten the sanctity of Darkshore with their sinister rituals. Delgren wants Athrikus stopped before the sorcerer can unleash whatever horrors he is preparing, but he knows a reckless assault could be fatal without intelligence on the tower's latest defenses.",al={"delgren motive","why does delgren care","delgren purpose tower"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The coordination between Delgren and Balthule represents a practical wartime partnership between human paladins and night elf scouts to keep northern Kalimdor safe.",["class:Paladin"]="Delgren's calculated approach demonstrates the discipline expected of warriors of the Light, favoring vigilant intelligence before rushing into unholy sanctums.",["race:NightElf"]="Balthule Shadowstrike defends ancestral lands from sorcery that mirrors the reckless arcane excesses that ruined night elf civilization ten millennia ago."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus","balthule","cultists","darkshore","delgren","tower"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",["end"]="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1167},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (7)"}}
E["quest:1442"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking the Kor Gem",z="darkshore",s="\"Seeking the Kor Gem\" is an Alliance paladin quest that sends an initiate deep into the ancient ruins of northern Kalimdor. Directed by the night elf Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, paladins venture into Blackfathom Deeps to wrest a potent Kor gem from the naga who corrupt it. The retrieved stone serves as a key material in Jordan Stilwell's craft.",h="\"Seeking the Kor Gem\" is an Alliance paladin quest that sends an initiate deep into the ancient ruins of...",sec={{t="A Trusted Alliance",b="When paladins in training seek the materials needed by the human smith Jordan Stilwell, their journey crosses continental borders to Darkshore. There, at Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver remembers the blacksmith with respect. Despite the natural aloofness of the night elves and the transgressions of certain fallen human figures, Thundris holds faith in paladins pursuing a righteous path and willingly reveals where such ancient gems are found.",sp=0},{t="Into the Deeps",b="The search leads directly to the subterranean temple complex of Blackfathom Deeps along the foggy northwestern coast of Ashenvale. Inhabited by Twilight's Hammer cultists and treacherous sea-dwellers, the watery depths are also home to naga priestesses who channel foul magic through ancient Kor gems. A paladin must brave these dark halls, defeat the sorceresses, and secure a gem steeped in serpentine malice.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Stone",b="Returning a corrupted Kor gem to Thundris Windweaver reveals the true purpose of seeking out an elven mystic. While the naga imbue the gem with raw magical potency, their enchantments twist it toward evil. Before Jordan Stilwell can forge it into a holy weapon, Thundris must excise the darkness, ensuring its power remains pure and stable for the sacred smithing ritual ahead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Kor Gem?",a="The quest is given by Thundris Windweaver, a night elf located in the coastal port of Auberdine in Darkshore. He directs paladins on behalf of the weaponsmith Jordan Stilwell.",al={"quest giver seeking kor gem","who gives seeking the kor gem","thundris windweaver quest"},it="arrival"},{q="Where is the Kor Gem located?",a="The gem is found inside Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient subterranean dungeon located in northwestern Ashenvale along the coast. It is carried by the naga priestesses inhabiting the ruins.",al={"kor gem location","where to get kor gem","where is corrupted kor gem"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Jordan Stilwell need a Kor Gem?",a="The gem contains potent magical energies required as a component for crafting Jordan's refined weapon during the paladin trial known as The Test of Righteousness.",al={"why kor gem","what is kor gem for","stilwell gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Thundris have to purify the gem?",a="The naga imbue Kor gems with substantial arcane power, but their foul nature taints the magic. Thundris purifies the gem of this corruption so that its remaining strength can be safely channeled into a weapon of the Light.",al={"why purify kor gem","corrupted kor gem cleansed","cleansing the gem"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Thundris mention a 'fallen kind'?",a="Thundris is likely alluding to high-profile human betrayals, such as Prince Arthas Menethil, whose descent into darkness tarnished the reputation of the Silver Hand across Azeroth. Despite this, Thundris chooses to judge individual paladins by their own merit.",al={"who is the fallen one","thundris fallen kind","fallen paladin reference"},it="history"},{q="Do I need a group to get the Kor Gem?",a="Thundris explicitly warns adventurers not to go alone. Because the gem drops from elite naga deep inside Blackfathom Deeps, entering with a dedicated adventuring party is strongly advised.",al={"is kor gem soloable","can you solo kor gem","blackfathom deeps group"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want this done?",a="Thundris Windweaver remembers Jordan Stilwell from long ago as a man of modest, honorable character. Although Kor gems are perilous and inherently steeped in dark magic, Thundris trusts that Stilwell's purpose is noble. Recognizing you as a champion walking a holy path, he agrees to help locate and cleanse the artifact so Stilwell can complete his work safely, ensuring its foul energies are stripped away before it is ever used.",al={"thundris motive","why does thundris help","why help stilwell"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Corrupted Kor Gem for?",a="The Corrupted Kor Gem is an arcane focus imbued with dark power by the naga dwelling in the submerged ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Jordan Stilwell requires a Kor gem as an essential component for forging his masterwork weapon. However, before it can serve a righteous weapon, the gemstone's vile naga corruption must be cleansed while preserving its raw inner potency for Stilwell's crafting ritual.",al={"what is kor gem for","corrupted kor gem use","purpose of kor gem"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who holds the Kor Gem in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The gem is held by the naga who have infested the sunken elven shrine of Blackfathom Deeps along the coast of Ashenvale. These serpentine creatures prize the Kor gems, imbuing them with foul, shadowy power to fuel their own sinister rites in the flooded depths.",al={"who has the kor gem","kor gem target","who drops kor gem"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="This quest is an essential trial of character and endurance for an Alliance paladin, testing your willingness to travel into hostile Kalimdor depths to forge a consecrated arm of the Light.",["race:NightElf"]="Thundris Windweaver's cooperation highlights the fragile yet growing bridge between the ancient Kaldorei and the newly allied practitioners of the Holy Light from the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="The mission illustrates Alliance unity in action, as a human blacksmith relies on night elf wisdom and dwarven steel to craft armaments against rising darkness."},kw={"auberdine","blackfathom deeps","darkshore","jordan stilwell","kor gem","naga","paladin","test of righteousness","thundris windweaver"},rel={"quest:1653","zone:blackfathom","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:naga"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1442,ri={"Corrupted Kor Gem"}},src={"Seeking the Kor Gem"}}
E["quest:1579"] = {t="quest",n="Gaffer Jacks",z="darkshore",s="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome inventor nursing a hangover in Auberdine, needs help retrieving a box of lost hardware he tossed into the sea. Having fled the clatter of Ironforge for the quiet shores of Kalimdor, he managed to drop his vital gaffer jacks overboard during the voyage. Anyone with a fishing rod and patience can dredge up these missing components along the coastline.",h="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome inventor nursing a hangover in Auberdine, needs help retrieving a box of lost...",sec={{t="A Cluttered Mind in a Quiet Haven",b="Seeking peace and quiet away from the deafening clatter of Ironforge's Great Forge, the eccentric gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle sailed across the Great Sea to Darkshore. Unfortunately, Wizbang indulged in a bit too much drink during the crossing. While leaning over the railing in an alcoholic haze, he managed to lose an entire crate of specialized metal components known as gaffer jacks into the coastal waters outside Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Tuning the Stintle Pegs",b="Gaffer jacks might look like obscure bits of metallic scrap to ordinary passersby, but to Wizbang they are indispensable precision tools. Without them, he claims it is entirely impossible to properly calibrate his stintle pegs or proceed with any of his delicate tinkering. Reluctant to plunge into the cold ocean surf himself, the gnome relies on local anglers to cast their lines along the Darkshore surf and fish up the scattered hardware.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are gaffer jacks?",a="Gaffer jacks are small gnomish mechanical fasteners and components. According to Wizbang Cranktoggle, they are vital specialized tools used specifically for tuning stintle pegs in his tinkering projects.",al={"what is a gaffer jack","gaffer jack use","gaffer jacks item"},it="item"},{q="How did the gaffer jacks end up in the sea?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle had a bit too much to drink while traveling by ship from the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor. While intoxicated aboard the vessel, he accidentally dropped his supply box overboard near the coast of Darkshore.",al={"how did he lose them","why are they in the water","why fish for gaffer jacks"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine instead of Ironforge?",a="Wizbang sought out Auberdine specifically for its silence and tranquility. He found the constant clatter, ringing anvils, and noisy workshops of Ironforge unbearable, particularly while nursing the persistent hangovers from his heavy drinking.",al={"why is wizbang in auberdine","why did wizbang leave ironforge"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can the lost gaffer jacks be fished up?",a="They can be fished out of the open saltwater along the Darkshore coastline near Auberdine. Anglers reel them in from regular coastal water casts rather than distinct schools of fish.",al={"where do i fish gaffer jacks","gaffer jacks location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after recovering the gaffer jacks?",a="Once Wizbang has his gaffer jacks returned to tune his pegs, he reveals that he also managed to lose another critical set of equipment in the sea: his electropellers, which require further fishing or diving to retrieve.",al={"what next after gaffer jacks","quest after gaffer jacks"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizbang need adventurers instead of retrieving them himself?",a="Between his throbbing hangover and lack of sea angling gear, Wizbang prefers to stay safely dry on the Auberdine docks, leaving the tedious dredging work to any passerby with a fishing rod.",al={"why cant wizbang get them","why doesnt wizbang fish"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want the gaffer jacks recovered?",a="Wizbang traveled all the way from Ironforge to Darkshore seeking peace and quiet to work on his inventions. Unfortunately, his clumsy drunken mishap on the voyage left his essential supplies resting at the bottom of the sea. Without those gaffer jacks, his tinkertastic work comes to an immediate halt, as he cannot even tune his stintle pegs without them.",al={"why does wizbang need gaffer jacks","wizbang cranktoggle motive","why help wizbang cranktoggle"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang embodies the restless eccentricity of gnomish tinkerers, though even fellow gnomes might cringe at his reckless combination of high-precision components and heavy drinking.",["profession:Engineering"]="Any engineer knows the misery of missing one tiny, non-standard mechanical component needed to finish calibrating a delicate device.",["race:NightElf"]="The quiet, sacred woods of Darkshore make an odd destination for an abrasive, hungover gnome inventor, testing the legendary patience of Auberdine's night elf sentinels."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","electropellers","fishing","gaffer jacks","ironforge","stintle pegs","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:1580","quest:1141","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1579,ri={"Gaffer Jack"}},src={"Gaffer Jacks"}}
E["quest:1580"] = {t="quest",n="Electropellers",z="darkshore",s="Electropellers is a lighthearted errand for the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine. After losing his bag of prototype components in Darkshore's freshwater streams during a misadventure with an explosive duck decoy, Wizbang asks passing anglers to fish them back out.",h="Electropellers is a lighthearted errand for the eccentric gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Tipsy Invention",b="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome tinkerer stationed in the quiet night elf port of Auberdine, spent an evening wandering inland Darkshore searching for testing grounds. His latest passion project was a self-propelled, exploding duck decoy. Unfortunately, a bit too much drink led to an untimely blackout. Wizbang woke hours later back in town with singed hair and a completely empty pack, having accidentally dropped his precious bag of electropellers into one of the coastal rivers.",sp=0},{t="Dredging the Waters",b="Rather than brave the wilds himself to retrieve his scattered mechanical parts, Wizbang calls upon local fishermen to dredge the freshwater streams of Darkshore. Anglers casting lines across waterways like the Wildbend River and Cliffspring River frequently snag these buoyant, metallic gizmos alongside the local fish. Recovering the components allows the oblivious gnome to resume his dangerously erratic waterfowl experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the electropellers?",a="They must be fished out of Darkshore's freshwater rivers and lakes, such as the Cliffspring River or the Wildbend River. They will not appear in the ocean waters along the coast.",al={"where are electropellers","how to get electropellers","electropeller location"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang is an eccentric gnomish engineer residing in Auberdine. Known for bizarre and explosive inventions, he relies on adventurous travelers to gather lost components and oddities for his experiments.",al={"who gives electropellers","wizbang cranktoggle"},it="identity"},{q="What was Wizbang trying to build?",a="He was working on a self-propelled, exploding duck decoy. His testing went awry after he indulged in a bit too much drink and accidentally detonated an early prototype, scorching his hair and losing his bag of parts in the water.",al={"exploding duck decoy","wizbang project"},it="purpose"},{q="Can electropellers be found in fish schools?",a="No, electropellers are hauled up from open freshwater casts. Casting your line directly into special schools, such as Lesser Oily Blackmouth nodes, will not yield the mechanical parts.",al={"fish schools electropellers","can i fish schools"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="You must first complete Gaffer Jacks, an earlier fishing task Wizbang assigns to test your angling luck in the local waters.",al={"prereq for electropellers","electropellers prerequisite"},gp=true},{q="Are electropellers dropped by monsters?",a="No. They cannot be looted from enemies or found in ground containers; they must be retrieved from the rivers using a fishing pole.",al={"do mobs drop electropellers","who drops electropellers"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want you to recover the electropellers?",a="Wizbang lost his entire bag of components during a drunken misadventure testing inventions along the waterways of Darkshore. He woke up back in Auberdine with singed hair and an empty pack. Without those missing parts, his ongoing engineering research into self-propelled, exploding duck decoys is at a complete standstill.",al={"why does wizbang need electropellers","wizbang motive","why get electropellers"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is an Electropeller used for?",a="Electropellers are specialized mechanical components Wizbang designed for propulsion. Specifically, they serve as the drive mechanism inside his prototype self-propelled, exploding duck decoy, allowing the mechanical decoy to steer and motor through bodies of water before its volatile payload detonates.",al={"what are electropellers","electropeller use","electropeller purpose"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Wizbang ask you to fish for the electropellers instead of doing it himself?",a="Wizbang has already seen proof of your uncanny luck and fishing prowess when you dredged up gaffer jacks for him previously. Having recovered in Auberdine disoriented and singed from his drunken mishap, he prefers relying on a proven angler rather than scouring the wilds of Darkshore on his own.",al={"why me wizbang","why doesn't wizbang fish them up"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's chaotic ambition to build exploding duck decoys is a familiar sight to any gnome, even if losing expensive parts in an elf-guarded river is slightly embarrassing.",["profession:Engineering"]="Electropellers are curious examples of miniaturized gnomish propulsion, designed to drive mechanical decoys before violently combusting.",["race:NightElf"]="Local night elves look upon Wizbang's loud, smoky inventions and river-littering mishaps with quiet disapproval, preferring Darkshore's streams remain natural."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring river","darkshore","duck decoy","electropellers","fishing","wildbend river","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","subzone:auberdine","subzone:wildbend-river","quest:4762","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1580,ri={"Electropeller"}},src={"Electropellers"}}
E["quest:2078"] = {t="quest",n="Gyromast's Revenge",z="darkshore",s="Gelkak Gyromast seeks payback against the local murlocs who plundered his wrecked ship along the Darkshore coastline. To carry out his vendetta, the eccentric captain sends adventurers to reactivate his mechanical first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100.",h="Gelkak Gyromast seeks payback against the local murlocs who plundered his wrecked ship along the Darkshore...",sec={{t="A Captain's Vendetta",b="Stranded upon the misty strands of Darkshore, Gelkak Gyromast refuses to accept defeat at the hands of the shore-dwelling murlocs. Having salvaged the pieces needed to fuel his schemes, the eccentric captain sets his sights on complete retaliation against the tribe and their chief. Rather than wading into the surf with cutlass in hand, Gelkak relies on heavy engineering to exact his vengeance, entrusting a winding key to any landlubber brave enough to handle his mechanical subordinate.",sp=0},{t="The First Mate's Mutiny",b="Gelkak's trusted first mate is no salty dwarf or sailor, but the Threshwackonator 4100—a clanking mechanical golem abandoned in the shallows south of the wreck. While wind-up automation promises an easy slaughter of the murlocs, gnomish and dwarven contraptions are notorious for volatile behavior when exposed to salt water. Upon being wound up and led back to the captain, the construct suffers a catastrophic malfunction, mistaking its rescuer and creator for hostile targets and forcing a battle on the beach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak's first mate?",a="Gelkak's first mate is the Threshwackonator 4100, an automated mechanical golem resting on the coast south of the stranded captain's camp.",al={"first mate","gelkak first mate","who is the first mate"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gelkak want revenge?",a="Gelkak's vessel was shipwrecked along Darkshore, and the native Greymist murlocs scavenged his belongings and harassed his surviving crew. Gelkak intends to use his golem to crush the tribe and their chief.",al={"why revenge","murloc revenge","gelkak motivation"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you bring the Threshwackonator back?",a="Once wound up and led back to Gelkak's camp, the Threshwackonator 4100 suffers an operational malfunction and turns hostile, forcing you to destroy it to protect the area.",al={"threshwackonator attack","robot malfunction","why does the golem attack"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What do I do with Gyromast's Key after finishing the quest?",a="Gyromast's Key serves no further purpose once the Threshwackonator 4100 has been activated and defeated, and it can be safely discarded.",al={"gyromast key use","keep gyromast key","can i delete key"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="Where did Gelkak get the Threshwackonator?",a="The golem is part of the cargo and equipment salvaged from Gelkak's ill-fated voyage along northern Kalimdor, designed as heavy mechanical muscle for his crew.",al={"who built threshwackonator","threshwackonator origin"},it="origin"},{q="Does Gelkak give up after the golem is destroyed?",a="Despite the destruction of his mechanical first mate, Gelkak grudgingly commends your survival, jokingly offering a promotion to poop deck swabby while remaining stranded on the beach.",al={"what happens to gelkak","after gyromast revenge"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Why does Gelkak need you to fetch his first mate instead of going himself?",a="Gelkak is stranded on the beach of Darkshore after a disastrous shipwreck, completely obsessed with recovering his sunken ship's cargo and taking vengeance against the local Greymist murlocs. Having already relied on you to dive for the vital components of his mechanical first mate, he remains camped by his salvaged gear and commands you as a hired crewmate—or in his terms, a landlubber—to start up the contraption and guide it safely back to him.",al={"why me gyromast","why does gelkak need help","why cant gelkak get the golem himself"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Threshwackonator 4100 is a classic example of clockwork automation gone awry after exposure to sea spray and water damage, reinforcing the engineering maxim to always double-check gyro-stabilizers.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes will immediately recognize the folly of trying to reboot sensitive mechanical automata with a simple winding key in the damp, briny environment of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing out malfunctioning machinery and aggressive murlocs helps secure the coastline for Alliance travel between Auberdine and the lands to the south."},kw={"darkshore","gelkak","golem","gyromast","key","murloc","threshwackonator","threshwackonator 4100"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2098","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc"},m={start="Gelkak Gyromast",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2078},src={"Gyromast's Revenge"}}
E["quest:2098"] = {t="quest",n="Gyromast's Retrieval",z="darkshore",s="Shipwrecked on the misty coast of Darkshore, the eccentric gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast seeks aid to restore his mechanical first mate. His vital winding key was shattered upon the rocks and scavenged by the local wildlife and murlocs. Recovering the three pieces is the first step toward getting his crew back in working order.",h="Shipwrecked on the misty coast of Darkshore, the eccentric gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast seeks aid to restore...",sec={{t="Castaway on Darkshore",b="Gelkak Gyromast is an odd sight along the gloomy sands of Darkshore: a gnome pirate stranded far from the typical sea routes of the South Seas. According to Gelkak, his vessel met an unfortunate end just off the coastline after being attacked and sunk by aggressive threshadons. Washing ashore amid the flotsam, he found himself utterly marooned and separated from his trusty crew.",sp=0},{t="The Scavenged Key",b="Gelkak's most pressing concern is not provisions or gold, but his first mate. Activating and operating this companion requires a specialized key, which shattered into three distinct fragments when Gelkak crashed onto the rocky shoals. Before he could gather the fragments, the indigenous wildlife—scuttling reef crawlers on the beach, towering foreststriders near the woods, and scavengers from the local Greymist murloc tribe—snatched the shiny metal pieces away.",sp=0},{t="A Peculiar Companion",b="Gelkak speaks of his first mate with the fierce loyalty of a sea captain, though references to needing to put the companion 'in workin' order' hint at an unorthodox crewmate. A gnome mariner stranded on foreign shores naturally relies on mechanical ingenuity, and reassembling the broken key proves vital to restarting whatever clockwork marvel Gelkak dragged from the depths.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is an eccentric gnome pirate who was shipwrecked off the coast of Darkshore when predatory threshadons attacked and sank his vessel.",al={"gelkak gyromast","who is the gnome pirate","darkshore gnome pirate"},it="identity"},{q="What is the key used for?",a="The key is required to reactivate and wind up Gelkak's first mate, a mechanical creation that was powered down during their disastrous shipwreck.",al={"why does gelkak need the key","gelkak key purpose","first mate key"},it="item"},{q="Where did the three pieces of the key go?",a="When the key broke on the shore, the pieces were scavenged by local creatures: the top piece was taken by foreststriders, the middle by Greymist murlocs, and the bottom by coastal reef crawlers.",al={"where are the key pieces","who stole the key","broken key darkshore"},gp=true},{q="Why was a gnome pirate sailing near Darkshore?",a="Gelkak was navigating the waters off northern Kalimdor in search of plunder, but hostile threshadons brought an abrupt end to his voyage.",al={"why is gelkak in darkshore","pirates in darkshore"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after the key is reassembled?",a="Once Gelkak has all three pieces of his key, he can proceed with winding up his companion, leading directly into the quest 'Gyromast's Revenge'.",al={"what next after key","gyromast retrieval follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are the murlocs holding the key piece?",a="The middle piece is scavenged by the Greymist tribe of murlocs, who have made their home among the wreckage of drowned ships along Darkshore's shoals.",al={"darkshore murlocs","greymist murloc key","shipwreck murlocs"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gelkak Gyromast want his key restored?",a="Gelkak Gyromast was shipwrecked off the coast of Darkshore when threshadons sank his vessel. Left stranded and surrounded by hostile wildlife, he desperately needs his mechanical first mate back in working order to defend himself and enact his revenge against the creatures that wrecked his voyage. Without the three shattered pieces of the winding key, his clockwork companion remains entirely inert.",al={"why gelkak wants key","gelkak gyromast motive","why help gelkak"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Gelkak Gyromast need your help?",a="Gelkak is a marooned pirate with no crew left beside him and no friends among the local night elves. Having barely survived his ship sinking and washing ashore battered on the beach, he is in no shape to battle the vicious reef crawlers, tallstriders, and murlocs that made off with his broken key shards.",al={"why does gelkak need me","why can't gelkak get the key","why me gyromast"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes will immediately recognize Gelkak's reliance on clockwork devices over flesh-and-blood shipmates, even if his pirate lifestyle is quite unusual for their kin.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the challenge of keeping clockwork contraptions functional after enduring a violent shipwreck in saltwater."},kw={"darkshore","first mate","foreststrider","gelkak gyromast","greymist","gyromast's retrieval","pirate","reef crawler","threshadon"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2078","zone:darkshore","topic:pirate","topic:murloc","quest:938"},m={start="Gelkak Gyromast",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2098,ri={"Bottom of Gelkak's Key","Middle of Gelkak's Key","Top of Gelkak's Key"}},src={"Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["quest:2118"] = {t="quest",n="Plagued Lands",z="darkshore",s="Plagued Lands is an Alliance quest offered by Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore. Driven to remedy the spreading corruption afflicting the native wildlife, Tharnariun tasks adventurers with trapping a rabid thistle bear alive using an enchanted relic to attempt a cure.",h="Plagued Lands is an Alliance quest offered by Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Blight on the Wilderness",b="A sinister affliction creeps through Darkshore's woods, twisting its beasts into maddened, aggressive shadows of their former selves. The native thistle bears have suffered the worst of this madness, succumbing to a rabid frenzy that threatens both passing travelers and the fragile ecological harmony of the coast. Where night elf sentinels often respond with steel, the druids seek to understand and heal the root cause.",sp=0},{t="Tharnariun's Hope",b="Refusing to slaughter the corrupted beasts without trying to save them, Tharnariun Treetender fashioned a specialized trap known as Tharnariun's Hope. Adventurers place the device on the forest floor, using its soothing light to temporarily calm a raging thistle bear's mind. Once pacified, the creature meekly follows the traveler back to Tharnariun's outpost for study.",sp=0},{t="Tragic Medicine",b="When an adventurer successfully guides an infected bear into camp, Tharnariun immediately attempts to purge the sickness with restorative magic. Sadly, his initial efforts prove catastrophic: the swirling cleansing energies overwhelm the creature's weakened constitution, causing the beast to collapse and die on the spot. The failure reveals just how deeply the dark plague has taken hold.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Plagued Lands?",a="The quest is given by Tharnariun Treetender, a night elf druid situated in Auberdine in Darkshore who seeks to cure the afflicted wildlife.",al={"quest giver plagued lands","tharnariun darkshore quest","who starts plagued lands"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What is the objective of Plagued Lands?",a="You must use the provided item, Tharnariun's Hope, to trap and pacify a Rabid Thistle Bear in Darkshore, then lead the subdued creature back to Tharnariun alive.",al={"plagued lands goal","what to do in plagued lands","how to catch bear darkshore"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What happens to the bear when you bring it back?",a="Tharnariun attempts to cleanse the animal with healing magic, but the sickness has progressed too deeply. The strain overwhelms the creature, and it dies immediately after the treatment.",al={"does the bear die","tharnariun bear cure result","bear death plagued lands"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What item do you use to capture the bear?",a="Tharnariun provides an enchanted trapping device named Tharnariun's Hope, which emits a calming light that pacifies the enraged bear so it will follow you.",al={"plagued lands trap","tharnariun's hope item","bear cage darkshore"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What quest follows Plagued Lands?",a="Plagued Lands is the first chapter of a three-part chain. Completing it unlocks the follow-up quest, Cleansing of the Infected, which eventually leads to the final quest, Tharnariun's Hope.",al={"next quest after plagued lands","plagued lands chain","tharnariun follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the thistle bears rabid?",a="A creeping, corruptive plague is spreading across Darkshore, poisoning the minds and bodies of the local wildlife and driving noble thistle bears into mindless aggression.",al={"why are bears sick in darkshore","darkshore plague bears","darkshore corruption"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Tharnariun Treetender want you to capture a rabid thistle bear?",a="A dark sickness spreads through Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of the local wildlife. The thistle bears have suffered the worst of it, turning from noble woodland beasts into frenzied engines of destruction. Tharnariun Treetender believes he may have devised a cure for the affliction, but he needs a living, rabid subject brought directly to him so he can test his remedy and halt the corruption before it claims all the forest's creatures.",al={"why capture thistle bear","tharnariun motive plagued lands","why does tharnariun want a bear"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are rabid thistle bears and why are you targeting them?",a="Thistle bears are native forest predators of Darkshore, typically revered as stalwart and noble beasts. However, an unnatural contagion has recently infected their ranks, driving them into a mad frenzy and warping their minds. You are sent after them not to slaughter them outright, but to lure and pacify a sick specimen with Tharnariun's trap so it can be safely examined in hopes of developing an antidote.",al={"what are rabid thistle bears","why target rabid thistle bears","rabid thistle bear darkshore"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, seeing Darkshore's native flora and fauna decay into rabid madness is an affront to Cenarius and the balance of nature they are sworn to protect.",["class:Druid"]="Druids share Tharnariun's grief upon witnessing nature corrupted, and the tragic loss of the bear underscores the insidious depth of the land's spreading disease.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance travelers journeying through northern Kalimdor must reckon with untamed corruption encroaching right on the borders of settled territories."},kw={"cleansing of the infected","darkshore","plagued lands","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun treetender","tharnariun's hope","thistle bear"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2139","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=2118},src={"Plagued Lands"}}
E["quest:2138"] = {t="quest",n="Cleansing of the Infected",z="darkshore",s="Cleansing of the Infected is an Alliance task in Darkshore given by Tharnariun Treetender in Auberdine. After his attempted cure fails to halt the woodland sickness, the caretaker reluctantly orders a cull of the rabid thistle bears roaming the misty wilderness. It represents a bitter turning point where preservation gives way to containment.",h="Cleansing of the Infected is an Alliance task in Darkshore given by Tharnariun Treetender in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Bitter Necessity",b="Tharnariun Treetender has spent long hours searching for a remedy to stem the creeping affliction corrupting Darkshore's wildlife. Despite his attempt to cleanse a captured bear, the thistle bears remain deeply diseased and violent. Having exhausted his gentler options, the night elf tender concludes that putting the beasts down is the only immediate way to prevent them from mauling other creatures and spreading their sickness further into the ancient woodlands.",sp=0},{t="Containing the Wilds",b="The culling of twenty rabid bears is an agonizing duty for any servant of nature. Tharnariun admits plainly that killing the beasts will not cure the underlying plague, but it purchases valuable time for the defenders of Auberdine. Until the primary source of the forest's corruption can be identified and severed, thinning the aggressive herds remains the settlement's only buffer against catastrophe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Tharnariun want the thistle bears killed instead of cured?",a="Tharnariun previously attempted to cleanse a captured bear, but the cure failed and the beast died. With the diseased bears turning violent and threatening other creatures, killing them is a last resort to slow the disease's spread.",al={"why kill the bears","why not cure bears","tharnariun bear quest"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun is a night elf caretaker stationed in Auberdine. He studies the ailments gripping Darkshore's flora and fauna, striving to preserve the natural balance against spreading corruption.",al={"tharnariun role","who gives cleansing of the infected"},it="identity"},{q="Does slaying the rabid bears actually end the plague?",a="No. Tharnariun explicitly warns that killing the rabid bears will not stop the plague. It only buys the forest and the residents of Auberdine precious time by slowing the rate of infection and violence.",al={"does this fix darkshore","is the plague cured"}},{q="What comes after Cleansing of the Infected?",a="Once you report back to Tharnariun, he asks you to prepare your spirit for further bloodshed and offers the follow-up quest, Tharnariun's Hope, to continue addressing the blighted wildlife.",al={"next quest after cleansing","what follows cleasning infected"},it="next_step"},{q="Where are the rabid thistle bears found?",a="Rabid thistle bears wander the coastal and inland forest stretches of central Darkshore, often found roaming among the misty pines south and east of Auberdine.",al={"rabid thistle bear location","where are bears darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What caused the thistle bears to go rabid?",a="The bears are victims of a mysterious taint sweeping through northern Kalimdor's woodlands, corrupting peaceful wildlife into frenzied, aggressive beasts that defy Tharnariun's attempted cure.",al={"why are bears sick","bear sickness darkshore"},it="origin"},{q="What are rabid thistle bears and why must they be killed?",a="Thistle bears are native forest predators that usually live in harmony with the wildlands of Darkshore. However, a creeping, unnatural plague spreading through the woods has driven many of them rabid and violently deranged. In their tainted madness, these diseased beasts attack other wildlife, menace travelers near Auberdine, and ravage the woodland ecology. Because attempts to cure their affliction have failed, putting them down is the only way to contain the devastation.",al={"rabid thistle bears","who are rabid thistle bears","why kill rabid thistle bears"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, ordering the slaughter of corrupted beasts is a heavy burden, underscoring how deeply post-war corruption has penetrated their ancestral homeland.",["class:Druid"]="Druids who revere the wild bear spirits find Tharnariun's command especially poignant: it is an act of mercy and forest triage rather than routine hunting.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters understand that culling diseased predators is sometimes mandatory to protect the wider ecology, even when the underlying cause remains unsolved."},kw={"auberdine","cleansing","darkshore","infected","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun","treetender"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2118","quest:2139","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=2138},src={"Cleansing of the Infected"}}
E["quest:2139"] = {t="quest",n="Tharnariun's Hope",z="darkshore",s="Tharnariun's Hope is the somber conclusion to Tharnariun Treetender's efforts to curb Darkshore's wildlife sickness. After mercy-killing numerous infected beasts across the woodlands, an Alliance champion is tasked with slaying the rabid Den Mother northeast of Auberdine.",h="Tharnariun's Hope is the somber conclusion to Tharnariun Treetender's efforts to curb Darkshore's wildlife...",sec={{t="A Tragic Necessity",b="Following the Third War, the wild creatures of Darkshore began succumbing to an unnatural, rabid sickness. Tharnariun Treetender, stationed in Auberdine, spent days tasking travelers with putting down infected beasts to ease the forest's agony. However, culling rabid thistle bears was merely treating the symptom. To halt the spread, he determined that the source within the local bears had to be excised: the matriarch known as the Den Mother.",sp=0},{t="The Den Mother",b="Lurking in a cavern northeast of Auberdine near the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran, the Den Mother was once a vital guardian of the woodland fauna. Consumed by the maddening affliction spreading across northern Kalimdor, she continuously bore and raised litters of rabid cubs. By hunting down the matriarch within her den, Alliance heroes put an end to her torment and stemmed the tide of frenzied bears prowling the coastal highway.",sp=1},{t="The Grim Reality of Kalimdor",b="Upon the Den Mother's demise, Tharnariun expresses profound gratitude, albeit clouded by melancholy. For the kaldorei, raising weapons against woodland creatures is an agonizing duty. Yet as dark forces press against their new home and many despair or seek shelter, deeds like this prove that the defenders of Auberdine are willing to bear the heavy moral burden required to protect their wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun Treetender is a night elf caretaker stationed in Auberdine. Distraught over the blight and madness warping Darkshore's wildlife, he oversees efforts to study, track, and ultimately put suffering animals out of their misery.",al={"tharnariun","who gives tharnariun's hope","treetender auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Den Mother located?",a="She dwells inside a cave nestled into the hills northeast of Auberdine, just east of the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",al={"where is den mother","den mother cave location","find den mother"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must the Den Mother be killed instead of cured?",a="The affliction ravaging Darkshore's wildlife is deeply ingrained and actively driving the beasts into violent frenzies. With no immediate cure and the Den Mother actively raising rabid offspring, Tharnariun determined that putting her down was the only way to stop the sickness from proliferating further.",al={"can den mother be saved","why kill den mother","cure den mother"},it="motive"},{q="What quests lead up to Tharnariun's Hope?",a="This quest is the final step in a three-part chain. It begins with 'Plagued Lands', continues through 'Cleansing of the Infected', and concludes with 'Tharnariun's Hope'.",al={"prerequisites for tharnariuns hope","quest chain tharnariun"},it="history",gp=true},{q="What is making the animals of Darkshore sick?",a="Tharnariun does not name a source. He knows only that a sickness is spreading across Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of all it touches, and that the thistle bears have been hit the hardest.",al={"why are bears rabid in darkshore","darkshore animal plague cause","what corrupted the bears"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Tharnariun mention people escaping to fortified lands?",a="Auberdine is an exposed coastal outpost beset by ghosts, corrupted wildlife, and hostile creatures. With night elf civilization struggling to rebuild in the aftermath of the Burning Legion's invasion, some residents feel overwhelmed and choose to hide or retreat toward safer Alliance bastions.",al={"fleeing auberdine","fortified alliance lands"},it="people"},{q="Who is the Den Mother?",a="The Den Mother is a massive, corrupted bear laired in a cave northeast near the ruins of Bashal'Aran. She is the source giving birth to or harboring the rabid thistle bears that plague the region. Slaying her cuts off the influx of diseased beasts menacing Auberdine.",al={"what is the den mother","who is den mother","den mother darkshore"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, slaying woodland beasts—especially a matriarch bear—goes against their fundamental reverence for nature, making this duty a bitter and sorrowful necessity.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold bears in high spiritual esteem through the teachings of Ursoc. Executing a corrupted Den Mother serves as a solemn reminder of nature's delicate balance and the tragedies of corruption.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters understand the tragedy of an apex predator driven mad by disease, recognizing when culling an infected beast is the truest act of mercy.",["faction:Alliance"]="Protecting Auberdine strengthens the Alliance's foothold along northern Kalimdor's coast, proving their readiness to defend night elf lands from escalating wilderness threats."},kw={"auberdine","bashal'aran","cleansing of the infected","darkshore","den mother","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun treetender","tharnariun's hope"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2118","subzone:auberdine","quest:954","zone:darkshore","topic:alliance"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=2139},src={"Tharnariun's Hope (quest)"}}
E["quest:2178"] = {t="quest",n="Easy Strider Living",z="darkshore",s="Easy Strider Living is a local culinary task offered by Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine. She is eager to share her prized recipe for strider stew, provided an adventurer is willing to hunt down the fierce foreststriders wandering Darkshore and retrieve their meat.",h="Easy Strider Living is a local culinary task offered by Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Taste of the Wild",b="Auberdine might be a quiet port village, but survival along the coast requires making good use of the local wildlife. Alanndarian Nightsong has developed a secret recipe for hearty strider stew, a savory dish made from the tall, fleet-footed foreststriders that stalk the shadowy woods of Darkshore. Rather than simply handing out culinary secrets, she asks aspiring cooks and hunters to venture out and cull the birds themselves.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Foreststriders",b="Foreststriders are swift, sharp-beaked avian predators that roam the mist-shrouded woodlands and beaches north and south of Auberdine. While they can be temperamental and aggressive when provoked, their succulent meat makes an excellent base for a rich stew. Bringing back fresh meat satisfies Alanndarian's hungry pot and earns the hunter her cherished recipe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf resident of Auberdine in Darkshore. Known for her simmering pot of strider stew, she offers to teach her culinary craft to travelers who prove their hunting prowess.",al={"alanndarian","who is alanndarian nightsong","stew cook auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find the strider meat?",a="Strider meat is obtained by hunting foreststriders throughout Darkshore. These large, flightless birds roam both the sandy shorelines and the forested groves outside Auberdine.",al={"strider meat location","where are foreststriders","how to get strider meat"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The quest tasks you with hunting down foreststriders to bring back five cuts of meat for Alanndarian Nightsong, in exchange for learning how to prepare Strider Stew.",al={"why do easy strider living","quest purpose","easy strider living objective"},it="purpose"},{q="Are the foreststriders dangerous to hunt?",a="Foreststriders are territorial birds armed with sharp beaks and swift legs, making them aggressive when approached. However, a reasonably equipped adventurer can hunt them down without much peril.",al={"are striders hard to kill","foreststrider danger"},it="danger"},{q="Does this quest unlock a cooking recipe?",a="Yes. Upon bringing Alanndarian her requested meat, she shares her culinary secrets, teaching adventurers the recipe for Strider Stew.",al={"do i get recipe","strider stew recipe","cooking reward"},gp=true},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest begins and ends in the settlement of Auberdine, with the hunting taking place in the wilderness of Darkshore.",al={"quest zone","where is easy strider living"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Alanndarian Nightsong want this done?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong has an empty cooking pot and an appetite for fresh strider stew. Before she is willing to part with her secret recipe, she insists on seeing whether you have the mettle to hunt the tallbirds yourself and bring back fresh cuts for her cooking fire.",al={"alanndarian motive","why does alanndarian want strider meat","why strider stew"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Strider Meat used for?",a="The succulent meat is the core ingredient in Alanndarian's savory strider stew. Bringing her five cuts fills her empty kettle and proves to her that you have earned the right to learn her secret wilderness recipe.",al={"what is strider meat for","why strider meat","strider meat use"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="This task is essential for culinarians traveling through Darkshore, rewarding the recipe to prepare nourishing Strider Stew from local wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="Living harmoniously in Kalimdor often involves living off the land, and hearty strider stews have become a coastal staple for night elves in Auberdine.",["class:Hunter"]="Foreststriders are both swift game and potential animal companions, offering tracking and hunting practice along Darkshore's mist-laden paths."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cooking","darkshore","easy strider living","foreststrider","strider meat","strider stew"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=2178,ri={"Strider Meat"}},src={"Easy Strider Living"}}
E["quest:3524"] = {t="quest",n="Washed Ashore",z="darkshore",s="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine on behalf of the Temple of the Moon. Mass strandings of giant sea creatures along the Darkshore coastline have raised alarms among the night elf priesthood in Darnassus. Adventurers are tasked with driving back scavenging murlocs to secure skeletal specimens for study.",h="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine on behalf of the Temple of...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Omen",b="Giant, majestic creatures of the deep have long been known to occasionally beach themselves on the foggy shoals of Darkshore. Recently, however, their deaths have ceased being tragic anomalies and become an escalating pattern. Beached leviathans are washing up along the coastline in alarming numbers. To the Priestesses of Elune residing in the Temple of the Moon, such unprompted mass strandings are treated not merely as natural oddities, but as potential ill omens threatening northern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="To decipher why these great beasts are hurling themselves onto the sands, scholar Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde was dispatched to the port town of Auberdine. Her task is to collect biological samples and send them by hippogryph to Darnassus for close examination. However, the Greymist murlocs infesting the surf line have swarmed the massive carcasses, aggressively scavenging the remains and preventing field researchers from reaching the bones without armed protection.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are giant sea creatures washing up on Darkshore?",a="The exact cause remains under active investigation by the Temple of the Moon. While occasional strandings are natural, the sudden surge in frequency has convinced night elf scholars that a deeper disturbance or ill omen lurks beneath the waves of the Great Sea.",al={"why beached creatures","sea creature strandings","dying sea beasts"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is an investigator sent from Darnassus by the Temple of the Moon. Stationed in Auberdine, she is responsible for cataloging coastal anomalies and collecting physical samples from beached leviathans to send back to the priesthood for analysis.",al={"gwennyth","who is gwennyth bly'leggonde"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the creature south of Auberdine lie?",a="The skeletal remains lie on the shoreline just a short march south of the Auberdine docks. The massive carcass rests in the surf, surrounded and guarded by hostile Greymist murlocs.",al={"creature location","sea creature bones location","where is the beached beast"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What will Darnassus do with the sea creature bones?",a="The bones are dispatched via hippogryph directly to Darnassus. Scholars and priestesses at the Temple of the Moon study the marrow, structure, and signs of decay to uncover whether disease, foul magic, or unnatural predation drove the beast ashore.",al={"why collect bones","purpose of sea creature bones","darnassus bones"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Greymist murlocs gathered around the carcass?",a="The Greymist tribe exploits the stranded giants as an effortless source of food, tools, and bonecraft. Their territorial claim over the carcasses makes it impossible for unarmed scholars to approach without risking their lives.",al={"murlocs at whale","why murlocs around creature"},it="target"},{q="Does this investigation conclude after retrieving the first set of bones?",a="No. The carcass south of town is only the first site. Gwennyth continues her research with further inquiries into other stranded leviathans that have perished along Darkshore's expansive, mist-shrouded coast.",al={"is this a chain","washed ashore follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want this done?",a="Gwennyth was dispatched by Darnassus's Temple of the Moon to investigate an alarming surge of giant sea beasts beaching themselves along Darkshore. She views this sudden spike in strandings as an ill omen for the region and urgently needs skeletal remains so scholars in the capital can determine what drives these majestic creatures ashore.",al={"gwennyth motive","why help gwennyth","why study beached creatures"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why can't Gwennyth collect the sea creature bones herself?",a="While Gwennyth is a capable researcher for the Temple of the Moon, she lacks the martial might to fight her way past the aggressive Greymist murlocs swarming the shoreline. The local sentinels have their hands full protecting Auberdine itself, so she relies on visiting adventurers to retrieve specimens from infested waters.",al={"why does gwennyth need me","why cant gwennyth get bones","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The coastal strandings disturb the delicate balance of Darkshore, prompting the Sisterhood of Elune to intervene directly from Darnassus.",["class:Priest"]="Serving the Sisterhood of Elune means interpreting spiritual omens and natural imbalances, exactly what Gwennyth seeks to decipher from the sea creature's remains.",["class:Druid"]="The mass death of noble marine life is an alarming sign of ecological discord along the Kalimdor coast that demands watchful attention."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","darnassus","greymist murlocs","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea creature bones","temple of the moon","washed ashore"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc","quest:4723","quest:2519"},m={start="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=3524,ri={"Sea Creature Bones"}},src={"Washed Ashore"}}
E["quest:4681"] = {t="quest",n="Washed Ashore",z="darkshore",s="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine to examine deceased marine life along Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast. Acting on behalf of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, she sends adventurers to inspect the skeletal remains of a giant sea turtle submerged west of the village. The research seeks to explain why so many sea creatures are stranding themselves or dying off the shore.",h="Washed Ashore is an investigation initiated by Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine to examine deceased marine...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Tide",b="The misty beaches of Darkshore have become a graveyard for oceanic giants. Beached behemoths and drowned leviathans line the sands and shallows, baffling the night elves of Auberdine. Having already looked into a grounded sea creature along the strand, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde tasks travelers with diving into the waters west of the docks, near a sunken vessel, to examine the bones of a massive sea turtle and gather evidence for the Temple of the Moon.",sp=0},{t="Flight from the World Tree",b="Gwennyth's ultimate goal is gathering enough physical evidence to submit a formal report to the Priestesses of Elune in Darnassus. Her preliminary findings point toward a deeply unsettling hypothesis: these gentle marine animals may not be dying by accident, but deliberately fleeing something out in the open sea—potentially the waters encircling Teldrassil itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are sea creatures washing ashore in Darkshore?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde suspects these marine creatures are deliberately fleeing something disturbing in the surrounding ocean. Preliminary findings suggest they may be escaping the waters encircling the newly grown World Tree of Teldrassil.",al={"why turtles dying","beached creatures darkshore","why beached whales"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher stationed in Auberdine who reports directly to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She is documenting the wave of dead and beached sea creatures along Darkshore's coastline.",al={"gwennyth","auberdine researcher","quest giver washed ashore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the skeletal sea turtle located?",a="The skeletal sea turtle rests on the ocean floor due west of Auberdine's docks, lying close to the wreckage of a sunken vessel off the Darkshore coast.",al={"turtle remains location","where skeletal turtle","sea turtle bones"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What does the Temple of the Moon have to do with this?",a="The Temple of the Moon directs ecological and spiritual matters for night elf lands. Gwennyth requires concrete physical samples to present a formal report to the priestesses regarding the strange die-off.",al={"why darnassus care","temple of the moon role","priestesses of elune involvement"},it="ties"},{q="Are there more beached creatures to find?",a="Yes. Gwennyth notes that beached creatures lie strewn all along the Darkshore coastline, encouraging adventurers to search the sands and recover remains from other stranded behemoths.",al={"other beached sea creatures","more sea creature quests","darkshore beached behemoth"},gp=true},{q="What is the difference between the two 'Washed Ashore' quests?",a="The first quest sends you to investigate a creature stranded on the beach nearby, while the follow-up asks you to swim west of the docks to inspect a submerged skeletal sea turtle.",al={"washed ashore part 1 vs part 2","two washed ashore quests","washed ashore chain"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want the sea turtle remains investigated?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is investigating an unsettling ecological crisis along the coastline of Darkshore. Massive sea creatures are dying and washing ashore in unusual numbers, and she needs physical evidence to send to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. Her goal is to assemble a formal report for the priesthood to discover what is driving these great beasts to perish—specifically investigating the alarming possibility that wildlife might be actively fleeing the waters around Teldrassil.",al={"gwennyth bly'leggonde motive","why investigate the turtle","why does gwennyth want this"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are the Sea Turtle Remains used for?",a="The remains serve as critical scientific and spiritual evidence for the night elves. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde and the Temple of the Moon intend to examine the bones to uncover signs of disease, corruption, or trauma. These samples allow researchers in Darnassus to piece together why large marine creatures are stranding themselves or dying off the coast, helping the priesthood understand the broader ecological threat facing the shores of northern Kalimdor.",al={"sea turtle remains purpose","what is sea turtle remains for","why sea turtle remains"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The mass death and erratic flight of Darkshore's ancient marine beasts hints at a corruption or disruption in the balance of nature radiating from the waters around Teldrassil.",["class:Priest"]="Carrying out this inquiry supports the Priestesses of Elune at the Temple of the Moon, who oversee the spiritual and natural well-being of northern Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine serves as the gateway between Teldrassil and the mainland; evidence that ocean life is actively fleeing your new home is a troubling omen."},kw={"auberdine","beached creature","darkshore","darnassus","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea turtle","sea turtle remains","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","quest:940","quest:2519","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4681,ri={"Sea Turtle Remains"}},src={"Washed Ashore (2)"}}
E["quest:4722"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the misty, surf-battered shores of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive beached sea turtle, surrounded by scavenging murlocs. Though picked over, viable biological samples can still be recovered from the remains. Naturalists in Auberdine collect such specimens to ship back to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus for formal study.",h="Along the misty, surf-battered shores of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive beached sea turtle...",sec={{t="A Stranded Leviathan",b="The long coastline of Darkshore frequently catches the casualties of the Great Sea, including massive ancient sea turtles that drift ashore after death or beach themselves in confusion. Once grounded, the carcasses quickly attract scavengers. Hostile Greymist murlocs have established crude camps around this turtle's skeletal frame, carving away flesh and shell. Despite their foraging, viable bone, shell, or tissue samples often remain intact within the wreckage.",sp=0},{t="Field Research for Darnassus",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, stationed in the settlement of Auberdine, serves as a field researcher documenting the unusual marine life and ecological disturbances along the coast. The night elves observe these stranded beasts with both reverence and scientific curiosity. Once recovered, suitable remains are carefully cataloged and prepared for shipment to scholars in Darnassus, who seek to understand why so many pelagic giants are washing ashore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many beached sea creatures in Darkshore?",a="Darkshore's turbulent waters and strong coastal currents naturally push drifting debris and dying sea beasts onto the sand. Night elf scholars suspect unnatural disturbances in the deep ocean are driving marine life toward the shallows, prompting local naturalists to study every corpse that washes up.",al={"why dead sea turtle","darkshore beached creatures","why stranded"},it="danger"},{q="Who wants the sea turtle remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a night elf researcher located in Auberdine, collects washed-up samples from adventurers on behalf of naturalists and scholars based in Darnassus.",al={"who do i turn this in to","gwennyth auberdine","where to turn in turtle remains"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle?",a="The local Greymist murlocs are opportunists who scavenge whatever drifts onto the beaches. A beached giant sea turtle provides them with an abundant supply of meat, tough hide, and bone for tools and shelters.",al={"murlocs near turtle","greymist scavengers","murloc camp"},it="threat"},{q="What happens to the samples once Gwennyth receives them?",a="Gwennyth packages the viable tissue and skeletal samples for transport across the sea to Darnassus, where scholars and priestesses examine them to monitor the health and behavior of the coastal ecosystem.",al={"what does darnassus do with remains","turtle sample research"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this the only beached creature along the coast?",a="No. Darkshore's long coastline holds multiple beached sea turtles as well as stranded sea behemoths, several of which yield research specimens for Auberdine's scholars.",al={"other beached animals","more dead turtles","washed ashore creatures"},it="place"},{q="Are sea turtles sacred to the night elves?",a="The night elves revere the native beasts of Kalimdor as part of the natural balance under Elune and the wild gods. While sea turtles are not solitary divine avatars, their unexpected deaths and beachings are treated as grave ecological warning signs.",al={"night elf turtles","druids and turtles"},it="history"},{q="Why does Gwennyth want the sea turtle remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is gathering specimens for scholars in Darnassus who are investigating Darkshore's blighted coastline. A rash of dead marine life has washed ashore, and by studying uncontaminated tissue from beached creatures before scavengers ruin them, researchers hope to uncover what sickness or disruption in the sea drove these great beasts ashore to die.",al={"why take sea turtle remains","why study turtle remains","gwennyth turtle motive"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The unexplained beaching of ancient sea creatures signals a deeper disruption in Kalimdor's waters, motivating the researchers of Auberdine and Darnassus to investigate every washed-up leviathan.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view the stranded sea life and the scavenging murlocs as symptoms of an ecological imbalance along Darkshore that demands close observation and healing."},kw={"auberdine","beached","darkshore","darnassus","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","remains","sea turtle"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=4722},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (1)"}}
E["quest:4723"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the fog-draped strand of Mist's Edge lies the massive carcass of a sea thresher, far larger than any native to Darkshore's shallows. While local murlocs pick through the carrion, naturalists in Auberdine seek bone samples to understand why such colossal deep-sea beasts are beaching themselves along the coast.",h="Along the fog-draped strand of Mist's Edge lies the massive carcass of a sea thresher, far larger than any...",sec={{t="A Giant on the Shallows",b="The Mist's Edge coastline is no stranger to shipwrecks and tide-washed debris, but the sudden appearance of enormous thresher remains is troubling. The creature dwarfs typical local wildlife, pointing to depths far beyond the calm waters of the Veiled Sea. Although coastal murlocs eagerly swarm and feast on the corpse, they lack the strength or coordination to bring down a leviathan of this scale. The predator succumbed to something else entirely before washing ashore.",sp=0},{t="Studies in Darnassus",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine coordinates field efforts to salvage bones and biological samples from Darkshore's stranded megafauna. Night elf researchers in Darnassus hope that by examining skeletal remains and tissue samples, they can determine whether illness, deep-sea disturbances, or arcane corruption drives these ocean giants onto the killing sands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of beast washed up on the shore?",a="It is the remains of a giant thresher, an aquatic predator vastly larger than the threshers typically spotted close to Darkshore's beaches.",al={"what creature is this","what is the dead monster","what animal is dead on the beach"},it="identity"},{q="Did the murlocs kill it?",a="No. Although murlocs swarm around the carcass to feed on the rotting meat, observers note they are far too weak, even in large groups, to hunt down a deep-water behemoth of that size.",al={"did murlocs kill the thresher","did murlocs kill the sea creature"},it="history"},{q="Why are sea creatures stranding themselves along Darkshore?",a="The exact cause remains unknown. Night elf researchers suspect unseen oceanic disturbances, disease, or ecological distress are forcing deep-sea fauna to swim into shallow surf where they beach and die.",al={"why are threshers dying","why do creatures beach themselves"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher stationed in Auberdine. She collects skeletal specimens and biological samples from beached wildlife along Darkshore to send to Darnassus for detailed study.",al={"who is gwennyth","who takes the bones in auberdine"},it="people"},{q="Where are the collected bones sent?",a="After Gwennyth catalogs and preps the samples in Auberdine, they are dispatched to scholars and naturalists in the capital city of Darnassus for anatomical and magical investigation.",al={"where do bones go","what does auberdine do with bones"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is this carcass located?",a="The carcass rests directly on the sandy shores of Mist's Edge, along Darkshore's western coastline.",al={"carcass location","where is the beached sea creature"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The strandings along Darkshore are a distressing sign of imbalance in the surrounding waters, prompting naturalists in Auberdine and Darnassus to investigate before more marine life perishes.",["class:Druid"]="Druids committed to the preservation of natural harmony look upon the stranded leviathan as an alarming symptom of disturbance in the Veiled Sea's ecosystem."},kw={"auberdine","beached","bones","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","mist's edge","murloc","sea creature","thresher"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:mist-s-edge","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc","quest:938"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=4723},src={"Beached Sea Creature (1)"}}
E["quest:4725"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the surf of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive sea turtle, fitted with a broken carriage and swarming with opportunistic Greymist murlocs. Unlike other dead leviathans on the coast, this creature was harnessed as a beast of burden by the serpent-like naga before dying on the sand.",h="Along the surf of Darkshore lies the carcass of a massive sea turtle, fitted with a broken carriage and...",sec={{t="A Beast in Harness",b="The mist-shrouded shores of Darkshore are troubled by an alarming number of stranded sea giants, but this particular sea turtle tells a far more sinister story. Strapped across the creature's colossal carapace sits a dilapidated carriage, abandoned and decaying in the tide. Rather than dying of sickness or natural exhaustion like other beached creatures, this giant was pressed into service and driven onto the coast by intelligent handlers.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="The carcass did not remain quiet for long. Local Greymist murlocs quickly swarmed the remains, carving out a den amidst the rotting meat and scavenged timber. Amidst the murlocs' refuse and the broken chassis of the sea carriage rests an intact, curiously marked container, left behind by the beast's original masters.",sp=0},{t="Naga Supply Lines",b="Upon delivering the strangely marked container to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine, the grim reality comes into focus. The container bears naga markings, and the harness matches the supply carriages used by the serpent folk to ferry weapons and war material from the oceanic depths. The dead turtle is direct proof of the naga staging incursions into northern Darkshore, and the recovered artifact is hurried off to Darnassus for further study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is there a carriage on the sea turtle's shell?",a="The carriage belonged to the naga, who harness giant sea turtles as pack animals and siege beasts. They use these carriages to transport supplies and weapons from the depths up onto the Darkshore coastline.",al={"turtle carriage","why carriage on turtle","harnessed turtle"}},{q="What is inside the carriage?",a="Within the ruins of the abandoned carriage lies a strangely marked box. Its runes identify it as naga property, prompting the scholars in Auberdine to send it along to Darnassus for official scrutiny.",al={"turtle box","strangely marked box","box in turtle carriage"},it="item"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle?",a="Greymist murlocs inhabit the coastline and regularly scavenge shipwrecks and beached carcasses. They have claimed the giant turtle's remains as a food source and nest.",al={"murlocs around turtle","greymist murlocs turtle","why murlocs eating turtle"},it="threat"},{q="Who studies the beached creatures in Darkshore?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine oversees the investigation into the wave of beached sea creatures, cataloging relics and strange materials found upon their remains.",al={"who studies beached sea creatures","auberdine researcher","gwennyth bly'leggonde role"},it="people"},{q="How does this turtle differ from other beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="While many other creatures wash ashore due to illness, corruption, or oceanic distress, this turtle was clearly domesticated, saddled with heavy cargo gear, and driven to the beach deliberately by the naga.",al={"other beached turtles","why this turtle different","turtle mystery darkshore"}},{q="What happens to the marked box after Auberdine?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde logs the discovery in Auberdine and sends the naga box up to Darnassus, where elven leadership analyzes the growing threat along their northern borders.",al={"where does box go","box sent to darnassus","what does auberdine do with box"},it="next_step"},{q="Why bring the marked box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Unlike other marine carcasses washing ashore along Darkshore, this turtle was clearly harnessed as a beast of burden. The abandoned carriage and its strangely marked cargo suggest an organized, hostile force rather than natural strandings. Taking the relic to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine allows the night elf researchers to study the markings, assess the creeping coastal threats, and forward their findings to Darnassus.",al={"why bring box to auberdine","why take turtle box to gwennyth","beached turtle box motive"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The presence of naga supply beasts washing up on Darkshore confirms that the ancestral enemies of the kaldorei are actively reinforcing beachheads uncomfortably close to Darnassus.",["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating beached creatures provides crucial intelligence for Auberdine's sentinels, tracking both murloc infestations and the rise of organized naga raiding parties."},kw={"auberdine","beached","carriage","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","naga","sea turtle","strangely marked box"},rel={"quest:4722","npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:naga","topic:murloc","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4725},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (2)"}}
E["quest:4727"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the northern shores of Darkshore lies the massive skeletal carcass of a beached sea turtle, curiously untouched by the local Greymist murlocs. A sample of its remains is gathered and delivered to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine on behalf of the Temple of the Moon. Naturalists and priestesses seek to uncover why these great oceanic creatures are washing ashore and why even scavengers seem reluctant to approach.",h="Along the northern shores of Darkshore lies the massive skeletal carcass of a beached sea turtle, curiously...",sec={{t="A Curious Absence",b="The northern coastline of Darkshore is thick with Greymist murlocs, creatures known to aggressively scavenge anything of nutritive value that washes up from the Veiled Sea. Yet this enormous turtle skeleton lies largely undisturbed. Whether the murlocs simply overlooked the bounty or actively avoided the remains for an unseen reason remains a troubling puzzle for those studying the beach's ecology.",sp=0},{t="Study of the Shoreline",b="In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde collects samples of these beached behemoths for the Temple of the Moon. The night elf priestesses seek to comprehend the disturbances troubling Darkshore's waters, using skeletal fragments to determine whether sickness, magical corruption, or foul marine predators are driving the sea's ancient dwellers to their deaths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the beached sea turtle?",a="It is the massive skeletal remains of an ancient sea turtle washed ashore in northern Darkshore. Its unusual presence and the lack of scavenger activity make it an object of study for the night elves.",al={"turtle carcass","sea turtle skeleton","what is this turtle"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the murlocs avoiding the carcass?",a="The Greymist murlocs usually tear through any carcass on the beach, yet they have left these remains alone. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde and the Temple of the Moon suspect the scavengers may be shying away due to an unnatural taint or an unseen danger surrounding the creature's death.",al={"why aren't murlocs eating it","greymist murlocs turtle","why avoid carcass"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher stationed in Auberdine who gathers field samples from Darkshore's beached marine life on behalf of the Temple of the Moon.",al={"gwennyth auberdine","who wants turtle remains","turtle quest turn in"},it="people"},{q="Why does the Temple of the Moon care about beached sea creatures?",a="The priestesses of Elune maintain balance and stewardship over the natural world in northern Kalimdor. With sea creatures dying in unusual numbers along Darkshore, the Temple is analyzing biological samples to diagnose the underlying affliction harming the seas.",al={"temple of the moon turtle","why study turtles","elune marine life"},it="motive"},{q="Where is this particular sea turtle located?",a="This particular carcass rests on the sandy northern coastline of Darkshore, situated near territory inhabited by the Greymist murloc tribes.",al={"where is the turtle","beached sea turtle location","turtle darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are there other beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="Yes. Multiple beached sea creatures and giant sea turtles litter the shores of Darkshore, each prompting an investigation by Auberdine's researchers into why the ocean's giants are perishing.",al={"other beached creatures","more sea turtles","beached sea creature quests"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The unexplained death and avoidance of majestic sea creatures along Darkshore highlights the growing imbalance threatening the ancestral lands of the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="Druids closely monitor the coastline, deeply troubled when scavenger species like murlocs refuse to touch the dead, signaling a possible unnatural taint in the waters.",["class:Priest"]="Serving the Temple of the Moon means extending Elune's compassionate stewardship to all living things, investigating deaths that disrupt nature's harmony."},kw={"auberdine","beached","carcass","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","remains","sea turtle","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:murloc","quest:4722","quest:2519","quest:938"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4727},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (3)"}}
E["quest:4728"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the misty coast of Darkshore lies the massive carcass of a sea mammal, abandoned mid-excavation. Scattered tools and an idle wheelbarrow reveal an expedition cut short, leaving the specimen to opportunistic murlocs and the curious eyes of passing travelers.",h="Along the misty coast of Darkshore lies the massive carcass of a sea mammal, abandoned mid-excavation.",sec={{t="A Halted Excavation",b="The carcass resting upon the sands of Darkshore is that of an enormous marine mammal, partially gutted and heavily weathered by sea spray. Strewn about its decaying frame are a rusted wheelbarrow and discarded excavation tools, clearly showing that someone attempted an organized study of the beast before being driven off or abandoning the site in haste.",sp=0},{t="The League and the Murlocs",b="The abandoned equipment belonged to dwarven field researchers of the Explorer's League operating in Darkshore. Their examination of the massive carcass came to an abrupt halt when local murlocs swarmed the site, claiming the washed-up giant for scavenging. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine, acting on behalf of the Temple of the Moon, gladly accepts any salvaged bone samples to further study the unnatural wash-ups plaguing the coastline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this creature lying on the beach?",a="It is the remains of a giant sea mammal that washed ashore on Darkshore's coast. The species is not definitively identified, but it is large enough to attract both scavenging murlocs and dwarven researchers.",al={"beached sea creature identity","what is this carcass","what died here"},it="identity"},{q="Who left the tools and wheelbarrow behind?",a="The tools were left by members of the dwarven Explorer's League. They set up an excavation site to study the beached beast, but were attacked and driven off by hostile coastal murlocs before they could finish.",al={"who left the tools","abandoned wheelbarrow darkshore","who was digging here"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want these bones?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde collects samples on behalf of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. The night elves are actively investigating the strange and unsettling phenomenon of massive sea creatures washing up dead along Darkshore's shores.",al={"why does gwennyth want bones","temple of the moon sea creature","auberdine sea bones"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are murlocs prowling around the carcass?",a="The murlocs were drawn by the colossal feast of meat and blubber, subsequently chasing off the dwarven scholars to scavenge and defend the remains for themselves.",al={"murlocs around carcass","why are murlocs here","murloc scavengers"},it="danger"},{q="Is the Explorer's League officially allied with Auberdine here?",a="Yes. As fellow members of the Alliance, the Explorer's League maintains a presence in Darkshore and collaborates with local night elf authorities, frequently sharing reports of their scientific discoveries and coastal investigations.",al={"explorers league auberdine","dwarves in darkshore","explorers league alliance darkshore"},it="allies"},{q="Are there other beached creatures along the Darkshore coast?",a="Yes. Multiple enormous marine beasts and skeletal remains have washed up along the length of Darkshore's misty beaches, suggesting widespread disturbance in the waters off Kalimdor.",al={"more beached creatures","other carcasses darkshore","multiple beached sea creatures"},it="place"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The abandoned tools around the carcass belong to your kin in the Explorer's League, who were chased from their dig site by native murlocs.",["race:NightElf"]="The Temple of the Moon is deeply concerned by the unnatural frequency of massive sea life dying and washing up on the sacred shores of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="This discovery highlights the cooperative efforts between Darnassus and the Ironforge Explorer's League to catalog the mysteries of Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","beached","bones","darkshore","explorers league","gwennyth","murloc","sea creature"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","quest:4723","quest:2519"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4728},src={"Beached Sea Creature (2)"}}
E["quest:4730"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the windswept coast of Darkshore, the half-devoured remains of a massive sea mammal have washed ashore, guarded by opportunistic murlocs. Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine seeks bone samples from these stranded giants to discern why normally docile ocean beasts are violently dying upon the sands.",h="Along the windswept coast of Darkshore, the half-devoured remains of a massive sea mammal have washed ashore...",sec={{t="A Gruesome Shoreline Discovery",b="North along the lonely beaches of Darkshore lies the rotting, half-eaten carcass of a gargantuan sea mammal. Waves crash against its exposed ribs while an unusually vicious tribe of murlocs picks the scavenged bones clean. The sight is both tragic and unnerving, signaling that the ocean's balance is tipping just as severely as the blighted forests inland.",sp=0},{t="Uncharacteristic Stranding",b="According to Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, the creatures washing up along the strand are typically gentle marine mammals native to the waters surrounding the base of Teldrassil. Unlike aggressive threshers, these gentle beasts have never been known to drive themselves violently onto the rocks. The Temple of the Moon is actively cataloging bone samples to uncover what foul corruption or hidden threat is driving them from the deep to perish on the coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creature washed up here?",a="The skeletal remains belong to a large, gentle sea mammal that usually inhabits the deep, tranquil waters around the base of Teldrassil. They are naturally peaceful giants and are not prone to aggressive behavior or beaching.",al={"what animal is this","what is the beached creature","sea monster bones"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the sea creature beach itself?",a="The exact cause is unknown, but Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde notes that such strandings are completely unnatural for this species. Night elf researchers suspect an underlying disturbance or corruption in the surrounding seas is disorienting the creatures or forcing them to flee their native habitats.",al={"why did it beach","why are sea creatures dying","darkshore strandings"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a priestess representing the Temple of the Moon stationed in Auberdine. She is coordinating the ecological investigation into Darkshore's coastline, collecting skeletal remains to study the affliction plaguing the local marine fauna.",al={"who turns in this quest","who is gwennyth","auberdine priestess"},it="people"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the corpse?",a="The murlocs are opportunists drawn to the beached giant as an easy, abundant food source. The band surrounding this particular carcass is notably stronger and more aggressive than the murlocs dwelling closer to Auberdine.",al={"why murlocs here","murlocs near bones","beach murlocs"},it="hostile"},{q="Where does this creature normally live?",a="These marine mammals make their home in the open waters encircling the giant boughs and roots of Teldrassil, rarely approaching the mainland shores under normal circumstances.",al={"where do these live","sea mammal habitat","teldrassil sea creatures"},it="place"},{q="How does this relate to other beachings in Darkshore?",a="Several marine species have washed ashore along Darkshore, including carnivorous threshers and giant sea turtles. While threshers are naturally turbulent, the beaching of peaceful mammals confirms that the maritime anomaly affects species across the entire coastal ecosystem.",al={"other beached sea creatures","beached thresher","beached sea turtle"},it="conflict"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The strandings along Darkshore strike a painful chord for the Kaldorei, who revere natural harmony and watch with dread as the waters around their new home of Teldrassil grow troubled.",["class:Priest"]="The Temple of the Moon funds and oversees this inquiry, seeking divine insight into the corruption unsettling Kalimdor's waters.",["class:Druid"]="Any disruption in marine behavior is a dire omen for the Cenarion Circle, pointing toward an unnatural blight poisoning the coastal wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing the shores around Auberdine protects vital Alliance shipping lanes between Darkshore, Teldrassil, and the eastern kingdoms."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","sea creature bones","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:4723","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940","topic:murloc","quest:2519","subzone:temple-of-the-moon"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=4730},src={"Beached Sea Creature (3)"}}
E["quest:4731"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="This beached sea turtle carcass along the Darkshore coastline carries a broken carriage and a box inscribed with strange runes. Unlike other naturally stranded marine life, this creature appears to have been slain while serving as a beast of burden.",h="This beached sea turtle carcass along the Darkshore coastline carries a broken carriage and a box inscribed...",sec={{t="A Beast of Burden",b="The Darkshore coast is littered with the bones of ancient sea creatures, but this turtle skeleton tells a distinctly artificial tale. Strapped across its massive shell are the splintered remnants of a buckled carriage. The creature did not die of sickness or disorientation like others washed ashore; it was driven onto the rocks while hauling cargo. In the wreckage of the carriage rests a container decorated with unfamiliar, serpent-like carvings, left behind amidst the scavengers who claimed the rotting shell.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Incursion",b="When Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde examines the salvaged box in Auberdine, she identifies the craftsmanship as belonging to the naga. The serpentine fiends frequently harness great sea beasts to ferry provisions and weapons ashore during their amphibious assaults. Given the location of the wreckage along the southern shores of Darkshore, Gwennyth suspects this supply transport met its end while ferrying gear toward Ashenvale, pointing toward expanding naga ambitions across northern Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does this sea turtle have a carriage on its back?",a="The carriage was fitted onto the creature by the naga, who use giant sea turtles as living pack animals to transport supplies, weapons, and war materiel from the ocean depths onto land.",al={"turtle carriage","why turtle has cart","sea turtle harness"},it="item"},{q="Who is currently inhabiting the remains?",a="A band of powerful Greymist murlocs took over the giant shell after the turtle died, using its massive hollowed-out carcass as a fortified seaside shelter.",al={"who lives in turtle","greymist murlocs turtle","what is guarding turtle"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Strangely Marked Box go?",a="The box should be brought to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, an emissary representing the Temple of the Moon stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",al={"where do i take the box","strangely marked box","turn in marked box"},it="next_step"},{q="What do the markings on the box mean?",a="The markings are naga script. They indicate that the box and its carriage were part of a naga supply convoy moving along the coast, likely heading south toward Ashenvale before disaster struck.",al={"turtle box lore","who made the marked box","naga box"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="Why is the Temple of the Moon interested in beached turtles?",a="The priestesses of Elune are investigating the environmental and military threats afflicting the Darkshore coastline. Recovered artifacts like this box are sent to Darnassus so scholars can map out hostile movements.",al={"why temple wants turtles","gwennyth darkshore mission"},it="motive"},{q="Where was the turtle traveling before it died?",a="Based on the location of the carcass along the coast, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde suspects the naga were directing the laden creature southward, potentially headed toward Ashenvale.",al={"turtle destination","where was turtle going"},sp=1,it="place"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of sea life for military transport by the naga is an outrage to the kaldorei, and discovering these tracks helps the Temple of the Moon track threats toward Ashenvale.",["class:Druid"]="Seeing a noble sea turtle enslaved to haul weapons of war and left to rot among scavengers illustrates the corrupting disregard the naga show toward wild beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating this wreckage alerts Auberdine and Darnassus to naga logistical routes threatening northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","beached sea turtle","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","naga","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","topic:naga","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","zone:ashenvale","zone:darnassus","quest:4722"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4731},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (4)"}}
E["quest:4732"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along the wind-battered coast of Darkshore, the bleached bones of giant sea turtles wash ashore with unsettling frequency. Investigating these tragic strandings provides Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine with specimens to study why Kalimdor's marine life is dying out.",h="Along the wind-battered coast of Darkshore, the bleached bones of giant sea turtles wash ashore with...",sec={{t="A Strand of Bones",b="The mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore is strewn with the remains of great leviathans and majestic sea turtles. Many of these ancient reptiles have drifted onto the shoals or hauled themselves onto the sand to perish. Greymist murlocs frequently swarm the massive carcasses, picking the flesh down to the shell and bone while establishing crude camps around the carrion.",sp=0},{t="Vanishing Waters",b="Before the Third War, sea turtles were known to thrive in the sacred waters around Mount Hyjal and the roots of the World Tree, Nordrassil. Following Nordrassil's sacrifice to defeat the Burning Legion and the subsequent planting of Teldrassil off Kalimdor's northern shore, the population collapsed. Priestesses of Elune like Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde study these coastal remains on behalf of the Temple of the Moon, seeking to understand whether dark magic, the changing sea, or the loss of their ancient sanctuary is driving these gentle giants to their deaths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are sea turtles beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="The exact reason remains a mystery to the night elves. Historically, sea turtles thrived in the waters beneath the World Tree Nordrassil. Following Nordrassil's destruction in the Third War and the raising of Teldrassil, their numbers have plummeted, and many seem to deliberately end their lives along the Darkshore shoals.",al={"why do turtles die here","darkshore turtle mystery","why beached"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf scholar and representative of the Temple of the Moon stationed in Auberdine. She is tasked with cataloging and studying the washed-up sea creatures along the coast to uncover why Darkshore's wildlife is suffering.",al={"who is gwennyth","where to turn in turtle remains","auberdine researcher"},it="identity"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle remains?",a="The local Greymist murlocs are opportunists who scavenge the enormous carcasses for sustenance and materials. They often pitch their shoreline settlements right next to beached sea turtles and sea creatures to strip them clean.",al={"why murlocs on turtle","greymist scavengers","murloc camps on beach"},it="why_here"},{q="What connection do these turtles have to Nordrassil?",a="According to the night elves, sea turtles were once common and playful in the pristine waters around the base of Mount Hyjal and the World Tree Nordrassil. The violent destruction of Nordrassil deeply disrupted the natural balance, after which sightings of these creatures drastically declined.",al={"nordrassil connection","hyjal turtles","mount hyjal turtle link"},it="history"},{q="Does Teldrassil have anything to do with their decline?",a="The priesthood notes that since the growth of Teldrassil, sea turtles have been seen in ever-decreasing numbers. Whether the new World Tree has altered coastal currents, disrupted their migration, or carries an unnatural aura affecting ocean life is an active area of study for the Temple of the Moon.",al={"teldrassil effect on turtles","why did teldrassil change turtles"},it="threat"},{q="Are there multiple beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="Yes. Darkshore's long coastline holds multiple beached sea creatures and sea turtles. Each carcass provides unique bone and tissue samples that Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde uses to piece together the broader ecological disaster unfolding along the shore.",al={"more beached quests","other beached turtles","beached sea creatures"}},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want the sea turtle remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde studies the remains on behalf of the Temple of the Moon in Auberdine. Sea turtles once flourished around the base of Mount Hyjal and Nordrassil, but ever since Teldrassil was planted, their numbers have plummeted and stranded carcasses have begun washing ashore along Darkshore. She collects these salvageable specimens hoping biological study will reveal why the creatures are perishing.",al={"why collect sea turtle remains","why does gwennyth want turtle bones","sea turtle remains purpose"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The tragic stranding of these ancient ocean dwellers is a stark sign of nature out of balance following the battle at Mount Hyjal and the sudden arrival of Teldrassil.",["race:NightElf"]="The Temple of the Moon seeks to honor and understand the fading creatures that once frolicked peacefully beneath Nordrassil's boughs.",["class:Priest"]="Serving the Temple of the Moon by retrieving these remains helps the Sisterhood of Elune diagnose the unseen spiritual sickness spreading through Kalimdor's waters."},kw={"auberdine","beached","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","nordrassil","sea turtle","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:nordrassil","quest:940","topic:murloc","quest:4722"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4732},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (5)"}}
E["quest:4733"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along the rocky inlets of the Twilight Shore, the colossal carcass of a giant thresher lies stranded in the surf. Far larger than any known local specimens, its sudden death and stranding are part of a worrying trend of deep-sea anomalies troubling the night elves of Darkshore.",h="Along the rocky inlets of the Twilight Shore, the colossal carcass of a giant thresher lies stranded in the...",sec={{t="A Giant Cast Ashore",b="The Twilight Shore in southern Darkshore is often strewn with driftwood and sea debris, but this inlet holds something far more striking: the remains of an enormous thresher. Although scavengers and the tides have begun picking it apart, its massive skeleton dwarfs any ordinary predator found in these coastal shallows. It is clearly an outsider to these waters, driven onto the rocks either by unnatural sickness, disorientation, or some deeper disturbance out in the Veiled Sea.",sp=0},{t="The Temple's Vigil",b="In Auberdine, priestesses representing the Temple of the Moon have taken great interest in the dead giants washing ashore. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde oversees the collection of skeletal samples to determine what drives such deep-dwelling predators to their deaths. While colossal threshers were once sighted near the roots of Teldrassil, their numbers have steadily plummeted, leading the priestesses to fear that the fragile marine balance off Kalimdor's northern coast is unraveling.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of beast is this beached carcass?",a="It is the skeleton of an immense thresher, a predatory marine beast. It is several times larger than the common threshers native to the Darkshore coastline, making its presence here deeply anomalous.",al={"what is the beached sea creature","giant thresher darkshore","beached monster carcass"},it="identity"},{q="Where did this creature originally come from?",a="Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde notes that while specimens of this immense scale were once known to roam the waters near Teldrassil, their population has declined steadily. It is not native to the immediate shallows of Darkshore.",al={"where do giant threshers live","thresher origin"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the Temple of the Moon studying these carcasses?",a="The Temple of the Moon seeks to understand the widespread beaching phenomena plaguing the Darkshore coast. By inspecting bones and remains, the priestesses hope to determine whether corruption, disease, or external forces are driving deep-sea beasts onto land.",al={"why does gwennyth want bones","temple of the moon sea creatures","why study beached animals"},it="motive"},{q="Where should the bones be brought?",a="The Sea Creature Bones are brought to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a night elf researcher located in the harbor town of Auberdine.",al={"where to turn in sea creature bones","who gets the thresher bones"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where on the coast is this carcass located?",a="The carcass rests in a rocky inlet along the Twilight Shore, the southern coastal strip of Darkshore.",al={"where is the beached creature","thresher location darkshore","twilight shore skeleton"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are there other creatures beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="Yes. Multiple distinct sea beasts and behemoths have washed up along the length of Darkshore's coastline, prompting an ongoing investigation by the researchers in Auberdine.",al={"other beached animals","beached sea creature questline"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The unexplained decline and beaching of marine life close to Teldrassil strikes a nerve among the Kaldorei, who look to Elune and the Temple of the Moon to interpret such dark omens.",["class:Priest"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde conducts her study under the auspices of the Temple of the Moon, seeking balance and divine insight through tangible scientific inquiry into the sea's balance.",["class:Druid"]="The stranding of apex marine predators is a telltale sign of an ecosystem in distress, aligning closely with the Cenarion Circle's wider concerns throughout Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea creature bones","temple of the moon","thresher","twilight shore"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:4723","quest:3524","quest:940","topic:elune"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4733},src={"Beached Sea Creature (4)"}}
E["quest:4740"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Murkdeep!",z="darkshore",s="WANTED: Murkdeep! is an Alliance bounty posted on the notice board outside the inn in Auberdine. The village council seeks the death of Murkdeep, a dangerous murloc chieftain blamed for slaying a night elf Sentinel and sinking merchant vessels off Darkshore. Adventurers must march south along the mist-shrouded coast to draw out the raider and deliver justice.",h="WANTED: Murkdeep!",sec={{t="A Threat on the Mist-Shrouded Shoals",b="The Greymist murlocs along the Darkshore coastline are usually considered a nuisance, but Murkdeep escalated matters into open warfare against Auberdine. According to the wanted poster pinned outside the town inn, the ferocious beast is directly responsible for killing at least one night elf Sentinel and is suspected of sabotaging or wrecking two cargo vessels in the waters offshore. Facing mounting maritime losses and coastal raids, the Auberdine Village Council authorized a public bounty to put an end to the rampaging murloc leader.",sp=0},{t="The Ambush at the Huts",b="Murkdeep does not idly wander the open shoreline. He lurks off the southern coast near a cluster of murloc huts centered around a bonfire. Anyone trespassing into the encampment triggers an organized defense: waves of Greymist coastrunners and shore-crawlers surge from the surf to protect their settlement before Murkdeep himself emerges alongside his vanguard to strike down intruders.",sp=0},{t="Justice for the Fallen",b="Returning to Auberdine with proof of Murkdeep's demise fulfills a grim necessity for the Sentinels. Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea handles the bounty payout on behalf of the council. By breaking the Greymist leadership, travelers and shipping lanes traveling through the Darkshore fog are granted a reprieve from coastal sabotage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I pick up the bounty on Murkdeep?",a="You can accept the quest from the wanted poster posted right outside the inn in the center of Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"where to start wanted murkdeep","murkdeep quest start","auberdine wanted poster"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Auberdine council offering a bounty on Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is a particularly violent murloc responsible for slaying at least one night elf Sentinel and suspected of sinking two cargo vessels off the coast of Darkshore.",al={"why kill murkdeep","what did murkdeep do","murkdeep crimes"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is found far south of Auberdine along the beach, guarding a cluster of three murloc huts positioned around a central bonfire.",al={"murkdeep location","where is murkdeep","murkdeep camp"},gp=true},{q="Why isn't Murkdeep at the murloc camp when I arrive?",a="Murkdeep does not stand out in the open. Stepping between the huts near the bonfire triggers waves of Greymist murlocs emerging from the ocean. Murkdeep appears with the final wave once the initial defenders are slain.",al={"murkdeep not there","murkdeep spawn","how to summon murkdeep"},gp=true},{q="Who turns in the quest once Murkdeep is dead?",a="Report the death of Murkdeep to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea, who is stationed on duty in Auberdine.",al={"who to turn in murkdeep","murkdeep turn in","glynda nalshea location"},gp=true},{q="Are the murlocs at this camp different from other murlocs in Darkshore?",a="Murkdeep commands members of the Greymist murloc tribe, including coastal scouts and warriors that work in coordinated waves to defend their seaside encampment.",al={"greymist murlocs","murkdeep tribe","what murlocs are with murkdeep"},gp=true},{q="Who is Murkdeep and why is he a target?",a="Murkdeep is an exceptionally dangerous murloc chieftain who guards the Greymist murloc huts along the Darkshore coast south of Auberdine. Unlike ordinary shore-dwelling pests, he is officially blamed for the death of at least one night elf Sentinel and suspected of orchestrating the sinking of two cargo ships off the coast. His lethality makes him a priority threat to Auberdine's maritime safety and coastal defense.",al={"who is murkdeep","why target murkdeep","what did murkdeep do"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei defending Darkshore, slaying Murkdeep avenges a fallen sister of the Sentinels and safeguards the fragile lifeline Auberdine's docks provide.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as a vital northern trade hub, making the cargo ships Murkdeep sank a costly strike against Alliance logistics in Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","greymist","murkdeep","murloc","sentinels","wanted poster"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","topic:sentinels","quest:938"},m={start="WANTED: Murkdeep!",["end"]="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=4740,ri={"Murkdeep"}},src={"WANTED: Murkdeep! (quest)"}}
E["quest:4761"] = {t="quest",n="Thundris Windweaver",z="darkshore",s="Thundris Windweaver is an Alliance quest connecting the ranger Terenthis's reconnaissance of the local furbolgs to the civic leadership of Auberdine. Having confirmed the growing aggression of the nearby Blackwood tribe, adventurers are directed to report directly to Elder Windweaver. The elder seeks to understand the root causes of the encroaching taint warping Darkshore's wilderness.",h="Thundris Windweaver is an Alliance quest connecting the ranger Terenthis's reconnaissance of the local...",sec={{t="A Report to the Elder",b="Following your scouting mission into the corrupted furbolg camps of Darkshore, the ranger Terenthis directs you to Auberdine's village elder, Thundris Windweaver. While Terenthis monitors martial threats along the woodland borders, Thundris oversees the daily welfare of the settlement and weighs the broader spiritual and environmental perils facing the kaldorei. The report provides leadership with clear evidence that the furbolgs are not simply territorial, but actively deteriorating under an unnatural malice.",sp=0},{t="Corruption Along the Coast",b="Upon receiving word of the furbolg encampment, Thundris confirms that Auberdine has been wrestling with mounting hostility from native forest dwellers for some time. More distressing than the aggression alone is the creeping corruption infecting Darkshore's soil, flora, and waters. Believing that healing the land requires discovering the wellspring of this blight, Thundris turns his focus toward tracing the taint upstream, enlisting capable allies to investigate the region's waterways.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver serves as the elder of Auberdine, acting as a sage steward over the town's governance and daily affairs. He works closely with sentinels and druids to understand and combat the strange corruption spreading through Darkshore.",al={"thundris windweaver","auberdine elder","who is thundris"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Terenthis send you to Thundris?",a="After scouting the Blackwood furbolg camps, Terenthis determines that the town's civic leadership must be briefed. Thundris Windweaver holds theories on why the wildlife and furbolgs are falling to madness and requires firsthand intelligence to coordinate a response.",al={"why go to thundris","terenthis report","auberdine report"},it="motive"},{q="What is happening to the furbolgs in Darkshore?",a="The native furbolgs of Darkshore have grown increasingly violent, succumbing to a dark corruption that is warping the forest itself. Rather than simple border disputes, their hostility stems from a sinister taint poisoning the land.",al={"corrupted furbolgs","furbolg hostility","why are furbolgs mad"},it="conflict"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Elder Windweaver suspects that Darkshore's water sources may be carrying the source of the rot. He promptly directs adventurers to sample the Cliffspring River to determine where the contamination originates.",al={"next quest","what after thundris","cliffspring river quest"},it="next_step"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine represents the kaldorei's primary port and foothold on the mainland coast; bringing intelligence to Elder Windweaver directly aids your people's effort to preserve their sacred wilderness.",["class:Druid"]="The rapid corruption of the local furbolgs and forest dwellers signals a severe ecological imbalance that Cenarion allies and village elders cannot afford to ignore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Auberdine from hostile woodland tribes is vital for ensuring the safety of Alliance supply lines and travelers crossing between Kalimdor and Teldrassil."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","darkshore","furbolg","terenthis","thundris windweaver"},rel={"npc:terenthis","quest:984","quest:4762","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Terenthis",["end"]="Thundris Windweaver",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4761},src={"Thundris Windweaver (quest)"}}
E["quest:4762"] = {t="quest",n="The Cliffspring River",z="darkshore",s="The Cliffspring River is a major waterway in northern Darkshore that is rapidly turning foul and threatening the settlement of Auberdine. Thundris Windweaver tasks Alliance investigators with gathering a water sample from beneath a river bridge waterfall to confirm the creeping blight. The analysis points beyond the riverbanks to a much darker source of corruption festering in the eastern highlands.",h="The Cliffspring River is a major waterway in northern Darkshore that is rapidly turning foul and threatening...",sec={{t="A Tainted Waterway",b="Running down from the eastern highlands, the Cliffspring River empties into the coastal shoals along Mist's Edge, just north of Auberdine. Recently, its waters have begun to turn foul, carrying an unnatural rot toward the night elf settlement. Fearing that the wash will poison the surrounding shores and the town's supplies, Thundris Windweaver sends scouts upriver to draw samples from the waterfall pool beneath the road bridge.",sp=0},{t="The Root in Felwood",b="While the local Blackwood furbolgs have set up encampments along the river and show severe signs of agitation, Thundris suspects they are merely victims and conduits rather than the creators of the blight. Examining the drawn water confirms his fears: the taint trickles down directly from Felwood, the blighted forest to the east scarred during the Third War. Remedying the water will require confronting the corrupted furbolgs and purifying the land's ancient sources.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I collect the water sample?",a="Head north from Auberdine until you reach the mouth of the Cliffspring River along Mist's Edge. Follow the river inland to the first waterfall, located just beneath an overhead road bridge, and fill the sampling tube in the pool.",al={"where is the water sample","cliffspring river location","waterfall pool location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Cliffspring River turning foul?",a="The foul runoff trickles down from the blighted heights of Felwood to the east, carrying demonic corruption into Darkshore's river system and driving the local Blackwood furbolg tribe mad.",al={"why is river corrupted","what is poisoning darkshore water","cliffspring taint source"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf scholar and investigator stationed in Auberdine. He studies the ecological decay spreading through Darkshore and works to divine the causes of regional corruption.",al={"thundris windweaver lore","who gives cliffspring river quest"},it="identity"},{q="Are the furbolgs responsible for poisoning the river?",a="No. While the Blackwood furbolgs live along the river and spread violence in their mad state, they are merely victims of the taint washing down from Felwood rather than the true root of the plague.",al={"did furbolgs taint the water","blackwood furbolg corruption"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="How does this river impact Auberdine?",a="The Cliffspring River empties out into Mist's Edge just north of town. The coastal currents threaten to carry the putrid runoff straight into Auberdine's shoreline, endangering their fisheries, flora, and freshwater supply.",al={"threat to auberdine","why does auberdine care about cliffspring"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after testing the sample?",a="Testing confirms the corruption matches the blighted magic of Felwood, leading Thundris Windweaver to send adventurers further into Blackwood territory to investigate the tribe and seek a cure.",al={"quest after cliffspring river","what follows cliffspring river"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want this done?",a="Thundris Windweaver fears that the corruption spreading down the Cliffspring River will wash out into Mist's Edge and taint Auberdine itself. While he suspects the local Blackwood furbolgs have poisoned the river, he believes a deeper, older darkness is behind their madness. He needs raw evidence to diagnose the taint and formalize a plan of action before the settlement's waters are completely ruined.",al={"why thundris water sample","thundris windweaver motive","why clean cliffspring river"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Cliffspring River Sample for?",a="The Cliffspring River Sample allows Thundris Windweaver to inspect the foulness creeping into Darkshore's waterways. Examining the tainted water gives him the physical proof he needs to test its properties, trace its true origin toward the blighted forests of Felwood, and prepare an eventual cure.",al={"cliffspring river sample use","what is the water sample for","why collect water sample"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of the Cenarion Circle, seeing clean woodland waters turn putrid with lingering demonic taint is a call to arms to cleanse Darkshore's wounded nature.",["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine relies on the balance of Darkshore's coastline, and allowing Felwood's rot to spill into Mist's Edge endangers the homes and livelihood of the Kaldorei."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","darkshore","felwood","river","taint","thundris","waterfall","windweaver"},rel={"quest:4761","quest:4763","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:mist-s-edge","zone:felwood","topic:furbolg","quest:938"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4762,ri={"Cliffspring River Sample"}},src={"The Cliffspring River"}}
E["quest:4763"] = {t="quest",n="The Blackwood Corrupted",z="darkshore",s="Following evidence found in the tainted waters of Cliffspring River, Thundris Windweaver sends adventurers to sever the dark influence strangling the Blackwood tribe. By purifying their food supply with moonwell water, you provoke their demonic handler into the open to shatter his hold on the northern camp.",h="Following evidence found in the tainted waters of Cliffspring River, Thundris Windweaver sends adventurers to...",sec={{t="A Hidden Master",b="The night elves of Auberdine have long struggled to understand why the once-peaceful Blackwood furbolgs turned so viciously against their neighbors. Investigations along the Cliffspring River traced the rot to satyr meddling. These ancient servants of the Burning Legion have been actively manipulating the tribe, channeling fel magic through insidious talismans to twist the minds of the furbolgs and drive them into feral aggression.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Shackles",b="To lure the puppet master into the open, Thundris Windweaver concocts a simple yet potent remedy. By gathering common rations—grain, fruit, and nuts—from the northern Blackwood settlement and immersing them in holy waters drawn from Auberdine's moonwell, the tainted nourishment is purified. Offering this blessed food at the central bonfire grants nearby furbolgs a brief respite from their madness, directly exposing the meddling satyr corruptor, Xabraxxis, who emerges in fury to defend his twisted dominion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the Blackwood furbolgs aggressive?",a="Their minds have been poisoned by demonic influence. Satyrs secretly planted themselves near the camps, channeling foul magic through enchanted talismans to twist the furbolgs' natural instincts into rabid violence.",al={"why furbolgs mad","why are furbolgs hostile","blackwood aggression"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Xabraxxis?",a="Xabraxxis is a satyr corruptor overseeing the northern Blackwood furbolg camp. He works from the shadows to ensure the tribe remains gripped by fel madness, relying on a Talisman of Corruption to sustain his control.",al={"xabraxxis lore","who is the satyr","satyr boss darkshore"},it="target"},{q="Does cleansing their food cure the furbolgs forever?",a="No. The moonwell-infused nourishment only breaks the demonic haze long enough for them to recognize peace and draw out Xabraxxis. Slaying the satyr and claiming his talisman is a significant victory, but Thundris Windweaver notes that discovering a permanent cure for the corrupted tribes will take further effort.",al={"is the cure permanent","did we save the furbolgs","are furbolgs cured"},sp=1},{q="Where did the idea to use moonwell water come from?",a="Moonwells are sacred pools blessed by the Goddess Elune, brimming with rejuvenating magic that counters fel and undeath. Thundris Windweaver provides a cleansing bowl so its sanctified waters can neutralize the demonic toxins woven into the furbolgs' foodstuffs.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell cleansing bowl"},it="history"},{q="What happens when the food bowl is placed at the bonfire?",a="The nearby furbolgs briefly snap out of their bloodlust, gather peacefully around the blessed food, and cease attacking. Enraged that his puppets are breaking free of their torment, Xabraxxis immediately manifests to punish the meddlers.",al={"bowl near bonfire","cleansing the furbolgs"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf researcher and investigator stationed in Auberdine. He coordinates efforts to uncover the root causes behind Darkshore's creeping ecological decay and the madness gripping local wildlife.",al={"thundris windweaver lore","who gives the quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want this done?",a="Thundris Windweaver sees the furbolgs not merely as dangerous beasts, but as ancient allies driven mad by dark magic. The night elves believe that purging the demonic influence gripping the Blackwood tribe is crucial to restoring the balance of Darkshore's forests. By identifying the root of the corruption and stripping the satyrs of their power, Thundris hopes to save the furbolgs from permanent spiritual ruin.",al={"why help thundris","thundris windweaver goal","why purify the furbolgs"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Talisman of Corruption for?",a="The Talisman of Corruption is a sinister demonic relic channeled by the satyr to subvert the natural will of the furbolgs. Through it, corruptors twist the minds of the Blackwood tribe, maintaining a relentless magical grip that drives them to madness and hostility. Thundris needs it seized and destroyed to break that hold and reclaim the forest.",al={"talisman of corruption purpose","what does the talisman of corruption do","satyr talisman"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The furbolgs were ancient allies of the kaldorei during the War of the Ancients; watching them fall under the sway of their ancestral enemies, the satyrs, is a bitter tragedy night elves are eager to right.",["class:Druid"]="Restoring balance demands cutting out the rot at its root. Seeing a satyr use fel talismans to warp primal woodland creatures makes confronting Xabraxxis an urgent priority for the Cenarion Circle.",["class:Priest"]="Channeling the pure, restorative grace of Elune through moonwell waters provides a stark contrast to the corrupting shadow and fel magic deployed by the satyr."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","furbolg","moonwell","satyr","talisman of corruption","thundris windweaver","xabraxxis"},rel={"quest:4762","quest:4761","topic:furbolg","topic:satyr","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=4763,ri={"Talisman of Corruption"}},src={"The Blackwood Corrupted"}}
E["quest:4811"] = {t="quest",n="The Red Crystal",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea of Auberdine tasks travelers with investigating rumors of a mysterious red crystal embedded along Darkshore's eastern mountains. With hostile moonkin multiplying nearby and appearing drawn to the formation, the Sentinels need to confirm whether the anomaly truly exists.",h="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea of Auberdine tasks travelers with investigating rumors of a mysterious red crystal...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Shift in the Wilds",b="For generations, the night elves of Kalimdor viewed moonkin as gentle, mystical creatures closely tied to the wilderness. In recent days, however, aggressive packs have multiplied rapidly along the slopes east of Auberdine. While some traditionalists maintain reverence for the moonkin, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea prioritizes the town's safety and cannot ignore the rising danger. Reports suggest the beasts are flocking to a specific location along the eastern peaks.",sp=0},{t="The Eastern Mountain Anomaly",b="Scouts and wanderers brought whispers of an unnatural red crystal jutting from the rocky hillside high above Darkshore. Because wild rumors spread easily in the fog-bound coast, Glynda seeks boots on the ground to separate myth from fact. Finding the crimson monolith confirms that the anomaly is very real, leaving the Sentinels to puzzle out why the local moonkin are inexplicably drawn to it and whether its presence portends a sinister influence over the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the red crystal in Darkshore?",a="It is an enigmatic, glowing crimson formation embedded in the eastern mountain range above Darkshore. The Sentinels initially knew little about its origins, only that local wildlife—particularly moonkin—appear irresistibly drawn toward its location.",al={"what is red crystal","darkshore crystal","red rock auberdine"},it="item"},{q="Who sends you to look for the red crystal?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea, stationed in Auberdine, assigns the mission. She is responsible for defending the settlement and wants firsthand confirmation of the rumors surrounding the eastern mountains.",al={"who gives the red crystal quest","glynda nalshea quest","auberdine crystal quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why are moonkin behaving aggressively around the crystal?",a="Historically regarded as gentle and mystical beings, the moonkin have become territorial and volatile. Sentinel Glynda suspects their sudden change in behavior and swelling numbers are linked directly to whatever power radiates from the mysterious red crystal.",al={"why are moonkin mad","angry moonkin darkshore","moonkin hostile"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the red crystal located?",a="The crystal lies due east of Auberdine, nestled high up along the rugged eastern mountain ridge of Darkshore, surrounded by prowling moonkin.",al={"where to find red crystal","red crystal location","darkshore red crystal map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the crystal considered dangerous by the night elves?",a="Sentinel Glynda is deeply cautious. While unsure whether the stone is benign or sinister, the fact that it agitates and congregates wild beasts makes it an immediate concern for the security of Auberdine.",al={"is the crystal bad","is red crystal evil"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after you discover the crystal?",a="Reporting its existence back to Glynda proves the rumors true. She immediately seeks to uncover its true nature, leading to efforts to cleanse and sample it using water from the Auberdine moonwell.",al={"what is after red crystal","as water cascades follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea want the red crystal found?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea is tasked with safeguarding Auberdine. While moonkin were once revered as gentle and mystical beings, their numbers east of the town are surging and they have turned increasingly aggressive. Rumors suggest the creatures are congregating around a mysterious red formation in the eastern mountains. Glynda needs to confirm whether the crystal actually exists so she can assess whether it poses a direct danger to Auberdine and determine why the wild moonkin are so strangely drawn to it.",al={"why glynda nal'shea wants red crystal","sentinel glynda motives","why find the red crystal"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The agitation of the moonkin is a troubling sight for Kaldorei, who revere these creatures as sacred wards of Elune and nature.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold close spiritual ties to moonkin and the natural order of Darkshore, making the crystal's corruptive or disruptive pull an urgent ecological concern.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary coastal port on northern Kalimdor; any unchecked threat gathering in the hills risks isolating the haven from the wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","moonkin","red crystal","sentinels"},rel={"quest:4812","quest:4813","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4811},src={"The Red Crystal"}}
E["quest:4812"] = {t="quest",n="As Water Cascades",z="darkshore",s="As Water Cascades is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where players test the nature of the mysterious red crystal jutting from the eastern mountain wall. By pouring sacred moonwell water from Auberdine over its surface, players attempt to pierce its opaque exterior and uncover where it came from.",h="As Water Cascades is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where players test the nature of the mysterious red...",sec={{t="Purifying the Unknown",b="After the red crystal is first sighted high on the eastern cliffs of Darkshore, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea devises a way to examine its composition safely. Moonwell waters carry potent divine and restorative magic, blessed by the night elves' devotion to Elune. Glynda reasons that dousing the alien monolith with water drawn from the moonwell in Auberdine will trigger a reaction, cutting through its strange, opaque shell without destroying it outright.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of Felwood",b="Nal'Shea's concern stems largely from geography. Darkshore's eastern ridge looms beneath the corrupted heights of Felwood, a forest twisted by demonic energies during the Third War. If the red spire is linked to Felwood's corruption, handling it carries immense risk. When the sacred water trickles down the crystal's lattice, the humming stone momentarily turns transparent, hinting that whatever lies trapped within requires a closer look.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I get the water for this quest?",a="You must draw the water from the moonwell located in the night elf settlement of Auberdine, using the empty vial provided by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",al={"where is the moonwell","moonwell water location","fill empty water tube"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does moonwell water affect the crystal?",a="Moonwells hold consecrated, magic-rich water blessed by Elune. Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea anticipates that its purifying essence will react against the foreign energy of the stone and reveal its hidden composition.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell magic on crystal"},it="power"},{q="Where is the red crystal located?",a="The mysterious red crystal rests along Darkshore's eastern mountain wall, nestled into the rocky foothills separating the shore from the highlands above.",al={"red crystal location","where is the crystal","red crystal darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Sentinel Glynda worried about Felwood?",a="Felwood lies directly east and above Darkshore, ravaged by demonic corruption from the Third War. Because the crystal appeared near the boundary ridge, Glynda fears it may share that foul, demonic origin.",al={"glynda felwood","connection to felwood"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you pour the water on the crystal?",a="As the moonwell water cascades down the crystal's facets, the stone hums and its normally opaque outer shell briefly turns transparent, revealing deeper secrets sealed inside.",al={"pouring water result","what happens to the crystal"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who gives the quest As Water Cascades?",a="The quest is given by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine, immediately following the reconnaissance mission, The Red Crystal.",al={"quest giver","who starts as water cascades"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What is the Moonwell Water Tube for?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea provides the tube so you can collect purified water from Auberdine's moonwell and carry it to the mysterious red crystal. Moonwells hold potent, blessed magic capable of reacting with magical anomalies. By pouring the water over the strange stone, Glynda hopes its sacred energy will react with the structure and reveal clues about what it is made of—and whether it poses a danger to Darkshore.",al={"moonwell water tube purpose","why do i need moonwell water","moonwell water tube quest"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, moonwells are sacred fonts of life and solace. Using their consecrated waters as a tool of revelation highlights how central Elune's grace is to untangling threats along their borders.",["class:Druid"]="Druids watching over Darkshore's fragile ecosystem are naturally suspicious of unnatural foreign formations, especially along the ridge below corrupted Felwood.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts based in Auberdine must keep the coast secure from looming corruption creeping down from the eastern highlands."},kw={"as water cascades","auberdine","darkshore","empty water tube","felwood","glynda nal'shea","moonwell","red crystal"},rel={"quest:4811","quest:4813","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:felwood"},m={start="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",["end"]="Mysterious Red Crystal",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4812,ri={"Moonwell Water Tube"}},src={"As Water Cascades"}}
E["quest:4813"] = {t="quest",n="The Fragments Within",z="darkshore",s="\"The Fragments Within\" is the concluding task in the investigation of the mysterious red crystal jutting from the cliffs east of Auberdine. Equipped with purified moonwell water, you are sent back to the site to examine what lies within the strange formation and report back to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",h="\"The Fragments Within\" is the concluding task in the investigation of the mysterious red crystal jutting from...",sec={{t="A Grim Revelation",b="Pouring blessed moonwell water over the crimson crystal clears away the murky exterior, exposing what lies trapped beneath its polished surface. Suspended inside the dense mineral are several small bone fragments and half of a humanoid jawbone. The stone encasing them is extraordinarily tough—so durable that even formidable spells would struggle to crack it open. Whatever entity or artifact spawned these remains, it has been preserved in uncanny isolation above the Darkshore coastline.",sp=1},{t="Reporting to Auberdine",b="Returning to Auberdine, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea takes note of your disturbing discovery. Rather than offering definitive answers, the revelation only raises more concerns among the local night elf leadership. Glynda promises to present the findings to the town council, though she takes solace in the fact that the strange crystal sits high in the eastern cliffs, far enough from town that it poses no immediate danger to the residents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is trapped inside the red crystal?",a="Washing the crystal with sanctified moonwell water makes it transparent enough to spot several bone fragments and half of a humanoid jawbone embedded deep inside.",al={"what is in the crystal","what are the fragments","what bones are inside"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Can the crystal be broken open to inspect the bones?",a="No. The crystal is exceptionally resilient. Even the strongest forms of magic would find breaking through its structure nearly impossible, leaving the exact identity of the bones a mystery.",al={"can you break the crystal","opening the red crystal"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="Who do you report the findings to?",a="You report your findings to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea, who is stationed in the port town of Auberdine.",al={"who turns in the fragments within","quest turn in","glynda nalshea"},it="next_step"},{q="What will the Sentinels do about the crystal?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea plans to inform the council in Auberdine so they can deliberate on potential actions. However, because the crystal rests high in the eastern cliffs, it is not viewed as an urgent threat.",al={"what happens next with the crystal","auberdine council crystal"},sp=1,it="today"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The discovery of humanoid bones suspended in strange crystal along the mountain borders of Ashenvale and Felwood warrants careful vigilance from the Sentinels guarding Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="The mysterious mineral resists natural wear and high magic alike, serving as a curious anomaly against the traditional balance of the wild."},kw={"auberdine","bone fragments","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","jawbone","moonwell water","mysterious red crystal"},rel={"quest:4812","quest:4811","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood"},m={start="Mysterious Red Crystal",["end"]="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4813},src={"The Fragments Within"}}
E["quest:5321"] = {t="quest",n="The Sleeper Has Awakened",z="darkshore",s="Kerlonian Evershade, a recently awakened Druid of the Claw, struggles to remain awake on his journey toward Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Entrusted with his Horn of Awakening, travelers must shepherd the lethargic druid along the forested border, rousing him when he drifts into slumber and defending him against wild furbolgs and sinister cultists.",h="Kerlonian Evershade, a recently awakened Druid of the Claw, struggles to remain awake on his journey toward...",sec={{t="A Slumbering Mind",b="For millennia, the Druids of the Claw slept within barrows, communing with the wild spirits across the Emerald Dream. Though the Third War demanded their awakening, shaking off centuries of hibernation does not come easily to every mind. Kerlonian Evershade set out south from Darkshore toward Ashenvale to rendezvous with Liladris Moonriver, but exhaustion overtook him shortly into his trek. Finding himself helplessly prone to sudden naps along the wilds, he relies on a brass Horn of Awakening and passing allies to keep his feet moving.",sp=0},{t="Peril Along the Road",b="The path connecting Darkshore to Ashenvale is far from tranquil. As Kerlonian meanders southward, his vulnerable state invites aggression from the surrounding wilderness. In Twilight Vale, corrupted Blackwood furbolgs stalk the roadway, while farther south into Ashenvale, members of the shadowy Dark Strand cult lurk in ambush. Escorting the groggy druid requires a vigilant watch, as Kerlonian will simply lie down to sleep wherever he stands unless forcefully roused with the horn.",sp=0},{t="Arrival at the Outpost",b="Upon surviving the ambushes and reaching Maestra's Post, Kerlonian promptly slips away to find another comfortable patch of grass to continue his interrupted nap. His contact, Liladris Moonriver, expresses little surprise at his habitual daze, greeting his arrival with fond exasperation. Kerlonian's struggle reflects the lingering disorientation shared by many druids who find the waking world jarring compared to the timeless tranquility of the Dream.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Kerlonian keep falling asleep?",a="Kerlonian Evershade is a Druid of the Claw who only recently awoke from centuries of hibernation in the Emerald Dream. Returning to the waking world leaves many druids disoriented and profoundly lethargic, making it nearly impossible for him to stay awake without constant external stimulation.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","why is he so sleepy","druid falling asleep"},it="why_here"},{q="How do you wake Kerlonian up when he naps?",a="You must use the Horn of Awakening, which is retrieved from a chest beside Kerlonian when the journey begins. Whenever he collapses into slumber along the trail, blowing the horn will snap him back to his senses so he can continue following.",al={"how to wake kerlonian","kerlonian horn","horn of awakening use"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is waiting for Kerlonian at Maestra's Post?",a="He is traveling to meet Liladris Moonriver, an elf stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. She is familiar with his chronic sleepiness and is simply relieved to see him arrive intact.",al={"who is liladris","who is kerlonian meeting"},it="target"},{q="What enemies attack along the way?",a="The road leads past Twilight Vale, where hostile Blackwood furbolgs ambush the party. Further south into Ashenvale, excavators, adepts, and cultists belonging to the secretive Dark Strand strike from the shadows.",al={"ambushes during escort","what attacks kerlonian","twilight vale ambush"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the title 'The sleeper has awakened' come from?",a="It is the iconic greeting spoken by Druids of the Claw upon being called into service during the Third War, highlighting Kerlonian's nature as an awakened shapeshifter.",al={"sleeper has awakened quote","druid voiceline"},it="origin"},{q="What happens to the horn if you take too long?",a="The Horn of Awakening carries a limited duration before it vanishes from your possessions. If the escort takes too long or must be restarted after a failure, a replacement must be gathered from the chest at Kerlonian's resting spot.",al={"horn expired","horn of awakening disappeared"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kerlonian Evershade need an escort to Maestra's Post?",a="Kerlonian is traveling south to reunite with Liladris Moonriver at Maestra's Post, but his long slumber in the Emerald Dream has left him chronically exhausted and disoriented. Unable to stay awake for long stretches and unfamiliar with the treacherous road into Ashenvale, he cannot safely make the journey alone without someone to guide him and stir him whenever he dozes off.",al={"why escort kerlonian","kerlonian evershade purpose","why go to maestras post"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Horn of Awakening?",a="The Horn of Awakening is Kerlonian's personal enchanted instrument, kept stored in a chest by his campsite. Because awakening from the Emerald Dream has left him battling overwhelming fatigue, the horn's sharp call cuts through his lingering, magically heavy drowsiness to shake him awake whenever he collapses into a roadside slumber.",al={"horn of awakening lore","what does horn of awakening do","kerlonian horn"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Kerlonian ask you for help instead of the night elf sentinels?",a="Kerlonian has stopped far from any fortified night elf outpost, isolated in the wilds of southern Darkshore. With Sentinel patrols stretched thin guarding against regional threats, no guards are stationed nearby to attend to a dozing druid. As a traveling adventurer passing through, you are his only immediate hope for a guide and protector on the road toward Ashenvale.",al={"why does kerlonian need me","why ask adventurer kerlonian","why not sentinels kerlonian"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids will recognize the heavy toll of deep communion with the Emerald Dream, as prolonged hibernation often leaves the waking mind slow to regain full consciousness.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Kerlonian is a familiar sight of their culture's recent upheaval, representing the thousands of druids who answered the call of the horn during the Third War and now adjust to daylight.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing the safe passage of travelers between Darkshore and northern Ashenvale helps maintain vital communication lines between Auberdine and outlying sentry posts."},kw={"ashenvale","dark strand","darkshore","druid of the claw","evershade","horn of awakening","kerlonian","liladris","maestra's post","twilight vale"},rel={"npc:kerlonian-evershade","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:twilight-vale","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid","quest:2561"},m={start="Kerlonian Evershade",["end"]="Liladris Moonriver",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=5321,ri={"Horn of Awakening"}},src={"The Sleeper Has Awakened (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5713"] = {t="quest",n="One Shot. One Kill.",z="darkshore",s="While carrying an urgent message toward Auberdine, Sentinel Aynasha was ambushed and poisoned by a hostile furbolg named Marosh the Devious and his pack of trackers. Immobilized while mixing an antidote, she relies on nearby travelers to hold off incoming attackers so she can survive and see her duty through.",h="While carrying an urgent message toward Auberdine, Sentinel Aynasha was ambushed and poisoned by a hostile...",sec={{t="Ambush on the Forest Road",b="The trails through northern Kalimdor have grown treacherous as corruption takes deeper root among the wild denizens. Sentinel Aynasha was journeying toward Auberdine bearing important communications when she was intercepted by hostile furbolgs. Led by Marosh the Devious, the ambushers struck fast, inflicting a debilitating venom that left the scout unsteady and unable to complete her trek on foot.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Line",b="Though skilled with natural concoctions, concocting and administering an antidote under the canopy takes time Aynasha does not possess while hunted. As Marosh's trackers close in, Aynasha must rely on travelers to guard her position while she works. Despite her failing strength, she steadies her bow to rain covering fire into the brush, determined that neither she nor her missive will fall in the wilds.",sp=0},{t="Report to Maestra's Post",b="Once the assault is broken and Marosh is slain, the antidote restores Aynasha's strength enough for her to finish her journey to Auberdine. To ensure the outpost south in Ashenvale is alerted to the aggressive furbolg activity threatening regional supply routes, she bids her protectors report directly to Sentinel Onaeya at Maestra's Post.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Aynasha?",a="Sentinel Aynasha is a night elf scout tasked with carrying critical messages across the borders of Darkshore and Ashenvale. Skilled with a bow and woodland survival, she was nearly undone by an unexpected poison ambush while on duty.",al={"sentinel aynasha","aynasha","who is aynasha"},it="identity"},{q="Who attacked Sentinel Aynasha?",a="She was ambushed by a pack of hostile furbolg led by Marosh the Devious. They poisoned her during the initial clash, hoping to overwhelm the immobilized scout before she could recover.",al={"who attacked her","marosh the devious","marosh","who poisoned her"},it="threat"},{q="Where was Sentinel Aynasha traveling?",a="Aynasha was bound for Auberdine to deliver an important dispatch before being trapped on the road by Marosh and his trackers.",al={"where was aynasha going","aynasha destination","lor'danel"},it="place"},{q="Why must you report to Sentinel Onaeya?",a="Because Aynasha must press forward immediately to Auberdine to deliver her message, she asks you to travel south to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale to inform Sentinel Onaeya about the furbolg hostility.",al={"sentinel onaeya","why maestra's post","onaeya"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in the area hostile?",a="Across Darkshore and Ashenvale, many furbolg tribes have succumbed to demonic taint and madness stemming from the Third War, driving them to attack traveling Sentinels and wayside travelers indiscriminately.",al={"why are furbolgs attacking","furbolg hostility","corrupted furbolg"},it="hostile"},{q="Does Aynasha fight during the ambush?",a="Yes. Even though the venom leaves her barely able to stand, she supports her defender by providing covering fire with her bow while preparing the antidote.",al={"does aynasha help","aynasha bow","does she fight"},gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Aynasha need your protection?",a="Aynasha carries an urgent message bound for Lor'danel, but an ambush by local furbolgs left her struck by a debilitating poison. She is barely able to stand, much less complete her journey on her own. She needs you to stand guard and keep the attackers at bay long enough for her to concoct and administer an antidote so she can recover and see her mission through.",al={"why help aynasha","aynasha motive","why does aynasha need help"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who is attacking Sentinel Aynasha?",a="The ambush is led by Marosh the Devious and his pack of furbolg trackers. The corrupted furbolgs stalking these borders prey on vulnerable travelers along the road, and they struck Aynasha to cut down an isolated night elf messenger.",al={"who leads the ambush","who is marosh","aynasha attackers"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why can't Aynasha fight off the furbolgs herself?",a="Although Aynasha is a skilled Sentinel archer and will support you with her bow, the venom coursing through her veins leaves her severely weakened and barely able to stand. She cannot manage close combat while simultaneously focusing on preparing her antidote, leaving her life entirely in your hands.",al={"why me aynasha","why does aynasha need me","why cant aynasha fight"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Defending Aynasha preserves both a sister of the Sentinels and critical communications moving between outposts in Ashenvale and northern Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the woodland paths clear of aggressive furbolg packs ensures safe passage between Ashenvale and the Alliance strongholds to the north.",["class:Hunter"]="Aynasha demonstrates the unwavering resolve of a marksman, continuing to loose deadly shots into the brush even while succumbing to potent venom."},kw={"ambush","antidote","aynasha","darkshore","furbolg","lor'danel","maestra's post","marosh","onaeya","sentinel"},rel={"npc:sentinel-aynasha","npc:sentinel-onaeya","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:elune"},m={start="Sentinel Aynasha",["end"]="Sentinel Onaeya",faction="Alliance",id=5713},src={"One Shot. One Kill."}}
E["quest:6122"] = {t="quest",n="The Principal Source",z="darkshore",s="The Principal Source is an essential rite of passage for young night elf druids learning to understand and mend the natural world. Dispatched from Moonglade by Dendrite Starblaze, initiates must collect corrupted water from Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore to help Auberdine naturalist Alanndarian Nightsong halt a spreading sickness among the forest deer.",h="The Principal Source is an essential rite of passage for young night elf druids learning to understand and...",sec={{t="A Vital Waterway Corrupted",b="Cliffspring Falls provides the primary freshwater supply for the northern reaches of Darkshore. When wildlife—particularly the local deer populations—began succumbing to an unnatural, lingering malady, the Cenarion Circle turned their attention to the river. Suspecting that the aquifer itself was compromised, Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade entrusts novice druids with the crucial task of traveling to the mouth of the cavern beneath the falls to gather an untouched sample of the tainted water.",sp=0},{t="Shadows at the Falls",b="Sampling the water is not without peril. Vicious naga have established a presence inside Cliffspring River Cave, nesting near the very headwaters of the falls. Their presence around the subterranean spring poses a direct threat to anyone investigating the blight. Despite the danger, securing an uncontaminated sample from the cave mouth is the only way for the Cenarion Circle to study the agent sickening the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="A Deeper Malady",b="Upon delivering the sample to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, the foulness of the water confirms the worst fears of the Circle. Yet examining the foul liquid reveals an unsettling truth: while the corrupted waterfall is indeed the main conduit poisoning the riverbanks, afflicted deer have been spotted far beyond its direct path. The water serves as a vital reagent to begin crafting an antidote, but Alanndarian suspects a deeper, broader corruption is spreading across Darkshore's entire water table.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?",a="Cliffspring Falls acts as the principal natural source of drinking water for northern Darkshore. Because its flows supply local streams, rivers, and the surrounding flora and fauna, any contaminant introduced at its headwaters quickly spreads throughout the entire regional biome.",al={"why cliffspring falls matters","cliffspring river importance","darkshore water source"},it="place"},{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore falling ill?",a="The local deer drink directly from Cliffspring Falls and the streams it feeds. A virulent pollutant has tainted the water table at the source, causing the woodland creatures to suffer from a crippling, debilitating illness.",al={"why are deer sick","darkshore sick deer","what poisoned the deer"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is an elder druid trainer residing in the sacred haven of Moonglade. Acting as a guide for ascending druids, he monitors disturbances across Kalimdor and coordinates the Cenarion Circle's response to natural crises.",al={"dendrite starblaze lore","who gave me this quest","starblaze moonglade"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf naturalist stationed in Auberdine. Distressed by the spreading corruption and suffering fauna across Darkshore, she petitioned the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade for experienced aid to study the affliction and formulate a cure.",al={"who is alanndarian nightsong","nightsong auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Why are naga at Cliffspring Falls?",a="Naga from the Darkshore coast have pushed inland and occupied the cave system behind Cliffspring Falls. Their encroaching presence creates extreme hazard for anyone attempting to access the headwaters to investigate the water supply.",al={"naga in cliffspring cave","why are naga here","cliffspring falls naga"},it="threat"},{q="What ability does this quest help druids learn?",a="This investigation is part of the 'Power over Poison' trial. By diagnosing this wildlife plague and synthesizing an antidote alongside Alanndarian Nightsong, druid initiates learn the vital magical art of curing poisons.",al={"what spell does this give","druid poison quest","cure poison chain"},it="power"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze want this done?",a="As an emissary of the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade, Dendrite Starblaze is bound to protect the natural balance of Kalimdor. Alanndarian Nightsong reached out from Auberdine seeking aid against a virulent sickness poisoning Darkshore's wildlife. Dendrite suspects the contamination originates at Cliffspring Falls, the region's main freshwater source, and must confirm its source to help create a cure.",al={"dendrite motive","why does dendrite send me","why investigate cliffspring falls"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler for?",a="The sampler holds corrupted water drawn directly from the cave mouth at Cliffspring Falls. Delivering it to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine allows her to analyze the precise nature of the poison afflicting Darkshore's wildlife and begin concocting an effective cure.",al={"filled cliffspring falls sampler use","what is the water sample for","why collect cliffspring water"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze send you instead of handling it himself?",a="Dendrite serves as a key liaison for the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade, coordinating broader druidic efforts across Kalimdor. Investigating the source and collaborating with Alanndarian on the ground in Darkshore offers an essential field trial for an advancing druid learning to wield power over poison.",al={"why me dendrite","why does dendrite need druids","why send an initiate"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This task is part of a foundational druidic trial. By confronting ecological decay at Cliffspring Falls and compounding remedies, you awaken the spiritual and botanical knowledge required to cure poisons in the wild.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the corruption of Cliffspring Falls represents a direct desecration of their ancestral forests, demanding immediate intervention to preserve the land's innocent creatures."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring falls","cure poison","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","naga","power over poison"},rel={"quest:6125","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","subzone:cliffspring-falls","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:cenarion-circle","quest:947"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6122,ri={"Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler"}},src={"The Principal Source (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6123"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering the Cure",z="darkshore",s="Gathering the Cure is an essential trial for young night elf druids learning to master nature's healing powers in Darkshore. Guided by Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, the druid collects vital natural reagents to brew a restorative salve for the region's ailing wildlife. This task lays the practical foundation for understanding how herbal remedies combat venom and disease.",h="Gathering the Cure is an essential trial for young night elf druids learning to master nature's healing...",sec={{t="A Remedy for Darkshore's Wildlife",b="Following the discovery of a contaminated water source plaguing the local wildlife, Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine sets out to concoct an effective curative salve. While pure water forms the base of the mixture, genuine healing requires potent natural catalysts. The afflicted forest deer cannot recover on their own, making the gathering of wholesome remedies a matter of urgency for the Cenarion Circle.",sp=0},{t="Roots and Lunar Blooms",b="The restorative salve demands two crucial flora: Earthroot and Lunar Fungus. Earthroot provides pure curative properties, requiring the practiced eye of an herbalist to harvest from the rocky soil. To lend the mixture potency, Alanndarian sends the druid into the nearby eastern caves to gather fungal blooms that flourish in the dark, nestled among increasingly territorial and agitated moonkin.",sp=0},{t="The Path to Poison Cleansing",b="Synthesizing a specific antidote for every toxin is a meticulous and demanding task. By walking the initiate through the delicate gathering and brewing of physical ingredients, Alanndarian demonstrates the sheer effort conventional medicine requires. This hands-on brewing serves as a stepping stone toward mastering the innate druidic art of purging toxins purely through nature magic.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Gathering the Cure?",a="The quest tasks a druid initiate with gathering Earthroot and Lunar Fungus for Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine. These reagents are used to craft a curative salve to treat the sick deer of Darkshore, serving as an instructional step in learning to neutralize poisons.",al={"why do this quest","gathering the cure goal","what is gathering the cure for"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Lunar Fungus grow?",a="Lunar Fungus grows inside the caves situated in the hills directly east of Auberdine. Druids must navigate these dens carefully, as the resident wild moonkin have grown territorial and aggressive.",al={"where is lunar fungus","lunar fungus location","how to find lunar fungus"},gp=true},{q="Do I need to be an herbalist to get Earthroot?",a="You do not need Herbalism yourself, though Earthroot is harvested from wild herb nodes. If you do not practice the trade, you must trade with an herbalist or acquire it from others to complete Alanndarian's recipe.",al={"need herbalism for earthroot","can non herbalists get earthroot","earthroot without profession"},gp=true},{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a Cenarion Circle druid stationed in Auberdine. She monitors the health of Darkshore's flora and fauna, guiding young druids through their initial trials to cleanse and preserve the wilderness.",al={"who is alanndarian","alanndarian nightsong lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore sick?",a="The deer have consumed water tainted by a contaminated spring in the wilderness. The resulting poison leaves them incapacitated and suffering, requiring an active curative salve to relieve their symptoms.",al={"why are deer poisoned","sick deer darkshore","what poisoned the deer"},it="origin"},{q="How does this quest help me learn Cure Poison?",a="This quest is part of the larger 'Power over Poison' training. By showing initiates how painstaking it is to prepare herbal antidotes for individual toxins, the Cenarion Circle prepares them to channel raw nature magic that can neutralize poisons effortlessly.",al={"cure poison quest druid","learn cure poison","power over poison chain"},it="power"},{q="Why does Alanndarian Nightsong want this done?",a="As a druid watching over Darkshore from Auberdine, Alanndarian cannot stand idly by while the native wildlife suffers. The local deer have succumbed to a debilitating affliction and cannot recover on their own. Crafting an effective curative salve is her immediate priority to halt their agony and restore balance to the corrupted woods.",al={"alanndarian motive","why help sick deer","why does alanndarian care"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Earthroot for?",a="Alanndarian uses the earthroot to imbue her curative salve with restorative properties. Mixed into the water drawn from the pure spring on Cliffspring Falls, the natural medicinal essence of the herb counteracts the toxins sickening the Darkshore deer.",al={"why earthroot","what does earthroot do","earthroot salve"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Lunar Fungus for?",a="The lunar fungus provides the necessary potency for the salve. Its potent natural bloom amplifies the mixture's curative strength, ensuring the remedy is powerful enough to purge the deep-seated poison affecting the afflicted deer.",al={"why lunar fungus","lunar fungus purpose","fungus for salve"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This rite of passage teaches young druids how mortal medicine interacts with natural toxins, laying the groundwork for channeling raw curative energy without mundane tools.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Alanndarian specifically notes the value of herbalists, who possess the trained eye needed to harvest Earthroot directly from the earth.",["race:NightElf"]="Protecting the sacred groves and fauna of Darkshore is a sacred duty for the kaldorei, who revere Elune and the spirits of the wild."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cure poison","darkshore","druid quest","earthroot","gathering the cure","lunar fungus","moonkin caves"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","quest:6125","topic:druid","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6123,ri={"Earthroot","Lunar Fungus"}},src={"Gathering the Cure (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6124"] = {t="quest",n="Curing the Sick",z="darkshore",s="Curing the Sick is an essential trial for young Alliance druids, tasking them with using a prepared salve to heal the poisoned wildlife wandering Darkshore. By directly relieving the afflicted deer, initiates address the encroaching malaise troubling northern Kalimdor before reporting back to the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade.",h="Curing the Sick is an essential trial for young Alliance druids, tasking them with using a prepared salve to...",sec={{t="A Plague in the Woodlands",b="Across the shadowed forests of Darkshore, from the waters of the Cliffspring River south to the borders of Ashenvale, the local wildlife suffers from a persistent sickness. Sickly deer wander aimlessly through the mist, weakened by unnatural toxins seeped into the soil and streams. Having gathered the necessary reagents, the herbalist Alanndarian Nightsong entrusts an aspiring druid with a freshly brewed curative animal salve to treat the afflicted creatures in the field.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Unveiled in Moonglade",b="Once ten deer have been treated, the initiate is sent to report to Dendrite Starblaze in the sacred haven of Moonglade. While Auberdine breathes a small sigh of relief, Dendrite views the sickly herds as a harbinger of a far more sinister corruption sweeping northern Kalimdor. He warns that while leaders in Darnassus debate and overlook the creeping rot, the Cenarion Circle must remain vigilant against the true scale of the ecological rot taking root across the continent.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore sick?",a="The deer are suffering from a spreading ecological corruption that has begun seeping into the waters and soil of Darkshore, stretching from the Cliffspring River all the way south to Ashenvale. As wild grazers, the deer inadvertently consume the tainted flora and river water, becoming weak and diseased.",al={"why are deer sick","darkshore sickly deer","what poisoned the deer"},it="threat"},{q="Who prepares the curative salve used on the deer?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong, an herbalist stationed in the night elf town of Auberdine, crafts the Curative Animal Salve from rare reagents gathered by the druid initiate. Her batch provides ten doses to immediately treat suffering animals while she attempts to produce more with the townsfolk.",al={"who makes the cure","alanndarian salve","curative animal salve maker"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze care about the deer?",a="Dendrite Starblaze oversees druidic training on behalf of the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade. For him, tending to the wildlife is both a practical test of a druid's duty and a stark confirmation that a wider, dangerous corruption is overtaking Kalimdor's wilderness.",al={"why dendrite moonglade","cenarion circle interest in deer","dendrite starblaze role"},it="purpose"},{q="What political tension does Dendrite Starblaze hint at?",a="Upon completing the task, Dendrite notes that while some night elf authorities in Darnassus acknowledge the growing environmental rot, others stubbornly ignore the warning signs. He urges the initiate never to place blinders over the uncomfortable truths facing the natural world.",al={"darnassus tension","who ignores the corruption","darnassus blinders"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can the sickly deer be found?",a="The sickly deer wander across almost the entirety of Darkshore. They can be found starting south of the Cliffspring River just north of Auberdine and roam throughout the coastal forests southward all the way to the border of Ashenvale.",al={"sickly deer location","where are the deer","darkshore deer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does a druid learn from completing this task?",a="The quest forms the practical culmination of druidic poison-cleansing studies. By witnessing the suffering of forest animals and applying a physical cure, the druid bridges the gap between botanical remedies and spiritual mastery over poison.",al={"what does this teach druids","cure poison training druid","lesson of curing the sick"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Alanndarian Nightsong want the deer cured?",a="Alanndarian sees Darkshore's wildlife suffering under an insidious and spreading affliction. While she remains behind in Auberdine to rally the villagers and brew more medicine, she needs an able druid to act immediately in the field. Tending to the afflicted deer halts their suffering before the sickness wipes out local herds entirely.",al={"alanndarian motive","why cure the deer alanndarian","alanndarian nightsong darkshore deer"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Alanndarian ask you instead of having the Auberdine guards cure the deer?",a="Auberdine's townspeople and Sentinels are tied up defending the settlement and working with Alanndarian to produce more salve. Furthermore, calming wild, feverish animals requires the steady hand and empathy of an initiate of the Cenarion Circle. As a druid in training, you are uniquely suited to minister directly to the beasts of the wild.",al={"why ask me alanndarian","why not auberdine sentinels","why send a druid to cure deer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This rite of passage tests an initiate's commitment to preserving balance, serving as the bridge to earning the innate ability to purge poisons with druidic magic.",["race:NightElf"]="Darkshore represents the ancestral perimeter of modern night elf settlement, making the sudden blight among the deer an ominous omen for the kaldorei."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring river","curative animal salve","curing the sick","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","poison","sickly deer"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:6125","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:5921","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",["end"]="Dendrite Starblaze",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6124,ri={"Sickly Deer"}},src={"Curing the Sick (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6341"] = {t="quest",n="The Bounty of Teldrassil",z="darkshore",s="The Bounty of Teldrassil is an introductory errand given by Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village. Seeking to compare the unusual size and abundance of island fish with those caught along the mainland, she prepares a collection of bones and scales to be shipped across the strait to Darkshore. Delivering this package to the local hippogryph handler marks the first step in crossing the sea to Auberdine.",h="The Bounty of Teldrassil is an introductory errand given by Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village.",sec={{t="A Fisherman's Study",b="Beneath the massive boughs of the World Tree, the sheltered waters surrounding Rut'theran Village teem with remarkably large and plentiful marine life. Nessa Shadowsong, observing the remarkable yields hauled in by local fishermen, seeks to discover whether this vitality extends to the ancient mainland coast or remains unique to the waters nourished by Teldrassil. To test her theory, she prepares a collection of scales and bones to be examined by Laird, a fellow fishmonger based across the water in Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Arranging Passage",b="Transporting cargo and travelers across the open sound between the island bough and mainland Kalimdor requires reliable wings. Rather than sending the parcel by small skiff, Nessa directs travelers directly to Vesprystus, the village hippogryph master. By handing the collection to him, travelers arrange the logistics needed to mount a trained beast and deliver the samples directly to the docks of Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Nessa trying to investigate?",a="Nessa Shadowsong notices that the fish drawn from the waters around Rut'theran Village are extraordinarily large and abundant. She wants to send samples of bones and scales across the water to compare Teldrassil's harvest with the fish found along the mainland coast of Darkshore.",al={"nessa goal","why compare fish","bounty of teldrassil purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is receiving the fish samples in Auberdine?",a="The collection is addressed to Laird, a fish vendor stationed in the coastal village of Auberdine on the mainland shore of Darkshore.",al={"who gets nessa collection","laird darkshore","auberdine fish vendor"},it="target"},{q="Why take the parcel to Vesprystus instead of traveling directly to Auberdine?",a="Vesprystus is the hippogryph master in Rut'theran Village. Handing the collection to him arranges for direct aerial transport, allowing you to secure passage on a hippogryph across the sea to Darkshore.",al={"why vesprystus","who is vesprystus","hippogryph master ruttheran"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Rut'theran Village located in relation to Teldrassil?",a="Rut'theran Village sits at the southern base of Teldrassil at sea level, connected to Darnassus through an emerald portal. It serves as the primary coastal haven and harbor for ships and hippogryphs traveling to and from the great tree.",al={"rut'theran location","where is nessa shadowsong","how to reach ruttheran"},it="place"},{q="What happens after giving the collection to Vesprystus?",a="Vesprystus accepts the collection and offers the follow-up task, Flight to Auberdine, which sends you soaring across the strait on the back of a hippogryph directly to Darkshore.",al={"flight to auberdine next","after bounty of teldrassil","what does vesprystus do"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this part of leaving the starting zone for Night Elves?",a="Yes. This chain introduces young night elf adventurers to flight paths and guides them out of the island canopy down toward mainland Kalimdor to continue their journeys in Darkshore.",al={"leaving teldrassil","level 10 night elf quest","moving to darkshore"},gp=true},{q="Why does Nessa Shadowsong need you to deliver the collection?",a="Nessa Shadowsong is tending to her duties and research among the docks of Rut'theran Village. With travelers regularly departing the island, handing her parcel of specimens to an able adventurer heading toward Darkshore is far simpler than abandoning her work to arrange transport across the sea herself.",al={"why me nessa","why does nessa need help","why send an adventurer to vesprystus"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elf travelers, this journey marks the traditional passage from the safe heights of Teldrassil down to the shadowed mainland shores of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="The route between Rut'theran and Auberdine serves as a crucial transit artery linking the night elf capital with the rest of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","bounty of teldrassil","darkshore","hippogryph","laird","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","vesprystus"},rel={"quest:6344","quest:6342","npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Nessa Shadowsong",["end"]="Vesprystus",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6341},src={"The Bounty of Teldrassil"}}
E["quest:6342"] = {t="quest",n="Flight to Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="This errand introduces adventurers leaving Teldrassil to the night elves' aerial transit network. Tasked by the hippogryph master Vesprystus at Rut'theran Village, travellers take wing across the sea to deliver a bundle of oversized marine specimens to Laird in Auberdine.",h="This errand introduces adventurers leaving Teldrassil to the night elves' aerial transit network.",sec={{t="Taking Wing to Darkshore",b="For many young adventurers departing the boughs of Teldrassil, Rut'theran Village marks the threshold between sanctuary and the wider world. While a mundane ferry plies the strait between the island haven and mainland Kalimdor, the night elves rely equally on their bonded hippogryphs. Entrusted with a parcel of rare fish parts from Nessa Shadowsong, travellers mount one of these winged beasts to establish their very first flight path onto the shores of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Curious Catches",b="The delivery itself is of keen interest to the fishermen of Darkshore. Laird, awaiting Nessa's findings at the docks of Auberdine, inspects the catch to find enormous scales the size of fists and a jawbone nearly twice the size of mainland specimens. The island waters around the base of the World Tree seem to produce altered or abnormally large life, a curiosity that hints at the potent, restless nature of Teldrassil itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this flight?",a="The journey serves as a practical lesson in connecting flight paths between settlements while also delivering research samples of unusual fish caught around Rut'theran Village to Laird in Auberdine.",al={"why do i fly to auberdine","flight to auberdine quest goal","why fly"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the parcel, and what is inside it?",a="The package comes from the fisherwoman Nessa Shadowsong. It contains fish specimens from the waters surrounding Rut'theran Village, including massive scales and an oversized jawbone.",al={"nessa's collection","what is in the package","who sent package"},it="item"},{q="Why are the fish from Teldrassil so large?",a="Laird notes that the jawbone is nearly twice normal size and the scales are as big as a fist. The waters encircling the World Tree of Teldrassil foster strangely magnified wildlife compared to the mainland shores of Darkshore.",al={"why are fish big","rut'theran fish size","huge scales"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Vesprystus?",a="Vesprystus is the hippogryph master stationed at Rut'theran Village. He tends the night elven mounts and coordinates aerial travel across the water to mainland Kalimdor.",al={"vesprystus lore","who is the hippogryph master"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Laird?",a="Laird is a night elf fisherman based in Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore. He studies local aquatic life and compares mainland catches against those caught near Teldrassil.",al={"laird lore","who is laird","laird darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Can you travel between Rut'theran and Auberdine without flying?",a="Yes. A regular ferry boat runs between the docks at Rut'theran Village and the pier at Auberdine, offering an alternative to the hippogryph flight.",al={"boat to auberdine","ferry to darkshore","other way to auberdine"},gp=true},{q="Why does Vesprystus send you to Auberdine?",a="As Rut'theran Village's hippogryph master, Vesprystus oversees vital travel between Teldrassil and the mainland of Kalimdor. While he holds Nessa Shadowsong's parcel of unusual fish specimens intended for Laird in Auberdine, his primary concern is introducing travelers to the night elves' flight network. By sending you across the waters on the back of a hippogryph, he ensures you establish a connection with Auberdine's flight master, opening rapid transit across Darkshore for your future journeys.",al={"why does vesprystus want this done","vesprystus motive","why send parcel auberdine"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Taking flight on a hippogryph to Auberdine marks an iconic rite of passage for young kaldorei stepping forth from Teldrassil onto the ancestral mainland.",["faction:Alliance"]="Hippogryphs serve as the Alliance's primary aerial network throughout northern Kalimdor, linking coastal outposts directly to the capital."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","flight path","flight to auberdine","hippogryph","laird","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6341","quest:6343","quest:940"},m={start="Vesprystus",["end"]="Laird",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6342},src={"Flight to Auberdine"}}
E["quest:6343"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Nessa",z="darkshore",s="This quest sends young travelers from Auberdine back to Rut'theran Village to deliver Laird's findings to Nessa Shadowsong. It concludes an introductory errand teaching adventurers how to navigate transit between the mainland of Kalimdor and Teldrassil.",h="This quest sends young travelers from Auberdine back to Rut'theran Village to deliver Laird's findings to...",sec={{t="A Messenger Across the Sea",b="Having delivered Nessa Shadowsong's initial inquiries to Laird in Auberdine, travelers are charged with carrying his written observations back across the water. Laird notes stark differences in the fish catches between Darkshore and Teldrassil's shores, suspecting that the great World Tree itself alters local marine life. To make the journey back to Rut'theran Village, adventurers can either hire a flight from the hippogryph master Caylais Moonfeather or board the regular ferry running from the Auberdine pier.",sp=0},{t="Curious Bounties",b="Upon receiving Laird's reply at Rut'theran Village, Nessa expresses fascination with the pronounced disparity in marine life. While the massive size of the fish near the World Tree provides an immediate boon to local fishermen, the underlying cause remains an open question among the Kaldorei. Nessa resolves to share the findings with her fellow villagers, content for now to harvest the abundant sea life while keeping a watchful eye on what forces might truly be responsible.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts and completes this quest?",a="The quest is offered by the fisherman Laird in Auberdine on the Darkshore coast. It is turned in to Nessa Shadowsong at Rut'theran Village, at the base of Teldrassil.",al={"quest giver","where to turn in","who gives quest"},gp=true},{q="What is the fastest way back to Rut'theran Village?",a="You can either take a swift hippogryph flight by speaking with Caylais Moonfeather in Auberdine, or walk out onto the long pier to catch the regular passenger ferry back to the docks of Rut'theran Village.",al={"how to get back","travel to ruttheran","ferry or hippogryph"},gp=true},{q="Why is Laird studying the fish?",a="Laird notices that marine catches along Darkshore differ dramatically from those harvested around Teldrassil. He suspects that the burgeoning growth and unique energies of the World Tree are directly altering the surrounding wildlife.",al={"why study fish","fish difference","laird response lore"},it="motive"},{q="Does Nessa find out why the fish are so strange?",a="Not immediately. Nessa notes the remarkable difference and agrees it warrants further investigation, but she is content to share the report with the local villagers and enjoy the bountiful catches in the meantime.",al={"why are fish big","teldrassil fish mystery"},it="next_step"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="This quest directly follows 'Flight to Auberdine,' which sends travelers from Rut'theran Village over to Darkshore with Nessa's original letter to Laird.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","flight to auberdine"},gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest chain?",a="Beyond introducing the mysterious ecological influence of Teldrassil on local wildlife, this delivery chain serves as a rite of passage teaching young night elf adventurers how to commute between their island home and the Kalimdor mainland via ship and flight master.",al={"why do this quest","travel quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Laird want this letter delivered to Nessa?",a="Laird wants Nessa Shadowsong to know right away about the dramatic disparity between the sea life along the Darkshore mainland and the waters of Teldrassil. He suspects that Teldrassil itself is exerting an unusual influence over the surrounding marine wildlife, and sharing his observations helps the villagers understand the strange bounty they are harvesting.",al={"why send response to nessa","laird response purpose","why does laird want this done"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves venturing away from the boughs of Teldrassil for the first time, this exchange marks their first official errand connecting the new island haven to the ancient mainland of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine and Rut'theran Village form the vital maritime gateway linking northern Kalimdor's night elf settlements to broader Alliance interests across Azeroth."},kw={"auberdine","caylais moonfeather","darkshore","laird","nessa shadowsong","return to nessa","rut'theran village","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:6342","npc:laird","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},m={start="Laird",["end"]="Nessa Shadowsong",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6343},src={"Return to Nessa"}}
E["quest:729"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="Archaeologist Hollee has fled to Auberdine after an excavation site in southern Darkshore was overrun by hostile stone golems. Terrified for her senior colleague, she asks travelers to rush south and rescue Prospector Remtravel, an esteemed dwarven scholar who is notoriously blind to mortal danger when engrossed in his research.",h="Archaeologist Hollee has fled to Auberdine after an excavation site in southern Darkshore was overrun by...",sec={{t="A Perilous Dig",b="Dispatched across the sea by the Explorers' League under orders from Master Greywhisker, Archaeologist Hollee was thrilled to apprentice under Prospector Remtravel. Renowned among Ironforge's academic circles for his groundbreaking discoveries, Remtravel was sent to investigate ancient ruins along the untamed coast of Darkshore. However, during an excavation into what appeared to be the remnants of an ancient, great civilization, violent stone golems burst forth from the earth, rapidly overrunning the dig site.",sp=0},{t="Oblivious to Doom",b="While Hollee fled in panic to seek help in the night elven port of Auberdine, Remtravel barely batted an eye. Wholly consumed by the relics he uncovered, the elderly prospector remained knee-deep in rubble, completely unbothered by the lumbering constructs surrounding his camp. Anyone who reaches him south of Auberdine finds him not cowering in fear, but grumbling about missing stone brushes and misplaced fossils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a celebrated dwarven researcher belonging to the Explorers' League of Ironforge. Famous in the dwarven academies for his monumental discoveries, he is equally infamous for an extreme lack of situational awareness whenever valuable relics are nearby.",al={"remtravel","prospector remtravel lore","who is the prospector"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine?",a="Hollee was assigned as an assistant to Remtravel by Master Greywhisker. When dangerous golems emerged from the ground at their dig site, she fled northward to Auberdine seeking reinforcements to mount a rescue.",al={"archaeologist hollee","hollee auberdine","why did hollee run"},it="why_here"},{q="What were the dwarves excavating in Darkshore?",a="The expedition had uncovered evidence of an ancient, advanced society buried beneath Darkshore. Remtravel discovered a mysterious fossil and various stone artifacts before the site was overtaken by subterranean constructs.",al={"what was remtravel digging","darkshore dig site","remtravel fossil"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Prospector Remtravel be found?",a="Remtravel is located in southern Darkshore, perched among ancient ruins south of Auberdine, surrounded by dangerous golems while obsessively looking for his stone brush and fossil.",al={"where is remtravel","remtravel location","find prospector remtravel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sent this expedition to Darkshore?",a="The expedition was organized by the Explorers' League in Ironforge and directly assigned by Master Greywhisker, who tasked Hollee with assisting Remtravel in cataloging the region's ancient wonders.",al={"who sent hollee","master greywhisker","explorers league darkshore"},it="origin"},{q="Is Remtravel in actual danger?",a="Yes. Hostile golems prowl the ruins directly around him. Remtravel is oblivious to the imminent threat, focusing entirely on cataloging his findings and wondering where his tools and assistant have wandered off to.",al={"is remtravel dead","remtravel alive","help remtravel"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Archaeologist Hollee want this done?",a="Hollee was thrilled to study under Prospector Remtravel, a famed researcher from the Ironforge Explorers' League. However, when hostile golems erupted from the dig site, Remtravel's deep distraction left him oblivious to the danger. Hollee fled to Auberdine for reinforcements, terrified that her mentor will be killed if someone does not pull him out of the ruins.",al={"why does hollee need help","hollee motive","why look for remtravel"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Hollee ask you to check on Remtravel instead of going herself?",a="Hollee barely escaped the dig site with her life when the stone golems arose. Terrified and lacking the martial prowess to fight through the hostile constructs alone, she must stay safely in Auberdine and rely on capable, passing adventurers to venture back into the fray and check on her mentor.",al={"why me hollee","why doesnt hollee go back","why doesn't auberdine help"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Remtravel embodies the obsessive curiosity and tunnel vision of the Explorers' League, willing to risk limb and life over an uncatalogued fossil.",["faction:Alliance"]="This mission highlights the cooperative presence of Ironforge researchers attempting to study the unfamiliar, ancient lands of their night elf allies in Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","explorers league","fossil","golems","greywhisker","hollee","remtravel"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:archaeologist-hollee","quest:730","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Archaeologist Hollee",["end"]="Prospector Remtravel",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=729},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector"}}
E["quest:731"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="Deep in the southern ruins of Darkshore, Prospector Remtravel refuses to abandon his dig site without a prize to show the Explorers' League. Despite his severe forgetfulness and an infestation of hostile troggs, he insists on uncovering a mysterious fossil before retreating. Ensuring the dwarven researcher survives his erratic search allows word of his safety to reach his assistant back in Auberdine.",h="Deep in the southern ruins of Darkshore, Prospector Remtravel refuses to abandon his dig site without a prize...",sec={{t="A Perilous Excavation",b="Remtravel's Dig lies far to the south of Darkshore, nestled among ancient ruins that were supposed to hold forgotten secrets. Instead, the dwarven excavators struck into pockets of savage troggs, driving out the workers and leaving the camp under siege. While most would flee for Auberdine immediately, Prospector Remtravel became fixated on salvaging his findings. Refusing to leave empty-handed, he wanders right into the teeth of danger to recover an elusive fossil to justify the expedition's costs to the Explorers' League.",sp=0},{t="Muddled Memories and Trogg Ambushes",b="Protecting Remtravel proves as frustrating as it is dangerous. His scatterbrained nature leads him in circles across the excavation site, mistaking brushes for fossils and blundering past scaffolding and abandoned tents. Each stop draws the attention of aggressive troggs lurking in the shadowed recesses of the quarry. Only by clearing wave after wave of subterranean brutes can an escort coax the scholar into finally locating his prize and securing his passage home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a senior field researcher for the dwarven Explorers' League. Stationed in Darkshore, he was tasked with excavating ancient ruins along the coast, though his extreme absent-mindedness frequently lands him in life-threatening situations.",al={"remtravel","who is the prospector","absent minded prospector guy"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Remtravel still at the dig site?",a="Despite the dig being overrun by troggs, Remtravel refuses to return to Darnassus without tangible proof of his work. He insists on recovering a mysterious fossil to present to the Explorers' League before he will consider abandoning the camp.",al={"why stay at dig","why is remtravel there","why hasn't he fled"},it="why_here"},{q="Where did the troggs come from?",a="Like many dwarven excavations, Remtravel's team dug deep into the earth and unwittingly breached subterranean pockets inhabited by troggs. The primitive creatures surfaced in droves, violently overrunning the machinery, tents, and workers.",al={"why are there troggs in darkshore","darkshore troggs","dig site troggs"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Hollee?",a="Archaeologist Hollee is Remtravel's colleague and assistant, based in the coastal town of Auberdine. Distraught over her mentor's prolonged absence and well aware of his forgetful habits, she recruits travelers to track him down and ensure his safe return.",al={"hollee","archaeologist hollee","remtravel assistant"},it="people"},{q="What happens after finding the fossil?",a="Once Remtravel recovers the fossil and reaches safety, you report back to Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine. She is relieved by the news and prepares for the prospector's eventual trek across the sea to present his findings in Darnassus.",al={"quest continuation","what next","after remtravel escort"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Prospector Remtravel want to find the fossil?",a="Remtravel is under pressure from the Explorers' League chapter in Darnassus to prove he has actually been making progress at the dig site. Despite being terribly confused and absent-minded, he knows he needs to show tangible results—specifically the mysterious fossil and written findings—to justify his expedition and satisfy his superiors.",al={"remtravel motive","why search fossil","why find fossil remtravel"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Remtravel need your help to search the excavation?",a="The excavation site has been overrun by hostile troggs, and Remtravel is a scatterbrained researcher, not a seasoned warrior. He is completely fixated on retrieving his lost artifacts and notes, leaving him entirely vulnerable to ambush as he wanders through the dig site without someone armed watching his back.",al={"why does remtravel need an escort","why remtravel needs protection","why not search alone remtravel"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Remtravel embodies both the relentless passion and perilous stubbornness of the Explorers' League, showing how dedication to ancient titan-lore can blind a scholar to immediate danger.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei generally view dwarven excavations in Darkshore with wariness; Remtravel unearthing a horde of violent troggs confirms their fears about digging too deep into sacred ground.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Remtravel and his findings maintains vital diplomatic and scholarly cooperation between the dwarven Explorers' League and the night elves of Teldrassil."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","escort","excavation","explorers' league","fossil","hollee","remtravel","troggs"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:archaeologist-hollee","quest:729","topic:explorers-league","topic:trogg","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Prospector Remtravel",["end"]="Archaeologist Hollee",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=731},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (2)"}}
E["quest:741"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="This errand delivers a strange petrified specimen recovered from the wild beaches of Darkshore to the Explorers' League outpost in Darnassus. Archaeologist Hollee refuses to abandon her distracted colleague in the field, entrusting the specimen's transport to a passing adventurer instead. The fossil's arrival in the night elven capital immediately captures the keen interest of Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker.",h="This errand delivers a strange petrified specimen recovered from the wild beaches of Darkshore to the...",sec={{t="A Courier to the Capital",b="Prospector Remtravel's excavations along the misty coast of Darkshore have unearthed a curious fossil, but digging deeper matters more to him than protocol. Archaeologist Hollee, unwilling to leave the wandering prospector alone amidst the shore's dangerous beasts and hostile cultists, remains behind to watch over him. In order to get the discovery documented, she requires an Alliance traveler to ferry the specimen up to Darnassus, where the dwarven guild maintains a scholarly delegation.",sp=0},{t="The Dwarven Stake in Kalimdor",b="Dwarves from Ironforge have crossed the Great Sea in force under the banner of the Explorers' League, eager to unearth ancient relics and lost history beneath the soil of Kalimdor. Receiving the artifact in the elven capital, Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker wastes no time in marveling over Remtravel's knack for uncovering ancient treasures. While night elves view their forests as living sanctuaries, the League views the ancient lands as an expansive archaeological dig waiting to be deciphered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the mysterious fossil?",a="It is an unidentified petrified specimen unearthed along the coast of Darkshore by Prospector Remtravel. Its antiquity and strange nature make it a prize finding for the Explorers' League scholars stationed in Darnassus.",al={"mysterious fossil","what fossil is this","remtravel fossil"},it="item"},{q="Why does Hollee stay behind in Darkshore?",a="Archaeologist Hollee feels obligated to watch over Prospector Remtravel. He has a habit of wandering off and ignoring danger while excavating, so she refuses to leave him alone in the wilds while delivering his discoveries to Darnassus.",al={"why doesn't hollee go","hollee staying","why hollee stays"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker?",a="Greywhisker is a senior representative of Ironforge's Explorers' League overseeing archaeological ventures in northern Kalimdor. He operates out of Darnassus, studying relics brought back from the field by dwarven diggers.",al={"greywhisker","who is greywhisker","chief greywhisker"},it="leader"},{q="Why is the Explorers' League operating in Darnassus?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard chartered the Explorers' League to unearth the origins of the dwarven race and ancient history across Azeroth. Having friendly diplomatic ties with the night elves allows dwarven scholars to base expeditions out of Darnassus to study Kalimdor's forgotten lands.",al={"dwarves in darnassus","explorers league darnassus","why are dwarves here"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this fossil end up after Darnassus?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker inspects the find in Darnassus, but discoveries of this scale are meant to be cataloged or routed further into League channels and back toward the great museum in Ironforge.",al={"where does fossil go","fossil next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Where did Remtravel find the specimen?",a="Remtravel uncovered the specimen along the wild coast of Darkshore, an area laden with shipwrecks, ancient ruins, and fossilized sea life dating back before the Great Sundering.",al={"where was fossil found","remtravel dig site"},it="place"},{q="Why does Archaeologist Hollee want the fossil delivered to Darnassus?",a="Prospector Remtravel wants his discovery examined right away, but someone needs to bring it to their superiors. Hollee is determined not to abandon Darkshore while Remtravel remains behind in the wilderness, so she relies on you to ferry the priceless find directly to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus on their behalf.",al={"why send fossil to darnassus","hollee motive","why deliver fossil"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Carrying Remtravel's fossil fulfills the primary mission of the Explorers' League: unearthing the world's deepest past and proving the boundless value of dwarven perseverance.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching dwarven excavators bring ancient remnants out of Darkshore's sacred soil can be jarring, but cooperating with the League preserves Alliance bonds.",["faction:Alliance"]="This task demonstrates the logistical reliance Alliance members have on each other, as dwarven researchers rely on traveling adventurers to safely bridge the remote shores of Darkshore and the heights of Darnassus."},kw={"archaeologist","darkshore","darnassus","explorers league","fossil","greywhisker","hollee","remtravel"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-hollee","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","npc:prospector-remtravel","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Archaeologist Hollee",["end"]="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=741},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (3)"}}
E["quest:8721"] = {t="quest",n="Starweave the Elder",z="darkshore",s="Starweave the Elder is a Lunar Festival quest encountered in Darkshore. Adventurers seek out Elder Starweave in the settlement of Auberdine to pay their respects to the ancestral spirits of Kalimdor. In exchange for honoring ancient traditions, she offers celestial wisdom and her blessing.",h="Starweave the Elder is a Lunar Festival quest encountered in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Auberdine",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits of venerated ancestors manifest across the continents of Azeroth, battened in pillars of radiant celestial radiance. Elder Starweave takes her place among the night elves of Auberdine, a critical harbor town situated along the mist-shrouded coast of Darkshore. Travelers honoring the festival make pilgrimage to her side, seeking the timeless guidance of ages past.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the Heavens",b="Elder Starweave contemplates the cosmic tapestry above Kalimdor, reminding all who approach that the stars carry answers to mortal doubts and worldly riddles. Those who take the time to seek her council are urged to look skyward for truth and receive ancestral favor alongside tidings of other wandering spirits across the wild frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Starweave?",a="Elder Starweave is located in the coastal night elf town of Auberdine in Darkshore. She stands illuminated by a brilliant beam of moonlight descending directly from the heavens.",al={"starweave location","where is elder starweave","elder starweave darkshore"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The quest is part of the yearly Lunar Festival celebration. Visiting and honoring the ancestral elders scattered across Azeroth awards recognition, festive currency, and ancestral goodwill.",al={"why do elder starweave","starweave the elder purpose","what does starweave do"}},{q="Who is Elder Starweave?",a="She is an ancient night elven spirit honoring the Lunar Festival. Bathed in starlight, she offers philosophical wisdom regarding the constellations and points pilgrims toward other revered elders, such as Elder Bladeswift.",al={"who is starweave","starweave lore","elder starweave backstory"}},{q="Can Horde players visit Elder Starweave?",a="Yes. Festival elders remain neutral and welcome respectful travelers of both factions. However, because Elder Starweave resides within the Alliance harbor of Auberdine, Horde adventurers must be cautious around the town's local night elven guards.",al={"can horde talk to starweave","horde elder starweave","starweave hostile horde"}},{q="What does Elder Starweave tell travelers?",a="Upon greeting visitors, she reminds them that the infinite stars above hold answers to mortal riddles, asking if the wise and fortunate might gaze upward to unveil truth.",al={"starweave dialogue","what does elder starweave say"}},{q="Which elder does Starweave point to?",a="Elder Starweave shares the location and tidings of Elder Bladeswift, guiding travelers onward across their festive journey through northern Kalimdor.",al={"who does starweave mention","elder after starweave","next elder darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Honoring Elder Starweave in Auberdine connects night elves directly to the ancient spirits of their forebears and the revered mysteries of Elune and the stars.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold ancestral spirits and the celestial balance in deep reverence, making communion with Elder Starweave a natural reflection of their beliefs.",["faction:Horde"]="Reaching Elder Starweave requires Horde wanderers to carefully infiltrate the Alliance-held docks of Auberdine to pay their respects without provoking the local sentinels."},kw={"ancestor","auberdine","darkshore","elder bladeswift","elder starweave","lunar festival","starweave"},rel={"npc:elder-starweave","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Starweave",id=8721},src={"Starweave the Elder"}}
E["quest:942"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="This quest bridges an excavation mystery from Darkshore across the Great Sea to the Wetlands. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker entrusts you with a strange Kalimdor fossil, directing you to Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor to unlock its secrets.",h="This quest bridges an excavation mystery from Darkshore across the Great Sea to the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Curious Discovery",b="While examining the strange fossil uncovered in Darkshore, Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker notices a striking resemblance to a relic shown at an Explorers' League conference back in Ironforge. That earlier piece was presented by Archaeologist Flagongut, who was convinced that such fossils held latent powers waiting to be unlocked. Greywhisker believes Flagongut is the only dwarf capable of discerning what makes this Kalimdor find so extraordinary.",sp=0},{t="A Voyage Across the Sea",b="Carrying the mysterious relic means undertaking a long journey out of Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms. Flagongut was last seen waiting for an armed escort to the Whelgar Excavation Site while lodging at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Delivering the fossil into his hands marks the turning point where a local Darkshore survey ties into a continent-spanning archaeological inquiry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Greywhisker send me all the way to Menethil Harbor?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker recalls that Archaeologist Flagongut displayed an identical relic at an annual Explorers' League conference in Ironforge. Believing Flagongut holds the expertise to unlock its hidden power, Greywhisker dispatches you to find him at his last known location in Menethil Harbor.",al={"why go to menethil","greywhisker fossil errand","why wetlands"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is an Explorers' League researcher stationed in the Wetlands. Waiting out delays at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, he is preparing for an expedition to the perilous Whelgar Excavation Site.",al={"who is flagongut","archaeologist flagongut lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is the mysterious fossil?",a="It is an ancient, curious specimen retrieved from Darkshore. Flagongut previously claimed that a twin specimen he studied possessed latent magical or historical power waiting to be unlocked.",al={"what is the fossil","mysterious fossil origin","remtravel fossil"},it="item"},{q="What does Flagongut say when you deliver the fossil?",a="Flagongut is astonished to discover that a relic identical to his own research sample originated from the distant continent of Kalimdor, verifying that ancient history links the two landmasses together.",al={"flagongut reaction","handing in the fossil"}},{q="Where does Flagongut want to go next?",a="Flagongut has been waiting in Menethil Harbor for an escort to travel inland toward the Whelgar Excavation Site, a major dig location situated in the Wetlands.",al={"where is flagongut going","flagongut excavation"},it="next_step"},{q="How does this quest fit into the Absent Minded Prospector storyline?",a="It serves as the transit leg of the questline. After escorting and rescuing Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore and analyzing his excavated relic with Greywhisker, the inquiry shifts from northern Kalimdor directly to League experts in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"absent minded prospector part 4","quest chain context"},it="history"},{q="Why does Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker want this done?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker recognizes that the mysterious fossil Remtravel uncovered bears a striking resemblance to a peculiar relic presented at an Explorers' League conference in Ironforge. Its discoverer, Archaeologist Flagongut, believed the relic possessed a latent power waiting to be unlocked. Greywhisker hopes Flagongut can study this new specimen and unlock ancient secrets of the past.",al={"why send fossil","greywhisker motive","why does greywhisker want the fossil examined"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers, this errand demonstrates the reach of the Explorers' League, connecting fieldwork in remote Kalimdor back to fellow scholars based in Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="This task requires utilizing Alliance shipping routes, taking sea voyages from Kalimdor over to Menethil Harbor to keep League branches connected."},kw={"absent minded prospector","archaeologist flagongut","chief archaeologist greywhisker","darkshore","deepwater tavern","explorers' league","menethil harbor","mysterious fossil"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker",["end"]="Archaeologist Flagongut",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=942},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (4)"}}
E["quest:943"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks the final chapter in the search sparked by Prospector Remtravel's excavations in Darkshore. Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor seeks to combine Remtravel's finds with his own fossil and the lost Stone of Relu to unlock the ancient titan relics' hidden powers.",h="This quest marks the final chapter in the search sparked by Prospector Remtravel's excavations in Darkshore.",sec={{t="Cross-Continental Archaeology",b="What began as an escort mission aiding the distracted Prospector Remtravel in the northern reaches of Darkshore leads across the Great Sea to the marshlands of the Wetlands. Flagongut's own original fossil is held by Prospector Whelgar at his excavation site in the Wetlands. Archaeologist Flagongut, reviewing the collected finds, realizes that unlocking the mysterious powers within the fossils requires a key artifact: the Stone of Relu.",sp=0},{t="Lost to the Marshes",b="Before Flagongut could rendezvous with Whelgar, a pack of mottled raptors ambushed his caravan along the road, devouring the Stone of Relu. To piece the mystery together, Flagongut requires an adventurer to hunt down the predatory beasts, recover the ingested stone, and retrieve the original fossil from Whelgar's camp. With both fossils and the key assembled, the dwarven researchers hope to uncover the relics' true origin and power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a Darkshore quest ending in the Wetlands?",a="The Explorers' League maintains active operations across both Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker sent Remtravel's fossil from Darkshore across the sea to Archaeologist Flagongut in the Wetlands, connecting the two dig sites through shared research.",al={"why wetlands darkshore quest","menethil harbor connection","why send to wetlands"},it="place"},{q="What is the Stone of Relu?",a="The Stone of Relu is an ancient relic recovered by Archaeologist Flagongut. He believes it acts as a cipher or catalyst capable of unlocking the dormant magical secrets preserved inside the fossils excavated in Darkshore and the Wetlands.",al={"stone of relu","what is relu stone","relu artifact"},it="item"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League based in Menethil Harbor. He studies ancient relics recovered from surrounding excavations and works closely with Prospectors Remtravel and Whelgar to decipher titan remnants.",al={"flagongut","who is flagongut"},it="identity"},{q="Who has the original fossil?",a="Prospector Whelgar holds Flagongut's original fossil at his excavation site in the Wetlands. Remtravel's fossil from Darkshore is the one you already delivered to Flagongut.",al={"where is the fossil","who has remtravel fossil","whelgar fossil"}},{q="Why do raptors have the Stone of Relu?",a="While traveling the Wetlands road to consult with Prospector Whelgar, Flagongut was ambushed by mottled raptors. In the chaos of the attack, one of the predatory beasts swallowed the stone whole.",al={"raptor swallowed relic","why raptors have stone"},it="target"},{q="What do the dwarves expect the fossils to do?",a="The Explorers' League believes ancient fossils from the dawn of Azeroth hold latent titan energies and forgotten history, which can be awakened and translated using specialized relic stones like the Stone of Relu.",al={"fossil power","what does the fossil do"},it="motive"},{q="What is Flagongut's Fossil for?",a="Flagongut's Fossil is one of the ancient specimens recovered by the dwarven excavators, alongside the piece uncovered by Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore. Archaeologist Flagongut believes these ancient relics hold dormant magical power and forgotten secrets, which he hopes to finally unlock and decipher using the resonant power of the Stone of Relu.",al={"flagonguts fossil","flagongut fossil use","what is flagonguts fossil"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The quest chain exemplifies the core mission of the Explorers' League, linking remote dig sites across continents to piece together dwarven heritage and the mysteries of the Titans.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance couriers and adventurers frequently bridge the maritime divide between the night elven lands of Darkshore and the dwarven settlements around Menethil Harbor."},kw={"darkshore","explorers league","flagongut","fossil","menethil","remtravel","stone of relu","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Archaeologist Flagongut",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=943,ri={"Flagongut's Fossil","Stone of Relu"}},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (5)"}}
E["quest:944"] = {t="quest",n="The Master's Glaive",z="darkshore",s="This quest sends Alliance adventurers south across Darkshore to scout the eerie Master's Glaive on behalf of the ancient of lore, Onu. The goal is to investigate whether the sinister Twilight's Hammer cult has infiltrated the remains of the fallen ancient horror.",h="This quest sends Alliance adventurers south across Darkshore to scout the eerie Master's Glaive on behalf of...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Presence",b="While investigating the lingering corruption and displaced wildlife along Darkshore, the ancient of lore Onu notices alarming clues. The naga along the coast are troubled enough, but the presence of the Twilight's Hammer cult is far more ominous. This fanatic sect does not worship ordinary dark powers; they venerate the ancient, primal lords of the world who were overthrown in ages past.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Lord",b="Southward lies the Master's Glaive, a grim excavation centered around a colossal creature impaled by an immense stone weapon. Onu provides a Phial of Scrying and tasks scouts with entering the pit to confirm if the cultists have gathered there. As Onu warns, even though the impaled behemoth has been dead for eons, slivers of its ancient, corruptive power still linger within its bones—a prize the Twilight's Hammer cannot resist.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="The quest is given by Onu, a venerable ancient of lore stationed along the road in southern Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"quest giver","who gives the masters glaive quest","start npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="The Master's Glaive is an ancient site in southern Darkshore where a monstrous ancient lord fell eons ago, impaled through its skull by a titanic stone glaive. Its massive petrified skeleton remains embedded in the earth.",al={"what is masters glaive","lore of masters glaive","giant skull in darkshore"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult interested in the site?",a="The Twilight's Hammer worships the old, dark powers of ancient Azeroth. Even though the titanic creature impaled at the glaive is long dead, dormant traces and slivers of its primeval power remain within its remains, which the cultists desperately seek to harness.",al={"twilight cult darkshore","why are twilight cultists here","twilights hammer masters glaive"},it="why_here"},{q="How do I report back to Onu?",a="You do not need to walk all the way back to Onu's physical location. Once you explore the excavation pit of the Master's Glaive, use the Phial of Scrying in your bags to conjure a Scrying Bowl on the ground, allowing you to speak directly with Onu via magic.",al={"where to turn in quest","how to use scrying phial","scrying bowl"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What follows this scout mission?",a="After you use the Scrying Bowl to confirm the cultists' presence, Onu immediately directs you toward their encampment in the quest 'The Twilight Camp' to uncover further details about their activities.",al={"next quest","followup to masters glaive"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Onu send you to investigate the Master's Glaive?",a="Onu is deeply unsettled by the presence of the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore. As an ancient ancient of lore watching over the woodlands, he knows this nihilistic cult venerates the defeated Old Gods of the earth. The Master's Glaive marks the ancient resting place of one such fallen monstrosity, and Onu fears that even in death, remnants of the entity's lingering dark power could be unearthed and wielded by the cultists.",al={"why does onu want this","onu motive masters glaive","why scout masters glaive"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent to investigate at the Master's Glaive?",a="You are sent to reconnoiter the Twilight's Hammer cultists lurking around the massive monument. These zealots revere primordial, ancient powers that once ruled Azeroth. They have gathered in the cavernous pit of the Master's Glaive to tap into whatever eldritch essence or remnant strength still radiates from the petrified skull of the ancient being slain there.",al={"masters glaive target","who am i looking for at masters glaive","who is at masters glaive"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Onu need you to scout the Master's Glaive instead of going himself?",a="Onu is a massive, rooted ancient of lore who cannot easily slip unnoticed into the deep ravine of the Master's Glaive. Furthermore, Darkshore's night elf forces are stretched thin dealing with the encroaching naga along the coast and corruption across the wild. A nimble, capable traveler armed with a Phial of Scrying can quietly scout the cultists' encampment and magically report back without drawing unwanted attention.",al={"why me onu","why send me masters glaive","why doesnt onu scout masters glaive"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the Master's Glaive is a stark reminder of primeval terrors that predated their civilization, and seeing mad cultists trespass upon Darkshore's sacred soil is an intolerable defilement.",["class:Druid"]="Druids answer Onu's call to understand how the ancient, dormant taint buried deep within the earth is disturbing the surrounding land and its wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance forces in Darkshore must keep the Twilight's Hammer from awakening ancient horrors that could overrun the struggling settlements of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","old lord","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:948","quest:949","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore","topic:naga"},m={start="Onu",["end"]="Scrying Bowl",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=944},src={"The Master's Glaive (quest)"}}
E["quest:947"] = {t="quest",n="Cave Mushrooms",z="darkshore",s="Cave Mushrooms is an Alliance assignment offered by the night elf Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine. While formulating a specialized potion, Barithras tasks an adventurer with venturing into a hidden cavern behind Cliffspring Falls to harvest rare fungi and verify disturbing premonitions felt by the Grove of the Ancients.",h="Cave Mushrooms is an Alliance assignment offered by the night elf Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Recipe Behind the Falls",b="Barithras Moonshade requires specific ingredients for a potent mixture: scaber stalks and an elusive death cap. These particular fungi thrive in the damp, shadowy cavern concealed directly behind Cliffspring Falls in northeastern Darkshore. While the alchemy itself is delicate, gathering these specimens is far more hazardous than harvesting typical woodland herbs.",sp=0},{t="The Ancients' Warning",b="Barithras did not avoid the cavern out of mere idleness. The venerable tree guardians at the Grove of the Ancients issued stern warnings, sensing that a foul presence had begun nesting inside the mountain caves. By sending a hardy explorer rather than investigating himself, Moonshade seeks to confirm whether the elders' dire intuitions about a creeping evil in northern Darkshore are indeed well founded.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this task begin?",a="You receive this assignment from Barithras Moonshade, who resides in the night elf coastal settlement of Auberdine in central Darkshore.",al={"where to pick up cave mushrooms","barithras moonshade location","cave mushrooms quest start"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where are the mushrooms located?",a="They grow inside a cavern hidden behind Cliffspring Falls, situated along the mountain face to the northeast of Auberdine.",al={"where are scaber stalks","death cap location","cave behind waterfall darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why won't Barithras Moonshade retrieve the mushrooms himself?",a="Barithras was specifically advised by the Grove of the Ancients to stay clear of the falls. The great ancients sensed that an unnatural, rising evil has taken refuge inside that cave.",al={"why barithras won't go","why barithras stays in auberdine"},it="why_me"},{q="What specific mushrooms are needed?",a="Moonshade needs five scaber stalks along with a single, highly dangerous death cap mushroom to complete his potion.",al={"required mushrooms","which fungi for moonshade"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What does this errand lead to next?",a="Once the presence in the cave is verified and the fungi delivered, the journey turns south toward the ancient protector Onu at the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"next quest after cave mushrooms","onu follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Are the Ancients' fears proven correct?",a="Yes. Upon returning the specimens, the adventurer confirms the dark foreboding of the elders, proving that a sinister force has indeed claimed the mountain cavern.",al={"is the cave actually evil","what is in cliffspring falls cave"},sp=1},{q="Why does Barithras Moonshade want this done?",a="Barithras Moonshade is an herbalist concocting a potent new potion that demands rare fungi found only in the cavern behind Cliffspring Falls. Beyond his alchemical work, however, he carries a deeper concern: the Grove of the Ancients warned him that a rising evil lurks within that very cave. By sending you to harvest the ingredients, he also hopes to learn whether the Ancients' grim omens are true.",al={"why does barithras want cave mushrooms","barithras moonshade motive","why collect mushrooms for barithras"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Death Cap for?",a="The Death Cap is an exceptionally rare and potent toxic fungus native to the cavern behind Cliffspring Falls. Barithras Moonshade requires a pristine specimen as a key reagent in a specialized potion he is crafting in Auberdine.",al={"what is death cap used for","death cap mushroom purpose","why does barithras need death cap"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Scaber Stalk for?",a="Scaber Stalks are rare mushrooms that flourish in the damp, shadowy cave behind Cliffspring Falls. Barithras Moonshade needs five of them to blend into his ongoing alchemical concoctions alongside the potent Death Cap.",al={"what are scaber stalks for","scaber stalk mushroom purpose","why does barithras need scaber stalks"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Foragers and herbalists will appreciate the hunt for the death cap and scaber stalks, though these specific specimens dwell in darkened caverns rather than lush woodland soil.",["race:NightElf"]="The Grove of the Ancients remains deeply attuned to the natural balance of Darkshore, making any disturbance they detect beneath the falls a matter of urgent concern to the Kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary bastion on the Kalimdor coast, and creeping evils in the eastern mountains directly endanger the stability of the entire shore."},kw={"auberdine","barithras moonshade","cave mushrooms","cliffspring falls","darkshore","death cap","grove of the ancients","onu","scaber stalks"},rel={"npc:barithras-moonshade","subzone:cliffspring-falls","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:952"},m={start="Barithras Moonshade",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=947,ri={"Death Cap","Scaber Stalk"}},src={"Cave Mushrooms"}}
E["quest:948"] = {t="quest",n="Onu",z="darkshore",s="This errand directs travelers from Auberdine south toward the Grove of the Ancients to consult with Onu. Having investigated the strange fungal growth deep within Cliffspring Falls, your findings have drawn the urgent attention of one of Darkshore's oldest guardians.",h="This errand directs travelers from Auberdine south toward the Grove of the Ancients to consult with Onu.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Ancients",b="After returning to Auberdine with fungal samples from the depths of Cliffspring Falls, Barithras Moonshade realizes that the implications stretch far beyond mere botanical curiosity. Word of the tainted caverns travels quickly to Onu, an Ancient of Lore rooted in the tranquil sanctuary of the Grove of the Ancients south of town. Patient and ponderous though the ancient treants are by nature, Onu's immediate desire for counsel signals that the corruption running through Darkshore's waterways may touch upon ancient, unsettling powers.",sp=0},{t="Journey to the Grove",b="Following the southern road out of Auberdine leads away from the coastal ruins and inland toward the mountain slopes. The Grove of the Ancients serves as an ancestral redoubt of nature, largely sheltered from the creeping decay that plagues the shoreline. Here, Onu waits among towering stone barrows and kindred spirits, preparing to direct allies toward deeper, more terrifying blights stirring at the edge of the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is an Ancient of Lore, a colossal, sapient tree-guardian dedicated to gathering and preserving knowledge. He presides over the Grove of the Ancients nestled in southern Darkshore, offering wisdom and guidance to defenders of the land.",al={"who is onu","onu identity","what is onu"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Onu want to speak with me?",a="You recently ventured into the caverns beneath Cliffspring Falls to gather fungal samples for Barithras Moonshade. The peculiar nature of what was uncovered there alarmed the naturalists, prompting Onu to request an audience to address the growing corruption.",al={"why onu summons","reason for talk","why go to onu"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The Grove of the Ancients lies south of Auberdine, nestled along the foothills of the eastern mountain range. Follow the main road south through Darkshore and head east toward the mountain slopes to find Onu.",al={"onu location","where is grove of the ancients","how to find onu"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of creature is an Ancient of Lore?",a="Ancients of Lore are ancient treant beings allied with the night elves and the Cenarion Circle. Revered for their deep wisdom and memory, they serve as living repositories of nature magic and historical secrets.",al={"ancient of lore","what creature is onu","treant vs ancient"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Onu's summons considered urgent?",a="Ancients are known for their deliberate, unhurried demeanor, rarely acting in haste. As Barithras Moonshade notes, if a being as patient and methodical as Onu actively calls for your counsel, the threat to Darkshore must be severe.",al={"why urgent","is onu worried","barithras warning"},it="danger"},{q="What comes after meeting with Onu?",a="Upon greeting you at the Grove of the Ancients, Onu enlists your aid in investigating a far darker threat situated further south along the coast: the ominous excavation taking place around the Master's Glaive.",al={"next quest after onu","what happens next","where does onu send you"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Barithras Moonshade send me to Onu?",a="Barithras knows that the Ancients of Lore possess deep wisdom regarding the land's corruption, and Onu has taken direct notice of what you found within the cave at Cliffspring Falls. Because an Ancient rarely reaches out unless Darkshore faces a profound and urgent threat, Barithras urges you to heed the summons immediately.",al={"barithras motive","why send to onu","why does barithras want this done"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Ancients of Lore are sacred partners to the Kaldorei, having guided your people since before the Sundering. Answering Onu's call is a solemn duty to preserve the sanctity of Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the Ancients in deep reverence as manifestations of nature's wisdom. Investigating strange cavern growths at Onu's behest aligns directly with the duties of the Cenarion Circle.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers helping secure Darkshore, gaining the trust and insight of the regional ancients is crucial to navigating Kalimdor's mysterious northern wilderness."},kw={"ancient of lore","auberdine","barithras moonshade","cliffwater falls","darkshore","grove of the ancients","onu"},rel={"npc:barithras-moonshade","quest:947","zone:darkshore","quest:952"},m={start="Barithras Moonshade",["end"]="Onu",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=948},src={"Onu (quest)"}}
E["quest:949"] = {t="quest",n="The Twilight Camp",z="darkshore",s="The Twilight Camp is an Alliance reconnaissance mission directed at the secretive cultists encamped around the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore. Having caught a glimpse of their ritual site through a scrying bowl, investigators must infiltrate the excavation to uncover what the Twilight's Hammer seeks to unearth.",h="The Twilight Camp is an Alliance reconnaissance mission directed at the secretive cultists encamped around...",sec={{t="Probing the Dig",b="The Master's Glaive has long stood as an ominous, petrified mystery along the craggy hills of southern Darkshore, but the sudden arrival of the Twilight's Hammer cult transformed an ancient curiosity into an active threat. After using a scrying bowl to peer into their fortifications, scouts are sent into the thick of their camp to determine their true designs before defensive measures can be enacted.",sp=0},{t="The Illustrated Tome",b="Scouring the encampment reveals that the cultists are not mere scavengers or bandits; their operation is guided by deep, occult study. Deep within their northern camp rests an ancient, meticulously hand-printed tome illustrated with masterful yet unsettling artwork. This text serves as proof that the Twilight's Hammer is deliberately investigating the colossal entity buried beneath the earth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of The Twilight Camp quest?",a="You must infiltrate the Twilight's Hammer encampment near the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore and recover a clue detailing their motives—specifically a hand-printed ritual book resting within their camp.",al={"twilight camp quest objective","what do i do twilight camp"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends you to investigate the camp?",a="The quest is received directly from the Scrying Bowl at the overlook above the Master's Glaive, continuing the investigation initiated on behalf of the ancient protector Onu.",al={"who gives twilight camp","twilight camp quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the clue found in the camp?",a="The valid clue is the Twilight Tome situated in the northern part of the encampment. Other tomes in the camp can be dangerous decoys that unleash warding magic against intruders.",al={"where is the book","twilight tome location","find clue twilight camp"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer at the Master's Glaive?",a="The cultists are obsessed with ancient, dark powers of the Old Gods and their servants. They are excavating the massive petrified carcass pinned by the giant stone blade to study or awaken whatever ancient evil remains there.",al={"why are cultists at masters glaive","twilights hammer darkshore purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after finding the tome?",a="Recovering the tome leads to the quest Return to Onu, instructing you to carry the discovered writings north to the ancient treant in the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"next quest after twilight camp","where to go after twilight tome"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Scrying Bowl direct you to investigate the camp?",a="The ancient scrying bowl, used by the night elves and ancients of Darkshore to monitor corruption, reveals that the sinister Twilight's Hammer cultists have established a presence around the Master's Glaive. Their exact purpose remains unknown, but any activity by nihilistic cultists around the petrified remains of an Old God's servant forebodes disaster. Before Onu and the defenders of the grove can take action or formulate a defense, they need hard intelligence on what rituals or abominations the cult is plotting.",al={"why investigate the twilight camp","scrying bowl purpose","why search twilight camp"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Twilight's Hammer defiles sacred Kalimdor lands with dark sorceries right beneath the boughs of Darkshore's ancient groves.",["class:Druid"]="Uncovering the cult's research is critical for Cenarion wardens seeking to keep corrupting ancient entities safely buried.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stopping the cult's strange excavations prevents a gathering threat from destabilizing northern Kalimdor."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","onu","scrying bowl","twilight camp","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","subzone:master-s-glaive","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Scrying Bowl",["end"]="Twilight Tome",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=949},src={"The Twilight Camp"}}
E["quest:950"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Onu",z="darkshore",s="Return to Onu is an Alliance quest concluding an initial investigation into the cultists encamped along the coast of Darkshore. After raiding the cultists' encampment and attempting to read the Twilight Tome, an adventurer recovers a single page of maddening scribbles to deliver to the ancient treant Onu in the Grove of the Ancients.",h="Return to Onu is an Alliance quest concluding an initial investigation into the cultists encamped along the...",sec={{t="A Glimpse into Madness",b="Upon discovering the Twilight Tome within the Twilight's Hammer encampment, anyone peering into its leaves suffers an immediate assault on the senses. The written text swims and dances across the parchment, and once-ornate scrollwork morphs into grotesque figures. The mental strain is so overwhelming that ripping free a single page of scribbled notes is all a mortal mind can endure before succumbing to vertigo.",sp=0},{t="Ancient Suspicions",b="When delivered to Onu, the towering treant recognizes the unnatural aura suffusing the scrap. The parchment radiates a chaotic, primal magic that Onu attributes directly to the work of the ancient, shadowy forces buried beneath the earth. While the scribblings are difficult to decipher, they confirm that the presence of the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore is not mere banditry, but part of a deeper, blasphemous design.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the page taken from the Twilight Tome?",a="The page, known simply as Insane Scribbles, is a torn leaf from the cult's sacred book. Looking upon it causes severe mental distress, as the script twists into grotesque, shifting patterns tied to primeval void magic.",al={"insane scribbles","what are the scribbles","twilight tome page"},it="item"},{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is an Ancient of Lore rooted in the Grove of the Ancients in southern Darkshore. He acts as an elder guardian and scholar, guiding night elves and Alliance allies against emerging corruptions in the forest.",al={"who is onu","onu darkshore","treant onu"},it="identity"},{q="What does Onu learn from the scribbles?",a="Onu senses chaotic, primal energies emanating from the page, identifying the influence of ancient, malevolent entities. The writings suggest the Twilight's Hammer cultists are actively pursuing relic sites and buried powers across Darkshore.",al={"what did onu find","meaning of scribbles"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore?",a="The cult is drawn to Darkshore to excavate ruined elven sites and uncover vestiges of ancient power linked to primeval darkness and the Old Gods, using the chaos of the land to mask their rites.",al={"cultists in darkshore","why twilight hammer here"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Following the discovery of the cult's presence, Onu turns attention toward the ancient elven ruins of Mathystra to the north, directing adventurers to secure ancient relics before the cultists can seize them.",al={"what quest is next","next after return to onu"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does reading the tome cause dizziness?",a="The Twilight Tome is inscribed with dark, maddening magic of void and chaos. The glyphs actively bewilder mortal minds, causing hallucinations and swoons to prevent outsiders from unraveling their secrets.",al={"why dizziness tome","twilight tome effects"},it="power"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Darkshore's shores by dark cultists threatens the balance guarded by the Ancients of Lore, making Onu's warnings deeply personal for the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="The chaotic, unnatural resonance of the scribbles represents an affront to the natural order that druids serve to preserve alongside treants like Onu.",["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating cult activity along Darkshore's coastline ensures that night elf settlements like Auberdine remain secure against hidden threats."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","insane scribbles","old ones","onu","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:949","quest:948","quest:951","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Twilight Tome",["end"]="Onu",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=950},src={"Return to Onu"}}
E["quest:951"] = {t="quest",n="Mathystra Relics",z="darkshore",s="This quest sends Alliance adventurers north along the coast of Darkshore to sift through the overgrown Ruins of Mathystra. Onu, an Ancient of Lore rooted in the Grove of the Ancients, seeks these ancient kaldorei artifacts to understand how the Twilight's Hammer cult is manipulating night elven sorcery for their sinister rites.",h="This quest sends Alliance adventurers north along the coast of Darkshore to sift through the overgrown Ruins...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Discovery",b="After adventurers recovered a tainted parchment from the cultists lurking around the colossal monument known as the Master's Glaive, Onu deciphered a disturbing revelation. The text was not native cult scripture, but a cursed fragment of ancient night elven writing. Tainted by the Twilight's Hammer, the parchment revealed that these apocalyptic zealots are harnessing forgotten elven magic to awaken or summon their ancient masters back into the mortal world.",sp=1},{t="The Fallen Bastion",b="To counteract this dark endeavor, Onu directs heroes to the Ruins of Mathystra, located along the northeastern shores of Darkshore. Long ago, Mathystra was a shining bastion of highborne civilization before it shattered during the Sundering. Though the city has collapsed into rubble, weeds, and naga infestation, powerful remnants of its original arcane and spiritual enchantments linger in shattered urns and ancient relics scattered across the stone foundations.",sp=0},{t="Divining Dark Designs",b="By collecting surviving artifacts from the ruin's grassy debris, defenders of Darkshore hope to unravel the specific techniques the cultists intend to exploit. Onu studies the residual magic imbued within the relics, racing against time to decipher the cult's plans before the Twilight's Hammer can fully bend ancient kaldorei sorcery toward freeing their subterranean masters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Mathystra Relics?",a="They are fragments of enchanted pottery, urns, and artifacts left behind in the Ruins of Mathystra. Created during the height of ancient night elven civilization prior to the Great Sundering, they still hum with lingering magical energy.",al={"what are the relics","mathystra relic lore","elven relics mathystra"},it="item"},{q="Why does Onu want these relics?",a="Onu discovered that the Twilight's Hammer cult is using ancient elven magic to try and bring their dark masters back into the world. By studying intact relics from Mathystra, Onu hopes to understand how the cult intends to manipulate that ancient power.",al={"why does onu want relics","purpose of mathystra relics"},it="motive"},{q="Where were the Ruins of Mathystra located?",a="The ruins sit along the northeastern coastline of Darkshore, north of the Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran ruins, just past the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"where is mathystra","mathystra location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is the Twilight's Hammer trying to bring back?",a="The cult is dedicated to ancient, malevolent masters; Onu warns they are using ancient elven magic to bring those old masters back to Azeroth.",al={"who are twilight hammer masters","cult masters darkshore"},it="threat"},{q="What was Mathystra before it became a ruin?",a="Mathystra was once a great bastion and city of the night elves thousands of years ago. It fell into ruin during the Great Sundering and has since been overrun by wilderness, ghosts, and vile beach-dwelling creatures like the naga.",al={"history of mathystra","what was mathystra"},it="history"},{q="Who gives the quest 'Mathystra Relics'?",a="The quest is provided by Onu, an ancient treant rooted at the Grove of the Ancients in south-central Darkshore, following the investigation of the Master's Glaive.",al={"who starts mathystra relics","quest giver mathystra relics"},gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, seeing relics of their pre-Sundering glory dug out of the dirt is a somber reminder of their civilization's fall—and an alarming warning that their ancestors' potent arts are being exploited by apocalyptic madmen.",["class:Druid"]="Aiding Onu allows druids to serve one of nature's greatest elder sentinels, safeguarding the ancient history of Darkshore from being twisted by dark cultists.",["faction:Alliance"]="Preventing the Twilight's Hammer from weaponizing ancient magic is essential to securing northern Kalimdor against dark, subterranean forces."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","mathystra","onu","relics","ruins of mathystra","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","quest:948","quest:952","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:944","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:950","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Onu",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=951,ri={"Mathystra Relic"}},src={"Mathystra Relics"}}
E["quest:953"] = {t="quest",n="The Fall of Ameth'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade tasks adventurers with exploring the haunting ruins of Ameth'Aran in Darkshore to decipher ancient stone tablets. These inscriptions record the tragedy and ruin that struck the Highborne city during the Sundering. The gathered knowledge is intended for the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine, recovering history largely lost during the War of the Ancients.",h="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade tasks adventurers with exploring the haunting ruins of Ameth'Aran in Darkshore to...",sec={{t="Echoes of the Highborne",b="Long before the coast fractured into the misty expanse of Darkshore, Ameth'Aran stood as a flourishing settlement where Queen Azshara's elite sorcerers practiced powerful arcane magic. Following the cataclysmic destruction of the Well of Eternity ten thousand years ago, the city was reduced to broken marble and cracked pillars. Today, it remains haunted by the restless, anguished spirits of the Highborne who died when their golden age tore apart.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering Lost Chronicles",b="Because the War of the Ancients plunged the night elf civilization into chaotic survival, remarkably few written accounts survived the Great Sundering intact. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade attempted to survey the ruins herself, discovering two large engraved tablets—the Lay of Ameth'Aran and the Fall of Ameth'Aran—before ghostly Highborne specters forced her to retreat. Retrieving these readings ensures that the historical truths of the ancient disaster reach the scholars of the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin located in central Darkshore. Ten thousand years ago, it was a city where Queen Azshara's Highborne nobility openly wielded and studied grand arcane magic before it fell during the Great Sundering.",al={"ametharan lore","what was ameth aran","who lived in ameth aran"},it="place"},{q="Why are there ghosts in Ameth'Aran?",a="The restless ghosts haunting the ruins are the spirits of the Highborne who lived and died there. Caught in the sudden, violent catastrophe that shattered the Well of Eternity and fragmented Kalimdor, their spirits remain bound to the ruins in eternal torment.",al={"why are there spirits in ameth aran","ameth aran ghosts","restless highborne"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf sentinel stationed along the road in Darkshore. She was tasked with scouting ancient sites and recovering lost historical records for the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine.",al={"tysha moonblade","who gives fall of ameth aran"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Circle of Ancients want these tablets read?",a="The destruction of the Well of Eternity plunged Kalimdor into immense upheaval, obliterating countless libraries and monuments. Because so few written records survived the War of the Ancients, the tablets provide rare firsthand accounts of the Sundering from the perspective of the Highborne.",al={"why read the tablets","circle of ancients tablets","lay of ameth aran meaning"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the tablets located?",a="The two large tablets—the Lay of Ameth'Aran and the Fall of Ameth'Aran—are etched into standing stone monuments nestled among the ruined courtyards of Ameth'Aran, surrounded by the wandering ghosts of the city's former residents.",al={"where are the ameth aran tablets","tablet locations","how to read ameth aran"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Highborne of Ameth'Aran during the Sundering?",a="When the Well of Eternity imploded at the climax of the War of the Ancients, massive tremors and arcane backlash tore Kalimdor apart. Ameth'Aran collapsed in the ruin, burying its citizens and leaving their ghosts lingering in the rubble.",al={"how did ameth aran fall","ameth aran destruction"},it="history"},{q="Why does Sentinel Tysha Moonblade want this done?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade was dispatched on behalf of the Circle of Ancients to survey the ancient ruins. Records from the era of the War of the Ancients and the Sundering are exceedingly rare due to the cataclysms of that age. Gathering the history carved upon the tablets allows her to provide a full accounting to the druids and elders in Auberdine.",al={"tysha moonblade motive","why does tysha need this","why study ameth'aran tablets"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Tysha Moonblade need your help?",a="Tysha previously ventured into Ameth'Aran to examine the tablets herself, but she was ambushed and driven off by the vengeful Highborne spirits haunting the ruins. Unable to safely transcribe the inscriptions on her own while under constant spectral attack, she requires a capable adventurer to breach the ruins and decipher the text in her stead.",al={"why cant tysha read the tablets","why does tysha need me","why doesn't tysha go herself"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins of Ameth'Aran are a grim reminder of your ancestors' hubris under Queen Azshara and the catastrophic consequences of unregulated arcane sorcery.",["class:Mage"]="The tablets offer a sobering glimpse into the heights of pre-Sundering elven spellcraft and the terrible ruin brought on when that power spiraled out of control.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the Sentinels in securing the history of Darkshore helps preserve crucial lore for the night elf leaders guiding the Alliance on Kalimdor."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","azshara","circle of ancients","darkshore","highborne","sundering","tablets","tysha moonblade"},rel={"subzone:ameth-aran","npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade","zone:darkshore","topic:highborne","topic:war-of-the-ancients","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=953},src={"The Fall of Ameth'Aran (quest)"}}
E["quest:954"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="The demonic satyrs and vicious grells that infest the ancient night elven city of Bashal'Aran will not approach one shrine, bathed in an unearthly blue aura. Thundris Windweaver, the elder of Auberdine, sends adventurers to investigate the source of this untouched sanctuary. Reaching the site reveals the lingering spirit of Asterion, an ancient highborne presence yearning for civil company.",h="The demonic satyrs and vicious grells that infest the ancient night elven city of Bashal'Aran will not...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Ruins",b="Bashal'Aran once stood as a glorious settlement of the ancient Kaldorei Empire, but its broken marble and overgrown arches now teem with demonic taint. Twisted satyrs and corrupt grells feed greedily upon the lingering magical energies of the ruins, their malice swelling with every passing day. Yet despite their predatory dominion, Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine spotted a curious curiosity: atop a western bluff in the ruins, an ethereal blue aura burns over a shrine that no demon will approach.",sp=0},{t="The Wounded Shade",b="Braving the demonic patrols to reach the elevated shrine reveals that the blue light is no natural phenomenon. It emanates from Asterion, an ancient spirit whose vigil has persisted through centuries of solitude. Surrounded by howling beasts and vile fiends, the weary shade views even a traveling stranger as a welcome respite from decades of isolation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the blue aura located?",a="The blue aura shines atop a small raised bluff on the western edge of the ruins of Bashal'Aran, just east of Auberdine in Darkshore. It sits slightly elevated above the surrounding crumbling walls.",al={"find blue aura","where is asterion","bashal'aran shrine location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the satyrs avoid the shrine?",a="No one knows yet. A strange blue aura permeates the shrine, and the demonic satyrs and grells that otherwise infest the ruins will not approach it. Thundris Windweaver sends you to find the aura's source, which leads you to the ancient spirit Asterion.",al={"why demons afraid","why satyrs stay away"},it="threat"},{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Thundris Windweaver, a night elf druid and the elder of Auberdine, provides the quest after observing the unnatural demonic movements within the eastern ruins.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","thundris windweaver location"},gp=true},{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf shade bound to a shrine in Bashal'Aran. Long separated from civilized society, he endures surrounded by hostile demonic beasts.",al={"who is the ghost","asterion lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient kaldorei ruin nestled in the forests of Darkshore. Sacked during the ancient Sundering, it has become infested with magical parasites, grells, and satyrs seeking to feast on its dormant ley powers.",al={"what happened to bashal'aran","history of bashal'aran"},it="history"},{q="Does this quest chain continue?",a="Yes. Upon speaking to Asterion, he enlists your help to strike back against the surrounding satyrs and grells to aid his lingering spirit.",al={"next quest","what comes after bashal'aran"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want me to investigate Bashal'Aran?",a="Thundris Windweaver watches the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran with growing dread. Corrupted sprites and satyrs swarm the grounds, drawing upon lingering arcane energies to magnify their demonic power. Yet among this infestation, a single shrine wrapped in a curious blue aura remains utterly untouched by the demons. Thundris needs to understand what power keeps them at bay—and whether it might hold the key to pushing back the corruption encroaching upon Darkshore.",al={"why investigate bashal'aran","thundris motive","why send me to bashal'aran"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Bashal'Aran is a somber reminder of what was lost during the Sundering, where your ancient kin's lingering shades still hold lonely vigils against encroaching demonic corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine's scouts rely on Alliance wanderers to push into Darkshore's contested ruins and neutralize demonic threats before they reach the coast."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","blue aura","darkshore","grell","kaldorei ruins","satyr","thundris windweaver"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:4761","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",["end"]="Asterion",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=954},src={"Bashal'Aran (quest)"}}
E["quest:955"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Asterion, a sorrowful highborne ghost haunting the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran, seeks a way to undo the binding magic that tethers his spectral form. Believing the mischievous local grells have touched the seal holding him, he tasks travelers with gathering their earrings to trace its lingering magical resonance.",h="Asterion, a sorrowful highborne ghost haunting the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran, seeks a way to undo the...",sec={{t="A Centuries-Old Torment",b="Amid the shattered marble of Bashal'Aran lingers Asterion, an ancient night elf spirit who has endured centuries of confinement. Trapped between life and true death, his existence has dwindled into an agonizing wait under the canopy of Darkshore. Bound directly to the ruined settlement by arcane craft, Asterion lacks the means to dispel his shackles alone, his mind worn thin by uncounted years of solitude and despair.",sp=0},{t="Traces in the Wild",b="Asterion suspects that the key to his release is an ancient seal hidden somewhere in the ruins. While he cannot physically scour the brush and collapsed stones himself, the feral grells infesting Bashal'Aran constantly forage and steal small baubles. Asterion asks travelers to collect the earrings worn by these creatures, intending to read the residual magical impressions on the trinkets and locate the seal that holds his soul in torment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf ghost bound to the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Trapped for centuries by a mystical seal, he has watched the ages pass in torment while longing for release from his spectral state.",al={"asterion lore","who is the ghost in bashal'aran","asterion quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Asterion want grell earrings?",a="Grells are notorious scavengers that hoard shiny trinkets and jewelry. Asterion believes the creatures have handled the magical seal that binds him, meaning their worn earrings may carry enough magical residue to help him locate it.",al={"why grell earrings","grell earring purpose","earrings quest darkshore"},it="item"},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin located along the forested coast of Darkshore, dating back to before the Great Sundering. It is overrun by wild grells, satyrs, and spectral remnants of its long-fallen inhabitants.",al={"what is bashal'aran","bashal'aran history","ruins of bashal'aran"},it="place"},{q="What happens after collecting the earrings?",a="Asterion examines the earrings and senses that while the grells do not carry the seal itself, they have brushed against it in what he considers relatively recent times. This trace allows him to narrow down its location within the ruins.",al={"what do the earrings show","did the grells have the seal","grell earring result"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Asterion trapped here?",a="Asterion was bound to Bashal'Aran by an ancient magical seal created centuries ago. The binding anchors his spirit to the physical site of the ruins, preventing him from moving on to a peaceful rest.",al={"who bound asterion","how is asterion bound","asterion's seal"},it="history"},{q="What are grells?",a="Grells are small, malicious woodland creatures native to Kalimdor's forests. Known for their mischievous nature, sharp claws, and love of trinkets, they frequently infest old ruins and attack passing travelers.",al={"what is a grell","grells lore","darkshore grells"},it="target"},{q="Why does Asterion want this done?",a="Asterion is trapped in an agonizing spectral form, anchored to the ruins of Bashal'Aran by an ancient magical seal. Centurylong confinement has slowly eroded his sanity, and he yearns for release from this torment. By inspecting the earrings carried by the local creatures, he hopes to magically scry the precise location of the ward that binds him so it can ultimately be destroyed.",al={"asterion motive","why help asterion","why does asterion want earrings"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Asterion need your help instead of acting himself?",a="Asterion is an insubstantial ghost bound directly to the ruins by powerful sorcery. Incapable of venturing far beyond his immediate resting place or physically fighting the grells and sprites himself, he relies entirely on passing mortals to hunt the creatures and gather their trinkets for his divinations.",al={"why does asterion need me","why can't asterion get the earrings","why can't asterion leave"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, encountering Asterion is a sobering reminder of the ancient civilization that fell during the Sundering, leaving tortured souls bound in ruin for millennia.",["class:Mage"]="Asterion's method of using enchanted trinkets to trace residual magical emanations reflects ancient Highborne practices of arcane divination.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing out the chaotic grells around Bashal'Aran helps pacify the treacherous northern reaches of Darkshore for the Alliance."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","binding","darkshore","ghost","grell","grell earring","seal"},rel={"npc:asterion","zone:darkshore","quest:954","quest:99141"},m={start="Asterion",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=955,ri={"Grell Earring"}},src={"Bashal'Aran (2)"}}
E["quest:956"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Asterion, a night elf spirit trapped amidst the ruined pillars of Bashal'Aran, seeks the relic holding him bound to this world. Having sensed the corruption of his prison among the local grells, he directs travelers to hunt the satyrs who command them and recover the Ancient Moonstone Seal.",h="Asterion, a night elf spirit trapped amidst the ruined pillars of Bashal'Aran, seeks the relic holding him...",sec={{t="A Prison of Ancient Stone",b="For well over a thousand years, the spirit Asterion has remained tethered to the fallen ruins of Bashal'Aran. The surrounding marble pillars serve as an unyielding cage that neither his fading spiritual strength nor his ancient magic can crack. Bound by a cursed relic, he has spent centuries staring out at Darkshore's mist-shrouded canopy, wondering whether even the erosion of the stone around him would grant him release.",sp=0},{t="Satyrs and the Moonstone Seal",b="After discovering that nearby grells bore traces of the magic maintaining his captivity, Asterion deduced that the source of the enchantment had fallen into the hands of the satyrs who direct the chaotic creatures. Wandering through the ancient groves, these demonic night elves keep a watchful grip on the Ancient Moonstone Seal. Reclaiming this talisman is the critical step toward shattering the invisible bars that anchor Asterion to his shrine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf ghost trapped within the ruins of Bashal'Aran. Bound by ancient magic, he has spent more than a thousand years confined to the shrine's standing pillars, unable to pass on or wander beyond his stony prison.",al={"who is asterion","asterion lore","ghost in bashal aran"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the satyrs have the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="Satyrs lead and influence the wild grells infesting northern Darkshore. Because the grells carried traces of the binding magic, Asterion realized that their wicked satyr masters had seized the Ancient Moonstone Seal to keep the local spirits tormented and tethered.",al={"why do satyrs have seal","satyr moonstone seal","ancient moonstone seal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens once the seal is recovered?",a="Asterion takes hold of the very relic that has bound him for centuries. Recovering the Ancient Moonstone Seal is the penultimate step in his liberation, allowing the seal to be broken so he may finally walk the forests freely again.",al={"what does seal do","recovering the seal"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin located along the mist-draped shores of northern Darkshore. Once a magnificent settlement or holy enclave, it now lies broken, plagued by grells, satyrs, and trapped spirits from an earlier age.",al={"bashal aran lore","what is bashal aran"},it="place"},{q="How long has Asterion been trapped here?",a="Asterion has been imprisoned for more than a thousand years. Without physical means or magic to dismantle the boundary, he was forced to wait through the centuries, wondering if he would ever be freed.",al={"how old is asterion","how long trapped"},it="history"},{q="Can Asterion simply walk away from the shrine?",a="No. The Ancient Moonstone Seal maintains a metaphysical barrier around the shrine. The stone pillars act as an impenetrable cage that prevents his spectral form from crossing beyond them.",al={"can asterion leave","why is ghost trapped"}},{q="Why does Asterion want the seal recovered?",a="Asterion is desperate for freedom. The ancient relic serves as the binding anchor of his eternal prison, holding his spirit trapped within the ruined shrine. For over a thousand years, he has stared past the stone pillars, unable to break their hold through strength or sorcery. Recovering the artifact is the only way to destroy it and finally allow him to walk the forests freely once more.",al={"why does asterion want this done","asterion motive","why help asterion"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="The Ancient Moonstone Seal is a magical relic that acts as the key to Asterion's captivity. It creates an intangible barrier between the pillars of Bashal'Aran, functioning like an eternal cell that no spell or physical strength of his can shatter. As long as the seal endures in the hands of the nearby corrupt forces, Asterion remains bound to the shrine.",al={"what is the ancient moonstone seal","what does the moonstone seal do","ancient moonstone seal purpose"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why are you sent against the local satyrs?",a="The satyrs command the vile grells swarming the ruins of Bashal'Aran. Because the lesser grells bore traces of the seal's enchantment, Asterion deduced that their masters must have claimed the artifact itself. Corrupt and drawn to ancient magical relics, the satyrs hold the seal within their encampment, making them your target.",al={"who are the satyrs in bashal'aran","why fight the satyrs","who has the seal"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why can't Asterion retrieve the seal himself?",a="Asterion cannot leave the confines of the shrine. The magic of the seal keeps him utterly bound within its perimeter, treating the stone pillars as impassable bars. He possesses neither the strength nor the sorcery to breach his confinement, leaving him completely reliant on an outsider to venture into the satyr camps on his behalf.",al={"why does asterion need me","why cant asterion get the seal","why me asterion"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Bashal'Aran is a somber reminder of your people's ancient past, where lingering ancestors remain chained to the earth by satyrs who embody the demonic betrayal of the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="The twisted influence of the satyrs continues to corrupt Darkshore's wildlife and disturb ancient spirits who should be resting peacefully in the cycle of nature.",["faction:Alliance"]="Cleansing the ruins of Darkshore from satyr corruption secures Kalimdor's northern coast and aids the Kaldorei in laying their tragic past to rest."},kw={"ancient moonstone seal","asterion","bashal'aran","darkshore","grell","kaldorei","night elf ghost","satyr"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:954","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Asterion",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=956,ri={"Ancient Moonstone Seal"}},src={"Bashal'Aran (3)"}}
E["quest:957"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="This quest tasks adventurers with helping the trapped spirit of Asterion in the ruins of Bashal'Aran. By carrying his binding seal south to the sister ruins of Ameth'Aran, adventurers seek a way to shatter his ancient bonds.",h="This quest tasks adventurers with helping the trapped spirit of Asterion in the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",sec={{t="A Prison of Ancient Sorcery",b="The spirit Asterion has lingered in Bashal'Aran for millennia, chained in death by an Ancient Moonstone Seal. Forged through the mighty sorceries of the Highborne caste before the Great Sundering, the seal cannot be shattered by mundane strength. Its destruction requires the specific magic of an ancient flame that still smolders amid the fallen stonework of Ameth'Aran to the south.",sp=0},{t="Twin Ruins of Darkshore",b="Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were once vibrant sister settlements of the kaldorei civilization, back when Queen Azshara reigned and the Well of Eternity still anchored their empire. Today, both sites are overgrown, haunted ruins filled with lingering ghosts and volatile arcane energies. Within a stone gazebo in Ameth'Aran, a mystical brazier holding a cyan-hued fire offers the only power capable of consuming Asterion's binding relic.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance Awakens",b="With the seal destroyed, Asterion is finally unburdened, gazing upon a shattered Kalimdor vastly altered from the golden age he remembers. Yet his freedom does not bring him peace. Sensing that his former master and jailor, the Highborne Athrikus, still endures, Asterion's ancient despair quickly turns into a cold, burning hunger for revenge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is a night elf spirit trapped within the ruins of Bashal'Aran. He dates back ten thousand years to the reign of Queen Azshara, having been bound to the ruined city by his former Highborne master.",al={"asterion","who is the ghost","npc asterion"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I destroy the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="The seal must be taken south to Ameth'Aran, the twin ruin of Bashal'Aran. Look for a stone gazebo sheltering a large cubical brazier that burns with an ancient, greenish-blue magical fire.",al={"where is the flame","ancient flame location","destroy seal"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the relationship between Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran?",a="They were sister cities of the ancient night elf empire before the Sundering. Both fell to devastation ten thousand years ago, leaving behind haunted stone pillars, residual arcane energies, and restless spirits.",al={"twin ruins","ametharan connection","bashalaran ametharan"},it="place"},{q="Who imprisoned Asterion?",a="Asterion was imprisoned by his former master, a powerful Highborne sorcerer named Athrikus. Upon being freed, Asterion senses that Athrikus somehow still survives in the world.",al={"who imprisoned asterion","who is athrikus","asterion master"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What era does Asterion remember?",a="Asterion last walked the world when the original Well of Eternity still existed, Queen Azshara ruled the empire, and the Highborne nobility held their majestic courts before the Sundering.",al={"asterion past","well of eternity era","how old is asterion"},it="history"},{q="Does freeing Asterion lay his spirit to rest?",a="No. Rather than crossing into peaceful rest, Asterion's sorrow turns toward retribution when he senses that Athrikus still lingers, prompting him to seek vengeance against his ancient captor.",al={"does asterion pass on","what happens to asterion","asterion after free"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Asterion want the Ancient Moonstone Seal destroyed?",a="The Ancient Moonstone Seal is the anchor binding Asterion's spirit in torment within the ruins of Bashal'Aran. Crafted millennia ago by powerful Highborne sorcery, it keeps him imprisoned and blind to the world beyond. Destroying it in the mystical ancient flame of Ameth'Aran is the only way to shatter his ethereal chains, granting him freedom and the clarity to witness what has become of Kalimdor.",al={"why destroy moonstone seal","asterion motive","why does asterion want to break the seal"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Asterion need you to take the seal to Ameth'Aran?",a="Bound by the ancient Highborne magic anchoring him to Bashal'Aran, Asterion cannot leave the immediate ruins, let alone travel south to Ameth'Aran. He lacks physical form to interact freely with the living world and cannot survive the dangerous ghosts and wild beasts haunting the twin ruins. Only an able mortal traveler can carry the seal directly into the heart of the ancient flame.",al={"why cant asterion destroy the seal","why does asterion need me","why send an adventurer to destroy the seal"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of modern Kalimdor, freeing Asterion is a sober encounter with their people's pre-Sundering past and the lingering corruption of Queen Azshara's Highborne nobility.",["class:Mage"]="The durable enchantments binding Asterion and the surviving flames of Ameth'Aran offer a glimpse into the raw arcane power wielded by ancient Highborne sorcerers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the ancient curses in Darkshore secures the borders for new night elf settlements pushing out from Auberdine."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus","azshara","bashal'aran","darkshore","highborne","moonstone seal"},rel={"npc:asterion","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:highborne","quest:954","zone:darkshore","zone:azshara"},m={start="Asterion",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=957},src={"Bashal'Aran (4)"}}
E["quest:960"] = {t="quest",n="Onu is meditating",z="darkshore",s="While investigating the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, the ancient of lore Onu enters a deep trance to contemplate the growing threat. Players who lose their mystical scrying phial can speak to the meditating ancient to receive a replacement. His thoughts center on the sinister alliance and motivations of the Twilight's Hammer cult and the serpentine naga.",h="While investigating the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, the ancient of lore Onu enters a deep trance...",sec={{t="A Mind in Deep Contemplation",b="Onu is an Ancient of Lore rooted in Darkshore's Grove of the Ancients, standing as a living repository of Kalimdor's history. When ominous reports surface concerning dark excavations at the Master's Glaive, Onu turns his immense consciousness inward. He meditates heavily on what could draw both the fanatic Twilight's Hammer cultists and the insidious naga to the petrified remains of an ancient behemoth. For adventurers carrying out his reconnaissance, he remains an accessible anchor, offering replacement scrying phials should theirs be misplaced in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Scrying the Depths",b="To monitor the ruins without risking the ancient's physical presence, Onu relies on nature-attuned divination. Adventurers are entrusted with a phial of scrying, meant to conjure a scrying bowl directly within the excavation site so Onu can commune from afar. Because the journey south through Darkshore is perilous and fraught with hostile wildlife and cultist patrols, Onu anticipates mishaps. His trance is not unbroken slumber, but an attentive vigil; he readily provides another vial of sacred waters to ensure the investigation of the Master's Glaive continues without delay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Onu meditating?",a="Onu is an ancient of lore pondering the disturbing presence of both the Twilight's Hammer cult and the naga at the Master's Glaive. He uses this meditation to perceive their motives and guide adventurers investigating the site.",al={"why is onu meditating","onu trance","what is onu doing"},it="motive"},{q="What is the purpose of this interaction?",a="It serves as a safety mechanism for players on the quest 'The Master's Glaive'. If you lose, destroy, or prematurely use your Phial of Scrying, speaking to the meditating Onu provides you with a replacement phial so you can complete the ritual.",al={"lost phial of scrying","get another phial","onu replacement quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Onu located?",a="Onu is rooted in the Grove of the Ancients, located in central-southern Darkshore, just off the main road.",al={"onu location","where to find onu"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do I do with the Phial of Scrying?",a="You carry the phial south to the Master's Glaive and use it near the scrying bowl at the site. This allows Onu to magically communicate with you and observe the dark activities taking place around the ancient remains.",al={"how to use phial of scrying","scrying bowl darkshore","phial of scrying purpose"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="The Master's Glaive is a massive, ancient excavation site in southern Darkshore where the colossal, petrified skull of a forgotten entity lies pierced by a gargantuan blade. Cultists and naga have converged there for unknown, malevolent purposes.",al={"what is masters glaive","monument in south darkshore"},it="place"},{q="Can Horde players interact with Onu here?",a="No. Onu is allied strictly with the night elves and the Alliance. Horde adventurers trespassing near the Grove of the Ancients will find Onu and his protectors hostile or uncooperative.",al={"is onu alliance only","horde onu meditating"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Onu need your help instead of investigating himself?",a="As an ancient of lore, Onu is deeply bound to the land and the grove of the Master's Glaive. Moving in secret among the hostile cultists and serpentine naga is impossible for a colossal tree-spirit. Instead, he remains rooted to ponder the deeper spiritual threat and commune through scrying bowls, relying on agile travelers like you to scout the tainted ground and bring back vital intelligence.",al={"why send me","why doesn't onu go","why onu needs you"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As stewards of Kalimdor's balance, night elves revere ancients of lore like Onu, relying on their ageless wisdom to interpret disturbances in the wilds of Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="Druids share a profound natural bond with ancients of lore. Maintaining communication via scrying rituals reflects the Cenarion Circle's method of surveying tainted ground from a distance.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Darkshore from cultists and aquatic invaders is critical for Alliance travelers journeying between Teldrassil and Ashenvale."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","meditating","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","quest:948","subzone:master-s-glaive","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Onu",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=960},src={"Onu is meditating"}}
E["quest:963"] = {t="quest",n="For Love Eternal",z="darkshore",s="\"For Love Eternal\" is a tragic quest given by Cerellean Whiteclaw in Auberdine. Haunted by memories of his lost lover, Anaya Dawnrunner, Cerellean asks an adventurer to travel to the shattered ruins of Ameth'Aran to release her restless spirit from an eternity of torment.",h="\"For Love Eternal\" is a tragic quest given by Cerellean Whiteclaw in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Slumber Full of Grief",b="Ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, the catastrophe surrounding the Well of Eternity tore ancient Kalimdor apart. Among the casualties was the city of Ameth'Aran, where Cerellean Whiteclaw lost his beloved, Anaya Dawnrunner. Stricken with despair, Cerellean followed Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage into the long hibernation of the druids, hoping the millennia spent walking the Emerald Dream would quiet his aching heart. Instead, his sorrow only lingered, following him through the ages.",sp=0},{t="The Ghost of Ameth'Aran",b="Upon awakening in recent times, Cerellean wandered through Darkshore in a stupor until his feet brought him back to the melancholy ruins of Ameth'Aran. There, wandering among the ancient stones, he beheld the tortured ghost of Anaya. Unable to bear raising a weapon against the woman he loved, he pleads with passing travelers to destroy her tormented manifestation, retrieve her pendant, and finally grant her troubled soul peace.",sp=0},{t="Parting Across the Veil",b="When Anaya's pendant is returned to Auberdine, a spectral remnant of Anaya appears before Cerellean one last time. Freed from the lingering anguish that bound her to the ruins, she shares a brief, silent goodbye before fading away into the ether, leaving the grieving druid to weep in bittersweet solace by the seaside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cerellean Whiteclaw?",a="Cerellean Whiteclaw is a night elf druid resting in Auberdine. After losing his beloved Anaya during the Sundering ten thousand years ago, he entered the long druidic hibernation alongside Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage, carrying his unhealed sorrow across millennia.",al={"cerellean whiteclaw","who gives for love eternal","cerellean lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner was a night elf who lived in the city of Ameth'Aran prior to the Great Sundering. She was killed when the city fell during the aftermath of the War of the Ancients, and her ghost has remained trapped in the ruins ever since.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","who is anaya","anaya darkshore"},it="target"},{q="Where is Anaya's spirit located?",a="Her spirit wanders among the ancient, ghost-infested ruins of Ameth'Aran, located in southern Darkshore east of the main road.",al={"anaya location","where is anaya dawnrunner","anaya's pendant location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why couldn't Cerellean free Anaya himself?",a="Despite the passage of ten thousand years, Cerellean's love for Anaya was so profound that he could not bear the heartbreak of raising his own hand or casting a spell against her apparition, even to end her suffering.",al={"why doesn't cerellean kill anaya","why cerellean asks for help"},it="why_me"},{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran was an ancient night elven settlement destroyed ten millennia ago during the Sundering that followed the War of the Ancients. Its ruins in Darkshore remain thick with lingering ghosts and lingering arcane echoes.",al={"ameth'aran history","fall of ameth'aran","what is ameth'aran"},it="history"},{q="What happens when you return Anaya's pendant?",a="Returning Anaya's pendant to Cerellean in Auberdine causes Anaya's ghost to appear briefly before him. She shares a final, silent moment of closure before dissolving, leaving Cerellean alone by the shore with his grief.",al={"quest turn in anaya","cerellean ending","for love eternal ending"},sp=1},{q="Why does Cerellean Whiteclaw want Anaya's spirit freed?",a="Cerellean believed his love, Anaya, had perished peacefully millennia ago when Ameth'Aran was shattered during the Sundering. Discovering her restless, tormented ghost wandering the ruins broke his heart. Knowing she suffers bound to this realm, he cannot endure the thought of her remaining in anguish, yet he cannot bear to raise a hand against her himself.",al={"why does cerellean want this done","cerellean motive","why destroy anaya spirit"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is Anaya's Pendant for?",a="Anaya's Pendant is a deeply personal keepsake carried by the spirit of Anaya Dawnrunner. Returning it to Cerellean Whiteclaw provides him tangible proof that her tormented soul has finally been released from the ruins of Ameth'Aran, granting him a tragic closure to a grief he carried across thousands of years.",al={"anayas pendant use","what does anayas pendant do","purpose of anayas pendant"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Cerellean's fate reflects the personal cost paid by the druids who entered thousands of years of slumber at Shan'do Stormrage's side, only to find the waking world still marked by their ancient losses.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Darkshore, this tragic reunion is a poignant reminder of the enduring scars left behind by the Great Sundering and the fall of their ancient cities.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Cerellean offers Alliance heroes a glimpse into the tragic, millennia-spanning lives of their night elven allies as they adjust to the waking world."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","anaya's pendant","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","sundering"},rel={"npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:shan-do"},m={start="Cerellean Whiteclaw",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=963,ri={"Anaya's Pendant"}},src={"For Love Eternal"}}
E["quest:965"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Charged with the defense of Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze suspects foul dealings at the ancient ruins to the north. She tasks adventurers with finding Balthule Shadowstrike, a scout dispatched to watch the enigmatic Tower of Althalaxx who has failed to report back on schedule.",h="Charged with the defense of Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze suspects foul dealings at the ancient ruins...",sec={{t="A Scout Unaccounted For",b="Auberdine's sentinels must remain ever watchful over Darkshore's creeping perils. Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze noticed suspicious activity stirring around the Tower of Althalaxx in the northern reaches of the forest. Unwilling to leave the town unprotected without clearer intelligence, she sent Balthule Shadowstrike to survey the ancient ruin. Days have passed without word from the scout, prompting Elissa to seek a willing traveler to journey north, locate Balthule, and ensure he has not met an untimely end.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Upon the Ruin",b="The road north from Auberdine crosses past ancient Kaldorei ruins and over the Cliffspring River before reaching the shadowy sprawl of the tower. Though cut off from sending word back to Auberdine, Balthule survived his initial surveillance. Upon being located in the surrounding woods, he confirms that Elissa's instincts were correct: dark and troubling developments are actively underway within the crumbling stone spire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf Sentinel stationed in Auberdine. She is charged with safeguarding the settlement from external threats across Darkshore and monitors regional dangers like the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"elissa starbreeze","who gives quest","auberdine questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is a scout dispatched by Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze to spy on the mysterious activity surrounding the Tower of Althalaxx. He maintains a vigil outside the ruin to keep track of hostile forces.",al={"balthule","who is the scout","shadowstrike"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Tower of Althalaxx located?",a="The tower sits in northeastern Darkshore. Travelers can reach it by heading east out of Auberdine, following the northern road past Bashal'Aran, and crossing the bridge over the Cliffspring River until the spire comes into view.",al={"tower of althalaxx location","where is the tower","how to find althalaxx"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was a scout sent to the tower in the first place?",a="Strange and threatening activity was detected around the ruins. Rather than committing Auberdine's garrison blindly, Sentinel Elissa sent Balthule ahead to investigate the nature of the disturbance.",al={"why watch the tower","what is wrong at althalaxx","why sent balthule"},it="origin"},{q="Why hasn't Balthule returned to Auberdine?",a="Balthule observed grave, troubling developments at the tower and lacked safe means to deliver his findings back to Auberdine without abandoning his vigil or risking interception.",al={"why balthule missing","is balthule trapped","why did balthule stay"},it="threat"},{q="Does this quest chain continue?",a="Yes. Locating Balthule Shadowstrike begins a multi-part investigation into the dark forces occupying the Tower of Althalaxx and their sinister ambitions in Darkshore.",al={"is this a chain","what quest comes next","althalaxx chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze want this done?",a="As a Sentinel charged with the defense of Auberdine, Elissa Starbreeze is responsible for safeguarding Darkshore from encroaching threats. She dispatched Balthule Shadowstrike to investigate suspicious occurrences near the Tower of Althalaxx, but he is long overdue. Fearing he has fallen into unexpected peril, she needs someone to locate him and confirm his safety.",al={"why find balthule","elissa starbreeze motive","why send me to tower of althalaxx"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze need an adventurer instead of handling it herself?",a="Elissa is sworn to protect the settlement of Auberdine itself. With Sentinel resources stretched thin across Darkshore, she cannot abandon her watch at the town post to mount an expedition into the northern wilds alone, making an able-bodied traveler the ideal envoy to check on her scout.",al={"why doesn't elissa go herself","why send an adventurer to althalaxx","why elissa needs help"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins of Althalaxx stand as a reminder of ancient Kalimdor's fallen highborne past, and preserving Auberdine from the corruption festering in those stones is a vital duty for night elf sentinels.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the Alliance's primary gateway into northern Kalimdor, making the defense of its surrounding roads and borders essential for all visiting allies."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","balthule shadowstrike","darkshore","elissa starbreeze","scout","sentinel","tower"},rel={"npc:sentinel-elissa-starbreeze","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:954"},m={start="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze",["end"]="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=965},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}}
E["quest:966"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Investigating suspicious activity around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, the scout Balthule Shadowstrike enlists aid to gather intelligence from the gathering warlocks. By recovering discarded parchment scraps from the fanatics encamped outside the ruins, he attempts to uncover the cultists' identity and sinister purpose.",h="Investigating suspicious activity around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, the scout Balthule...",sec={{t="Eyes in the Shallows",b="Balthule Shadowstrike stands watch along the misty shoreline of northern Darkshore, keeping a vigilant eye on the ancient ruin known as the Tower of Althalaxx. Sent to monitor the site for Auberdine and warn Delgren the Purifier of any rising danger, Balthule hesitated to leave his post to report. Fearing he would miss crucial movements by the dark spellcasters occupying the stones, he instead relies on passing travelers to scout the perimeter camps.",sp=0},{t="Deciphering the Cult",b="The lesser followers haunting the ruined grounds carry fragmented scrolls and notes. By piecing together several worn parchments recovered from these outer cultists, Balthule discovers a disturbing name: the Cult of the Dark Strand. Entirely unfamiliar with this shadowy sect, the scout realizes the peril is more organized than a simple band of rogue warlocks, demanding an immediate warning to Delgren.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is an Alliance scout stationed on the road near the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He was dispatched to monitor suspicious gatherings at the tower on behalf of Auberdine's leadership and the paladin Delgren the Purifier.",al={"balthule shadowstrike lore","who is balthule","balthule darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven ruin in northern Darkshore. Recently, sinister warlocks and their cultist thralls have occupied the surrounding grounds and the interior of the tower, conducting dark rituals far from the watch of Auberdine.",al={"tower of althalaxx","what is althalaxx","darkshore ruined tower"},it="place"},{q="Who are the cultists surrounding the tower?",a="They belong to the Cult of the Dark Strand, a secretive organization of warlocks and zealots who have gathered at the ancient elven ruins to pursue dark summoning rituals.",al={"who are the warlocks","cult of the dark strand","dark strand fanatics"},it="target"},{q="Why does Balthule warn against entering the tower?",a="Balthule notes that the warlocks residing inside the upper tower are far more powerful and dangerous than the fanatics camping outside among the ruins. He advises gathering intelligence from the perimeter before attempting to storm the stronghold.",al={"can i go into the tower","tower warlocks dangerous","inside the tower"},it="danger"},{q="What do the worn parchments reveal?",a="Piecemeal scraps carried by the cult's fanatics provide the first clear confirmation of the group's name—the Cult of the Dark Strand—revealing to Balthule that the occupants are an organized sect whose presence poses an immediate threat to the region.",al={"what is on the parchments","worn parchment lore","cult notes"},it="item"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale who works to cleanse demonic and corrupt influences. He suspected malicious activity was taking root at the Tower of Althalaxx and depends on scouts like Balthule for intelligence.",al={"delgren","who is delgren","delgren the purifier"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike want this done?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike fears that dark forces are gathering in secret right on Darkshore's borders. While Delgren suspected warlocks were congregating at the ancient ruins, neither of them knows who they are or what foul ritual they intend to enact. Balthule needs enough written evidence to piece together their identity and motives before taking decisive action to protect the region.",al={"why balthule wants parchments","balthule motive","why investigate althalaxx"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike send you instead of going himself?",a="Balthule is stationed on a solitary reconnaissance watch outside the ruins. He cannot leave his post to scour the surrounding cultist camps or return to Auberdine to report, terrified that any absence might cause him to miss critical enemy movements. By having you confront the outer cultists and retrieve their writings, he can maintain continuous surveillance over the tower.",al={"why does balthule need help","why not balthule","why balthule asks you"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The discovery of a cohesive dark cult operating in northern Darkshore directly aids the crusade of Delgren the Purifier, an ally dedicated to purging fel and demonic corruption.",["class:Warlock"]="The Cult of the Dark Strand demonstrates that unaligned covens will seize ancient ruins to perform their summonings far away from the prying eyes of Alliance and Horde authorities alike.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of the Tower of Althalaxx by human and demonic cultists represents yet another defilement of ancient elven heritage across the shores of Kalimdor."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","balthule","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","fanatics","parchment","purifier","shadowstrike","warlocks"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=966,ri={"Worn Parchment"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (2)"}}
E["quest:967"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest bridges the investigation of the Dark Strand cult in northern Darkshore with the broader defense of northern Kalimdor. Balthule Shadowstrike dispatches an Alliance courier south to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale to alert his mentor, Delgren the Purifier, of the cult's sinister gathering at the Tower of Althalaxx.",h="This quest bridges the investigation of the Dark Strand cult in northern Darkshore with the broader defense...",sec={{t="A Plea for Reinforcements",b="Following initial clashes with the Dark Strand cultists around the Tower of Althalaxx, the night elf scout Balthule Shadowstrike recognizes that the threat surpasses his solitary vigil. To mount a decisive response, he writes a detailed report and entrusts it to an Alliance messenger bound for his master, Delgren the Purifier. Because the cult's summoners are growing bolder by the hour, word must reach seasoned leadership capable of directing an eradication effort.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Ashenvale",b="Carrying Balthule's dispatch requires a trek across the full length of Darkshore, following the long coastal highway south out of the mist and over the forested border into Ashenvale. Stationed at Maestra's Post along the western road, Delgren the Purifier has dedicated himself to cleansing demons and undead lingering in the woodland. Though initially unfamiliar with night elven customs, the human paladin has forged a deep mutual respect with the Sentinels as an indispensable ally.",sp=0},{t="A Holy Warrior Awakened",b="Delgren receives Balthule's urgent letter with grim resolve. As a warrior devoted to the Holy Light, he views the presence of dark cultists, soul corruption, and demonic fiends in these ancient woods as an intolerable blight. Reading of the Dark Strand's entrenched foothold at the ruined highborne tower, Delgren immediately prepares to take charge of the operation and strike back.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Devoted to the Holy Light, he offers his martial and spiritual expertise to the night elf Sentinels to cleanse demons and undead encroaching upon their ancestral forests.",al={"delgren the purifier","who is delgren","delgren lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Balthule Shadowstrike sending a messenger to Ashenvale?",a="Balthule is a scout stationed outside the Tower of Althalaxx who has been studying the Dark Strand cult. Recognizing that the cult's dark rituals and numbers are escalating rapidly, he sends his findings to his mentor Delgren so an organized strike can be mounted.",al={"why send letter to delgren","balthule letter reason"},it="motive"},{q="What is the relationship between Balthule and Delgren?",a="Delgren is Balthule's master. The human paladin has instructed the night elf in the art of battle and introduced him to the teachings of the Holy Light, fostering an unusually close bond across their cultural divides.",al={"balthule and delgren","how do balthule and delgren know each other"},it="ties"},{q="Where is Maestra's Post?",a="Maestra's Post is an Alliance outpost situated in western Ashenvale along the main road leading south from Darkshore. It serves as an early sentry point for travelers moving between Darkshore and the depths of the forest.",al={"maestras post location","where is maestras post"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Dark Strand cult doing at the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Dark Strand is a cult operating out of the ruined highborne Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. They practice dark arts, consort with demonic powers, and threaten to unleash corrupting forces across the shoreline.",al={"dark strand cult althalaxx","tower of althalaxx cultists"},it="threat"},{q="How does Delgren view his alliance with the night elves?",a="Delgren admitted that he was initially unaccustomed to night elven manners and lifestyle when he first arrived in Kalimdor. Over time, however, standing alongside them against common evils has led him to develop immense respect for the Sentinels.",al={"delgren night elves","human paladin night elves"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Balthule choose you as his messenger instead of going himself?",a="Balthule must remain stationed near the Tower of Althalaxx to keep a watchful eye on the Dark Strand cultists and monitor their escalating threat. With the journey stretching across the entire length of Darkshore into Ashenvale, he needs a capable and well-armed traveler who can survive the dangerous roads and guarantee the urgent warning safely reaches Delgren's hands.",al={"why send me to delgren","why balthule messenger","why can't balthule deliver the letter"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Meeting Delgren offers paladins an inspiring example of their holy calling in unfamiliar lands: a human crusader wielding the Light to earn the deep trust of Kalimdor's reclusive night elves.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, this mission highlights the growing, practical partnership between their Sentinels and the eastern races who have come to help purge demonic remnants from their woods.",["faction:Alliance"]="The cooperation between Balthule in Darkshore and Delgren in Ashenvale shows the vital communication lines binding northern Kalimdor's scattered Alliance garrisons together."},kw={"ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","dark strand","darkshore","delgren the purifier","holy light","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:light","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",["end"]="Delgren the Purifier",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=967},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (3)"}}
E["quest:968"] = {t="quest",n="Tools of the Highborne",z="darkshore",s="Tools of the Highborne is an Alliance quest offered by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. Travelers are dispatched south into the shattered ruins of Ameth'Aran to pry lingering magical relics from the hands of restless Highborne apparitions. The goal is simple: recover these ancient artifacts before their latent sorcery can unleash further harm upon Kalimdor.",h="Tools of the Highborne is an Alliance quest offered by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",sec={{t="Echoes in the Ruins",b="South of Auberdine, east of the coastal highway, lie the overgrown stone foundations of Ameth'Aran. Ten thousand years ago, this settlement served as a bastion for the Highborne—the privileged aristocracy of the ancient night elven empire. When their unchecked arcane dabbling culminated in the Sundering of the world, Ameth'Aran was shattered. Yet its inhabitants never truly departed. Sentinels patrolling Darkshore report that the ghosts of these aristocrats still haunt the sunken plazas, clutching the enchanted tools and trinkets they possessed in life.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Arcane Past",b="For modern kaldorei society, the arcane is not merely forbidden knowledge; it is an existential danger that nearly obliterated life on Azeroth. Thundris Windweaver recognizes that leaving these Highborne implements in ghostly hands leaves the doorway open to corruption. By dispatching adventurers to wrench these relics away from the restless spirits, Thundris intends to see them thoroughly destroyed, ensuring the dormant, tainted sorcery can never again fuel another disaster.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Highborne relics?",a="The relics are found within the ruins of Ameth'Aran, located south of Auberdine on the eastern side of the main path through Darkshore. Wandering spirits throughout the ruined stone courtyards carry these ancient implements.",al={"where are the relics","ameth'aran location","where to find relics"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf scholar and elder residing in the port town of Auberdine. Working closely with the local Sentinels, he coordinates efforts to protect Darkshore from lingering magical taints and ancient curses left behind by the Sundering.",al={"thundris windweaver","who gives tools of the highborne"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thundris want these relics destroyed?",a="Night elf society strictly rejects arcane magic due to the devastating Great Sundering caused by Highborne reckless sorcery. Thundris fears that the lingering arcane power inside these items could reawaken dormant evils if left unchecked.",al={"why destroy the relics","purpose of tools of the highborne"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of spirits haunt Ameth'Aran?",a="The spirits are the spectral remains of the Highborne elite who perished during the War of the Ancients. Even in death, they cling to their former pride, power, and magical artifacts, reenacting their faded lives among the ruined stone.",al={"ghosts in ameth aran","what are the spirits"},it="target"},{q="Why are the Highborne still bound to the ruins?",a="The sudden, cataclysmic destruction during the Sundering ripped through the empire with such magical violence that many souls remained trapped, bound by trauma and arcane resonance to the ruins of their former homes.",al={"why are they ghosts","highborne curse"},it="history"},{q="What happens to the relics after you turn them in?",a="Thundris Windweaver takes custody of the collected relics with the explicit plan to have them permanently dismantled and destroyed so their dormant arcane taint can never be harnessed or released again.",al={"what does thundris do with relics","relic fate"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the Highborne Relics?",a="These relics are ancient magical implements preserved from before the Great Sundering, once wielded by the elite sorcerers of Queen Azshara's court. Even after ten thousand years, they retain the lingering taint of the arcane reckless dabbling that tore ancient Kalimdor apart. Left in the hands of lingering ghosts, they remain conduits of dormant, dangerous power.",al={"what are highborne relics","what is highborne relic","highborne relic lore"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, confronting the ghosts of Ameth'Aran is a somber reminder of their ancestors' hubris and the catastrophic sundering of their ancestral empire.",["class:Mage"]="While kaldorei society seeks to smash these artifacts out of fear, arcane scholars recognize them as rare, pristine examples of pre-Sundering Highborne craftsmanship.",["class:Druid"]="Clearing the corrupted arcane remnants from Ameth'Aran helps heal the spiritual wounds that disrupt the natural tranquility of the Darkshore wilderness.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting the night elves in securing their haunted territories cements the Alliance's presence and solidarity in the ancient forests of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","highborne","relics","sundering","thundris windweaver"},rel={"subzone:ameth-aran","quest:4761","subzone:auberdine","topic:highborne","zone:darkshore","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=958,ri={"Highborne Relic (Classic)"}},src={"Tools of the Highborne"}}
E["quest:970"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest marks a critical turn in the investigation of the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand, shifting the pursuit from the ruined Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore across the border to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier dispatches adventurers into nearby cultist camps to secure a potent Glowing Soul Gem. Unlocking this artifact reveals the grim sorcery that fuels the cult's influence over the northern forests.",h="This quest marks a critical turn in the investigation of the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand, shifting the...",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Border",b="After uncovering the ominous activities around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, reports led directly south into Ashenvale to Delgren the Purifier. Stationed at Maestra's Post, Delgren has long contended with the Cult of the Dark Strand encroaching on the ancient elven woods. Recognizing that the cult's threat spans across both territories, Delgren resolves to strike at the heart of their vile sorcery.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Ordil'Aran",b="Northeast of Maestra's Post lies the ruins of Ordil'Aran, now overrun by fanatical Dark Strand cultists. Delgren identifies that their operatives carry glowing soul gems—dark vessels enchanted with sinister magic that sustain the cult's power. By hunting down the cultists among the ruins and reclaiming one of these gems, Delgren intends to shatter their enchantment and expose the true source behind their malevolent rite.",sp=0},{t="A Spirit Trapped",b="Upon deciphering the foul enchantments bound to the glowing soul gem, Delgren does not merely unearth dark incantations; he unravels a vessel of torment. Breaking the gem's wards releases the spirit of Sargath, one of the elves of Ameth'Aran whom Athrikus Narassin trapped in soul gems during the Sundering and has been slowly draining ever since. The apparition names Athrikus's lieutenant, Ilkrud Magthrull, whose tome may reveal where the remaining soul gems are held.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Glowing Soul Gem?",a="The Glowing Soul Gem is held by members of the Cult of the Dark Strand located northeast of Maestra's Post at the ruins of Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale. Various cultists lurking within the ruins carry it, though it can take some persistence to recover one.",al={"soul gem location","where does soul gem drop","dark strand soul gem"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. He actively fights the sinister forces invading the forest, with a particular focus on hunting down and destroying the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"delgren","who is delgren"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Cult of the Dark Strand?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand is a malevolent sect operating out of the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore and ancient elven ruins like Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale. They practice dark sorcery, soul binding, and necromantic rituals.",al={"dark strand cult","who are dark strand"},it="threat"},{q="Why is a Darkshore quest sending me to Ashenvale?",a="While the investigation begins at the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore, the cult's network extends south across the border into Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post holds the expertise needed to counter the cult's soul-binding magic.",al={"why maestra's post","why go to ashenvale"},it="place"},{q="What happens when the soul gem is deciphered?",a="When Delgren unravels the dark enchantments binding the soul gem, he releases a tormented ghost imprisoned within the stone. The freed spirit reveals key information about the cult's sinister workings.",al={"what is in the soul gem","soul gem ghost"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Ordil'Aran located?",a="Ordil'Aran is an ancient elven ruin situated just northeast of Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale, currently infested by the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"ordil'aran location","where is ordilaran"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want this done?",a="Delgren has been locked in combat against the Cult of the Dark Strand, who have entrenched themselves northeast of Maestra's Post. To him, they are a dangerous thorn that must be torn out completely. The dire warnings in Balthule Shadowstrike's letter confirm that their corrupt influence is escalating, and Delgren believes unraveling the secrets trapped within their enchanted soul gem is the only way to expose and dismantle their power.",al={"delgren motive","why does delgren want soul gem","why fight cult of dark strand"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Glowing Soul Gem for?",a="The Glowing Soul Gem is a dark, enchanted artifact carried by the Cult of the Dark Strand at Ordil'Aran. Delgren believes it holds the secret to the cult's vile magic and the power they wield. By bringing the gem to him, you allow Delgren to decipher the dark enchantments woven into the stone and uncover whatever essence or entity is trapped inside.",al={"what is glowing soul gem","glowing soul gem purpose","soul gem dark strand"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who are you sent against at Ordil'Aran?",a="You are sent to confront the Cult of the Dark Strand occupying the ruins of Ordil'Aran, northeast of Maestra's Post. Cultists, fanatics, acolytes, and adept spellcasters have gathered among the elven ruins to conduct forbidden rites. One of their members carries an enchanted soul gem that Delgren needs to unlock the cult's secrets, requiring you to cut through their ranks until the relic is recovered.",al={"who is at ordil'aran","dark strand at ordil'aran","who holds soul gem"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Purifying dark soul vessels and putting twisted cultists to the sword aligns closely with the paladin's duty to purge unholy corruption from the world.",["class:Priest"]="The release of a bound spirit from dark torment echoes the priest's calling to bring redemption and solace to tormented souls.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching vile cultists defile ancient ruins like Ordil'Aran and corrupt the northern woods makes eliminating the Cult of the Dark Strand an urgent priority for any night elf.",["faction:Alliance"]="Coordinating between outposts in Darkshore and Ashenvale secures the northern frontier against dark practitioners threatening Alliance travelers."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","delgren the purifier","glowing soul gem","maestra's post","ordil'aran"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=970,ri={"Glowing Soul Gem"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (4)"}}
E["quest:973"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This quest is the fifth chapter in the investigation of the Tower of Althalaxx, leading Alliance adventurers south from Darkshore into Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier dispatches you to strike down Ilkrud Magthrull, an orc warlock residing at the corrupted Fire Scar Shrine, and retrieve his esoteric tome.",h="This quest is the fifth chapter in the investigation of the Tower of Althalaxx, leading Alliance adventurers...",sec={{t="A Hunt Into Ashenvale",b="Following the trail of dark cultist activity uncovered at the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore, the holy warrior Delgren the Purifier recognizes the signature of a dangerous practitioner: the orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull. Operating out of the demonic blight known as Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale, Ilkrud's shadowy dealings threaten to spread foul magic across the pristine elven woodlands. Delgren tasks you with slaying the warlock and seizing his grimoire to expose his master's designs.",sp=0},{t="The Warlock's Lair",b="Fire Scar Shrine is a fel-scarred ruin swarming with demonic thralls. Marked by ominous red pillars along its rocky ascent, the shrine houses Ilkrud alongside a summoned succubus and guardian felslayers. Defeating the orc in the heart of his fel domain allows Delgren to scour Ilkrud's tome for the dark knowledge and commands tying back to the sinister rituals unfolding at Althalaxx.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post, a night elf outpost on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale. He directs operations against demonic corruption and cultists operating in the region.",al={"delgren","delgren lore","who starts quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ilkrud Magthrull?",a="Ilkrud Magthrull is a formidable orc warlock making his lair at the Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale. Though initially deemed a minor annoyance by Delgren, his connection to the dark rites at the Tower of Althalaxx makes him a critical target.",al={"ilkrud","who is ilkrud magthrull","orc warlock ashenvale"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Fire Scar Shrine located?",a="The shrine is situated in southwestern Ashenvale, south of the Shrine of Aessina and west of Astranaar. It is a corrupted, demon-infested enclave flanked by two distinct red pillars leading up to Ilkrud's altar.",al={"fire scar shrine location","where is ilkrud","how to reach ilkrud"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Delgren need Ilkrud Magthrull's tome?",a="Ilkrud's tome contains his dark rituals and communications. Delgren aims to decipher the writings to uncover what sinister plot links the orc warlock to the cultists lingering around the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"why tome","what is in ilkrud's tome","purpose of tome"},it="item"},{q="How does this quest connect Darkshore to Ashenvale?",a="The storyline begins with investigations at the Tower of Althalaxx on the northern coast of Darkshore. As the mystery deepens, the cultists' network leads adventurers down through Darkshore into the contested forests of Ashenvale.",al={"darkshore to ashenvale quest","althalaxx chain connection"}},{q="What happens after recovering the tome?",a="Delgren examines the text to deduce the deeper schemes behind the cultist presence at the Tower of Althalaxx, leading into the final confrontations of the quest chain.",al={"next quest","what follows althalaxx 5"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want this done?",a="Delgren the Purifier is dedicated to rooting out demonic corruption in the region. While he previously viewed Ilkrud Magthrull as little more than a minor annoyance, the warlock's sinister research and active presence at the corrupted Fire Scar Shrine make him a growing menace that Delgren can no longer ignore.",al={"delgren motive","why kill ilkrud magthrull","delgren the purifier goal"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This task takes Alliance adventurers out of the safety of Darkshore and deep into the demon-tainted corners of Ashenvale to cleanse a growing dark menace.",["class:Paladin"]="Working alongside Delgren the Purifier to strike down fel summoners and confiscate corrupt tomes reflects the classic calling of the Holy Light against demonic corruption.",["class:Warlock"]="Confronting Ilkrud Magthrull pits you against a fellow practitioner of the dark arts who uses summoned succubi and voidwalkers to guard his unholy texts.",["race:NightElf"]="The Fire Scar Shrine represents a vile defilement of Ashenvale's ancient forests, making the elimination of Ilkrud a matter of defending sacred ancestral lands."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","delgren","fire scar shrine","ilkrud","maestra","magthrull","tome","warlock"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:fire-scar-shrine","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","subzone:shrine-of-aessina","subzone:astranaar","npc:lars"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=973,ri={"Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (5)"}}
E["quest:981"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="This errand marks the triumphant conclusion of the campaign against the Cult of the Dark Strand at the Tower of Althalaxx. Having eliminated the cult's leadership within the sinister ruins of Darkshore, an adventurer carries word south into Ashenvale to Delgren the Purifier. It represents a vital victory for the Alliance in purging demonic corruption from the ancient night elven borders.",h="This errand marks the triumphant conclusion of the campaign against the Cult of the Dark Strand at the Tower...",sec={{t="A Threat Severed",b="The Tower of Althalaxx stood for weeks as a festering wound in northern Darkshore, occupied by the fanatical Cult of the Dark Strand and their shadowy masters. Through relentless tracking, intelligence gathering, and violent skirmishes, the cult's operations were systematically dismantled. With their sorcerers slain and their dark rituals broken, the immediate danger of demonic infiltration in Darkshore has finally been stayed.",sp=0},{t="Report to Maestra's Post",b="Following the cult leader's death, Balthule Shadowstrike directs the victor south to Maestra's Post in the Ashenvale canopy. There waits Delgren the Purifier, a devoted warrior of the Holy Light who oversaw the crusade against Althalaxx's wicked occupants. Delivering news of the cult's collapse brings peace of mind to the regional defenders, earning the champion Delgren's lasting blessing and well-earned gratitude.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="This quest serves as the final turn-in for the long Tower of Althalaxx storyline. You simply need to journey from the tower's vicinity down to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale and report your decisive victory to Delgren the Purifier.",al={"tower of althalaxx objective","turn in tower of althalaxx","where to turn in quest 981"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. Wielding the Holy Light, he is dedicated to purging corruption and combating demonic threats like the Cult of the Dark Strand across northern Kalimdor.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","delgren the purifier"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is an Alliance operative positioned near the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore. Working closely with Delgren, he monitors the cult's movements and guides adventurers through dismantling the dark cabal from within.",al={"balthule","balthule lore","who is balthule shadowstrike"},it="identity"},{q="What was the Cult of the Dark Strand doing at the tower?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand occupied the ancient ruins of the Tower of Althalaxx to perform dark rituals, summon demonic entities, and expand their sinister influence across the coastal lands of Darkshore.",al={"cult of the dark strand","what happened at althalaxx","tower of althalaxx lore"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Maestra's Post located?",a="Maestra's Post is an Alliance outpost situated in northwestern Ashenvale, just south of the border crossing from Darkshore along the main road.",al={"maestra's post location","where is maestras post","delgren location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the Cult of the Dark Strand completely destroyed?",a="While their leadership at the Tower of Althalaxx has been executed and their primary ritual broken, scattered cultists and remnants still haunt isolated corners of Kalimdor. However, their organized threat in Darkshore has been shattered.",al={"is the cult gone","dark strand destroyed","did we kill the cult"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike want this done?",a="With the Cult of the Dark Strand shattered and their leadership broken, Balthule wants you to carry word of the victory back to Delgren the Purifier. Delgren initiated the campaign against the cultists lurking at the tower, and Balthule believes your efforts deserve proper recognition and the paladin's promised reward.",al={"why send me back to delgren","balthule motive","why report to delgren"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Reporting to Delgren the Purifier carries special resonance for paladins, who share his holy mission to cleanse demonic corruption and wicked cults from the world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Eliminating the cult protects the overland road connecting Darkshore and Ashenvale, ensuring Alliance scouts and travelers remain safe from demonic ambushes.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, cleansing the Tower of Althalaxx removes a foul blight from the ancient Highborne ruins that litter their sacred coastal forests."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","balthule","cult","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","maestra's post"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",["end"]="Delgren the Purifier",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=981},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (9)"}}
E["quest:982"] = {t="quest",n="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea",z="darkshore",s="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea is an Alliance quest offered by Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine. Players are tasked with diving into the waters north of the village to recover personal lockboxes from two sunken night elf vessels, the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil. Both ships were ambushed by coastal murlocs, leaving their surviving crew members in search of closure.",h="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea is an Alliance quest offered by Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine.",sec={{t="Tragedy off the Coast",b="The waters off Darkshore have grown increasingly hazardous, not just from treacherous currents and natural reefs, but from aggressive coastal tribes. The vessels Silver Dawning and Mist Veil were making their way into port at Auberdine when they were overwhelmed by swarming murlocs. Neither ship survived the encounter, and both sank into the shallows north of the settlement. The surviving crew made it ashore, but the loss of their ships and captains cast a heavy shadow over the port.",sp=0},{t="Recovering Lost Memories",b="Gorbold Steelhand, a dwarf stationed in Auberdine, takes up the cause of honoring the fallen night elf captains. Although the vessels are now underwater ruins claimed as trophies and nests by the local murlocs, the captains' lockboxes remain locked in the flooded holds. Recovering the logs and personal effects inside allows the surviving sailors in Auberdine to properly mourn their commanders and lay their spirits to rest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the sunken ships located?",a="The wrecks of both the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil lie submerged off the coast of Darkshore, directly to the north of the Auberdine docks.",al={"where are the shipwrecks","wreck location","where to find silver dawning"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil?",a="Both vessels were ambushed by murlocs as they sailed toward Auberdine across the sea. The crews were overrun, both captains died, and the ships foundered and settled on the ocean floor.",al={"how did ships sink","why did ships wreck","what sank mist veil"},it="history"},{q="Who is Gorbold Steelhand?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarf residing in the night elf port of Auberdine. He looks out for the surviving sailors around town and tasks adventurers with recovering the lost captains' belongings.",al={"who gives deep ocean vast sea","gorbold steelhand lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is inside the lockboxes?",a="The lockboxes contain the personal effects and logs belonging to the fallen night elf captains, items cherished by the surviving crew members who escaped the wreck.",al={"what are in the lockboxes","captains lockbox contents"},it="item"},{q="Why do the survivors care so much about these effects?",a="The captains were respected night elf mariners. Recovering their logs and possessions provides closure to their surviving crew and is believed to help put their spirits to rest.",al={"why recover lockboxes","why help the captains"},it="motive"},{q="What creatures inhabit the shipwrecks now?",a="The ruins have been overtaken by murlocs, who treat the wrecked hulls as trophies and prowl the surrounding waters.",al={"what is guarding the ships","mobs at the shipwrecks"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The fallen captains were night elf mariners serving Auberdine's maritime trade, making the recovery of their belongings a matter of ancestral honor.",["race:Dwarf"]="Gorbold Steelhand shows the typical dwarven instinct to honor fallen comrades and support his fellow sailors in foreign ports.",["faction:Alliance"]="The shared grief of the crew in Auberdine demonstrates the close maritime cooperation between dwarfs and night elves along the Kalimdor coast."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","deep ocean vast sea","gorbold steelhand","lockbox","mist veil","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"npc:gorbold-steelhand","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","quest:938"},m={start="Gorbold Steelhand",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=982,ri={"Mist Veil's Lockbox","Silver Dawning's Lockbox"}},src={"Deep Ocean, Vast Sea"}}
E["quest:983"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 827",z="darkshore",s="Buzzbox 827 is the first in an experimental communication relay built by the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle along the coastline of Darkshore. Plagued by breakdowns, these curious mechanical contraptions rely on an eccentric design that uses local wildlife parts for field repairs. Restoring the silent machine allows Wizbang to test his long-distance voice network directly from Auberdine.",h="Buzzbox 827 is the first in an experimental communication relay built by the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle along...",sec={{t="Gnomish Innovation on Ancient Shores",b="While visiting Auberdine, the eccentric gnomish engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle sought to bridge the long distances of the wild coast with a series of long-range acoustic relays called Buzzboxes. Designed to transmit voice over great distances, these lever-laden devices stand out starkly against the ancient ruins and somber forests of Darkshore. However, like many ambitious gnomish inventions, they suffer from chronic instability and require near-constant upkeep to keep their internal gears churning.",sp=0},{t="Ecological Maintenance",b="Rather than hauling refined iron gears and copper pins across the wilderness, Wizbang adopted an unconventional solution: he built each Buzzbox to be serviced using components harvested from nearby native fauna. Buzzbox 827, stationed just south of Auberdine along the misty shoreline, was engineered to function with the sturdy, jointed legs of local tide and reef crawlers. Depositing the legs into the receiver hopper prompts the machine to self-assemble and jump back to life, broadcasting Wizbang's distant voice through its speakers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Buzzbox?",a="A Buzzbox is a long-distance voice communication machine invented by the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle. Equipped with levers and internal machinery, it is designed to transmit voices across the untamed expanse of Darkshore, allowing people to speak across miles.",al={"what does a buzzbox do","buzzbox purpose","gnome box darkshore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does a metal machine need crab legs to run?",a="Wizbang purposefully designed each Buzzbox to use organic components from surrounding wildlife as improvised replacement parts. By placing Buzzbox 827 near the beach where crawlers dwell, he ensured travelers could make emergency mechanical repairs using chitinous limbs instead of rare machined metal.",al={"why crawler legs","crawler leg repair","why feed it legs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Buzzbox 827 located?",a="Buzzbox 827 is situated along the shoreline of Darkshore, just a short trek south of the coastal settlement of Auberdine.",al={"buzzbox 827 location","where is buzzbox 827","find buzzbox 827"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is a gnome tinkerer staying on the upper floor of the Auberdine inn. Ambitious and enterprising, he is attempting to construct an interconnected communication network across Darkshore despite the constant malfunctions of his prototypes.",al={"wizbang cranktoggle","who made buzzbox","auberdine gnome"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Crawler Legs for the repair?",a="Crawler Legs can be gathered from Pygmy Tide Crawlers and Young Reef Crawlers scuttling along the sands and shallows of the Darkshore beach just south of Auberdine.",al={"crawler leg location","how to get crawler legs","pygmy tide crawler"},gp=true},{q="What happens once Buzzbox 827 is repaired?",a="Once the Crawler Legs are fed into the hopper, the machine churns them into place, hums back to life, and relays Wizbang's voice from Auberdine. Pleased with the success, he immediately asks you to travel further down the coast to repair the next unit in the chain, Buzzbox 411.",al={"after buzzbox 827","buzzbox questline next","buzzbox 827 completion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want Buzzbox 827 repaired?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is testing his latest invention: an experimental communication network across Darkshore that allows people to speak to each other across long distances. Unfortunately, his buzzboxes require constant maintenance and break down frequently. Getting Buzzbox 827 operational is the first step in proving that his network actually works.",al={"wizbang cranktoggle motive","why fix buzzbox 827","why does wizbang need this done"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are the Crawler Legs used for?",a="Wizbang designed each buzzbox to rely on parts harvested from nearby native wildlife. Buzzbox 827 specifically requires six crawler legs to replace worn or broken mechanical components within its holding mechanism. Once inserted, the device's inner gears grind and slot the legs into place to restore power and transmission.",al={"what are crawler legs for","crawler leg buzzbox","why crawler legs"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic chitin and arthropod limbs in place of forged brass gears is quintessential gnomish improvisation, trading durability for readily scavenged local materials.",["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang's device represents classic gnomish ambition, attempting to bring technological connectivity to an ancient, untamed land that has never seen a telephone or radio.",["race:NightElf"]="The clanking, smoking Buzzboxes are a bizarre eyesore on the sacred, somber shores of Kalimdor, though the night elves of Auberdine tolerate the tinkerer's experiments."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 827","crawler legs","darkshore","gnomish engineering","reef crawler","tide crawler","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",["end"]="Buzzbox 827",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=983,ri={"Crawler Leg"}},src={"Buzzbox 827 (quest)"}}
E["quest:984"] = {t="quest",n="How Big a Threat?",z="darkshore",s="How Big a Threat? is an Alliance quest given by Terenthis in Auberdine. Having witnessed furbolg madness taking root across Teldrassil, the night elf druid directs scouts to investigate local furbolg settlements in Darkshore to confirm whether the same dark taint has crossed the sea.",h="How Big a Threat?",sec={{t="Shadows Across the Sea",b="The night elves of northern Kalimdor have long maintained cordial or peaceful relations with indigenous furbolg tribes. However, following the Third War, strange corruptions began unhinging furbolg minds in Teldrassil, resulting in violent kidnappings and feral attacks against their former allies. Stationed in Auberdine, the druid Terenthis fears that this sinister affliction is not isolated to the World Tree, but is actively spreading among the mainland tribes along the misty coasts of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="A Gathering Storm",b="Reconnaissance of a furbolg encampment nestled near the ruins of Ameth'Aran confirms Terenthis's worst suspicions. The furbolgs there display erratic, hostile aggression, bearing the clear marks of the same corruption plaguing the north. Their close proximity to Auberdine elevates them from a peaceful wilderness neighbor to an urgent defensive hazard for the Alliance settlement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a night elf druid stationed in the coastal haven of Auberdine. Haunted by accounts of night elves assaulted and captured by maddened furbolgs across Teldrassil, he works to monitor and suppress emerging threats throughout Darkshore.",al={"terenthis questgiver","who gives how big a threat","terenthis auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Darkshore turning hostile?",a="Historically friendly or neutral toward the night elves, many furbolg clans have fallen victim to a spreading supernatural taint following the Third War. This unseen corruption drives them into frantic, territorial madness, causing them to attack travelers and former allies alike.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","corrupt furbolgs darkshore","furbolg corruption"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the corrupt furbolg camp located?",a="The encampment lies inland in central Darkshore, situated just north of the ancient highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran and southeast of Auberdine.",al={"camp location","where is the furbolg camp","how big a threat location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does this relate to events on Teldrassil?",a="In Teldrassil, several corrupted furbolgs kidnapped and injured night elf sentinels and civilians. Terenthis references those recent rescues when seeking to verify if mainland Darkshore faces the exact same crisis.",al={"teldrassil connection","teldrassil furbolgs","why does terenthis mention teldrassil"},it="history"},{q="What happens after reporting back to Terenthis?",a="Confirming the corruption prompts Terenthis to prepare defensive measures for Auberdine, continuing a quest chain focused on investigating the root source and countering the aggressive furbolgs nearby.",al={"next quest","what follows how big a threat","quest continuation"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are night elves so concerned about furbolg camps near Auberdine?",a="Auberdine serves as the principal Alliance port and supply lifeline on the mainland. Having deeply corrupted, hostile tribes nesting within striking distance leaves trade roads, scouting parties, and the town itself vulnerable to sudden assaults.",al={"threat to auberdine","why care about furbolgs"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Terenthis want this done?",a="Terenthis took a personal vow to prevent further bloodshed after his night elf brethren had to be rescued from corrupted furbolgs over on Teldrassil. He has already noticed faint hints of corruption touching Darkshore, and he fears the contagion could spread undetected through the local furbolg tribes. By sending you to scout their camps, he hopes to gauge whether the danger is already at Auberdine's doorstep before more lives are lost.",al={"terenthis motive","why investigate furbolgs darkshore","why does terenthis care"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent to investigate?",a="You are dispatched to scout the local furbolg tribes inhabiting Darkshore. While many furbolg clans once lived peacefully or reclusively alongside the night elves, dark influences have begun warping their minds and driving them to madness. Terenthis sends you to inspect their settlements to confirm whether this affliction has taken root among the tribes living dangerously close to Auberdine.",al={"who am i investigating","what furbolg camp","who is the target"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, watching ancient allies like the furbolgs succumb to irrational darkness so soon after the Third War is both a bitter tragedy and an immediate danger to sacred lands.",["class:Druid"]="Furbolgs share deep bonds with nature and ancient wilderness spirits, making their sudden descent into corruption a grave concern for druids tasked with healing Kalimdor's balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As the Alliance's primary gateway to mainland northern Kalimdor, safeguarding Auberdine from wilderness threats is essential for regional security and logistics."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","corruption","darkshore","furbolg","teldrassil","terenthis","threat"},rel={"npc:terenthis","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg","quest:940"},m={start="Terenthis",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=984},src={"How Big a Threat?"}}
E["quest:985"] = {t="quest",n="How Big a Threat?",z="darkshore",s="How Big a Threat? is an Alliance quest offered by the night elf Terenthis in Auberdine. Having already scouted the hostile Blackwood furbolg camp south of town, adventurers are sent to cull the corrupted pathfinders and windtalkers before their frenzy threatens the settlement.",h="How Big a Threat?",sec={{t="A Necessary Cull",b="Following initial scouting south of Auberdine, the Sentinels have determined that the Blackwood furbolgs pose an immediate danger to Darkshore's refugees and defenders. Terenthis tasks combat-capable travelers with striking directly at their camp, eliminating Blackwood Pathfinders and Windtalkers to break their offensive momentum.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy of the Corrupted",b="Night elves traditionally view furbolgs as spiritual kin and historic allies of the wilderness. However, the malignant spread of fel moss and demonic taint across northern Kalimdor has driven the Blackwood tribe mad. With no known remedy to restore the furbolgs' minds, the defenders of Auberdine view violence as a grim necessity to prevent innocent deaths.",sp=0},{t="Grimclaw's Arrival",b="Upon reporting the cull back to Terenthis, a white bear named Grimclaw rushes into Auberdine toward the night elf. The arrival signals urgent new developments regarding the wildlife and corruption ravaging the coastline, setting off the next stage in Auberdine's defensive efforts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Terenthis want the Blackwood furbolgs killed?",a="The Blackwood tribe south of Auberdine has fallen to corruption, turning violent and irrational. Because their camp poses an imminent threat to the settlement and no cure exists for their madness, Terenthis orders a preemptive strike to keep Auberdine safe.",al={"why kill blackwood furbolgs","reason for furbolg cull","terenthis furbolg quest"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Blackwood furbolg camp located?",a="The camp lies just south of Auberdine along the coastal forest of Darkshore, nestled among the corrupted trees where the Blackwood tribe has gathered.",al={"blackwood furbolg location","where are pathfinders and windtalkers","furbolg camp darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is a white bear companion tied to the wilderness investigations in Darkshore. When you complete the cull of the Blackwood furbolgs, Grimclaw sprints into Auberdine to alert Terenthis of further troubles in the wild.",al={"white bear auberdine","who is the bear running to terenthis","grimclaw the bear"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="What is causing the furbolgs to go mad?",a="The furbolgs have been poisoned by fel moss and lingering demonic corruption left behind after the Third War. The dark energies ravaging Darkshore warp both mind and body, driving peaceful tribes into uncontrollable aggression.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","darkshore furbolg corruption","what corrupted blackwood"},it="conflict"},{q="Why are night elves reluctant to kill furbolgs?",a="The furbolgs and night elves have shared a bond of friendship and reverence for nature for thousands of years. Putting them down feels to the night elves like slaughtering their own brothers of the wild, but the corruption leaves them no alternative.",al={"night elves and furbolgs","why mourn furbolgs"},it="people"},{q="What is the difference between the first and second 'How Big a Threat?' quests?",a="The first quest tests scouting ability by requiring you to locate and observe the Blackwood camp. The second quest is a direct combat assignment to thin out the camp's pathfinders and windtalkers once the threat is confirmed.",al={"how big a threat parts","how big a threat difference"},gp=true},{q="Who are the Blackwood pathfinders and windtalkers?",a="They are members of the Blackwood furbolg tribe who have established an encampment south of Auberdine. Driven mad and aggressive by the spreading forest corruption, their scouts and shamans represent an immediate, escalating danger to the night elf settlement. Until a cure for their affliction is discovered, Terenthis considers culling their ranks the only way to safeguard his people.",al={"blackwood pathfinders","blackwood windtalkers","who are we killing"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Terenthis send an adventurer instead of the Auberdine sentinels?",a="Auberdine's Sentinels and guardians are stretched thin defending the settlement against corrupt wildlife and coastal incursions. Because you already proved your competence by stealthily scouting the Blackwood encampment earlier, Terenthis trusts your capability and calls upon you to strike directly at the camp before its threat spills over into the town.",al={"why send me","why not use guards","why terenthis needs me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, culling the Blackwood is a bitter grief; centuries of kinship with the furbolgs have been shattered by the lingering demonic blight of the Third War.",["class:Druid"]="Druids feel the tragedy keenly, as the furbolgs' plight reflects the ongoing suffering of Cenarius's creations beneath the taint of fel moss.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine serves as the vital port anchor for the Alliance in Darkshore, making the elimination of nearby hostile encampments crucial to securing the region."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","fel moss","furbolg","grimclaw","pathfinder","terenthis","windtalker"},rel={"npc:terenthis","quest:984","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Terenthis",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=985},src={"How Big a Threat? (2)"}}
E["quest:986"] = {t="quest",n="A Lost Master",z="darkshore",s="A Lost Master tasks an Alliance adventurer with gathering materials to aid in the search for Volcor, a night elf lost in the wilderness of Darkshore. Terenthis in Auberdine offers to weave an enchanted camouflage cloak to protect the rescuer, requiring pelts from the coast's fiercest moonstalkers.",h="A Lost Master tasks an Alliance adventurer with gathering materials to aid in the search for Volcor, a night...",sec={{t="A Search into the Wilds",b="While tracking threats along the coast of Darkshore, Terenthis in Auberdine becomes concerned for the fate of Volcor and his companion, Grimclaw. Venturing deep into the southern reaches of the region is notoriously dangerous due to aggressive predators and corrupted wildlife. Rather than sending a scout unprotected, Terenthis devises a plan to craft a protective cloak imbued with wild illusions.",sp=0},{t="Pelts of the Pride",b="To weave a cloak capable of confounding Darkshore's beasts, standard hides are insufficient. Terenthis requires fine moonstalker pelts taken specifically from mature moonstalker sires or matriarchs. These formidable great cats prowl the woodlands south of Auberdine near the Wildbend River and extend toward the forested border of Ashenvale.",sp=0},{t="Delicate Magic",b="The finished garment uses moonstalker fur and nature enchantments to let the wearer pass unhindered through hostile territory while searching for Volcor. However, Terenthis warns that the illusion is delicate: engaging in strenuous activity or combat breaks the enchantment, leaving the searcher exposed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout or tracker who went missing in the wilds of southern Darkshore. His companion Grimclaw and Terenthis in Auberdine seek his whereabouts, prompting the search.",al={"who is volcor","volcor lore","lost master volcor"},it="identity"},{q="Who offers this task?",a="Terenthis, a night elf stationed in the settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore, provides the quest after adventurers assist him with earlier local concerns.",al={"quest giver","where to get a lost master","terenthis location"},it="people"},{q="Where are moonstalker sires and matriarchs found?",a="These mature moonstalkers roam southern Darkshore, particularly near the banks of the Wildbend River and farther south approaching the border with Ashenvale.",al={"fine moonstalker pelt locations","where to find moonstalkers","wildbend river cats"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the cloak meant to do?",a="Terenthis intends to craft an enchanted cloak that conceals the wearer from the hostile beasts of Darkshore, allowing them to search for Volcor without constantly drawing attacks.",al={"what does the cloak do","terenthis cloak","cloak enchantment"},it="power"},{q="Why does Terenthis need specific pelts?",a="Ordinary pelts lack the strength and natural presence required to channel the camouflage illusion. Only the thick, resilient hides of sires and matriarchs can carry the enchantment.",al={"why sires and matriarchs","why fine pelts"},it="item"},{q="Does the camouflage cloak have limitations?",a="Yes. Terenthis warns that the enchantment is fragile. Speaking to others is permitted, but strenuous interactions or combat will quickly dispel the illusion.",al={"does the illusion break","cloak restrictions"},it="power"},{q="Why does Terenthis want this done?",a="Terenthis is deeply concerned for his fellow night elf Volcor, who went missing in the perilous wilds of southern Darkshore, and for the loyal bear Grimclaw who arrived wounded in search of help. Terenthis refuses to send you into such dangerous territory unprotected, so he insists on preparing a magical camouflage cloak first to ensure you can safely locate Volcor without being mauled by the coast's predators.",al={"why help volcor","terenthis motive","why does terenthis want pelts"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Locating Volcor reflects the night elves' duty to safeguard their kindred and wild companions across the untamed reaches of Darkshore.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters will recognize the bond between Volcor and Grimclaw, as well as the skill demanded to track and hunt Darkshore's matriarchs and sires.",["class:Druid"]="Druids can appreciate Terenthis's respect for the natural stealth of moonstalkers, turning their wild essence into protective camouflage."},kw={"a lost master","auberdine","darkshore","fine moonstalker pelt","grimclaw","moonstalker","terenthis","volcor","wildbend river"},rel={"npc:terenthis","npc:volcor","subzone:auberdine","subzone:wildbend-river","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Terenthis",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=986,ri={"Fine Moonstalker Pelt"}},src={"A Lost Master"}}
E["quest:993"] = {t="quest",n="A Lost Master",z="darkshore",s="Having gathered pelts and fine thread, you carry the completed Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak into the wilds of Darkshore to find the missing night elf, Volcor. Guided by his loyal white bear Grimclaw, you must track down the wounded scout before hostile furbolgs finish him off.",h="Having gathered pelts and fine thread, you carry the completed Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak into the wilds of...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Woods",b="After Terenthis in Auberdine weaves the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak, the search for the missing scout Volcor begins in earnest. His bear companion, Grimclaw, has returned to the road south of the settlement, standing watch for any ally sent by Terenthis. By offering a familiar greeting to the loyal beast, travelers are led directly off the beaten track toward the cave where Volcor lies in hiding.",sp=0},{t="Hiding in the Dark",b="Volcor sought refuge within a cavern after suffering severe injuries at the hands of the local corrupted furbolgs. Trapped and bleeding, he has had to rely entirely on stealth and Grimclaw's wits to avoid being overrun. The enchanted cloak provides him with the concealment and hope necessary to plan his extraction, though his wounds leave him in precarious condition for the return trek to Auberdine.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout based out of Darkshore who went missing while venturing near hostile furbolg encampments. He was badly wounded during a confrontation and managed to crawl into a nearby cave, while his companion bear Grimclaw sought aid.",al={"volcor lore","who is the lost master"},it="identity"},{q="How do you find Volcor's hiding spot?",a="Grimclaw waits alongside the road south of Auberdine. Waving to the beast lets him know you are the helper sent by Terenthis, prompting Grimclaw to run directly toward the secluded cave where Volcor is nursing his injuries.",al={"where is volcor","find volcor cave","how to follow grimclaw"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak?",a="Terenthis enchanted the cloak crafted from fine thread and moonstalker pelts to grant brief, potent magical stealth. Its magic lets you walk unhindered by Darkshore's creatures while you search for Volcor, and the cloak is then given to him.",al={"moonstalker cloak","cloak magic"},it="item"},{q="Who attacked Volcor?",a="Volcor was ambushed and wounded by the corrupted furbolg tribes roaming Darkshore. Though he managed to evade immediate slaughter, his injuries prevented him from making the journey back to Auberdine unassisted.",al={"who hurt volcor","why is volcor bleeding"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after finding Volcor?",a="Once Volcor receives the enchanted cloak, he catches his breath and asks for your assistance in escaping the wilderness, offering you a choice between guiding him out through careful stealth or cutting a path through the furbolgs by raw force.",al={"volcor next quest","after a lost master"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Terenthis want to find Volcor so urgently?",a="Terenthis fears that time is slipping away for his fellow night elf. Volcor was ambushed by corrupted furbolgs, and with only the loyal sabercat Grimclaw returning to plead for help, Terenthis knows Volcor cannot survive alone in hiding for long. Having completed the enchanted cloak to mask his scent and presence, Terenthis needs you to reach Volcor before the furbolgs hunt him down or his injuries claim him.",al={"terenthis motive","why save volcor","why does terenthis care about volcor"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The bond between night elf scouts and their animal companions is demonstrated here by Grimclaw's steadfast loyalty in seeking aid for his master Volcor.",["class:Hunter"]="Seeing Grimclaw navigate the road to locate help for Volcor highlights the remarkable intelligence and devotion of well-trained Kalimdor beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine depends on scouts like Volcor to monitor the rising corruption of Darkshore's furbolg tribes, making his rescue a vital priority for the outpost."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","furbolg","grimclaw","moonstalker cloak","nightsaber","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","quest:986","topic:furbolg","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Terenthis",["end"]="Volcor",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=993},src={"A Lost Master (2)"}}
E["quest:994"] = {t="quest",n="Escape Through Force",z="darkshore",s="Escape Through Force is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where the adventurer helps Volcor break through surrounding threats by direct combat. After fighting past the perils of the wild to reach the road and reunite with his faithful companion Grimclaw, the player reports Volcor's safe escape back to Terenthis in Auberdine.",h="Escape Through Force is an Alliance quest in Darkshore where the adventurer helps Volcor break through...",sec={{t="A Direct Way Out",b="When stranded in the perilous wilderness of Darkshore, subtle movement is not always the chosen path. Faced with danger, the night elf Volcor accepts a blunt strategy: cutting directly through the surrounding hostile creatures to reach safety. Rather than attempting to slip away unseen, Volcor relies on martial prowess to carve a corridor straight down to the main road.",sp=0},{t="Reunion on the Road",b="Reaching the thoroughfare safely allows Volcor to reunite with Grimclaw, his stalwart bear companion who has been waiting by the path. With their escape secured, Volcor prepares for his next journey while urging the adventurer to report directly to Terenthis in Auberdine. Delivering news of Volcor's safety reassures the night elf leadership and immediately draws the attention of Sentinel Selarin, pointing toward deeper troubles brewing southward in Ashenvale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout or woodsman in Darkshore who went missing along with his companion Grimclaw. After being located by adventurers searching on behalf of Terenthis, he requires assistance escaping hostile wildlife and dangerous terrain.",al={"volcor identity","who is volcor","volcor darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is Volcor's loyal companion bear. During Volcor's entrapment, Grimclaw remained separated near the road, serving as the landmark rendezvous point for Volcor's escape.",al={"grimclaw","volcor bear","volcor pet"}},{q="Why does Terenthis care about Volcor's return?",a="Terenthis coordinates scout movements and local defense efforts out of Auberdine. Tracking down lost allies and assessing threats along the coastline is critical to maintaining night elf control across a rapidly destabilizing Darkshore.",al={"terenthis volcor","why help volcor","terenthis quest"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Upon returning to Terenthis in Auberdine, Sentinel Selarin rushes into the outpost with urgent news, opening the path for the adventurer to take on the trek south into Ashenvale.",al={"after escape through force","what comes next","next quest after volcor"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is there an alternate way to finish Volcor's escort?",a="Yes. When rescuing Volcor, adventurers are offered a choice in approach: fighting their way out head-on via Escape Through Force, or guiding him quietly past danger using stealth.",al={"escape through force alternate","escape through stealth","volcor choices"},gp=true},{q="Where does this quest lead in the broader storyline?",a="Securing Volcor's survival serves as a bridge between the local conflicts of Darkshore and the larger regional defense of the night elf lands, directly opening up assignments in Ashenvale.",al={"volcor storyline","darkshore to ashenvale questline"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Volcor want to fight his way out?",a="Volcor has spent too long trapped and endangered in the wilds of Darkshore away from his companion, Grimclaw. Having resolved to break out directly rather than sneak away, he is determined to carve a path through whatever hostiles block the path down to the road. His sole focus is reaching safety and reuniting with his loyal bear before reporting back toward Auberdine.",al={"volcor motive","why escape through force","why does volcor want this"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Volcor need your help to escape?",a="Volcor is separated from Grimclaw and surrounded by hostile threats in the wilderness. Alone and exposed, breaking through the wilderness by brute force carries immense risk. With you lending martial support, his chances of surviving the gauntlet down to the safety of the main road are far higher than trying to cut his way out single-handedly.",al={"why does volcor need me","why can't volcor escape alone","why help volcor"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Rescuing scouts like Volcor is vital to the Kaldorei's tenuous grip on Darkshore, where wild beasts, corruption, and outside invaders threaten their ancestral woodlands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting local scouts deepens the bond between the young Alliance and the Night Elves, proving the faction's value in securing Kalimdor's northern frontier."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","escort","grimclaw","selarin","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","npc:sentinel-selarin","quest:990","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Volcor",["end"]="Terenthis",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=994},src={"Escape Through Force"}}
E["quest:995"] = {t="quest",n="Escape Through Stealth",z="darkshore",s="Escape Through Stealth is an Alliance escort quest set in Darkshore. After locating the trapped night elf scout Volcor deep within a furbolg den, the player helps guide him safely past hostile beasts to freedom before reporting back to Terenthis in Auberdine.",h="Escape Through Stealth is an Alliance escort quest set in Darkshore.",sec={{t="The Trapped Scout",b="Volcor, an operative sent into the depths of Darkshore to investigate the region's mounting threats, ended up cornered inside a furbolg cave. Outnumbered and cut off from the main roads, he relies on a passing ally to coordinate an exit before the hostile furbolgs realize he is slipping away.",sp=0},{t="A Careful Flight",b="Rather than attempting a suicidal frontal charge, Volcor chooses caution. Relying on shadows and deliberate maneuvering, he slips past the corrupted denizens of the cavern. Knowing that speed and quiet are paramount, Volcor separates from his rescuer once outside the mouth of the cave, racing ahead on foot while instructing his savior to meet him at the settlement of Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Auberdine",b="Upon returning to Auberdine, the player delivers news of the rescue to Terenthis, a night elf leader coordinating efforts to protect the troubled coastline. Terenthis views Volcor's safe return as proof that the encroaching darkness throughout Darkshore and the wilderness beyond can be resisted with discipline and teamwork.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout who ventured deep into Darkshore's wilderness on a mission for his superiors. He became trapped inside a hostile furbolg cavern until rescued by an Alliance adventurer.",al={"volcor lore","who is volcor","volcor darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Volcor run off alone once outside the cave?",a="Volcor notes that he can travel faster on his own once clear of the cavern's confined passages. He instructs the adventurer to reconvene in Auberdine rather than stick together along the open roads.",al={"why does volcor leave","volcor splits up"}},{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a prominent night elf coordinator stationed in Auberdine. He oversees local scouting efforts and organizes responses to the corruption and hostile denizens threatening Darkshore.",al={"terenthis auberdine","who is terenthis"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this rescue take place?",a="The rescue begins deep inside a furbolg cave located within the wilder, contested forests of Darkshore, far from the safety of Auberdine.",al={"volcor cave location","where is volcor cave"},it="place"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="After Volcor is safely accounted for and Terenthis is debriefed, players are directed toward the next stage of their journey south toward Ashenvale in the quest Trek to Ashenvale.",al={"what comes after escape through stealth","next quest after volcor"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the alternative to stealth in this rescue?",a="Volcor offers an alternative approach: instead of sneaking out through stealth, adventurers can choose to fight their way out through sheer force in a separate, combat-focused escort option.",al={"escape through force","volcor other quest","stealth vs force"},gp=true},{q="Why does Volcor want to escape through stealth?",a="Trapped deep within a hostile furbolg den, Volcor's primary concern is surviving long enough to return to Auberdine and report back to Terenthis. Slipping past the corrupted furbolgs without raising an alarm offers him the cleanest path out of the den without risking an overwhelming fight in tight quarters.",al={"why escape through stealth","volcor motive stealth","why sneak out with volcor"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, aiding Volcor reinforces the vital network of scouts watching over Kalimdor's troubled forests while corruption spreads outward from corrupted barrows and dens.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues appreciate Volcor's tactical instinct to bypass an entrenched enemy rather than waste time and blood in a reckless frontal brawl.",["faction:Alliance"]="Successfully securing Volcor's escape proves to the night elf leadership in Auberdine that non-kaldorei Alliance allies can be trusted with delicate wilderness operations."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","darkshore","escort","furbolg","stealth","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:990","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Volcor",["end"]="Terenthis",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=995},src={"Escape Through Stealth"}}
E["subzone:ameth-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Ameth'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Ameth'Aran is an ancient ruin in southern Darkshore, once a thriving city where Queen Azshara's Highborne practiced arcane sorcery. When the Great Sundering shattered the ancient world, the city fell with it. Today, its broken colonnades are haunted by the vengeful ghosts of the elves who died there.",h="Ameth'Aran is an ancient ruin in southern Darkshore, once a thriving city where Queen Azshara's Highborne...",sec={{t="A City of Sorcerers",b="Before the Great Sundering, Ameth'Aran and its sister settlement, Bashal'Aran, stood as twin centers of Highborne influence along the ancient coastline. Under the favor of Queen Azshara, the city boasted bustling bazaars and graceful shrines to Elune, though its ruling nobility dedicated themselves to unrestrained arcane experimentation. Governed from afar by the sorcerer Athrikus Narassin in the Tower of Althalaxx, the city thrived until the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity tore the Kaldorei Empire apart.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal and Eternal Torment",b="As the world began to tear itself apart, Athrikus Narassin returned to Ameth'Aran, promising his panicked subjects salvation through powerful shielding magic. Instead of shielding them, the sorcerer enacted a horrific betrayal, stealing their life force to feed his own soul gems under the cruel guise of giving them eternal preservation. Shattered by cataclysm and dark magic, Ameth'Aran fell. Today, its grounds are stalked by anguished Highborne specters, unable to find rest ten thousand years after their murder.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran was already in ruins in the final days of the Kaldorei Empire, and it was destroyed when the Well of Eternity was shattered in the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago. The ruins remain haunted by the spirits of the Highborne who died there.",al={"why is ametharan ruined","ameth aran history","fall of ametharan"},it="history"},{q="Who are the ghosts wandering the ruins?",a="They are the restless spirits of the Highborne elves who lived and practiced arcane magic in the city before the Great Sundering. Unable to find rest, they wander the broken stones in perpetual agony and fury.",al={"ghosts in ameth aran","ametharan specters","highborne ghosts darkshore"},it="residents"},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner was a resident of Ameth'Aran and the beloved of Cerellean Whiteclaw. She perished when the city fell during the Sundering, and her ghost remained bound to the ruins until Cerellean sought outside aid to finally grant her soul release.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","cerellean lover","ameth aran lost love"},sp=1},{q="What are the stone tablets found in the ruins?",a="The ruins contain ancient stone tablets inscribed with the history of Ameth'Aran and the account of its fall. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade attempted to decipher them to deliver a historical report to the Cenarion Circle, but hostile ghosts forced her to rely on passing travelers.",al={"ametharan tablets","runestones in ameth aran","fall of ametharan tablets"}},{q="What is Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran is an ancient ruined night elf settlement in southern Darkshore, situated southeast of Auberdine. Before the Sundering, it stood as a magnificent twin city alongside Bashal'Aran, where Queen Azshara's favored Highborne practiced their arcane craft amidst vibrant bazaars and grand temples.",al={"what is ametharan","about ameth'aran","ameth aran ruins"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is Ameth'Aran ruined?",a="The city met catastrophe ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients and the shattering of the Well of Eternity. As the world tore apart, its governor, Athrikus Narassin, claimed he would shield his people, but instead cast a spell that slew them to trap their souls, leaving the settlement shattered and cursed.",al={"why is ameth'aran destroyed","how was ameth'aran ruined","ameth aran fall"},sp=1,it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Ameth'Aran dangerous?",a="Yes. The ruins are haunted by restless Highborne ghosts who violently defend their former home against the living. Sentinel scouts like Tysha Moonblade have been driven out by their wrath, and any traveler seeking the ancient tablets must tread carefully among the spectral apparitions.",al={"is ameth aran safe","ameth'aran danger","threats in ameth aran"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Ameth'Aran is a grim monument to the hubris and treachery of the Highborne caste that brought about the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view the ruins as an unhealed scar upon Darkshore, where tormented spirits linger and disrupt the natural balance of the wilds."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","highborne","tysha moonblade"},rel={"quest:953","quest:963","quest:954","zone:darkshore","npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","topic:highborne"},src={"Ameth'Aran"}}
E["subzone:auberdine"] = {t="subzone",n="Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine is a coastal night elven port town on the gloomy shores of Darkshore, serving as the Alliance's primary maritime gateway to northern Kalimdor. Sheltered beneath overcast skies and pine-covered bluffs, it connects the island home of Teldrassil to the Eastern Kingdoms while serving as an administrative haven against the encroaching wilderness.",h="Auberdine is a coastal night elven port town on the gloomy shores of Darkshore, serving as the Alliance's...",sec={{t="Gateway to Northern Kalimdor",b="Resting along the shores of the Veiled Sea, Auberdine is the only major settlement to successfully endure in modern Darkshore. Unlike the secluded treetop cities of Teldrassil, Auberdine looks outward, serving as the Alliance's busiest port in the north. Regular ships sail between here and Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms, while local ferries run to Rut'theran Village at the boughs of the World Tree. Because of its trade role, Auberdine embraces a more cosmopolitan air than traditional elven enclaves; visitors find lamps illuminating stone-laid streets, bilingual signs in Darnassian and Common, and outland merchants including dwarves and gnomes mingling among the low-slung, arched timber houses.",sp=0},{t="A Beleaguered Haven",b="Governed by elder Thundris Windweaver and the Auberdine Village Council, the town coordinates the defence of Darkshore alongside the local Sentinels. Despite its role as a vital trade hub, highborn denizens of Darnassus often look askance at Auberdine, viewing its population of traders, fishermen, and outsiders as misfits. The town endures relentless regional perils: aggressive murlocs raid the fishing boats along the strand, corrupted Blackwood furbolgs press from the south, and foul magic seeping down from Felwood agitates the local wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the ships in Auberdine go?",a="The docks connect northern Kalimdor to the wider Alliance world. One pier hosts the ferry to Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil, while another berths large ocean-going vessels that sail across the Great Sea directly to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"auberdine boats","where do boats go","auberdine travel"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who rules Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is stewarded by elder Thundris Windweaver alongside the Auberdine Village Council. The settlement's defense is overseen by the Sentinels, led locally by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",al={"auberdine leader","who is in charge","village council"},it="leader"},{q="Why are there dwarves and humans living in a night elf town?",a="Because Auberdine serves as the Alliance's chief port on northern Kalimdor, foreign traders, craftsmen, and travelers arrive here first. Dwarves have set up a local smithy to service visiting ships and travellers, making the town unusually diverse and welcoming compared to traditional night elf settlements.",al={"non elves in auberdine","why dwarves here"},it="people"},{q="Why do night elves from Darnassus look down on Auberdine?",a="Traditionalists and isolationists in Darnassus often regard Auberdine as tainted by worldly commerce and outland influences. Some orthodox elves consider its people to be misfits, and the bustling trade hub is viewed as poorly suited to strictly traditional druidic lifestyles.",al={"darnassus auberdine rivalry","auberdine outcasts"},it="fame"},{q="What is Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is a tranquil coastal port settlement on the misty shores of Darkshore, serving as the primary gateway between northern Kalimdor and the wider Alliance. Built along the Veiled Sea, it features classic night elven wooden architecture, glowing streetlamps, and expansive docks. It welcomes travelers arriving by ship from Menethil Harbor or traveling by ferry to Teldrassil, offering shelter, trade, and fellowship amidst the shadowed wilderness.",al={"what is this town","tell me about auberdine","auberdine overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Auberdine?",a="Following the Great Sundering that shattered the ancient Kaldorei Empire and created Darkshore's coastline, numerous attempts to resettle the desolate region failed. Auberdine became the sole settlement to endure and thrive along these haunted shores. After the night elves aligned with the Grand Alliance, the quiet fishing community expanded its harbors to become the essential maritime nexus connecting the night elven homeland to the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"auberdine history","past of auberdine","what is auberdine's past"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Auberdine dangerous?",a="Within its perimeter, Auberdine remains secure thanks to vigilant night elven Sentinels stationed along the roads and docks. However, the surrounding wilderness is beset by mounting perils. Corrupted furbolgs lurk to the south, agitated wildlife roams the forests, and aggressive murlocs prowl the shallows, actively threatening local fishermen and coastal shipping lanes.",al={"is it safe here","threats to auberdine","is auberdine under attack"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For kaldorei venturing out from Teldrassil, Auberdine is the first true mainland hub where ancient tradition meets the strange ways and bustling industry of younger Alliance allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="This port is the lifeblood of Alliance travel and supply lines into northern Kalimdor, ensuring steady logistics between Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","docks","kaldorei","lighthouse","port","sentinels","thundris windweaver"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:4761","zone:darnassus","topic:sentinels","quest:4740","topic:alliance"},src={"Auberdine"}}
E["subzone:bashal-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Bashal'Aran is an ancient Highborne ruin situated in northern Darkshore, just east of Auberdine. Once a flourishing sister city to Ameth'Aran before the Great Sundering, the site now crawls with demonic satyrs and grells feeding on lingering arcane magic, while a solitary elven ghost remains trapped by a centuries-old curse.",h="Bashal'Aran is an ancient Highborne ruin situated in northern Darkshore, just east of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Shattered Twin City",b="Before the Great Sundering broke ancient Kalimdor ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne subjects in the twin towns of Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran. Governed by the powerful mage Athrikus Narassin, the cities boasted splendid markets and temples dedicated to Elune. When the Well of Eternity collapsed, the cataclysm laid both settlements to waste. For reasons lost to time, Athrikus used his arcane mastery to bind his own second-in-command, the mage Asterion, into a moonstone seal within Bashal'Aran. Even after his physical body perished, Asterion's ghost remained shackled to the ruined shrine.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Infestation",b="In the modern day, the crumbled stones of Bashal'Aran have been claimed by vile squatters: the Deth'ryll satyrs and mischievous grells. Drawn by residual magic clinging to the ancient masonry, these corrupted beings drink in the lingering energy to bolster their foul arts. Though they swarm the broken courtyards and terrorize travelers along Darkshore's forest paths, the demons give a wide berth to the central shrine where Asterion endures his endless vigil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Bashal'Aran before it was destroyed?",a="Bashal'Aran was a magnificent Kaldorei city established by Queen Azshara for favored Highborne aristocrats before the Great Sundering. Along with its twin city of Ameth'Aran, it was governed by the mage-lord Athrikus Narassin.",al={"bashal'aran history","who built bashal'aran","what was this ruin"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is the ghost wandering the shrine?",a="The spirit is Asterion, a respected Highborne warrior-mage who once oversaw both Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran. He was mysteriously betrayed and bound to the site with a moonstone seal by his governor, Athrikus Narassin, enduring imprisonment even beyond mortal death.",al={"who is asterion","bashal'aran ghost","why is there a ghost"},it="residents"},{q="Why are satyrs inhabiting the ruins?",a="Satyrs and grells were lured to Bashal'Aran by the remnants of powerful arcane energy left behind by the ancient Highborne. They feast on these lingering magical emanations to empower their dark demonic magic.",al={"why are there satyrs here","deth'ryll satyr lore","grells at bashal'aran"},it="threat"},{q="How does Bashal'Aran relate to Ameth'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister cities governed together under Queen Azshara's reign. Asterion made frequent journeys between both settlements to tend to the people's needs before both were shattered by the Sundering.",al={"ameth'aran connection","twin cities darkshore","ameth'aran bashal'aran"},it="ties"},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient night elven ruin situated in northern Darkshore. Long ago, before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor, it was a prosperous Highborne city adorned with bustling bazaars and grand temples dedicated to Elune. Alongside its twin city Ameth'Aran to the south, it stood as a testament to the heights of early night elven civilization. Today, it lies broken and haunted, choked by wild overgrowth and lingering arcane remnants.",al={"what is bashal'aran","bashal'aran overview","about bashal'aran"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to Bashal'Aran?",a="In the days of the Kaldorei Empire, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne here under the governorship of Athrikus Narassin and his lieutenant Asterion. When the first Well of Eternity imploded during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, the city was utterly ruined. During its collapse, Athrikus used a moonstone seal to magically bind Asterion to a shrine. While Asterion perished, his spectral form remained eternally trapped among the ruins long after his people vanished.",al={"history of bashal'aran","bashal'aran lore","what happened at bashal'aran"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Bashal'Aran dangerous?",a="Yes. The shattered stonework is overrun by hostile grells and vile Deth'ryll satyrs. These demonic creatures are drawn to the potent arcane energies still seeping from the ancient Highborne stones, feeding on the remnants to fuel and swell their own dark magic. While they fear and avoid the sanctified shrine where the ghost Asterion lingers, any traveler venturing into the surrounding ruins will be attacked on sight.",al={"is bashal'aran safe","danger in bashal'aran","enemies in bashal'aran"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Bashal'Aran serves as a tragic reminder of the reckless arcane hubris that doomed the ancient Kaldorei Empire and paved the way for demonic corruption.",["class:Mage"]="The moonstone ward binding Asterion showcases the terrifying permanence and potency of pre-Sundering Highborne spellcraft."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","darkshore","deth'ryll","grell","highborne","satyr"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","npc:asterion","quest:954","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","topic:elune","topic:alliance"},src={"Bashal'Aran"}}
E["subzone:blackwood-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwood Den",z="darkshore",s="Blackwood Den is a corrupted furbolg encampment nestled in the southern reaches of Darkshore near the border of Ashenvale. Once a peaceful dwelling, the cave and surrounding camps have fallen into madness alongside the rest of the Blackwood tribe. A lone night elf scout named Volcor sits trapped within the cavern, awaiting aid from Auberdine.",h="Blackwood Den is a corrupted furbolg encampment nestled in the southern reaches of Darkshore near the border...",sec={{t="A Corrupted Stronghold",b="Situated near the southern border where Darkshore meets Ashenvale, Blackwood Den consists of a winding network of crude camps and a rocky cave. The Blackwood furbolgs who dwell here have succumbed to the pervasive corruption gripping the region, turning violently hostile toward outsiders. Deep inside the den's cave, the night elf Volcor remains pinned down and endangered by the aggressive tribe, desperately needing assistance from scouts and travelers dispatched from Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Blackwood Den?",a="Blackwood Den is a furbolg settlement and cave complex located in far southern Darkshore, close to the border of Ashenvale. It serves as a base for the corrupted Blackwood furbolg tribe.",al={"what is blackwood den","blackwood hold","where is blackwood den"},it="place"},{q="Who is inside the cave at Blackwood Den?",a="Inside the cave sits Volcor, a night elf who has become trapped behind enemy lines. Travelers who encounter him must coordinate with allies in Auberdine to stage an escape and guide him safely out of the den.",al={"who is trapped in the cave","who is volcor","elf in blackwood den"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="The Blackwood furbolgs have fallen victim to the dark corruption spreading across Darkshore and Kalimdor following the Third War. The affliction has driven them into a maddened frenzy, causing them to attack any outsiders on sight.",al={"why are blackwood furbolgs aggressive","are blackwood furbolgs evil","corrupted furbolgs darkshore"},it="hostile"},{q="What happened at Blackwood Den?",a="Blackwood Den was once a regular settlement of the Blackwood furbolg tribe in southern Darkshore. However, along with much of the local wildlife and indigenous tribes, the furbolgs here fell victim to a dark corruption spreading through the land. Twisted from their formerly peaceful ways, they turned fiercely aggressive, establishing fortified camps and trapping outsiders who dared to tread near their hollows.",al={"blackwood den history","what happened at blackwood den","blackwood den story"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in Blackwood Den?",a="The den and its surrounding camps are held by the corrupted Blackwood furbolgs, who aggressively guard their territory against any intruders. Deep inside the cave, an unfortunate night elf named Volcor has found himself trapped, cornered by the hostile furbolgs and awaiting rescue from anyone brave enough to fight through the den.",al={"who lives in blackwood den","blackwood den inhabitants","who holds blackwood den"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Blackwood Den dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very perilous. The Blackwood furbolgs inhabit several clustered camps right outside the cave entrance and throughout the den itself. Corrupted and violent, they attack any outsiders on sight in packs, making any attempt to venture inside—especially to reach the trapped night elf Volcor—a deadly undertaking without careful preparation.",al={"is blackwood den dangerous","blackwood den dangers","how dangerous is blackwood den"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Blackwood Den?",a="The den takes its name from the Blackwood furbolg tribe that makes its home here. Nestled in the southern reaches of Darkshore near the border with Ashenvale, the cave and surrounding camps serve as the central hollow and sanctuary for this corrupted clan.",al={"why is it called blackwood den","blackwood den name meaning","where does blackwood den get its name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, the loss of the Blackwood tribe to corruption is a tragic development, and rescuing Volcor from their clutches is an urgent duty to keep their people safe along the southern road.",["class:Druid"]="Druids mourn the fall of the furbolgs, who were once steadfast protectors of the wilderness, and view the madness at Blackwood Den as another painful symptom of Kalimdor's tainted nature."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackwood den","blackwood hold","darkshore","furbolg","volcor"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:auberdine","npc:volcor","topic:furbolg","topic:night-elf"},src={"Blackwood Den"}}
E["subzone:cliffspring-falls"] = {t="subzone",n="Cliffspring Falls",z="darkshore",s="Cliffspring Falls marks the dramatic origin of Darkshore's vital Cliffspring River, tumbling down from the eastern cliffs into the coastal forest. Long celebrated as the principal source of clean drinking water for the region, its waters have recently fallen victim to a foul, spreading taint. The subterranean cavern feeding the waterfall has become infested with hostile naga and shadowy Twilight's Hammer cultists.",h="Cliffspring Falls marks the dramatic origin of Darkshore's vital Cliffspring River, tumbling down from the...",sec={{t="A Tainted Source",b="Pouring out from caverns perched high in the rocky bluffs along Darkshore's eastern border, Cliffspring Falls feeds the Cliffspring River, which winds westward across the woods to empty into the sea. Traditionally, this cascade provided the purest drinking water for local night elf settlements. In recent times, however, the waters have turned foul and murky, spreading sickness and ecological decay throughout the river basin. Investigating naturalists have discovered that the cave network at the falls' headwaters is overrun by vile naga and dark cultists, who plot in the shadows while demonic corruption from neighboring Felwood threatens to seep through the highland bedrock.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Cliffspring Falls?",a="Cliffspring Falls is a major waterfall in eastern Darkshore that forms the headwaters of the Cliffspring River. It historically supplied the primary fresh drinking water for the surrounding forest.",al={"cliffspring falls","cliffwater falls","what is cliffspring falls"},it="place"},{q="Why is the water coming from the falls corrupted?",a="Two sinister influences are suspected: demonic taint seeping through the mountains from corrupted Felwood, and the active presence of Twilight's Hammer cultists and hostile naga lurking inside the caverns feeding the cascade.",al={"why is water tainted","cliffspring river corruption","corrupted water"}},{q="Who occupies the caverns behind the falls?",a="The caverns above and behind the waterfall are infested with hostile naga slithering through the flooded chambers, alongside cultists belonging to the apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer.",al={"who is in the caves","cliffspring cave mobs","who lives in cliffspring falls"},it="residents"},{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?",a="The Cliffspring River cuts through the center of northern Darkshore. Because it serves as the principal source of fresh water, its poisoning directly endangers wildlife, ancient groves, and local night elf habitations.",al={"why does darkshore care","cliffspring importance"},it="power"},{q="What happened to Cliffspring Falls?",a="Cliffspring Falls was once a pristine mountain cascade providing clean drinking water across northern Darkshore. Following the devastation of the Third War, dark powers crept into the surrounding wilds. Corruption took hold of the cavern at the river's headwaters, turning the pure mountain flow foul and attracting malevolent entities to its hidden depths.",al={"cliffspring falls history","what happened at cliffspring falls","why did cliffspring falls change"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Cliffspring Falls dangerous?",a="The falls and the caverns behind them are extremely hazardous. Hostile naga crawl through the waterways, while fanatical Twilight's Hammer cultists lurk deep inside the cave network conducting foul rituals. Beyond the deadly inhabitants, the tainted water itself poses a grave hazard to anyone who dares drink from it.",al={"cliffspring falls danger","is cliffspring falls safe","threats at cliffspring falls"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the corruption of Cliffspring Falls is an environmental and spiritual crisis, polluting the vital waters that nourish Darkshore's ancient forests.",["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle monitor the river closely, striving to diagnose and cleanse the unnatural rot that threatens to choke the wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring falls","cliffspring river","cliffwater falls","darkshore","felwood","naga","twilight's hammer","water corruption"},rel={"quest:6122","quest:4762","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","zone:felwood","topic:alliance"},src={"Cliffspring Falls"}}
E["subzone:grove-of-the-ancients"] = {t="subzone",n="Grove of the Ancients",z="darkshore",s="The Grove of the Ancients is a sacred night elven sanctuary set amidst old temple ruins in southeastern Darkshore. Nestled beside the Wildbend River, this serene haven serves as a gathering ground for nature spirits and is watched over by the venerable Ancient of Lore, Onu.",h="The Grove of the Ancients is a sacred night elven sanctuary set amidst old temple ruins in southeastern...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Wildbend",b="Tucked away near the southeastern mountains of Darkshore, the Grove of the Ancients stands as a peaceful haven surrounded by aged temple stones. Through its heart flows the surging Wildbend River, providing a quiet refuge amidst a coastline increasingly plagued by corruption and restless wildlife. The grove serves as a meeting place for the Circle of Ancients, where nature spirits and kaldorei tend to the delicate balance of the forest.",sp=0},{t="Keepers and Watchers",b="The focal presence within the grove is Onu, a towering Ancient of Lore who observes the land's shifting fortunes and offers ancient wisdom to passing travelers. Alongside Onu, wandering merchants and slumbering druids find rest beneath the boughs. Though quiet, the grove lies close to territorial furbolg camps to the southeast, making it an essential frontier outpost for Alliance sentinels and druids monitoring southern Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The grove is located in the southeastern region of Darkshore, nestled against the mountain foothills near the banks of the Wildbend River.",al={"grove of ancients location","where is grove of the ancients","onu location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is a wise Ancient of Lore residing in the grove. He acts as an elder guide, watching over the southeastern woods and advising druids and travelers attempting to mend the balance of Darkshore.",al={"who is onu","ancient in grove of ancients","tree guy darkshore"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Circle of Ancients?",a="The Circle of Ancients is an assembly of great nature spirits and ancient treants who gather at the grove to commune, share knowledge, and discuss the welfare of the wild lands.",al={"circle of ancients","ancients meeting darkshore"}},{q="Are there dangers near the grove?",a="While the grove itself is a safe sanctuary with friendly guardians and merchants, hostile wildlife and territorial furbolg encampments lie just across the river and to the southeast.",al={"grove threats","is grove safe","monsters near grove"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The Grove of the Ancients is a sacred night elven ruin situated along the Wildbend River in southeastern Darkshore. Built around the crumbling remnants of an ancient temple, it serves as a secluded sanctuary where the Circle of Ancients gathers, watched over by revered tree guardians and slumbering keepers of nature.",al={"grove of the ancients","what is grove of ancients","about grove of the ancients"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is the Grove of the Ancients called that?",a="The sanctuary takes its name from both the massive, sentient Ancients who reside here and the ancient night elven legacy embedded in its soil. As a meeting ground for the Circle of Ancients and home to the venerable Ancient of Lore, Onu, it stands as an enduring monument to the primeval guardians of the forest.",al={"why grove of ancients","how did it get its name","grove of ancients name meaning"},it="name",add=true},{q="Why is the Grove of the Ancients in ruins?",a="The stone structures scattered across the grove are the remains of an ancient night elven temple that fell into decay over millennia. While the architecture has long surrendered to the elements and encroaching woodland, the land remains deeply sacred and actively tended by nature spirits rather than rebuilt in stone.",al={"why is grove of the ancients ruined","grove of ancients temple ruins","who destroyed the grove"},it="ruin",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The grove is a revered natural sanctuary, offering druids a direct connection to the wisdom of the Ancient of Lore Onu and the spirits of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="Surrounded by ancient temple ruins and tended by nature spirits, the grove serves as a solemn reminder of long-standing kaldorei harmony with the land."},kw={"ancient of lore","circle of ancients","darkshore","grove of the ancients","onu","wildbend river"},rel={"quest:952","zone:darkshore","subzone:wildbend-river","topic:druid","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg"},src={"Grove of the Ancients"}}
E["subzone:long-wash"] = {t="subzone",n="Long Wash",z="darkshore",s="The Long Wash is a bleak, windswept stretch of beach in Darkshore running just south of Auberdine toward the ruins of Ameth'Aran. Gloomy and scattered with marine carcasses and flotsam, the shoreline has recently grown dangerous due to an increasing presence of hostile murlocs.",h="The Long Wash is a bleak, windswept stretch of beach in Darkshore running just south of Auberdine toward the...",sec={{t="A Gloomy Shoreline",b="Despite its name, the Long Wash is actually the shortest distinct stretch of coastline in Darkshore. It sits under the region's perpetual overcast skies, an expanse of damp sand littered with flotsam, beached driftwood, and the carcasses of sea creatures washed up by the Veiled Sea. While local crabs and snails comb through the surf, travelers southward from Auberdine must tread cautiously: murloc tribes have established camps along the water's edge, aggressively attacking anyone encroaching on their scavenged territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Long Wash located?",a="The Long Wash stretches along the coastline of Darkshore immediately south of Auberdine, extending down until it lies roughly west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran.",al={"long wash location","where is long wash","how to find long wash"},it="place"},{q="Why is it called the Long Wash?",a="A 'wash' is an archaic term referring to the portion of a shore swept and washed over by ocean waves. Ironically, despite being named the Long Wash, it is actually the shortest distinct stretch of beach in Darkshore.",al={"why long wash","long wash meaning","what does wash mean"},it="name"},{q="What threats can be found along the Long Wash?",a="The main danger along the Long Wash comes from aggressive murloc clans that have begun gathering in greater numbers along the coastline, alongside territorial tide crawlers and other beach wildlife.",al={"dangers in long wash","long wash mobs","what lives in long wash"},it="danger"},{q="Why are there so many dead creatures on the beach?",a="The rough surf of the Veiled Sea and the encroaching corruption affecting the coastal waters of Darkshore regularly wash up debris, ship drift, and dying marine life onto the damp sands of the shore.",al={"dead animals long wash","beached creatures darkshore beach","flotsam on the shore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the encroaching murlocs along the Long Wash represent another sign of unsettling imbalance creeping right up to the doorstep of their main port."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","long wash","murloc","tide crawler","veiled sea"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:murloc"},src={"Long Wash"}}
E["subzone:master-s-glaive"] = {t="subzone",n="Master's Glaive",z="darkshore",s="The Master's Glaive is an ancient, unsettling landmark tucked into southwestern Darkshore where a colossal adamantine weapon stands impaled in a massive petrified skull. Long revered by local night elves as a sacred mystery, the site now swarms with Twilight's Hammer cultists drawn to the lingering malevolence of an ancient entity.",h="The Master's Glaive is an ancient, unsettling landmark tucked into southwestern Darkshore where a colossal...",sec={{t="A Monument of an Ancient Clash",b="Rising out of the Darkshore earth, the Master's Glaive is a massive adamantine blade buried deep in a colossal petrified skull. No record names the creature that died here or the hand that drove the blade home. Onu, the Ancient of Lore, says only that an old, old lord of the earth fell on this spot, and the night elves long believed that only the titans could have wielded so gigantic a weapon. Today, the impaled monolith stands as a stark, petrified monument to that forgotten struggle.",sp=0},{t="Dark Excavations",b="Though the site was held in solemn reverence by night elves for generations, sinister forces have recently seized the grounds. Fanatics of the Twilight's Hammer cult have established a camp around the sunken carcass, carving out trenches and uncovering petrified ribs. Drawn by whispers beneath the stone, the cultists obsessively study the remains and commune with the malevolent power that still clings to the ancient remains, seeking to revive or harness whatever fell essence slumbers within the earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the massive weapon stuck in the skull?",a="No one knows for certain. The colossal adamantine blade is the Master's Glaive itself, driven into the skull in some forgotten age. The night elves believed that only the titans could have wielded a weapon of such size.",al={"what is the sword","masters glaive sword","who put the sword there"},it="item"},{q="What creature's skull is buried here?",a="Its name is lost. Onu, the Ancient of Lore, says only that an old, old lord of the earth fell here, and the Twilight's Hammer believe the petrified remains belong to a servant of the Old Gods.",al={"what died here","who is buried at masters glaive"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult gathered here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult worships the Old Gods. They have overrun the Master's Glaive to excavate the petrified remains, drawn by the lingering dark power and hoping to restore the fallen creature to life.",al={"why are cultists here","twilight hammer darkshore","what are cultists digging"},it="motive"},{q="Who knows about the history of this site?",a="Onu, the Ancient of Lore residing in Darkshore, recognizes the site as the resting place of an ancient lord of the earth and bids investigators to look into it.",al={"who studies the glaive"}},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="The Master's Glaive is an ancient, monumental site nestled in southwestern Darkshore. The landmark is dominated by a colossal petrified skull, impaled through the crown by an immense adamantine blade. What was once treated as a reverent holy site by the night elves is now a sinister excavation shrouded in dark worship.",al={"what is masters glaive","masters glaive darkshore","what is this place"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at the Master's Glaive?",a="No record tells the full story. Onu, the Ancient of Lore, says only that an old, old lord of the earth fell here, slain by a blade so vast that the night elves believed only the titans could have wielded it. Its petrified skull still lies where it fell, the glaive buried in its crown.",al={"masters glaive history","what battle happened here","soggoth history"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who controls the Master's Glaive?",a="The site has fallen under the sway of the Twilight's Hammer cult. Fanatical cultists swarming the basin conduct excavations around the petrified remains, driven by mad prophecies to unearth and awaken the fallen creature.",al={"who lives at masters glaive","who is at masters glaive","masters glaive cultists"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Master's Glaive dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Zealous Twilight's Hammer cultists actively guard the excavations and will attack any intruders on sight. Beyond the fanatic mortals, the lingering malevolence radiating from the dormant remains makes the basin a perilous place for the unwary.",al={"is masters glaive dangerous","is it safe here","masters glaive threat"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Master's Glaive?",a="The location is named for the colossal weapon embedded in the earth. The massive blade, driven into the skull of a long-fallen creature in some forgotten age, came to be remembered in legends as the Master's Glaive.",al={"why is it called masters glaive","masters glaive name origin","where does the name come from"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For generations, night elves treated the strange petrified monument as a solemn holy place, making the recent intrusion of the Twilight's Hammer cult an intolerable defilement of Darkshore's sacred grounds."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","old god","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:titan","topic:night-elf"},src={"Master's Glaive"}}
E["subzone:mist-s-edge"] = {t="subzone",n="Mist's Edge",z="darkshore",s="Mist's Edge is the long, windswept coastline spanning the western border of Darkshore. Shrouded in damp ocean fog, these gray beaches are littered with shipwrecks, colossal sea creature remains, and roving packs of crabs and murlocs.",h="Mist's Edge is the long, windswept coastline spanning the western border of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Shore",b="Running along the western edge of Darkshore, Mist's Edge is defined by damp sands, rocky tidepools, and perpetual coastal fog. The beach is a graveyard of the sea, littered with decaying sea behemoths, drift timber, and the shattered ribs of wrecked vessels. While seemingly barren, the coastline teems with shoreline scavengers, notably aggressive crabs and territorial murloc tribes that nest in the surf.",sp=0},{t="Wrecks and Scavengers",b="The treacherous waters off the coast of Darkshore have claimed countless vessels, depositing shattered hulls and discarded cargo all along the sands. Night elf sentinels and local scavengers keep a wary eye on the coastline, where opportunistic murloc encampments frequently menace travelers heading up and down the coast from Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mist's Edge?",a="Mist's Edge is the expansive stretch of coastline that forms the entire western shore of Darkshore, known for its cold ocean fog, shipwrecks, and beached sea creatures.",al={"mists edge","darkshore beach","what is mists edge"},it="place"},{q="What threats wander this coast?",a="The shoreline is heavily populated by hostile coastal crabs and aggressive murloc packs that dwell in primitive camps along the water's edge.",al={"mists edge monsters","what attacks you on the beach","darkshore coast dangers"},it="threat"},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks and skeletons here?",a="The harsh currents, hidden reefs, and heavy mist off Darkshore make navigation hazardous, driving ships onto the rocks. Similarly, ocean currents often wash the remains of massive leviathans and sea creatures ashore.",al={"darkshore beached whales","shipwrecks mists edge","giant bones darkshore"},it="history"},{q="Is Mist's Edge dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers must stay vigilant along these bleak sands. The shore is crawling with aggressive coastal crabs, while aggressive tribes of murlocs build camps along the water and attack anyone trespassing near their fishing grounds. Between the prowling scavengers feeding on beached sea carcasses and the lurking murlocs, wandering the coast alone poses a constant threat.",al={"is mists edge safe","danger mists edge","how dangerous is mists edge"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, Mist's Edge represents both a vital maritime boundary and an untamed border plagued by invading murlocs and foul scavengers."},kw={"auberdine","beach","coast","crabs","darkshore","mist's edge","murloc","shipwreck"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc"},src={"Mist's Edge"}}
E["subzone:moonspray"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonspray",z="darkshore",s="The Moonspray is an Alliance transport vessel belonging to the Kaldorei Fleet. It provides essential maritime passage across the waters separating mainland Kalimdor from the great World Tree, Teldrassil.",h="The Moonspray is an Alliance transport vessel belonging to the Kaldorei Fleet.",sec={{t="A Vital Island Ferry",b="Graceful in design like all night elven ships, the Moonspray serves as an indispensable lifeline between the docks of Auberdine on Darkshore's coast and Rut'theran Village at the root of Teldrassil. Traversing the Veiled Sea, the transport carries adventurers, couriers, and vital provisions between the isolated night elf sanctuary in the crown of the World Tree and the ancient mainland of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Moonspray travel?",a="The Moonspray sails between the harbor town of Auberdine in Darkshore and Rut'theran Village, which sits at the oceanic base of Teldrassil.",al={"moonspray route","where does moonspray go","moonspray destination"},it="place"},{q="Who owns and operates this ship?",a="The Moonspray is a night elven vessel operating as part of the Kaldorei Fleet, sailing under the banner of the Alliance.",al={"who sails the moonspray","kaldorei fleet moonspray","is moonspray alliance"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is this ferry route important?",a="Teldrassil is an island perched high in the sea off the northwestern coast of Kalimdor. Ships like the Moonspray are the primary means of transferring troops, provisions, and travelers across the water to the mainland.",al={"why take moonspray","teldrassil boat"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Moonspray?",a="The Moonspray is a graceful night elven transport vessel belonging to the Kaldorei Fleet. It plies the waters between the docks of Auberdine on the Darkshore coast and Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil, serving as a vital naval ferry that connects the great world tree to the Kalimdor mainland.",al={"what is moonspray","moonspray ship","moonspray darkshore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What is the history of the Moonspray?",a="Constructed as part of the night elves' naval transport fleet, the Moonspray was chartered to bridge the gap across the sea after the growth of Teldrassil. Since the establishment of Auberdine and Rut'theran Village, it has steadily carried travelers, supplies, and messengers back and forth to keep the secluded capital connected to the shores of Kalimdor.",al={"moonspray history","what happened to moonspray","history of the moonspray"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Moonspray dangerous?",a="Not for travelers of the Alliance. The Moonspray is a peaceful civilian and supply ferry operated safely by night elf mariners. However, any members of the Horde attempting to board will find themselves in hostile territory, facing swift retaliation from both the crew and the night elf guards stationed at the harbor docks.",al={"is moonspray dangerous","moonspray danger","threats on moonspray"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil to explore the wider world, the Moonspray is often the very vessel that carries them from their secluded home to the mainland for the first time.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Moonspray forms a key transport link connecting the Alliance's primary coastal hub in northern Kalimdor with the isolated capital of Darnassus."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","ferry","kaldorei fleet","moonspray","rut'theran village","teldrassil","transport"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","subzone:rut-theran-village","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},src={"Moonspray"}}
E["subzone:remtravel-s-excavation"] = {t="subzone",n="Remtravel's Excavation",z="darkshore",s="Remtravel's Excavation is an archaeological dig site located in the southern reaches of Darkshore. Established by the dwarven Prospector Remtravel, the expedition recently struck ancient subterranean ruins, inadvertently unearthing hostile troggs and stone golems that quickly overran the quarry.",h="Remtravel's Excavation is an archaeological dig site located in the southern reaches of Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Quarry Overrun",b="Prospector Remtravel came to Darkshore in search of relics of the distant past, establishing an ambitious dig far from the safety of Auberdine. While excavating ancient strata, his team unearthed a swarm of subterranean Gravelflint troggs alongside hulking stone golems buried beneath the earth. The site was instantly transformed from a scholarly quarry into a hazard zone, scattering the miners and leaving Remtravel scrambling to retrieve his most promising findings.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Fossil",b="Before the excavation descended into chaos, Remtravel had uncovered a rare fossil radiating curious mystic properties. In the panic of the trogg onslaught—and hindered by his notorious absent-mindedness—the prospector misplaced the valuable relic amid the sprawling dirt pits. Venturing down into the dig to recover it means braving both the vicious troggs and the ancient automatons awakened by the pickaxes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Remtravel's Excavation?",a="It is an archaeological dig site in southern Darkshore founded by Prospector Remtravel, an explorer searching for ancient fossils and subterranean relics.",al={"what is this place","darkshore dig site","remtravel site"},it="place"},{q="Why are there troggs here?",a="Dwarven miners dug too deeply into the earth and breached subterranean caverns, awakening a local tribe known as the Gravelflint troggs alongside dormant stone golems.",al={"why troggs in darkshore","gravelflint troggs","where did troggs come from"},it="hostile"},{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="He is a dwarven archaeologist leading the excavation. Known for his keen eye for artifacts as well as his absent-minded nature, he lost track of a key fossil when his dig was attacked.",al={"who is remtravel","prospector remtravel lore"},it="leader"},{q="What kind of relic was discovered here?",a="Remtravel discovered an unusual fossil imbued with strange, mystic properties shortly before the troggs surged from the lower depths.",al={"what did they find","remtravel fossil","mystic fossil"},it="item"},{q="What happened at Remtravel's Excavation?",a="Prospector Remtravel established this archaeological dig in Darkshore and unearthed an unusual fossil possessed of mystic properties. However, his delving broke into subterranean chambers, awakening hostile Gravelflint troggs and massive ancient golems. Overwhelmed by these emerging creatures, the expedition lost control of the site, and the absent-minded dwarf misplaced his prized relic amidst the chaos.",al={"remtravels excavation history","what happened at the dig site","history of remtravel excavation"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who runs Remtravel's Excavation?",a="The excavation was established and led by the renowned dwarven archaeologist Prospector Remtravel. In his absence, however, no peaceful workers remain on site. Hostile Gravelflint troggs and animated stone golems have overrun the trenches, driving out the researchers and seizing control of the diggings.",al={"who controls remtravel excavation","who lives in remtravel excavation","remtravel excavation inhabitants"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Why was Remtravel's Excavation abandoned?",a="The expedition had to abandon active work when their digging broke open buried caverns, unleashing a swarm of aggressive Gravelflint troggs alongside unearthed stone golems. The diggers could not hold the grounds against such brute strength, forcing them to flee and leave their equipment behind.",al={"why is remtravel excavation abandoned","why did remtravel leave the dig site","what ruined remtravels excavation"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Remtravel's Excavation dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for anyone without proper combat training. The open pits and trenches are teeming with feral Gravelflint troggs and colossal, unearthed golems that attack any intruders on sight.",al={"how dangerous is remtravels excavation","is it safe at remtravel excavation","dangers of remtravel excavation"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Remtravel's Excavation?",a="The dig site takes its name from Prospector Remtravel, the famed dwarven archaeologist who spearheaded the operation in Darkshore to uncover ancient relics.",al={"remtravel excavation name origin","why is it named remtravel","who named remtravels excavation"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven explorers of the Explorers' League are well known for seeking the secrets of the past, though unearthing dangerous troggs in foreign lands often leads to familiar headaches.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei generally observe the deep meddling of Alliance dwarven picks with skepticism, especially when careless delving awakens wild troggs on Darkshore's ancient soil."},kw={"darkshore","excavation","fossil","golem","gravelflint","prospector","remtravel","trogg"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","zone:darkshore","topic:trogg"},src={"Remtravel's Excavation"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-auberdine"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine is the bustling coastal port town of Darkshore, serving as the primary maritime link between Kalimdor's northern forests and the outside world. The settlement stands whole and vital under the stewardship of the night elves.",h="Auberdine is the bustling coastal port town of Darkshore, serving as the primary maritime link between...",sec={{t="The Northern Haven",b="In Darkshore, Auberdine stands as the central haven for travelers, druids, and sentinels safeguarding northern Kalimdor. Its docks provide steady passage across the waters to Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil and south to the wetlands of the Eastern Kingdoms. The town's moonwell provides spiritual solace to all who venerate Elune, and its craftsmen supply travelers braving the haunted shoreline.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of Ruin",b="Auberdine stands proud against the misty gloom of Darkshore, its towers intact, its docks alive with cargo, and its community resolute.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Is Auberdine in ruins?",a="No. Auberdine is completely intact and serves as the primary quest hub and harbor for the Alliance along the coast of Darkshore.",al={"auberdine ruined","ruins of auberdine classic","destroyed auberdine"},it="ruin"},{q="What services are available in Auberdine?",a="The town features an inn, hippogryph roost, blacksmithing forge, profession trainers, and a moonwell. Ferries run regularly from its long wooden piers.",al={"auberdine vendors","auberdine trainers","what is in auberdine"},gp=true},{q="Where do the ships in Auberdine sail?",a="Vessels dock here carrying passengers to and from Rut'theran Village beneath Teldrassil, as well as Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"auberdine boat","auberdine docks destination","where does auberdine boat go"},gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine is the first major mainland settlement welcoming young night elves after they leave the boughs of Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine acts as the vital strategic bridgehead connecting Alliance territories across the seas to northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","docks","ferry","kaldorei","moonwell","port"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Auberdine"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-mathystra"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Mathystra",z="darkshore",s="The Ruins of Mathystra are the crumbled remnants of an ancient night elven city sitting along the northern coast of Darkshore. Shattered during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, the coastal ruins are now overrun by hostile Stormscale naga and prowled by elusive Ghost Sabers.",h="The Ruins of Mathystra are the crumbled remnants of an ancient night elven city sitting along the northern...",sec={{t="A City Cast into the Sea",b="Ten millennia ago, Mathystra stood as a bustling night elven settlement, home to high-ranking Highborne nobility. When the Well of Eternity collapsed during the Great Sundering, cataclysmic waves shattered the coastal city, toppling its grand marble arches and washing much of its stonework into the sea. The surviving night elves abandoned the ruined city in favor of smaller woodland villages further south, leaving Mathystra's sunken courtyards and cracked foundations to the relentless coastal elements.",sp=0},{t="The Stormscale Vipers and Ghost Sabers",b="In the modern era, Mathystra has become a dangerous domain ruled by the Stormscale naga. Creeping up from the dark depths, these serpentine abominations guard the broken halls fiercely, driving away any travelers who venture north past the Tower of Althalaxx. Among the shattered flagstones, ancient Highborne relics still lie half-buried in sand and seafoam. Daring young night elves sometimes brave the naga vipers hoping to recover remnants of their lost heritage, often contending not only with serpent blades but also with the spectral Ghost Sabers that stalk the broken streets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What used to be here before the ruins?",a="Mathystra was a thriving night elven city built during the height of the ancient Highborne empire. It was shattered and largely drowned ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering, when the Well of Eternity exploded and cleaved Kalimdor apart.",al={"mathystra history","who built mathystra","what was mathystra"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Ruins of Mathystra right now?",a="The ruins are currently occupied by the Stormscale naga, who have emerged from the sea to claim the sunken pavilions and coastlines. They aggressively attack any land-dwellers who intrude upon their territory.",al={"who lives in mathystra","mathystra mobs","who is at mathystra"},it="residents"},{q="What are Ghost Sabers?",a="Ghost Sabers are ethereal, translucent felines that haunt the ruined stonework of Mathystra. Hunters often seek them out along the coast, though disturbing the ancient figurines in the area is known to draw these spirits out from the shadows.",al={"ghost saber mathystra","glowing cat darkshore","ghost sabers"}},{q="Why do night elves visit these ruins today?",a="Young night elves and scholars occasionally venture into the ruins to recover ancient Highborne relics left behind after the Sundering. However, the presence of fierce Stormscale naga makes recovering these historical treasures extremely perilous.",al={"mathystra relics","why go to mathystra"}},{q="What are the Ruins of Mathystra?",a="The Ruins of Mathystra are the crumbled remnants of an ancient night elven city, resting along the northern coast of Darkshore just beyond the Tower of Althalaxx. Once a magnificent center of Highborne civilization, all that remains today are weathered stone foundations, shattered pillars, and long-buried relics swallowed by the wilderness.",al={"what is mathystra","ruins of mathystra lore","about ruins of mathystra"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why was Mathystra ruined and abandoned?",a="Mathystra was devastated ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering, when the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity tore ancient Kalimdor apart. The city was decimated by the cataclysm, and surviving night elves chose to abandon the shattered ruins entirely, settling instead in coastal havens further south.",al={"why is mathystra ruined","what destroyed mathystra","how was mathystra destroyed"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Are the Ruins of Mathystra dangerous?",a="Yes, you should tread carefully among the stones. The ruins are fiercely held by the Stormscale naga, who violently defend their claiming of the coast against any outsiders. In addition to these serpent trespassers, ethereal Ghost Sabers and remnants of ancient Highborne magic linger across the rubble.",al={"is mathystra safe","threats in mathystra","ruins of mathystra danger"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Mathystra stands as a somber monument to the hubris of the ancient Highborne, whose reckless sorcery brought cataclysm down upon their own grand coastal settlements.",["class:Hunter"]="The translucent Ghost Sabers prowling among the rubble of Mathystra are renowned beasts for beastmasters seeking a striking companion with ties to the spirit world."},kw={"darkshore","ghost saber","great sundering","highborne","mathystra","naga","ruins of mathystra","stormscale"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","topic:naga","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Mathystra"}}
E["subzone:shatterspear-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Shatterspear Vale",z="darkshore",s="Shatterspear Vale is a hidden valley tucked deep in the jagged mountains between Darkshore, Moonglade, and Felwood. It houses an isolated village of the Shatterspear troll tribe, living quietly around a secluded mountain lake. Largely sealed off from the wider world by sheer cliffs, it remains one of the most enigmatic settlements in northern Kalimdor.",h="Shatterspear Vale is a hidden valley tucked deep in the jagged mountains between Darkshore, Moonglade, and...",sec={{t="A Secluded Sanctuary",b="Ringed completely by steep mountain cliffs, Shatterspear Vale was carved over millennia by a towering waterfall that cascades into a wide, gray-blue lake. Scattered around the shoreline are simple wooden huts, fishing tents, and carved tribal dwellings. Split into two halves by a tumbling mountain river crossed by a rope bridge, the settlement feels entirely isolated from the tumultuous politics of modern Kalimdor. Flight paths connecting northern Kalimdor to Nighthaven in Moonglade occasionally offer passing travelers a fleeting aerial glimpse of the vibrant, dancing villagers far below.",sp=0},{t="An Uneasy Truce",b="The Shatterspear tribe originally split from the ancient Gurubashi Empire following the fall of Hakkar the Soulflayer, wandering far north until settling in this verdant basin. To survive in lands claimed by the night elves, the tribe struck an ancient pact: they were permitted to dwell unmolested so long as they remained strictly within their hidden vale. Should they leave, or should disaster strike them, the elves pledged no aid. To this day, the Shatterspear maintain their insular existence, wary of outsiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shatterspear Vale located?",a="The vale is nestled high in the mountain ridge bordering Darkshore, Moonglade, Felwood, and Winterspring. It is virtually enclosed by sheer cliffs and has no established road connecting it to the lowlands of Darkshore.",al={"shatterspear village location","where is the troll village in darkshore","how to get to shatterspear vale"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives in Shatterspear Vale?",a="It is home to the Shatterspear tribe, a splinter group of jungle trolls who migrated north centuries ago following the defeat of Hakkar the Soulflayer in the ancient Gurubashi Empire.",al={"who lives here","what tribe is this","shatterspear tribe"},it="residents"},{q="Why don't the night elves attack them?",a="The Shatterspear trolls established a historic pact with the local night elves. They agreed to remain entirely confined to their isolated valley and mind their own affairs; in exchange, the Kaldorei left them in peace, neither aiding nor harassing them.",al={"why night elves allow trolls here","night elf troll truce"},it="conflict"},{q="How can you view the village?",a="Adventurers traveling on flight paths to or from Nighthaven in Moonglade can often look down into the gorge and spot the village huts, the waterfall, and dancing trolls below.",al={"see troll village flight path","flight path view of village"},gp=true},{q="Are the Shatterspear trolls hostile?",a="The Shatterspear keep to themselves within their sealed valley, remaining cautious toward all outsiders and defending their home fiercely if provoked.",al={"are shatterspear trolls friendly","can horde visit shatterspear"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Shatterspear Vale?",a="Shatterspear Vale is a hidden valley tucked deep within the rugged mountains bordering Darkshore, Moonglade, Felwood, and Winterspring. Ringed by towering cliffs and ancient trees, the secluded bowl is carved out by a mountain waterfall that cascades into a wide, gray-blue pool. Along the pool's shores rests a quiet settlement of thatched huts and fishing tents belonging to the Shatterspear troll tribe. Surrounded by sheer stone and virtually cut off from the lands below, it remains one of the most isolated sanctuaries in northern Kalimdor.",al={"what is shatterspear vale","shatterspear vale overview","about shatterspear vale"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Shatterspear Vale?",a="The vale became home to the Shatterspear trolls long ago after they broke away from the Gurubashi Empire following the defeat of Hakkar the Soulflayer. Migrating far north to Kalimdor, they settled this secluded mountain bowl and struck an uneasy pact with the local night elves. Under the terms of their agreement, the trolls promised never to leave the borders of their hidden valley in exchange for being left in peace. The night elves honor the solitude, refusing to intervene in the vale's affairs even if it falls under attack.",al={"shatterspear vale history","how was shatterspear vale settled","lore of shatterspear vale"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Shatterspear Vale dangerous?",a="The vale is home to seasoned troll warriors, hunters, and mystical practitioners who are quite formidable, generally matching seasoned adventurers in martial prowess. While the tribe is disinclined to venture out into the world and generally minds its own affairs, intruders who manage to scale the treacherous peaks surrounding the valley will find its defenders fully capable of lethal force if provoked, though members of the Horde will find they are greeted without hostility.",al={"is shatterspear vale dangerous","shatterspear danger","how dangerous are shatterspear trolls"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The Shatterspear demonstrate that jungle trolls migrated far beyond Stranglethorn Vale, having managed to survive surrounded on all sides by suspicious night elves.",["race:NightElf"]="While your people generally harbor an ancient enmity toward all trolls, an exception was made for the Shatterspear, bound by a strict agreement that they never stray from their valley."},kw={"darkshore","jungle trolls","kaldorei pact","moonglade","shatterspear vale","shatterspear village","trolls","waterfall"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:nighthaven","zone:felwood","zone:winterspring","topic:troll","topic:night-elf","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Shatterspear Vale"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-althalaxx"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient Highborne spire standing in northern Darkshore near the coast. Once an isolated retreat for the sorcerer Athrikus Narassin before the Great Sundering, it has become infested by demonic cultists and warlocks practicing dark arts.",h="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient Highborne spire standing in northern Darkshore near the coast.",sec={{t="A Highborne Retreat",b="Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne servants in the coastal towns of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, placing the powerful sorcerer Athrikus Narassin in authority over them. Growing distant from civic governance, Athrikus chose to isolate himself within the nearby Tower of Althalaxx. When the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, the tower endured along the desolate coastline of Darkshore, standing as a quiet ruin of forgotten elven magics.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Strand",b="In the modern era, the tower has stirred with malignant sorcery. Warlocks, dark cultists calling themselves the Cult of the Dark Strand, and allied satyrs have congregated within the ruin under the leadership of Athrikus Narassin himself. Their rites channel demonic magic and torment the lingering spirits of the ancient dead, serving sinister designs tied directly to the demonic Shadow Council.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="It is an ancient elven mage tower built in northern Darkshore during the reign of Queen Azshara, now occupied by dark sorcerers and cultists.",al={"tower of althalaxx","althalaxx tower","what is althalaxx"},it="place"},{q="Who originally built and lived in the tower?",a="Athrikus Narassin, a powerful Highborne sorcerer appointed by Queen Azshara to oversee the nearby settlements of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, retreated here when he grew bored of his duties.",al={"who lived here","athrikus narassin","who built the tower"},it="history"},{q="Who are the cultists occupying the tower now?",a="They belong to the Cult of the Dark Strand, a sect of warlocks, cultists, and satyrs practicing dark rites within the ruined tower.",al={"who are the cultists","cult of the dark strand","althalaxx enemies"},it="residents"},{q="Why are there ghosts and tortured spirits here?",a="The cultists conduct dark rituals and soul-binding magic, subjecting the long-dead elven spirits of ancient Darkshore to agonizing torment for their spells.",al={"why are there ghosts","tortured spirits althalaxx"}},{q="Is the Tower of Althalaxx dangerous?",a="The tower is extremely dangerous. It swarms with fanatical warlocks and cultists of the Cult of the Dark Strand, who serve demonic masters under the direction of the Shadow Council. In addition to these dark spellcasters and their satyr allies, the grounds are haunted by tortured spirits and wraiths bound by foul sorcery.",al={"is tower of althalaxx safe","tower of althalaxx danger","threats at tower of althalaxx"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The tower represents a grim reminder of Highborne corruption and demonic folly lingering on ancestral lands, demanding swift intervention from Darnassus.",["class:Warlock"]="The dark rites conducted by the Cult of the Dark Strand demonstrate the far-reaching influence and lingering presence of the Shadow Council in Kalimdor."},kw={"althalaxx","ameth'aran","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","dark strand","darkshore","highborne","satyr","shadow council"},rel={"quest:965","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:954","topic:highborne","topic:shadow-council","topic:satyr","topic:alliance"},src={"Tower of Althalaxx"}}
E["subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Shore (Darkshore)",z="darkshore",s="The Twilight Shore is a rugged stretch of coast in southern Darkshore, running south from the Long Wash down to the border of Ashenvale. Its gloomy, mist-laden beaches are interrupted by jutting sea cliffs, offshore islets, and treacherous surf. The area is infested with aggressive murloc tribes and ravenous aquatic predators like threshadons.",h="The Twilight Shore is a rugged stretch of coast in southern Darkshore, running south from the Long Wash down...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coastline",b="Stretching south of the Long Wash past the ruins of Ameth'Aran toward Ashenvale, the Twilight Shore is among the most rugged and inhospitable parts of Darkshore's coastline. Gray sand gives way to sharp, wave-battered cliffs and scattered rocky islands. The waters here are notoriously hostile; swimming off the coast invites attacks from territorial threshadons and sea crawlers, while the beaches themselves are dominated by thriving camps of aggressive murlocs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Shore located?",a="It encompasses the southernmost coastal strip of Darkshore, beginning south of the Long Wash (roughly west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran) and continuing southward until reaching the rocky borders of Ashenvale.",al={"twilight shore location","where is twilight shore","twilight shore map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats can be found along the Twilight Shore?",a="The shoreline is heavily settled by aggressive murloc tribes, while the surrounding cold surf is home to territorial threshadons, lurkers, and giant crabs that prey upon unwary travelers.",al={"twilight shore mobs","dangers at twilight shore","what is at twilight shore"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the terrain so rugged here?",a="Unlike the flatter, expansive beaches farther north, the Twilight Shore is fragmented by sharp sea cliffs, rocky shoals, and small offshore islands shaped by the relentless pounding of the Veiled Sea.",al={"why are there cliffs","twilight shore geography"}},{q="What is the Twilight Shore?",a="The Twilight Shore is a rugged stretch of coastline along southern Darkshore, running from the edge of the Long Wash down toward the border of Ashenvale. Unlike the flatter sandy reaches farther north, this coast is jagged and unforgiving, marked by jutting sea cliffs, rocky islets, and misty gray beaches battered by cold ocean waters.",al={"twilight shore lore","what is twilight shore","about twilight shore"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Twilight Shore dangerous?",a="Yes, it is among the most hazardous stretches of shoreline in the region. Swarms of aggressive murlocs claim the rocky banks and outcroppings, while the surf is prowled by starving threshadons eager to snap at swimmers. Traveling near the churning surf or clambering along its isolated bluffs leaves you vulnerable to ambush from both land and sea.",al={"is twilight shore safe","how dangerous is twilight shore","twilight shore dangers"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Twilight Shore marks the lonely, mist-shrouded threshold between the haunted ruins of Darkshore and the sacred ancestral forests of Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","coast","darkshore","long wash","murlocs","threshadons","twilight shore"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:long-wash","zone:ashenvale","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:murloc"},src={"Twilight Shore (Darkshore)"}}
E["subzone:twilight-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Vale",z="darkshore",s="Twilight Vale encompasses the dense, shadowed southern woodlands of Darkshore stretching toward the Ashenvale border. Beneath its gloom, corrupted furbolgs, rabid bears, and vicious nightsabers prowl the undergrowth, making off-road passage perilous. It serves as a grim threshold between the tainted coast of Darkshore and the sacred canopies to the south.",h="Twilight Vale encompasses the dense, shadowed southern woodlands of Darkshore stretching toward the Ashenvale...",sec={{t="A Perilous Threshold",b="Running from the south of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran all the way to the border of Ashenvale, the Twilight Vale blankets the southern reaches of Darkshore in perpetual dusk. The encroaching corruption plaguing northern Kalimdor has bitten deep into the wildlife here. Rabid bears roam alongside feral nightsabers, and hostile furbolg tribes stalk the dark wood. Sentinels and travelers alike advise sticking strictly to the main road, as straying even a few paces into the trees invites swift and deadly ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Vale located?",a="Twilight Vale forms the southern portion of Darkshore. It begins just south of the highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran and extends all the way to the border pass that enters Ashenvale.",al={"twilight vale location","where is twilight vale","twilight vale map"},it="place"},{q="What threats wander this forest?",a="The vale is infested with afflicted wildlife and hostile tribes. Travelers will encounter rabid bears, aggressive nightsabers, and corrupted furbolgs who attack anyone intruding upon their territory.",al={"twilight vale monsters","what is in twilight vale","danger twilight vale"},it="threat"},{q="Is it safe to travel through the vale?",a="No wilderness in Darkshore is entirely safe, but sticking firmly to the established dirt road is far safer than cutting through the underbrush. Straying off the beaten track puts you directly in the path of feral beasts.",al={"is twilight vale safe","safe path darkshore to ashenvale"},it="danger"},{q="Why is the wildlife in the vale corrupted?",a="Darkshore has suffered heavily since the Third War and the sundering magic lingering across northern Kalimdor. Tainted water and dark magical residue have maddened the local wildlife and turned peaceful furbolgs violent.",al={"why are bears rabid in darkshore","furbolg corruption twilight vale"},it="origin"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The degradation of the southern woods weighs heavily on the night elves, who mourn the corruption of the native beasts and the fall of their furbolg neighbors so close to Ashenvale's threshold.",["class:Druid"]="Druids passing between Darkshore and Ashenvale witness firsthand the sickness afflicting the vale's creatures, underscoring the urgent need to cleanse the land."},kw={"ameth'aran","ashenvale","darkshore","furbolgs","nightsabers","rabid bears","twilight vale"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Twilight Vale"}}
E["subzone:wildbend-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Wildbend River",z="darkshore",s="Wildbend River is a tainted waterway winding through the southern forests of Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients. Flowing down directly from the corrupted heights of Felwood, its waters carry demonic poison toward the sea, endangering the surrounding wilderness.",h="Wildbend River is a tainted waterway winding through the southern forests of Darkshore near the Grove of the...",sec={{t="A Toxic Mountain Stream",b="Wildbend River cuts through the southern reaches of Darkshore, flowing westward past the sacred Grove of the Ancients before emptying into the sea. Rather than offering clean nourishment to the woodland, it brings corruption down from the mountains. The river is the direct continuation of Felwood's Bloodvenom River, tumbling through the rocky ridges and dragging foul, corrupted runoff into Darkshore's ecosystem. The night elves monitor its banks closely, watching for twisted wildlife and the creeping spread of demonic blight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Wildbend River corrupted?",a="The river originates high in the mountains of Felwood, where it is known as the Bloodvenom River. Felwood was thoroughly saturated with demonic magic during the Third War, and that foul runoff spills down the cliffs into Darkshore as the Wildbend River.",al={"why is water tainted","wildbend river poison","darkshore dirty water"},it="ruin"},{q="Where does the river flow?",a="Cascading down from the eastern ridges that separate Felwood from Darkshore, the river winds through southern Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients before flowing into the Veiled Sea.",al={"where is wildbend river","wildbend path","wildbend river location"},it="place"},{q="Does the river affect the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The river passes close to the Grove of the Ancients, posing a constant environmental threat to the ancient protectors rooted there. The night elves work tirelessly to contain the blight and prevent the poisoned water from rotting the sacred groves.",al={"grove of the ancients water","is grove of ancients corrupted"}},{q="What is the Wildbend River?",a="The Wildbend River is a corrupted waterway winding through southern Darkshore, near the Grove of the Ancients. It originates high in the corrupted highlands of Felwood, tumbling down the mountains as a continuation of the Bloodvenom River before carving its way toward the sea.",al={"what is wildbend river","wildbend river","about wildbend river"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Wildbend River dangerous?",a="Yes, its waters are deeply foul and treacherous. Because the river is the downstream continuation of Felwood's Bloodvenom River, demonic corruption cascades straight from the tainted highlands into Darkshore, polluting the surrounding landscape and threatening the sacred groves nearby.",al={"wildbend river dangerous","dangers of wildbend river","is wildbend safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The polluted waters cascading from Felwood threaten the ancient roots of Darkshore, making the riverbanks a frequent concern for night elf wardens.",["class:Druid"]="Druids studying the ecological aftermath of the Third War keep a wary eye on the river, monitoring how deeply Felwood's corruption penetrates downstream flora and fauna."},kw={"bloodvenom river","darkshore","felwood","grove of the ancients","tainted water","wildbend river"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:felwood","subzone:bloodvenom-river","quest:952"},src={"Wildbend River"}}
E["zone:darkshore"] = {t="zone",n="Darkshore",z="darkshore",s="Darkshore is a cold, mist-shrouded strip of coast lining northwestern Kalimdor, dotted with ancient Kaldorei ruins and troubled wildlife. Anchored by the Alliance harbor town of Auberdine, it serves as the primary continental gateway for travelers arriving from Teldrassil and the Eastern Kingdoms. Beyond the patrolled road, demonic cults, encroaching naga, and a creeping corruption from the highlands threaten the region's delicate balance.",h="Darkshore is a cold, mist-shrouded strip of coast lining northwestern Kalimdor, dotted with ancient Kaldorei...",sec={{t="A Land of Mist and Memory",b="Stretching beneath the western shadows of Mount Hyjal and Felwood, Darkshore is characterized by pine groves, sea fog, and rocky beaches beaten by cold waves. Millennia ago, this coast was home to the flourishing Kaldorei twin cities of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. Shattered during the Great Sundering, their skeletal pillars and marble arches now lie half-drowned in the surf or overgrown with roots, haunted by restless Highborne spirits and overrun by scavenger murlocs and invasive naga.",sp=0},{t="The Haven of Auberdine",b="Following the Third War and the planting of Teldrassil, the night elves established Auberdine as a bustling maritime haven amidst the wilderness. Featuring wooden piers that welcome regular vessels from Rut'theran Village and Menethil Harbor in the distant Wetlands, Auberdine is the lifeline linking night elf territory to the rest of the Alliance. Sentinels diligently patrol the trade highway south toward Ashenvale, though their small garrison struggles to police the deep wilds beyond the path.",sp=0},{t="Poisoned Waters and Whispering Depths",b="Despite its shelter against the eastern mountains, Darkshore suffers from a slow, malignant rot. Corrupted run-off trickling down from Felwood poisons sources like Cliffspring Falls, fouling the water table and driving the local bears, stags, and furbolgs of Blackwood Den into violent madness. Worse still, sinister organizations have established footholds in the shadows: the Dark Strand and Twilight's Hammer cultists perform foul rituals at the Tower of Althalaxx and convene around the terrifying, ancient monument known as the Master's Glaive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Darkshore?",a="Alliance players can take a boat directly to Auberdine from either Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil or from Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Horde travelers journeying north must walk through Ashenvale, following the main road northeast from Zoram'gar Outpost up across the border.",al={"getting to darkshore","how to reach auberdine","darkshore boat"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What is wrong with the local wildlife and furbolgs?",a="Rivers running out of the tainted heights of Felwood, such as the Cliffspring River, wash demonic pollution straight down into Darkshore's water table. Drinking from these foul streams has driven the native furbolg tribes feral and infected the local deer and predators with disease and aggression.",al={"why are animals sick","furbolg corruption","darkshore taint"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran?",a="They were prosperous twin Kaldorei cities destroyed ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering. Their ruler, Athrikus Narassin, claimed he would rescue his people from the cataclysm, but he instead bound their souls into gems to preserve them as eternal power sources for himself, leaving the ruins full of weeping ghosts.",al={"ameth'aran history","bashal'aran lore","ruins in darkshore"},sp=1,it="ruin"},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="Located in southern Darkshore, the Master's Glaive is a massive petrified skull impaled by an enormous stone weapon. It is an ancient relic associated with the primordial Old Gods and their servitors, and it currently attracts dangerous cultists from the Twilight's Hammer.",al={"what is the masters glaive","giant skull darkshore","masters glaive monster"},it="place"},{q="Who is the giant tree in the Grove of the Ancients?",a="That is Onu, a wise and venerable Ancient of Lore. Resting in his tranquil grove south of Auberdine, he ponders the disturbing encroachment of the Twilight's Hammer cult and assists travelers in investigating disturbances throughout the forest.",al={"ancient of lore darkshore","who is onu","tree person darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Who lives in the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The tower is occupied by the Dark Strand, a vicious cult practicing dark sorcery and summoning demonic entities. Their cabal actively ambushes unwary travelers along the northern reaches of the coastal woods.",al={"tower of althalaxx","darkshore tower cultists","althalaxx cult"},it="residents"},{q="What is Darkshore?",a="Darkshore is a long, foggy strip of rocky coast running along northwestern Kalimdor. Sheltered beneath mountains to the east and the Veiled Sea to the west, it features shadowed woods, rainswept beaches, and crumbling elven ruins. It serves as the night elves' primary gateway between their island home of Teldrassil and the mainland.",al={"tell me about darkshore","what kind of zone is darkshore","darkshore overview"},it="place",add=true,nx={8,9}},{q="Why does it look so ruined and gloomy?",a="Much of Darkshore was shattered ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering, reducing grand Kaldorei cities to rubble. Today, an ever-present sea mist, stormy winds, and creeping magical pollution trickling down from tainted mountain rivers give the coast its persistent, mournful atmosphere.",al={"why is darkshore gloomy","why is darkshore ruined","darkshore destroyed"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Who lives here now?",a="Night elves maintain the settlement of Auberdine alongside visiting Alliance traders, including dwarves and humans. Outside the town, the wilderness is occupied by hostile naga, troggs, corrupted furbolgs, and remnants of the dark cults that lurk among the ancient stones.",al={"who inhabits darkshore","darkshore population","who lives in darkshore"},it="residents",add=true},{q="What is Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is a quiet coastal settlement and the primary Alliance port in northern Kalimdor. Featuring low wooden elven halls, earthen paths, and a prominent harbor lighthouse, it connects Darnassus across the water to the mainland and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"auberdine town","tell me about auberdine","what is the town in darkshore"},it="place",add=true,nx={11,12}},{q="Who runs Auberdine?",a="Auberdine's civic affairs are led by the elder Thundris Windweaver, supported by the Auberdine Village Council. The town's military guard is handled by the Sentinels, with officers like Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea coordinating local patrols and defense.",al={"auberdine leader","who is in charge of auberdine","auberdine village council"},it="leader",add=true},{q="Why is it built on the coast?",a="After night elves returned following the Third War, they chose this spot to revive maritime travel and supply lines. The port provides a vital ferry link to Rut'theran Village at Teldrassil and hosts long-distance trading vessels sailing from Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why build auberdine on the beach","auberdine port purpose","why coast auberdine"},it="purpose",add=true},{q="Who's in charge here?",a="The night elves claim Darkshore as part of their burgeoning kingdom. Elder Thundris Windweaver oversees civil matters from Auberdine, while the night elf Sentinels maintain military command along the coastal road and regional borders.",al={"who rules darkshore","who controls darkshore","darkshore leadership"},it="in_charge",add=true,nx={14,15}},{q="Who are the Sentinels?",a="The Sentinels are the traditional standing army of the Kaldorei, composed primarily of elite night elf warrior women. They patrol the roadways, guard settlements like Auberdine, and defend elven territory from encroaching monsters and invaders.",al={"sentinel army","night elf sentinels","what are the sentinels"},it="people",add=true},{q="Do they answer to Darnassus?",a="Yes. Darkshore's defenders owe allegiance to the Kaldorei leadership residing in Darnassus atop Teldrassil, even though the capital's high authorities sometimes view the rugged frontier town of Auberdine as a remote outpost of outcasts and misfits.",al={"do sentinels serve darnassus","darnassus authority darkshore","does auberdine answer to darnassus"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks on the beach?",a="Darkshore is notorious for brutal weather, heavy rain, dense sea mist, and jagged shallows. Wicked winds stir sudden waves that drive vessels onto the rocks, leaving shallow waters littered with hulls that failed to navigate the passage to Auberdine.",al={"darkshore shipwrecks","why are ships wrecked here","sunken boats darkshore"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why are the Highborne haunting these ruins?",a="Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne were the sorcerous nobility of Queen Azshara who ruled twin cities like Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. When the Great Sundering shattered their empire, their ruler trapped their souls in binding gems, leaving their tormented spirits to haunt the stone pillars for eternity.",al={"why are highborne ghosts here","ameth'aran ghosts","who were the highborne"},it="history",add=true},{q="What corrupted the Blackwood tribe?",a="Though once friendly neighbors to the night elves, the Blackwood furbolgs have been driven into an insatiable madness by dark corruption. Rivers running down from the tainted heights of Felwood carry poisoned water across Darkshore, twisting the minds of beasts and furbolgs alike.",al={"blackwood furbolgs crazy","why are furbolgs mad darkshore","furbolg taint source"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Who are the Twilight's Hammer and why are they camped here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer is a nihilistic apocalyptic cult dedicated to the dark entities known as the Old Gods. They have gathered at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, conducting rituals and excavations around ancient subterranean remains buried beneath the earth.",al={"twilight hammer darkshore","cultists darkshore","why are twilight cultists here"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Why is Darkshore dangerous?",a="Beyond Auberdine's immediate borders, the coast is fraught with perils. Feral beasts and enraged furbolgs stalk the trees, naga and murlocs infest the beaches, and shadowy cults like the Dark Strand and Twilight's Hammer ambush travelers from hidden outposts.",al={"is darkshore safe","darkshore threats","dangers of darkshore"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Darkshore?",a="The coast earned its name from the thick, shadowed woods and the somber, unusual mist that blankets the entire shoreline, obscuring daylight and casting the beaches in perpetual gloom.",al={"why darkshore named","name origin darkshore","why is it called darkshore"},it="name",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Darkshore?",a="You likely arrived through Auberdine, the bustling coastal port and trade hub that connects northern Kalimdor to the wider world. If you journeyed from the boughs of Teldrassil, a ferry carried you across the mist-shrouded waters from Rut'theran Village to the mainland docks. Travelers venturing from the Eastern Kingdoms often take the long voyage aboard the great sailing ships from Menethil Harbor. Alternatively, hardy wanderers trekking overland from the deep forests of Ashenvale follow the patrolled Sentinel road northward onto the rocky, mist-blanketed shore.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to darkshore","how did i arrive here"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Darkshore?",a="The night elves in Auberdine desperately need help containing a spreading malaise across the coast. A foul corruption trickling from the Felwood heights has poisoned the rivers and water table, driving the local wildlife and peaceful Blackwood furbolgs into violent madness. Beyond the woods, ancient Highborne ruins like Ameth'Aran are stirring with restless ghosts, naga and murlocs encroach upon the rocky beaches, and sinister Twilight's Hammer cultists gather around the ancient titan weapon at the Master's Glaive. The Auberdine Village Council and the Sentinels rely on travelers like you to restore balance.",al={"why am i here","what should i do in darkshore","what is my purpose here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Darkshore serves as the front line for Cenarion Circle initiates answering summons from Moonglade to diagnose tainted waterways and brew cleansers for sick forest creatures.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil, Darkshore is their first step onto mainland Kalimdor, confronting the painful ruins of their ancient civilization and the spreading corruption of the wild.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine represents the Alliance's primary trade nexus in northern Kalimdor, maintaining the direct maritime link connecting Stormwind and Ironforge to the night elf capital of Darnassus.",["faction:Horde"]="A remote, heavily patrolled Alliance bastion, Darkshore sits directly north of Horde encampments in Ashenvale, offering a treacherous coastline prowled by hostile sentinels and dangerous cults."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","bashal'aran","blackwood den","cliffspring falls","darkshore","master's glaive","onu","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:952","quest:965","quest:6122","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:ashenvale"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Darkshore (Classic)","Darkshore"}}
